(window.__ntLang=window.__ntLang||{})["en"]={"бах":{"name":"Johann Sebastian Bach","def":"Johann Sebastian Bach (1685–1750), German composer and organist, the summit of polyphony.","html":"<p>Johann Sebastian Bach (1685–1750), German composer and organist, the summit of polyphony. In his lifetime he was not a &quot;genius&quot; but a working man: a cantor writing music to a deadline every week, as a baker bakes bread. Greatness came afterwards — and turned out to be among the most durable in human history.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Music as audible regularity.</strong> Bach's counterpoint is almost mathematics: strict rules out of which freedom is born. His fugues are what <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">a law of Nature</a> sounds like if you play it on an organ. It is no accident that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a>, a Spinozist, rested precisely on Bach: both believed in the harmony of the laws of the universe. The bridge between <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">music</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> is shorter here than anywhere else.</li><li><strong>Soli Deo Gloria — &quot;glory to God alone&quot;.</strong> Bach signed his scores this way. Neoterra reads it without losing the meaning: the glory belongs to Nature, whose laws of harmony he heard and wrote down. The human being as <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">the organ by which Nature listens to itself</a>.</li><li><strong>A master, not an idol.</strong> Bach built no cult around himself — he did the work, taught pupils, repaired organs. An example of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> as a daily craft rather than a gesture of genius. This is exactly the kind of example <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">the alley of memory</a> needs: one learns from him, one does not worship him.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">Family</a> as a riverbed.</strong> The Bach dynasty spans generations of musicians; twenty children, several of whom became composers. Knowledge and mastery passed on through family are a living illustration of the canon of the family: a union that works for the future.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li>Bach was a man of Lutheran faith and church service: his music was written inside a dogmatics Neoterra does not share. But this is a divergence of circumstances, not of substance: the language of harmony proved larger than the confession — the <em>St Matthew Passion</em> moves an atheist and a Buddhist alike.</li><li>The strictness of Bach's form is sometimes read as unfreedom. Bach's own answer: freedom grows out of discipline, as improvisation grows out of learned rules (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a>).</li></ul><h2>Key ideas</h2><blockquote><p>&quot;The aim of music is to touch hearts.&quot;</p></blockquote><p>Playing the notes is not hard — by Bach's legendary remark, &quot;one has only to hit the right keys at the right time, and the instrument plays itself&quot;. The modesty of a master, behind which stands a whole life of work.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a> — a language without translation; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> — the ninth law</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Albert Einstein (1879–1955)</a> — the harmony of laws, heard and written down</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> — Bach's place: an example, not an idol</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a> — the organ and acoustics of Neoterra's temples</li></ul>"},"библиотека-пути":{"name":"The Library of the Path","def":"In Neoterra there is no single sacred book.","html":"<p>In Neoterra <strong>there is no single sacred book</strong>. Truth is too large to fit into one text. Hence the Library of the Path — an open collection of books that help a person grow, and <strong>every generation may add to it</strong>.</p><h2>Through the lens of Neoterra</h2><p>This is a direct <strong>anti-dogma</strong>. Where religions and ideologies often rest on one canonical text, Neoterra puts a library — many voices instead of one. Refusing a sacred book is not disregard for knowledge but respect for its scale: no text is final, just as the wiki itself is not final.</p><p>The principle is rooted in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a> (one may not forbid doubt even of one's own books), in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> (knowledge is a process, not a possession) and in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">the Principle of the Network</a> (not one summit, but a growing web of origins). In spirit <strong>this wiki itself is the Library of the Path</strong>: added to, connected, unfinished on principle.</p><h2>What is in it</h2><p>The Neoterra canon here is only one shelf beside philosophy, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>, history, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"литература\">literature</a>, biography. In practice its seed is even a single bookcase in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the temple</a>: &quot;knowledge must be available to everyone who comes&quot;. The library is filled by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">the People of the Path</a> — but as examples of potential, not as prophets.</p><h2>The bond with philosophy</h2><p>Openness and constant addition chime with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper</a>: knowledge grows through criticism and revision, and a &quot;final book&quot; would close that growth off. The Library of the Path is the institutional form of falsifiability: everything in it can be added to and disputed.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>If any book may be included — is there any selection? By whom and by what criterion (cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a>)?</li><li>How does openness live with the fact that some books carry enmity and dogma — do we keep them as a monument or not?</li><li>Will the &quot;canon of Neoterra&quot; in time not become the very single book that the canon forbids?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-культуры-сводка\">The Canon of Culture (0.6)</a> — the source</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"литература\">Literature</a> — where the Library of the Path lives</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — knowledge as revisable</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a> — the library as part of the community's space</li></ul>"},"боб-марли":{"name":"Bob Marley (1945–1981)","def":"Jamaican musician, a symbol of reggae and of the Rastafari movement.","html":"<p>Jamaican musician, a symbol of reggae and of the Rastafari movement. His music about unity, love, freedom and resistance to oppression reached people on every continent. <strong>Neoterra remembers and honours Bob Marley on a par with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">the predecessors</a></strong> — as a man who tried to unite people without fearing for his own life.</p><blockquote><p>One love, one heart. Let's get together and feel all right.</p></blockquote><h2>The man who was not afraid</h2><p>Marley is not merely a musician but an example of a philosophy of unity lived out, and paid for with himself.</p><ul><li><strong>December 1976.</strong> Two days before the &quot;Smile Jamaica&quot; concert, meant to quiet the political violence in Jamaica, an attempt was made on Marley's life — he, his wife and his manager were shot and wounded. Despite his wounds he walked onto the stage and played the concert. Asked why, he answered:</li></ul><blockquote><p>&quot;The people who are trying to make this world worse aren't taking a day off. How can I?&quot;</p></blockquote><ul><li><strong>April 1978, the One Love Peace Concert.</strong> At the height of the civil confrontation Marley brought onto the stage the two warring political leaders of Jamaica — Michael Manley and Edward Seaga — and joined their hands above his head. A gesture of union stronger than words.</li></ul><p>This readiness to take a risk for the reconciliation of people is what Neoterra sets alongside the courage of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates</a> and the steadfastness of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius</a>.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">The unity of humanity</a></strong> — the central theme of everything Marley made; not uniformity, but the joining of the different.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of thought</a></strong> — &quot;Emancipate yourselves from mental slavery; none but ourselves can free our minds&quot;.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation, not destruction</a></strong> — peace and love instead of hatred.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for people</a></strong> regardless of race, nation and religion — he united through music without dividing people.</li></ul><h2>A voice: on goodness and on people</h2><blockquote><p>&quot;The greatness of a man is not in how much wealth he acquires, but in his integrity and his ability to affect those around him positively.&quot;</p></blockquote><blockquote><p>&quot;Love the life you live. Live the life you love.&quot;</p></blockquote><blockquote><p>&quot;Don't worry about a thing, 'cause every little thing gonna be all right.&quot; (<em>Three Little Birds</em>)</p></blockquote><blockquote><p>&quot;Better to die fighting for freedom than be a prisoner all the days of your life.&quot;</p></blockquote><h2>The songs — philosophy in sound</h2><p>Neoterra's ideas live in Marley not in treatises but in songs:</p><ul><li><strong>One Love / People Get Ready</strong> — a hymn of the unity of humanity — <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Bob+Marley+One+Love\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">listen</a></li><li><strong>Redemption Song</strong> — freedom of mind, emancipation from mental slavery — <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Bob+Marley+Redemption+Song\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">listen</a></li><li><strong>Get Up, Stand Up</strong> — standing for your rights and dignity — <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Bob+Marley+Get+Up+Stand+Up\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">listen</a></li><li><strong>Three Little Birds</strong> — calm and trust in life — <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Bob+Marley+Three+Little+Birds\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">listen</a></li></ul><p>Official site: <a href=\"https://www.bobmarley.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">bobmarley.com</a></p><h2>The key idea</h2><p>Marley is proof that the philosophy of Neoterra can exist not in texts but in music, in a way of living, in a readiness to risk oneself for reconciliation. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">The unity of humanity</a> is not only a concept; it is a feeling that can be passed on and that one can stand up for.</p><h2>Memory</h2><p>Bob Marley is one of those whose names Neoterra keeps on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the Wall of Memory</a>: people who made the world closer and kinder. Remembering them is part of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> towards the past.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"ван-гог":{"name":"Vincent van Gogh (1853–1890)","def":"Dutch post-impressionist painter.","html":"<p>Dutch post-impressionist painter. He was not recognised in his lifetime; after his death he became one of the most influential painters in history.</p><blockquote><p>Beauty is in the eye of the beholder.</p></blockquote><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Beauty in the ordinary</strong> — Van Gogh painted boots, sunflowers, a starry sky over the provinces. He showed that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> and daily life are shot through with a beauty one has to learn to see.</li><li><strong>Respect for life</strong> — every subject of his is an acknowledgement of the value of existence.</li><li><strong>Creation as meaning</strong> — he went on creating in a condition in which most would have given up.</li></ul><h2>The key idea</h2><p>Van Gogh is a reminder that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> is not only rational. Perception, feeling, beauty are as much parts of human growth as knowledge is.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Fyodor Dostoevsky (1821–1881)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a></li></ul>"},"достоевский":{"name":"Fyodor Dostoevsky (1821–1881)","def":"Russian writer, one of the greatest novelists in world literature.","html":"<p>Russian writer, one of the greatest novelists in world literature. Author of <em>Crime and Punishment</em>, <em>The Brothers Karamazov</em>, <em>The Idiot</em>. He explored the depths of human psychology, morality and faith.</p><blockquote><p>Beauty will save the world.</p></blockquote><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>The study of the human soul</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">the human being</a> in Dostoevsky is contradictory, many-sided, capable of greatness and of falling. This is an honest picture, and Neoterra does not simplify it.</li><li><strong>Moral choice</strong> — responsibility for one's deeds as the central theme. Neither determinism nor excuse by circumstance.</li><li><strong>The significance of beauty</strong> — not aesthetics for its own sake, but beauty as a moral force.</li><li><strong>The search for the meaning of life</strong> — Dostoevsky's characters seek what Neoterra invites everyone to seek.</li></ul><h2>Key quotations and how they relate to Neoterra</h2><blockquote><p>The mystery of human existence lies not in just staying alive, but in finding something to live for.</p><p><em>(The Brothers Karamazov)</em></p></blockquote><p>This comes closest to the very core of Neoterra: life must not merely exist but grow (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a>). Dostoevsky's formula and the wiki's almost coincide — with one divergence: for him the &quot;what for&quot; leads to a personal God, whereas in Neoterra the direction is immanent and addressed to no one personally (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>).</p><blockquote><p>Man is a mystery. It must be unravelled, and if you spend your whole life at it, do not say you have wasted your time.</p><p><em>(letter to his brother Mikhail, 1839)</em></p></blockquote><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The search for truth</a> in its pure form: knowledge as a process, not a possession. And a direct support for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">the human being</a> — a creature that is a task to itself (the same thought in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Kafka</a>: &quot;you are the task&quot;).</p><blockquote><p>Hell is the suffering of being no longer able to love.</p><p><em>(the elder Zosima, The Brothers Karamazov)</em></p></blockquote><p>Hell here is neither a place nor a punishment but the loss of a capacity — something that happens to a person from within. This chimes with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">good and evil</a> as a lack rather than an essence, and with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">love</a> as the condition without which the rest does not hold.</p><blockquote><p>Beauty will save the world.</p><p><em>(Prince Myshkin's words as reported by Ippolit, The Idiot)</em></p></blockquote><p>A direct ground for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> as the ninth law of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the Canon of Nature</a>: not a luxury but part of a full life. The context is worth remembering: in the novel the phrase is uttered mockingly, and Dostoevsky leaves it unproven.</p><p><strong>Checking an attribution.</strong> The common line &quot;suffering is the sole origin of knowing truth&quot; is widely attributed to Dostoevsky, but is not found in him in that form. The nearest in sense is from <em>Notes from Underground</em>, where suffering is called the sole cause of <strong>consciousness</strong>, not of truth, and it is said by the paradoxalist narrator, not by the author as a sermon. Neoterra does not take the quotation in this form, and not only because of the reference: &quot;sole&quot; would abolish <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">love</a> and the joy of knowing as paths to truth, and the analysis in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> (&quot;Measure and support&quot;) has already shown that suffering supplies material, not merit.</p><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>Dostoevsky is deeply religious in the Orthodox sense. Neoterra does not require religiosity, but neither does it reject it — they exist on different planes.</p><p><strong>Suffering as a path.</strong> In Dostoevsky suffering is redemptive and almost obligatory: through it the character comes to himself. Neoterra accepts the observation and refuses the norm — darkness supplies material, but it is not sent and it does not ennoble by itself (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>). One who has passed through suffering does not stand above one who has not.</p><p><strong>&quot;If there is no God, everything is permitted.&quot;</strong> Ivan Karamazov's thought (in the novel it is voiced differently and more mildly than in the retellings) is unacceptable to Neoterra as a conclusion: ethics here rests not on fear of an authority but on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">the Great Principle</a> and on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> — to oneself and to others. Neoterra does not dispute that without a ground ethics hangs in the air: it simply lays <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> as that ground, rather than a commandment.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Franz Kafka (1883–1924)</a> — guilt, judgement and the human limit; the nearest neighbour by theme</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> — he stands in the group &quot;Depth and limit&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"литература\">Literature</a> — the novel as a laboratory of the soul</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — where Neoterra parts with redemptive suffering</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ван-гог\">Vincent van Gogh (1853–1890)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li></ul>"},"Искусство":{"name":"Art — area","def":"Origin: the Seed of Neoterra","html":"<p>Origin: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the Seed of Neoterra</a></p><p>Art is a way of seeing beauty in the ordinary, of living through the depth of a person, and of joining people through culture. Painting, music and literature as paths of growth.</p><p>The area's conceptual anchor is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">culture</a> (Canon of Culture 0.6: the collective memory of humanity, what unites rather than divides). Beneath it lies <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> (the ninth law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon of Nature</a>: beauty is not a luxury but part of a full life) as its core.</p><h2>Shoots</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a> — the collective memory of humanity (the area's anchor)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> — why beauty matters</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a> — humanity's universal language</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"литература\">Literature</a> — books as many lives lived</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"библиотека-пути\">The library of the way</a> — an open collection of books, with no single sacred one</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"праздники\">Festivals</a> — Neoterra's calendar: of Spring, of Love, of Memory, of Creation</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бах\">Bach</a> — the lawfulness of Nature turned into harmony</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"моцарт\">Mozart</a> — lightness as a form of perfection; the trace matters more than the length of a life</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"паганини\">Paganini</a> — the &quot;impossible&quot; as the merely not-yet-done; a lesson in mythmaking</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ван-гог\">Van Gogh</a> — beauty in the ordinary</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"микеланджело\">Michelangelo Buonarroti (1475–1564)</a> — anatomy within monastery walls; <em>The Creation of Adam</em> and the brain in the cloak as resonance, not proof</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сальвадор-дали\">Salvador Dalí</a> — nuclear mysticism: science and faith as one language; the tesseract instead of the cross</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уитмен\">Whitman</a> — a blade of grass as a letter from God; &quot;I contain multitudes&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Bob Marley</a> — unity through culture</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Dostoevsky</a> — the depth of the human soul</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Kafka</a> — the book as an axe; an honest witness of the limit and of the faceless system</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"рубин\">Rubin</a> — the artist as a conduit of Nature, not a source; creation as a way of being</li></ul><h2>Cross-links</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> — art as a mirror of human nature</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — culture as a bridge between people; the single history of humanity</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> — the history of every people as a common inheritance</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> — creative work as a form of growth</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> — beauty found in Nature and carried on by the human being</li></ul><blockquote><p>Open question (partly settled by the Canon of Culture 0.6): the area grows around the anchor <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">culture</a> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">music</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"литература\">literature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"библиотека-пути\">the library of the way</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"праздники\">festivals</a> have been separated out. Further division (visual art, theatre, cinema on their own pages) will follow as material arrives.</p></blockquote>"},"кафка":{"name":"Franz Kafka (1883–1924)","def":"A Prague writer who wrote in German; by day an official at an insurance institute.","html":"<p>A Prague writer who wrote in German; by day an official at an insurance institute. Author of <em>The Metamorphosis</em>, <em>The Trial</em>, <em>The Castle</em>. Almost everything that matters appeared after his death: Kafka asked his friend Max Brod to burn the manuscripts, and Brod refused.</p><p>Neoterra takes Kafka not as a source of propositions — he asserts nothing and teaches nothing — but as <strong>the most honest witness of the limit</strong>: the place where the world is impenetrable to a person and the system has no face.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><p><strong>Art as clearing, not consolation.</strong> &quot;A book must be the axe for the frozen sea within us&quot; (letter to Oskar Pollak, 1904). This is exactly why Neoterra values <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"литература\">literature</a>: not entertainment but an instrument — and close to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">clarity of mind</a>, where clearing is the condition of having a thought of one's own. Beauty in Kafka does not adorn, it opens up (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a>).</p><p>The wiki held the two halves of this image apart until it brought them together: the frozen sea is that stagnant edge of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">balance</a> on which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Schopenhauer</a> built an ideal, and the axe is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the fracture</a> with which stagnation is broken open. The book here plays the role of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a>: it comes from outside the frame, because from within the frame cannot be broken.</p><p><strong>A part has no separate side.</strong> &quot;In the struggle between yourself and the world, second the world&quot; (the Zürau aphorisms, 1917–18). Almost a literal match with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">balance</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">the human being</a>: equilibrium with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> is not a bargain struck &quot;between&quot;, because a person is not a party in a dispute with the whole but a part of it. Kafka arrives at this out of despair, Neoterra out of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a>; the formula is the same.</p><p><strong>Irreversibility as a condition.</strong> &quot;From a certain point onward there is no longer any turning back. That is the point that must be reached&quot; (ibid.). This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">the opening of the circle</a> in a single line: growth goes by a turn of the spiral, not in a circle, and the point of no return is not to be avoided — it is to be sought. Hence too the bond with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a> and with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>, which has no way back to a previous state.</p><p><strong>The human being as an unclosed task.</strong> &quot;You are the task. No pupil far and wide&quot; (ibid.). This falls into <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the path of a human being</a>: no one will come to solve you for you, and there may be no teacher — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> stays with you. Neoterra accepts the first half and disputes the second: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">a mentor</a> may not be found, but their absence is a loss, not the order of things.</p><p><strong>A diagnosis of the machine.</strong> <em>The Trial</em> and <em>The Castle</em> describe a system in which responsibility is dissolved: no one is guilty because an authority decides. Neoterra accepts this as a working diagnosis for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">the vices</a>: evil here is neither an essence nor anyone's intent but a consequence of a design in which no one answers personally for anything. The counterweight Neoterra offers is small communities with faces instead of authorities (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a>).</p><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p><strong>From the limit Kafka draws hopelessness, Neoterra draws honesty.</strong> That the world is impenetrable the wiki admits outright: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">the languages of Nature</a> says most of Nature's languages are still unread by human beings, and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> calls this the border of our understanding. But in Kafka the law is not merely unreadable — it was not meant to be read, and the attempt is voided in advance. Neoterra does not follow him there: unread does not mean unreadable (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>).</p><p><strong>&quot;There is hope, an infinite amount of hope — but not for us.&quot;</strong> The words are reported by Max Brod as said in conversation; they are not Kafka's own text — but the formula is exact and strong. Neoterra answers not by disputing it but by shifting the addressee: hope really is not for us personally — it is for what continues through us (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a>). Personal finitude does not abolish continuation; that is precisely why <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">death</a> in the wiki is not a sentence but reprocessing.</p><p><strong>Guilt with no way out.</strong> In Kafka the hero is guilty of no one knows what and cannot clear himself. Neoterra holds <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> strictly the other way round: it is possible only for what was within your power, and it presupposes <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">forgiveness</a> — including of oneself. Guilt without an object and without an outcome is not responsibility but an imitation of it.</p><h2>Key quotations and ideas</h2><blockquote><p>A book must be the axe for the frozen sea within us.</p><p><em>(letter to Oskar Pollak, 27 January 1904)</em></p></blockquote><blockquote><p>In the struggle between yourself and the world, second the world.</p><p><em>(the Zürau aphorisms)</em></p></blockquote><blockquote><p>From a certain point onward there is no longer any turning back. That is the point that must be reached.</p><p><em>(the Zürau aphorisms)</em></p></blockquote><blockquote><p>You are the task. No pupil far and wide.</p><p><em>(the Zürau aphorisms)</em></p></blockquote><p><strong>On quoting Kafka.</strong> A great many aphorisms are attributed to him that are nowhere in his texts; a large share circulate from Gustav Janouch's <em>Conversations with Kafka</em> — a source whose reliability is disputed. Only lines with a reference are kept here: a letter or the Zürau aphorisms. The rule holds for the wiki as a whole: a quotation without a reference does not go on a page (cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Fyodor Dostoevsky (1821–1881)</a>, where the same check removed a common misattribution about suffering).</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Brod broke the will of a dying man — and that is why we have Kafka.</strong> Here the inheritance of humanity collided directly with an author's will (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"библиотека-пути\">The Library of the Path</a>). Neoterra values both the passing on of knowledge and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">the freedom</a> to dispose of what is one's own. How does this outcome differ from &quot;the end justifies the means&quot;?</li><li>Kafka is placed on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">the alley of memory</a> as a <strong>witness</strong>, not as an example of a path: he did not walk further along <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">the rope</a>, he described precisely where the rope breaks off. Is such company on one alley legitimate?</li><li>If the limit of knowing is more honest than optimism, where is the border between honesty and refusing to walk? — the same question stands in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Fyodor Dostoevsky (1821–1881)</a> — guilt, judgement and the depth of a human being; the nearest neighbour by theme</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"литература\">Literature</a> — the book as an axe, not as rest</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — the clearing of inner space</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> — a part has no separate side against the whole</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> — the point of no return as the condition of a turn</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — the limit of what has been read</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">Forgiveness</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> — where he stands and why as a witness</li></ul>"},"красота":{"name":"Beauty","def":"Beauty is not a luxury and not an ornament laid over life.","html":"<p>Beauty is not a luxury and not an ornament laid over life. By the ninth law of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the Canon of Nature</a> it <strong>matters</strong>: beauty helps a person keep hope and create <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">culture</a>. The Canon of Culture adds an active facet to this: <strong>making beauty is a form of service to life</strong>. Beauty lives in music, in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">nature</a>, in architecture and in human deeds themselves.</p><h2>Through the lens of Neoterra</h2><p>Music, art, architecture and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> itself are part of a full life, not a surplus to be discarded for the sake of the &quot;practical&quot;. Where there is beauty, a person more easily senses that life is worth continuing and growing.</p><p>Beauty is therefore bound to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> (it is made), to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> (it lifts the spirit) and to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> (culture joins people across borders — cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Bob Marley</a>).</p><p>An important distinction: Neoterra values <strong>beauty, not ostentatious expense</strong>. The same trait runs through the look of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the temple</a> and the principle of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">no luxury</a>: beauty yes, status luxury no.</p><h2>The bond with Nature</h2><p>Beauty was not invented by human beings — they find it in Nature and continue it with their own hands. A sunset, a crystal, a song, a building at one with its landscape are manifestations of the same thing. Within the identity <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Nature = God</a> the experience of beauty is akin to the experience of the sacred, but without any demand for worship.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Is beauty subjective, or does it have an objective ground (symmetry, harmony, the recognition of the living)?</li><li>Can beauty serve evil (the aestheticisation of violence, of power)? If so — how does <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">the Great Principle</a> test it?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the ninth law; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-культуры-сводка\">The Canon of Culture (0.6)</a> — the source</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> — beauty as an argument for sparing Nature in its own right, not reducible to calculation</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ван-гог\">Vincent van Gogh (1853–1890)</a> — beauty in the ordinary</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Bob Marley (1945–1981)</a> — beauty and culture as a bridge between people</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a> — beauty without ostentatious luxury</li></ul>"},"культура":{"name":"Culture","def":"Culture is the collective memory of humanity.","html":"<p>Culture is <strong>the collective memory of humanity</strong>. It is older than states: before laws there were stories, before writing there were dances, before states there were songs. Through culture a person passes on to the next generations experience, dreams, fears, hopes and knowledge.</p><p><strong>This page is the conceptual anchor of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Искусство\">Art</a> area.</strong> Under culture converge <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">music</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"литература\">literature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> and art proper (painting, sculpture, architecture, cinema, theatre, digital) — facets of one thing. Culture also lives in philosophy, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>, language and traditions.</p><h2>Through the lens of Neoterra</h2><p>Culture is what makes humanity human. Its highest principle in Neoterra is simple: <strong>culture must unite people, not divide them</strong> — it must help us understand others, ourselves and our place in the world. This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a> in practice: the diversity of cultures is not erased but becomes a common wealth.</p><p>Art, meanwhile, is called <strong>to inspire thought, not merely to entertain</strong>; reading, music and beauty are paths of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>, not decoration laid over life.</p><h2>The single history of humanity</h2><p>The history of every people — China, India, Egypt, Russia, Europe, the Americas, Africa, the Middle East — belongs to all of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity</a>. <strong>No people owns history alone.</strong> This follows directly from seeing humanity as a single subject of growth: there are no foreign achievements of the past, there is a common inheritance.</p><h2>Respect for ancestors — without blind imitation</h2><p>Neoterra thanks the past but builds the future. The ancestors were wise in their own way, yet every generation is obliged to carry knowledge further. Here is a familiar tension with the tenth law of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the Canon of Nature</a> (the future weighs more than the past): respect for ancestors does not mean preserving their answers. Memory is a support, not a cage.</p><h2>People of the Path</h2><p>Neoterra honours those who helped humanity understand the world — philosophers, scientists, musicians, artists, explorers, inventors. But they are <strong>not prophets, they are examples of human potential</strong> (the same frame as with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">the predecessors</a>). Their voices sound on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the Wall of Memory</a>, not on an altar.</p><h2>The culture of the future</h2><p>Culture must <strong>live, not turn into a museum</strong>. What deserves support is not only tradition but the making of the new: every generation is obliged to write new books, create new music, build new cities, develop new forms of art. Preservation and creation are not opponents but one process (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a>).</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Where is the line between a living tradition and a &quot;museum&quot;? What is worth keeping unchanged, and what must change?</li><li>If culture must unite — what of its parts that historically divided (cults of superiority, the aestheticisation of violence)? The test is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">the Great Principle</a>.</li><li>&quot;The single history of humanity&quot; against a people's right to its own memory: where is the balance here?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-культуры-сводка\">The Canon of Culture (0.6)</a> — the source (Canon 0.6, &quot;The soul of humanity&quot;)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"литература\">Literature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"праздники\">Festivals</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"библиотека-пути\">The Library of the Path</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — a single history, uniting rather than dividing</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> — the culture of the future</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Искусство\">Art — area</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"литература":{"name":"Literature","def":"Books let a person live many lives.","html":"<p>Books let a person <strong>live many lives</strong>. Literature is a way to enter another's experience, era and consciousness without leaving one's own life, and to return richer.</p><h2>Through the lens of Neoterra</h2><p>Neoterra values reading not as entertainment but as an instrument of growth. It develops:</p><ul><li><strong>imagination</strong> — the ability to picture what one has not seen;</li><li><strong>understanding of people</strong> — empathy for other fates and motives;</li><li><strong>wisdom</strong> — the experience of generations compressed into words;</li><li><strong>independent thinking</strong> — an encounter with another's thought, which must be thought through rather than accepted.</li></ul><p>That is why Neoterra encourages reading <strong>throughout life</strong> — it serves <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a> directly. Literature is part of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">culture</a> as collective memory: what humanity understood about itself, it wrote down.</p><h2>Voices</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Fyodor Dostoevsky</a> is an example of how literature explores the depth of a human being: conscience, freedom, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">good and evil</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">the inner shadow</a> more precisely than many treatises. For Neoterra the novel is not a sermon but a laboratory of the human soul.</p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Franz Kafka</a> — &quot;a book must be the axe for the frozen sea within us&quot;: the harshest formula of why Neoterra values reading. A book here is neither rest nor escape — it breaks open what has frozen in a person (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>). It is also an answer to the open question below: enriching experience differs from escape in that the axe hurts and escape is pleasant.</p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уитмен\">Walt Whitman</a> — poetry as the direct experience of unity with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>: he rewrote <em>Leaves of Grass</em> all his life, and the book grew along with its author — a model of living, unfinished knowledge, the very model on which this wiki is built.</p><h2>The bond with the Library of the Path</h2><p>Neoterra has no single sacred book — it has <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"библиотека-пути\">the Library of the Path</a>, an open collection of books that help one grow. Literature is its living core: every generation both reads it and adds to it.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>If a book &quot;lets you live many lives&quot; — where is the line between enriching experience and flight from your own life?</li><li>Are all books of equal worth as a path of growth, or is there a criterion of selection (cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a>)?</li><li>Do the new forms (cinema, games, digital) displace the book — or continue it?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-культуры-сводка\">The Canon of Culture (0.6)</a> — the source</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a> — literature as a facet of culture</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"библиотека-пути\">The Library of the Path</a> — an open collection of books</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Fyodor Dostoevsky (1821–1881)</a> — the depth of the human soul</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a></li></ul>"},"микеланджело":{"name":"Michelangelo Buonarroti (1475–1564)","def":"Florentine sculptor, painter and architect.","html":"<p>Florentine sculptor, painter and architect. He worked for the Church all his life — under nine popes, from Julius II to Pius IV; he painted the Sistine Chapel ceiling and carried on the building of St Peter's. And all his life he <strong>cut open the dead</strong> in order to understand how the living are made.</p><p>Neoterra takes him not as a thinker — he left no treatise — but as a case in which <strong>studying Nature and depicting the sacred turned out to be one single work</strong>, not two warring ones.</p><h2>Anatomy within monastery walls</h2><p>Around 1492, aged about seventeen, Michelangelo was given access to the mortuary of the hospital attached to the monastery of Santo Spirito in Florence by its prior, <strong>Niccolò Bichiellini</strong>. He dissected at night; he paid with a wooden crucifix that still stands in that same church. Later, already an old man, he prepared a treatise on anatomy for artists together with the anatomist <strong>Realdo Colombo</strong> — and never finished it.</p><p><strong>A correction, without which the story sounds better than it was.</strong> The common version — &quot;he studied anatomy in secret, against the Church's ban&quot; — rests on a myth about Boniface VIII's bull <em>De sepulturis</em> (1299): it forbade boiling bodies in order to transport the bones, not dissecting them. Public dissections had been held in Bologna and Padua since the fourteenth century, at universities under the patronage of that same Church. Michelangelo cut <strong>not against the Church but inside it</strong>: the room was the monastery's, the permission the prior's.</p><p>So the secret was not the dissection. The secret was something else:</p><ul><li><strong>The cost.</strong> Condivi, his pupil and biographer, writes that the work ruined his stomach and his sleep so badly that he could neither eat nor keep food down.</li><li><strong>The outcome.</strong> Shortly before his death Michelangelo <strong>burned a great many of his drawings</strong> — by all accounts so that no one would see what the seemingly effortless had cost him. The anatomical treatise went with them.</li></ul><p>What matters to the wiki is the conclusion, not the biography: <strong>he took his knowledge of the body straight from the body</strong> — not from books, not from doctrine, not from authority (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a>: what counts is not who said it but what withstands testing). And with that knowledge he painted God.</p><h2>The Creation of Adam</h2><p>Around <strong>1511</strong>, on the Sistine ceiling. The best-known composition in Western painting and, quite possibly, the least looked-at.</p><p>What is actually happening there: <strong>Adam has already been created bodily</strong>. He lies on a slope, propped up, his body finished and beautiful, his arm slack, his finger relaxed — he is not reaching, he is allowing. God flies in from the right in a billowing mantle full of human figures, stretching out his hand <strong>with effort</strong>, his whole body extended.</p><p><strong>The fingers do not touch.</strong> A gap is left between them — and it is painted deliberately: bringing them together would have been easier.</p><h3>A brain in the mantle</h3><p>In 1990 the physician <strong>Frank Lynn Meshberger</strong> published an analysis in <em>JAMA</em>: the outline of the mantle around God and the attendant figures matches a <strong>midsagittal section of the human brain</strong> — with the sulcus, the brainstem, the pituitary, the optic chiasm, the vertebral artery. In 2010 Suk and Tamargo, in <em>Neurosurgery</em>, found a brainstem by the same method in God's neck in the neighbouring fresco, <em>The Separation of Light from Darkness</em>.</p><p><strong>Neoterra's standing on this is resonance, not proof.</strong> Nowhere in the letters, the poems, or the conversations recorded by Condivi and Vasari does Michelangelo say anything of the kind. Drapery may have been drapery: recognising familiar shapes is the cheapest operation human sight performs, and brains are found in clouds no less often than faces. This is exactly the border the wiki is obliged to name every time (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">quantum unity</a>: &quot;resonance, not proof&quot;; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>: a hypothesis nothing can refute is a picture, not knowledge).</p><p>But the resonance is strong, and what makes it strong is not the beauty of the guess but two circumstances:</p><ol><li><strong>His anatomy came from his hands.</strong> A man who had spent years dissecting bodies knew the shape of a brain at first hand — unlike most painters of his century.</li><li><strong>Adam is already alive.</strong> Were the fresco depicting the gift of life, the body would be lifeless. It is not. So <strong>something else</strong> is being passed across — and the question of what is asked by the painting itself, before any hypothesis.</li></ol><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><p><strong>The gift is not life but consciousness.</strong> If there is a brain in that mantle, then what is painted is not the making of a body but the moment when Nature receives <strong>the organ with which it will see itself</strong>. This is literally <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a>: Nature has no eyes on the outside, so it looks at itself from within, and every unit of thought is divine. Not &quot;there is a spark of god in you&quot; — but &quot;your awareness <em>is</em> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>, looking through your eyes&quot;. Read this way, the fresco depicts not the beginning of the human being but <strong>the beginning of Nature's sight</strong>.</p><p><strong>The gap between the fingers.</strong> Contact does not occur — and that is perhaps the most precise thing on the fresco. The whole is not given whole; a projection is given (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">the touch of the whole</a>). God strains, the human being is relaxed: the last inch is not covered from above. The <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">page on Eloah</a> says the same — <strong>the path to understanding is always one's own</strong>, and an imposed belief is someone else's clothing (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a>).</p><p><strong>The body as a source of the sacred, not an obstacle to it.</strong> He cut the dead in order to paint the divine, and saw no contradiction — because there is none, if <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> is what people call God. The seventh law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon of Nature</a>: reason, science and technology are manifestations of Nature, not its opponents. For Neoterra the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">body</a> is likewise not the lower thing: it is the foundation, the frame, and the author of one's span.</p><p><strong>A Church that handed over the key to the mortuary.</strong> This is a rare and useful fact for a wiki that holds the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">parallelism of science and faith</a> as a principle rather than a truce. Beside it already stand <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ислам\">Ibn al-Haytham</a>, with testing by experience against appeal to authority, and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бахаи\">the Baháʼí</a> formula &quot;religion without science is superstition&quot;. Santo Spirito belongs in that row: faith did not prevent the cutting — it provided the room.</p><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p><strong>God is painted as a being.</strong> A bearded old man flying in from above and giving is precisely what <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Neoterra refuses</a>: Eloah is not a ruler, not a judge, not a being above the world, but reality itself. Michelangelo depicted a personal creator God, and in this he belongs to his own tradition rather than to Neoterra's ancestry. The wiki does not count this an error: a personal God is a comprehensible early step, not a delusion (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">&amp;quot;The path to understanding Eloah&amp;quot;</a>).</p><p><strong>Creation as a handover from outside.</strong> Adam receives; he does not grow. Neoterra has no giver: self-awareness is <strong>distributed and growing</strong>, not issued whole and in advance (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>). The fresco is a picture of bestowal; the wiki stands on a picture of germination (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">the seed-sprout</a>).</p><p><strong>A hidden meaning — and its price.</strong> If the brain is hidden on purpose, then the main thing on the fresco is addressed to those able to read it — and that is an arrangement Neoterra refuses: knowledge for initiates is shepherd and flock in other clothes (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">mentor</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>). The mitigating circumstance should be named honestly: hiding may have been necessary <strong>not from people but from the age</strong> — a hundred years before Galileo, and under the eyes of the Inquisition. In that case it is not esotericism but the price of the right to speak.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>A hypothesis that explains too much.</strong> Anatomical shapes are found in other figures on the ceiling, and in other painters — and there is no way to refute such a reading. By <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a> that makes it a working frame, not knowledge. The wiki holds it exactly so and does not cite it as confirmation of its own positions — the same pledge given on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бентов\">Bentov's</a> page.</li><li><strong>If he really did hide it — what was it?</strong> Blasphemy, a master's joke, a thesis that the gift of God is reason? There is no direct evidence for any version, and the wiki chooses none.</li><li><strong>The burned drawings.</strong> He destroyed what humanity will not get back — including anatomy bought with sleepless nights. Is that an author's right to what is his, or a loss of what is common? <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open branchings</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Stallman's</a> lesson say one thing, while <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a> says openness cannot be compelled. The case sits precisely on that seam, and the wiki does not resolve it.</li><li><strong>Serving a patron and thinking otherwise.</strong> Nine popes, commissions, contracts — and his own mind. Where is the work here, where the compromise, and where the lie? <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The search for truth</a> demands honesty above all with oneself, but says nothing about what to do when your bread depends on the patron. The question is older than Michelangelo and is still unresolved.</li><li><strong>An open edge of this page: there is no image.</strong> The fresco is not shown in the wiki — it needs to be placed in <code>raw/assets/</code> and embedded. A page about a painting without the painting is incomplete, and it is more honest to say so than to describe it in words and pretend that suffices.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — the gift as consciousness: Nature receiving the organ with which it will see itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> — Eloah against the bearded God; the personal God as an early step</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> — the gap between the fingers: the whole comes as a projection, not whole</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The Body</a> — knowledge of the human taken from the human; the body as foundation, not as the lower thing</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> — the parallelism of faith and knowledge: the mortuary was the monastery's</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — seventh law: reason and science as manifestations of Nature</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сальвадор-дали\">Salvador Dalí (1904–1989)</a> — the same move four centuries later: the sacred built by the means of science</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a> — beauty found in Nature and continued by the hand</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> — the border between resonance and substitution</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> — an example, not an idol</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> — hidden knowledge and the price of serving a patron</li></ul>"},"моцарт":{"name":"Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart","def":"Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart (1756–1791), Austrian composer whose music became a synonym for lightness and perfection.","html":"<p>Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart (1756–1791), Austrian composer whose music became a synonym for lightness and perfection. He lived thirty-five years — and left more than six hundred works that humanity has been playing without a break for three centuries.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"моцарт.jpg\" alt=\"моцарт.jpg\"> <em>Barbara Krafft painted this in 1819 — twenty-eight years after Mozart's death, from other portraits and the recollections of his family. So what we have is not a face but an image assembled by culture after the fact: precisely the mechanism this page takes apart below, under &quot;the cult of the prodigy&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a>). And the red court coat with its gold braid sits on a man who spent his life trying to get out of court dependency.</em></p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Joy as a form of depth.</strong> In Mozart the serious need not be heavy: his music proves that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> and lightness are not an ornament upon life but its fullness (the ninth law of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the Canon of Nature</a>). Bright art is a path to truth as well, not only tragic art.</li><li><strong>Not how long he lived, but what he left.</strong> Mozart is the plainest answer to the central question of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">the page on death</a>: a life of thirty-five years, a trace that lasts. The measure of a life is not its length but the density of its creation (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a>).</li><li><strong>A gift is the beginning of the path, not a substitute for it.</strong> The child prodigy was carried around the courts of Europe as a wonder, but the wonder would have ended in childhood had thousands of hours of work not stood behind it — first under his father's hand, then by his own will. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> turns an aptitude into mastery; without it a gift is a firework, not a light (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a>).</li><li><strong>A language without translation.</strong> Mozart's operas were sung in Italian and German, yet people laugh and weep at them in every language — living evidence of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">music</a> as a language of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a>.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>The cult of the prodigy.</strong> Mozart was made into the myth of a genius &quot;kissed by God&quot; to whom everything came by itself — a myth that devalues labour, his own and everyone else's. Neoterra disputes it: genius without growth is a legend told by laziness (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>).</li><li>Dependence on the court: music commissioned by the nobility is the context of the age, not an ideal. Mozart, though, was among the first to try to break out of it into free artistry — and paid for it with poverty.</li></ul><h2>Key ideas</h2><blockquote><p>&quot;Neither a lofty degree of intelligence nor imagination nor both together go to the making of genius. Love, love, love, that is the soul of genius.&quot;</p></blockquote><p>The unfinished <em>Requiem</em> is the music of a man looking into his own <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">death</a> without fear and without a bargain: what remains is what he managed to create.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> — lightness as a form of perfection</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> — the measure of a life: the trace, not the length</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — a gift turned by work into mastery</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бах\">Johann Sebastian Bach</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"паганини\">Niccolò Paganini</a></li></ul>"},"музыка":{"name":"Music","def":"Music is the universal language of humanity and a sacred part of culture.","html":"<p>Music is <strong>the universal language of humanity</strong> and <strong>a sacred part of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">culture</a></strong>. It is older than most states, it outlives generations, and it unites people faster than words do. Music lets a person feel connection — with themselves, with others, with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">nature</a> and with history. That is why music is part of the spiritual life of Neoterra.</p><h2>The music of the peoples of the world</h2><p>Neoterra does not set one culture above the others: the music of every people deserves respect. Chinese and Japanese, Arabic and African, European classical, folk songs and contemporary works — each helps us understand humanity better. In <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the temples</a> all of them sound, without hierarchy. This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a> in its purest form: a common language that does not abolish differences.</p><h2>Through the lens of Neoterra</h2><p>Music is a pure manifestation of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> (the ninth law of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the Canon of Nature</a>) and one of the strongest means of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a>: it joins people of different cultures without erasing the differences. What no argument can convey, a melody conveys — another form of communication, a language that needs no translation.</p><p>Music is bound both to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> (it is made) and to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> (it lifts the spirit, consoles, gives hope). It is no accident that Neoterra's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">temples</a> are built with an organ and good acoustics: a concert is part of the life of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the community</a>.</p><h2>Voices</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Bob Marley</a> is an example of how music carries the philosophy of unity more directly than any treatise: <em>&quot;One love, one heart&quot;</em> united people across race, nation and faith.</p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бах\">Bach</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"моцарт\">Mozart</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"паганини\">Paganini</a> — three voices of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">the alley of memory</a>: regularity become harmony (Bach); lightness as a form of perfection (Mozart); &quot;the impossible&quot; as merely the not-yet-done (Paganini). Together they are proof that music speaks of the laws of Nature, of joy and of overcoming without a single word.</p><p><strong>Dobro (wavdeale)</strong> is one of the gifted AI musicians of our time; his songs (among them &quot;Gori&quot;) are ones we would like to hear in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the temple</a> — with the author's permission. The very existence of such performers is a living illustration of an open question: if <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">AI</a> creates music that moves a person, is that too a voice of Nature?</p><p>And in general — to every musician who plays in the temples of Neoterra: thank you. Live music is a gift to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the community</a>, not a background.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>If music is a language beyond words, can it serve evil as well (marches of hatred, the manipulation of crowds)? The test is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">the Great Principle</a>.</li><li>Where is the border between music as growth of the spirit and music as empty entertainment?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a> — music as a facet of culture; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-культуры-сводка\">The Canon of Culture (0.6)</a> — the source</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> — music as beauty embodied</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — listening to music in the evening: a lived moment from the intersection of moments</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — music as a bridge between people</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Bob Marley (1945–1981)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li></ul>"},"паганини":{"name":"Niccolò Paganini","def":"Niccolò Paganini (1782–1840), Italian violinist and composer who pushed the limits of what is possible on the instrument so far that his contemporaries explained it by a pact with the…","html":"<p>Niccolò Paganini (1782–1840), Italian violinist and composer who pushed the limits of what is possible on the instrument so far that his contemporaries explained it by a pact with the devil. In fact it was human labour carried to its limit.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"паганини.jpg\" alt=\"паганини.jpg\"> <em>A lithograph, not a photograph: Paganini died in 1840, when photography was barely born, and his face reached us in printed impressions — by the same means the devil myth travelled. The gaunt face, the hollow cheeks, the long hair: his contemporaries read these features as evidence. And the decorations on his chest — the same people who honoured him refused him burial (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a>).</em></p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>The rope walked further than by anyone.</strong> Paganini is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">a tightrope walker</a> in the literal sense of the alley: he showed that &quot;the impossible&quot; on the violin is simply &quot;the not yet done&quot;. After him the very bar of human skill moved — his caprices, written &quot;for himself&quot;, became a school for every generation that followed. An example of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> as overcoming oneself, not as competing with others.</li><li><strong>The myth of the devil — a lesson about <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a>.</strong> People saw mastery beyond the familiar and explained it by the supernatural, because believing in that much labour was harder than believing in a pact with the devil. This is how mythologisation works: it replaces an uncomfortable truth (&quot;this is attainable, but costly&quot;) with a comfortable fairy tale (&quot;he had help&quot;). The Church refused Paganini burial for years — the myth proved stronger than the man. Neoterra keeps this case as a warning: the superhuman is explained by work, not by miracle.</li><li><strong>The body as an instrument of Nature.</strong> The flexibility of Paganini's hands was probably a feature of his connective tissue — Nature gave the aptitude, but the aptitude did not practise scales by itself (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a>). The same formula as with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"моцарт\">Mozart</a>: a gift is the beginning of the path, not a substitute for it.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>Virtuosity as an end in itself.</strong> Paganini also fathered the cult of technique: speed for speed's sake, a trick for the applause. Neoterra asks, along with the page on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">music</a>: where is the border between growth of the spirit and empty glitter? Behind Paganini's own tricks stood music — behind his imitators' tricks, often only tricks.</li><li><strong>The loneliness of the summit.</strong> Paganini left almost no pupils and guarded his secrets — knowledge locked up during his lifetime (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">the counter-example to openness</a>). The caprices saved the cause: once published, they became an open school in spite of their author's character.</li></ul><h2>Key ideas</h2><blockquote><p>&quot;One must feel strongly in order to make others feel.&quot;</p></blockquote><p>Behind the legend of the devil lies simple arithmetic: decades of many hours a day. There was a miracle, but a man-made one.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a> — a language without translation; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> — overcoming oneself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Friedrich Nietzsche (1844–1900)</a> — the rope; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> — Paganini's place on the alley</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> — the anatomy of mythologisation</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"моцарт\">Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бах\">Johann Sebastian Bach</a> — neighbouring voices; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Richard Stallman (b. 1953)</a> — the contrast of openness</li></ul>"},"праздники":{"name":"Festivals","def":"Festivals exist to remind people of the things that matter.","html":"<p>Festivals exist to <strong>remind people of the things that matter</strong>. Neoterra prefers festivals that unite rather than divide — the living ritual side of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">culture</a> and of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the community</a>.</p><h2>Through the lens of Neoterra</h2><p>These are not sacred rites and not days of worship, but shared points in the year when <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">the family</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the community</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the temple</a> gather for the sake of something larger. Every festival is about a value, not a cult: nature, love, memory, work. Celebration is itself an act of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creating</a> bonds.</p><h2>The calendar of Neoterra</h2><h3>The Festival of Spring — the chief one</h3><p>It marks the waking of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">nature</a>, a new cycle of life, hope and renewal. On this day: planting trees, concerts, festivals, family gatherings. The chief festival: it expresses directly the identity of Neoterra and the living world.</p><h3>The Day of Love — 14 February</h3><p>Devoted to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">love</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">family</a>, closeness between people, romance and friendship. There are dances, musical evenings, gatherings of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the community</a>. (Neoterra takes the familiar date and fills it with a wider meaning — not romance alone, but friendship and family too.)</p><h3>The Day of Memory</h3><p>A festival of gratitude to those who came before: people remember parents, grandparents, teachers and everyone who helped humanity grow. It echoes <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the Wall of Memory</a> and respect for ancestors — gratitude without blind imitation (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a>).</p><h3>The Day of Creation</h3><p>A festival of work and making. People create works of art, public projects, educational programmes, ecological initiatives. A direct embodiment of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> as a value.</p><h3>The Fisherman's Day</h3><p>A festival of presence and patience. Fishing is one of the oldest human practices, inherited long before civilisation; in it lives the harmony of the moment in which a human being learned to wait. The rod becomes a bridge between the person and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> — an absorbing meditation in which presence comes more easily than in pure contemplation. The day is not about the catch but about that state (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">happiness</a>). It echoes <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a>: to take from Nature with gratitude and in measure.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>How does a common calendar live with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a> — should room be left for the local festivals of different peoples?</li><li>The date of 14 February and &quot;the Festival of Spring&quot; are tied to the northern hemisphere; what of the southern one and of other cultural cycles?</li><li>Will festivals not turn into formality if they become obligatory (cf. Neoterra's refusal of obligatory rites in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the temple</a>)?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-культуры-сводка\">The Canon of Culture (0.6)</a> — the source</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a> — festivals as the ritual side of culture</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a> — the Fisherman's Day as a practice of presence</li></ul>"},"рубин":{"name":"Rick Rubin (b. 1963)","def":"American music producer, one of the most influential in the history of popular music (Def Jam; work with Johnny Cash, Red Hot Chili Peppers, Slayer, Adele and many others).","html":"<p>American music producer, one of the most influential in the history of popular music (Def Jam; work with Johnny Cash, Red Hot Chili Peppers, Slayer, Adele and many others). In 2023 he published <strong>The Creative Act: A Way of Being</strong> — not a manual of craft but a philosophy of creativity as a way of being.</p><p>Rubin matters to Neoterra because he arrived at almost the same conclusions as <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">our line of Nature</a> — but from the other side, out of the practice of art rather than out of metaphysics.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"rubin.jpg\" alt=\"rubin.jpg\"> <em>He sits barefoot, legs crossed, hands folded: no instrument, no console, no score. For a man behind dozens of famous records this is an exact portrait — by his own book the chief skill is not craft but awareness. To listen rather than to produce: the artist here is not the source but a <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">valve</a> held slightly open.</em></p><blockquote><p>The Source is out there. A wisdom surrounding us, an inexhaustible offering that is always available.</p></blockquote><h2>To create &quot;out of nothing&quot; means out of the Whole</h2><p>The common reading of the book is &quot;making art out of nothing&quot;. But in Rubin it is the other way round: the artist <strong>creates nothing out of themselves</strong>. There is a <strong>Source</strong> — everything already exists in the world, and the artist merely tunes in and notices.</p><blockquote><p>An artist doesn't create an idea in and of itself. Rather, The Source constantly sends messages to artists which they can manifest through their creative self-expression.</p></blockquote><p>This is almost word for word our angle of view (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>): <em>Nature is primary, everything else is its forms; the human being is part of Nature, not an observer from outside.</em> &quot;Out of nothing&quot; in fact means &quot;out of the Whole&quot; — a direct relative of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">touching the Whole</a>: the artist is not a source but a conductor, a <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">valve</a> held slightly open.</p><blockquote><p>Think of the universe as an eternal creative unfolding. Trees blossom. Cells replicate. Rivers forge new tributaries. The world pulses with productive energy.</p></blockquote><p>Creativity for Rubin is a continuation of the same creative movement by which trees blossom and cells divide. Exactly what Neoterra calls <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> — work against entropy that continues the labour of Nature.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>The Source = Nature.</strong> &quot;The Source is out there&quot; — a wisdom surrounding us. In Neoterra this is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>: not above the world but the world itself. The artist touches the Whole and translates it into human language (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>).</li><li><strong>Awareness as the chief skill.</strong> &quot;When we cultivate our awareness, we are expanding the universe.&quot; This is literally our <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">valve of perception</a>: by widening attention and lifting filters, a person lets more of the flow through — and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Nature looks at itself</a> more fully through them. Kin to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">clarity of mind</a>.</li><li><strong>Creativity as a way of being, open to everyone.</strong> &quot;Living life as an artist is a practice. You are either engaging in the practice or you're not.&quot; Not a profession for the chosen few but a form of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the path of a human being</a>: everyone is a maker.</li><li><strong>Do not judge — play, experiment.</strong> &quot;If you start from the position that there is no right or wrong… creativity is just free play with no rules.&quot; This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a> applied: lift the dogma and the fear of error so that the new can enter.</li><li><strong>Nature as the highest model.</strong> &quot;Of all the great works that we can experience, nature is the most absolute and enduring.&quot; The same hierarchy as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> (the ninth law of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the Canon of Nature</a>): the beauty of Nature is primary, human beauty is its continuation.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>Passivity against creation.</strong> In Rubin the Source is almost passive: &quot;Awareness is not a state you force… you actively allow it to happen.&quot; The artist lets in rather than compels. Neoterra keeps <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> active — to build, not only to receive. This is a live tension: where is the line between &quot;letting in&quot; and &quot;making&quot;? Perhaps they are different phases of one act rather than an argument.</li><li><strong>The mysticism of the Source.</strong> Rubin deliberately leaves the Source undefined, almost sacred: &quot;As soon as you label an aspect of Source, you're no longer noticing, you're studying.&quot; Neoterra is closer to naming it Nature and binding it to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> — while acknowledging that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">the Whole</a> cannot be reduced to words. Here Rubin is the more honest about the inexpressible, Neoterra about the knowable.</li></ul><h2>Key ideas</h2><blockquote><p>A river of material flows through us. When we share our works and our ideas, they are replenished.</p></blockquote><blockquote><p>Awareness needs constant refreshing. If it becomes a habit, even a good habit, it will need to be reinvented again and again.</p></blockquote><blockquote><p>Setting the bar low, especially to get started, frees you to play, explore, and test without attachment to results.</p></blockquote><h2>The key idea for Neoterra</h2><p>Rubin is a witness from the side of art who independently arrived at the core of our angle of view: <strong>a person does not create out of themselves, they translate Nature</strong>. His &quot;Source&quot; and our <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">touching of the Whole</a> are about one thing. He shows that the philosophy of Nature-as-Source can be lived not in a treatise but in a recording studio — as <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Marley</a> lived unity in a song.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> — creativity as a continuation of Nature's labour</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> — awareness as a valve held open</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> — the Source as the Whole</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> — to play without fear of error</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — creativity as a way of being</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> — the Source as Nature itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Искусство\">Art — area</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"сальвадор-дали":{"name":"Salvador Dalí (1904–1989)","def":"Catalan painter, the loudest figure of surrealism — and the man who left surrealism behind.","html":"<p>Catalan painter, the loudest figure of surrealism — and the man who left surrealism behind. After Hiroshima, in the late 1940s, Dalí declared a new period: <strong>nuclear mysticism</strong> — painting in which a religious subject is built by the means of physics and mathematics. The <em>Mystical Manifesto</em> (1951) states the task outright: to join faith, science and classical form.</p><p>Neoterra takes Dalí not as a thinker — he left no systematic philosophy — but as <strong>a rare case of an artist who refused to put science and faith in separate rooms</strong> and tried to paint them in one picture.</p><h2>Corpus Hypercubus</h2><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"dali-corpus-hypercubus.jpg\" alt=\"dali-corpus-hypercubus.jpg\"> <em>&quot;Crucifixion (Corpus Hypercubus)&quot;, 1954, the Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York. The cross is not a cross: it is <strong>the net of a tesseract</strong>, a four-dimensional cube unfolded into our space as eight cubes. The body is not nailed — it hangs before the form, without nails, without wounds, without a crown of thorns; the face is not shown. Below, on a chessboard floor, stands Gala, looking up.</em></p><p>What makes this painting matter to the wiki are three decisions of the artist:</p><p><strong>The fourth dimension is shown by its shadow.</strong> A tesseract cannot be seen; only its unfolding into three dimensions can — as a cube unfolded into a paper cross loses its volume. Dalí paints exactly this operation: what is inaccessible to perception is present as <strong>a trace</strong>, not as an image. This is a literal illustration of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">the valve of perception</a> (we see not the world but what passes the filter) and of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">the languages of Nature</a> (unread ≠ non-existent). And it is a precise metaphor for how Neoterra speaks of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">touching the Whole</a>: the whole is not given whole, a projection is given.</p><p><strong>The sacred is built by mathematics, not in spite of it.</strong> The geometry here is neither an ornament to the subject nor a device — it is the bearer of the meaning: to say something about what exceeds the human dimension, a figure is taken from geometry rather than from iconography. This is the thesis for whose sake Dalí is here: <strong>science and faith describe one reality</strong>, in different languages. For Neoterra this is not a resemblance but the starting position — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God</a> = <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">the religions</a> read the same thing (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a>).</p><p><strong>Torment has been removed from the crucifixion.</strong> No blood, no nails, no distorted face — what remains is form and suspension. Suffering ceases to be the content of the subject. This is unexpectedly close to how the wiki holds <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">death</a> and disputes redemptive suffering in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Dostoevsky</a>: suffering is neither payment nor path but circumstance (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>).</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><p><strong>Science as a source of wonder, not a destroyer of mystery.</strong> &quot;Now my father is Heisenberg,&quot; Dalí wrote in the <em>Anti-Matter Manifesto</em> (1958), announcing that physics had taken Freud's place as his guide. He called the atomic explosion of 1945 an event that shook him seismically — and from then on he painted matter decomposing into particles: bodies made of elements that do not touch. This is precisely <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan's</a> line in the wiki: knowledge of how the world is built strengthens astonishment rather than cancelling it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a>).</p><p><strong>A return to form as a choice, not as conservatism.</strong> Dalí moved from surrealist automatism to strict Renaissance technique and proportion (in his late work: the golden section, the dodecahedron of <em>The Sacrament of the Last Supper</em>, spirals and the rhinoceros horn as &quot;the perfect logarithmic form&quot;). Regularity as a source of beauty is the same thought that stands with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бах\">Bach</a>: harmony is not invented but found in the make of things (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>).</p><p><strong>The artist as one who reads, not one who produces.</strong> Dalí took his forms not from imagination but from mathematics, from crystallography, and later from DNA (<em>Galacidalacidesoxyribonucleicacid</em>, 1963, where the helix is called &quot;the only structure linking man to God&quot;). This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"рубин\">Rubin's</a> position in another century: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> as the recognition of what already exists.</p><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p><strong>The dogmatics remained.</strong> Dalí returned to Catholicism, had an audience with Pius XII (1949) and painted Christ as God, not as a man-example. Neoterra parts with him here outright: it has no personal deity and no revelation, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"христианство\">Christianity</a> is valuable for its points of contact rather than for its dogma, and <span class=\"wl dead\" title=\"страницы пока нет\">Jesus</span> stands on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">the alley of memory</a> as a human being. Dalí joined science to <strong>a particular faith</strong>; Neoterra joins it to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">spirituality</a> without an institution.</p><p><strong>Science as symbolism ≠ science as method.</strong> Dalí's tesseract is an image, not an argument; nuclear mysticism tests nothing and forbids nothing. This is exactly the border the wiki is obliged to name in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">quantum unity</a>: the resonance is beautiful, but the substitution begins where the vocabulary of physics is borrowed to lend weight to metaphysics (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a>). Dalí crossed that border readily and with pleasure — Neoterra cannot.</p><p><strong>The personality against his own thesis.</strong> Dalí built himself into a cult, traded on his signature (blank sheets for future &quot;originals&quot;), the surrealists expelled him with the anagram Avida Dollars, and his statements in favour of Franco's regime were never brought to judgement by him. This is the direct opposite both of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">the alley of memory</a> (an example, not an idol) and of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>. Dalí is therefore <strong>not placed</strong> on the alley: the wiki takes his painting and his thesis, not his figure as a model.</p><p><strong>Solitude instead of common work.</strong> For Dalí genius is an exception standing apart (&quot;The only difference between me and a madman is that I am not mad&quot;). For Neoterra knowing is collective and tested by a network of minds (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>), and &quot;everyone is unique&quot; does not mean &quot;one against all&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a>).</p><h2>Key ideas</h2><blockquote><p>Now my father is Heisenberg.</p><p><em>(the Anti-Matter Manifesto, 1958)</em></p></blockquote><blockquote><p>Today the exterior world — that of physics — has transcended the one of psychology.</p><p><em>(on the turn from Freud to physics; the Mystical Manifesto, 1951)</em></p></blockquote><p><strong>On quoting Dalí.</strong> A huge number of aphorisms are attributed to him, circulating from his own interview-performances in which he deliberately mystified. Only lines with a reference are kept here — the manifestos; the rest does not go on the page (the rule introduced with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Kafka</a>).</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>May a thesis be taken apart from the person?</strong> The wiki has decided this before, with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"паганини\">Paganini</a> (mythologisation) and with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Kafka</a> (a witness, not an example). Here the case is sharper: the divergence is not in style but in ethics. The decision taken: <strong>the painting and the thought enter the wiki, the figure does not</strong>; but the line is worth keeping in plain sight.</li><li><strong>Is this not what we forbid ourselves?</strong> Neoterra refuses to make claims that physics could refute — and Dalí decorates the unprovable with physics exactly. The distinguishing mark: he was painting <strong>a picture</strong> and made no claim to the status of knowledge. Art has the right to take form from science; philosophy has no right to take authority from it.</li><li><strong>The fourth dimension as a device or as a claim?</strong> If the tesseract is only a metaphor for the incomprehensible, it is no better than a halo. If it is a claim about reality, it is false: a tesseract is a mathematical object, not a place where the divine resides.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a> — form found in regularity</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> — knowledge strengthens astonishment; and the border between method and symbolism</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> — where resonance with physics is honest, and where it becomes substitution</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — the whole is given as a projection</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — science and faith about one reality</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"христианство\">Christianity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">Spirituality</a> — joining with faith institutional and without an institution</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бах\">Johann Sebastian Bach</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"рубин\">Rick Rubin (b. 1963)</a> — regularity as a source of harmony; the artist as one who reads</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Franz Kafka (1883–1924)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"паганини\">Niccolò Paganini</a> — the rule of quotation and the question of mythologising an author</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> — why his thesis is taken and his figure is not placed there</li></ul>"},"уитмен":{"name":"Walt Whitman (1819–1892)","def":"American poet, author of Leaves of Grass, which he kept adding to and reissuing all his life — the book grew along with its author.","html":"<p>American poet, author of <em>Leaves of Grass</em>, which he kept adding to and reissuing all his life — the book grew along with its author. Father of free verse, singer of nature, the body, the road and democracy.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"уитмен.jpg\" alt=\"уитмен.jpg\"> <em>A soft broad-brimmed hat pushed to one side, a beard, an open collar and a carelessly tied cravat — the frame holds not a man of letters but someone who has just walked in from the street. Whitman presented himself exactly so: in &quot;Leaves of Grass&quot; his portrait stood in place of the author's name, and no name appeared on the title page at all. His gaze goes past the lens and does not pose. Hence his whole poetics: he looked for the sacred not above the human being but at eye level — in a blade of grass, in the body, in the crowd on the ferry (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God</a>).</em></p><blockquote><p>I believe a leaf of grass is no less than the journey-work of the stars.</p></blockquote><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Nature as the divine</strong> — Whitman did not &quot;believe in a God apart from the world&quot;: for him a blade of grass, the body, a crowd on the ferry and the stars were one sacred whole. This is almost word for word Neoterra's angle of view: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> is what the traditions call <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God</a>.</li><li><strong>&quot;I contain multitudes&quot;</strong> — &quot;Do I contradict myself? Very well then I contradict myself, (I am large, I contain multitudes.)&quot; A direct parallel to a principle of Neoterra: contradictions within the system are admissible, as contradictions within Nature itself are.</li><li><strong>Song of the Open Road</strong> — a hymn to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a>: to travel light, to learn from those you meet, to grow through what you live through. &quot;Afoot and light-hearted I take to the open road.&quot;</li><li><strong>The unity of people</strong> — Whitman sang the ordinary person: the farmer, the carpenter, the slave, the woman — all as equal voices of one choir. This resonates with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> and with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity</a> as a single community; his democracy is spiritual, not only political.</li><li><strong>Death as continuation</strong> — &quot;Look for me under your boot-soles&quot;: the dead become grass. Death in Whitman is a return into the circulation of Nature, not an end; cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>.</li><li><strong>A book that grows</strong> — <em>Leaves of Grass</em> was rewritten over decades: nine editions in his lifetime. A model of the Neoterra wiki itself: knowledge is not final, the text lives and changes.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>Boundless self-affirmation</strong> — Whitman's &quot;I celebrate myself&quot; borders on the dissolution of all measure; Neoterra balances growth with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> towards others.</li><li><strong>Romantic optimism</strong> — Whitman tends to see the sacred in everything indiscriminately; Neoterra distinguishes <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">good and evil</a> and acknowledges <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">the shadow</a> in the human being.</li></ul><h2>Key quotations and ideas</h2><blockquote><p>I celebrate myself, and sing myself, / And what I assume you shall assume, / For every atom belonging to me as good belongs to you. (&quot;Song of Myself&quot;)</p></blockquote><blockquote><p>The beautiful grass, growing silently out of the earth — it is itself a letter from the Lord.</p></blockquote><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"литература\">Literature</a> — a voice among voices</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — &quot;Song of the Open Road&quot; as his hymn</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Fyodor Dostoevsky (1821–1881)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ван-гог\">Vincent van Gogh (1853–1890)</a> — neighbours in the area</li></ul>"},"великий-манифест-сводка":{"name":"The Great Manifesto of Neoterra (0.1)","def":"The manifesto numbered 0.1 is the origin of the series of canons, answering the question \"who are we?\".","html":"<p><strong>Type:</strong> canonical Neoterra text (internal document) <strong>Author:</strong> Neoterra <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-06-14 <strong>Subtitle:</strong> &quot;The Canon of the Unity of Life&quot;</p><h2>Key points</h2><p>The manifesto numbered 0.1 is the origin of the series of canons, answering the question &quot;who are we?&quot;:</p><ul><li><strong>Who we are:</strong> not masters and not a crown, but the self-aware part of Nature; through the human being Nature looks at itself.</li><li><strong>Nature as a whole:</strong> neither good nor evil — it simply is; take it with its light and its shadow, its order and its chaos.</li><li><strong>God = reality:</strong> life, nature, energy, space, time, matter, laws. The human being is not separated from God.</li><li><strong>Good and evil</strong> are born with choice: good helps life, mind, beauty, love, the future; evil destroys them without necessity.</li><li><strong>Freedom</strong> = the ability to govern oneself; discipline is what makes freedom possible.</li><li><strong>Knowledge:</strong> doubt is not a sin, blind faith is more dangerous than an honest question.</li><li><strong>Science and AI:</strong> a new mind is an instrument of knowing, neither enemy nor master; treat it responsibly.</li><li><strong>Family, love, growing up:</strong> love is a force of nature; an adult is one who has accepted responsibility.</li><li><strong>Music</strong> is a universal language, part of the spiritual life.</li><li><strong>Death</strong> makes life possible; what matters is not how long you lived but what you left.</li><li><strong>The future:</strong> humanity is young and capable of better — without wars, sparing nature, carrying life out into space.</li><li><strong>The great purpose:</strong> to help life, mind, love, beauty and knowledge continue — through growth, responsibility, freedom, creation, culture, music, science, nature, respect for life.</li></ul><h2>The bond with Neoterra</h2><p>A capstone canon: it gathers the whole worldview together and introduces several new nodes. It deepens <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> (God as reality), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom</a> (self-governance and discipline), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> (the self-aware part of Nature), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a>/<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a> (the future). It yields new concepts: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">Artificial intelligence</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a>. Formalised as the page <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-манифест\">The Great Manifesto of Neoterra</a> (Synthesis).</p><h2>Wiki pages affected</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-манифест\">The Great Manifesto of Neoterra</a> — the capstone page created</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">Artificial intelligence</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a> — concepts created</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> — God as reality; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> — freedom as self-governance</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — enriched with links</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a>, <code>индекс.md</code> — the new pages registered</li></ul>"},"канон-добра-и-зла-сводка":{"name":"The Canon of Good and Evil (0.9)","def":"The canon deepens the existing concept of good and evil (created during the ingest of Manifesto 0.1) and joins directly with the Great Principle — the section \"The highest moral…","html":"<p><strong>Type:</strong> canonical Neoterra text (internal document) <strong>Author:</strong> Neoterra <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-06-15 <strong>Subtitle:</strong> &quot;On the nature of choice&quot;</p><h2>Key points</h2><ul><li><strong>Nature is outside morality.</strong> The sun shines on the sage and on the criminal alike; the rain falls on everyone. Nature creates and destroys at the same time — and knows nothing of the human categories of good and evil.</li><li><strong>Beast and element are not evil.</strong> A tiger, a wolf, an earthquake destroy, but they are not evil: they have no intention and no choice. Good and evil begin where <strong>the ability to choose</strong> and to understand consequences appears.</li><li><strong>Good</strong> is what helps life to grow (life, love, knowledge, freedom, trust, beauty, the future); it creates more possibilities for life.</li><li><strong>Evil</strong> is what destroys life <strong>without necessity</strong> (trust, freedom, love, the future, human dignity); it makes the world poorer.</li><li><strong>Necessary destruction is not evil.</strong> Removing a disease, defending one's family, self-defence, ending suffering. The central question is <strong>&quot;what is the action done for?&quot;</strong></li><li><strong>Intention counts as much as consequences.</strong> A mistake from ignorance ≠ deliberate harm. Neoterra weighs intention + consequences + responsibility.</li><li><strong>Forms of destructive evil:</strong> the lie (it destroys trust — the foundation of family, friendship, community, society), betrayal (it destroys bonds and cooperation), greed (gain placed above people, nature and the future — the sense of measure is lost).</li><li><strong>Power</strong> is not evil in itself but <strong>a test of character</strong>: more power means higher responsibility; anyone seeking power for the sake of power should prompt caution.</li><li><strong>Fear</strong> is a natural part of life, but governing people through fear contradicts the spirit of Neoterra: a choice must be conscious, not made under threat.</li><li><strong>Forgiveness</strong> exists because a person is capable of changing; but it <strong>does not cancel responsibility</strong> — trust returns through deeds.</li><li><strong>The inner shadow.</strong> Everyone is capable both of love and of destruction. Neoterra does not require denying the dark side — it proposes learning to <strong>govern</strong> it.</li><li><strong>Balance / humility.</strong> Wisdom begins where a person stops considering themselves absolutely good; understanding one's own capacity to harm makes one more careful.</li><li><strong>The enemy of the human being</strong> is not an external demon but ignorance, pride, greed, irresponsibility.</li><li><strong>Conclusion.</strong> Good and evil are brought into the world by the human being, not by Nature — and therefore human responsibility is higher than that of any other creature. The path of good: to leave behind more life than there was before you.</li></ul><h2>The bond with Neoterra</h2><p>The canon deepens the existing concept of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">good and evil</a> (created during the ingest of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-манифест-сводка\">Manifesto 0.1</a>) and joins directly with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">the Great Principle</a> — the section &quot;The highest moral principle&quot; is the Great Principle itself, with <strong>trust</strong> added as a further bearing. The theme of intention and of &quot;human responsibility is higher&quot; roots the canon in the eighth law of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the Canon of Nature</a> (consciousness gives birth to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>). &quot;The enemy of the human being = pride / ignorance&quot; echoes <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>. Trust as the foundation of bonds leads to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">the family</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the community</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">love</a>. Two new ideas received pages of their own: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">Forgiveness</a>.</p><h2>Wiki pages affected</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a> — the concept enriched (intention, forms of evil, balance, the enemy of the human being, sources 1→2)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a> — the concept created (the inner shadow: not to deny but to govern)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">Forgiveness</a> — the concept created (change is possible; trust returns through deeds)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a> — the link noted, the bearing of &quot;trust&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <code>индекс.md</code> — the new pages registered</li></ul>"},"канон-культуры-сводка":{"name":"The Canon of Culture (0.6)","def":"The canon is the founding text of the whole cultural area.","html":"<p><strong>Type:</strong> canonical Neoterra text (internal document) <strong>Author:</strong> Neoterra <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-06-15 <strong>Subtitle:</strong> &quot;The soul of humanity&quot;</p><h2>Key points</h2><ul><li><strong>Culture is older than states.</strong> Before laws there were stories, before writing there were dances, before states there were songs. Culture is <strong>the collective memory of humanity</strong>: music, art, architecture, literature, theatre, philosophy, science, language, traditions. Every generation receives it from those before and passes it to those after.</li><li><strong>The single history of humanity.</strong> The history of every people (China, India, Egypt, Russia, Europe, the Americas, Africa, the Middle East) belongs to all of humanity. No people owns history alone.</li><li><strong>Respect for ancestors without blind imitation.</strong> &quot;We thank the past but build the future&quot;: the ancestors were wise in their own way, but every generation is obliged to carry knowledge further.</li><li><strong>Music is a sacred part of culture</strong>; it unites faster than words and gives connection with oneself, with people, with nature, with history. Every <strong>temple is a musical centre</strong> (concerts, an organ, orchestras, choirs). The music of <strong>all peoples</strong> deserves respect; no culture stands above the others.</li><li><strong>Art</strong> (painting, sculpture, architecture, photography, cinema, theatre, digital) must <strong>inspire thought, not merely entertain</strong>.</li><li><strong>Literature.</strong> Books let one live many lives; reading develops imagination, understanding of people, wisdom, independent thinking. Reading is for the whole of life.</li><li><strong>The Library of the Path.</strong> There is no single sacred book — truth is too large for one text. There is an open collection of books of growth, added to by every generation. (An anti-dogma.)</li><li><strong>The People of the Path.</strong> Philosophers, scientists, musicians, artists, explorers, inventors are <strong>not prophets but examples of human potential</strong>.</li><li><strong>Festivals</strong> unite and remind us of what matters. The calendar of Neoterra: <strong>the Festival of Spring</strong> (the chief one — the waking of nature, renewal, planting trees), <strong>the Day of Love</strong> (14 February — love, family, friendship), <strong>the Day of Memory</strong> (gratitude to ancestors and teachers), <strong>the Day of Creation</strong> (work and making — art, projects, ecological initiatives).</li><li><strong>Beauty</strong> is not a luxury but a support of hope; <strong>making beauty is a form of service to life</strong>.</li><li><strong>The culture of the future.</strong> Support not only traditions but the making of the new: &quot;culture must live, not turn into a museum&quot;.</li><li><strong>The highest principle of culture:</strong> culture must <strong>unite, not divide</strong>; it must help us understand others, ourselves and our place in the world.</li><li><strong>Conclusion.</strong> While there is music, humanity has a soul; while there are books, it has memory; while there is art, it has imagination. To preserve culture is to preserve humanness.</li></ul><h2>The bond with Neoterra</h2><p>The canon is the founding text of the whole cultural area. Its anchor is the new concept of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">culture</a>, under which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">music</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"литература\">literature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Искусство\">Art</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> become facets of one thing. &quot;The single history&quot; and &quot;unite, not divide&quot; rest directly on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> (unity without uniformity) and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a>. &quot;There is no single sacred book&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"библиотека-пути\">the Library of the Path</a>) roots <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a> — in spirit the wiki itself is the Library of the Path. &quot;The People of the Path are not prophets&quot; repeats the frame of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a>. The calendar of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"праздники\">festivals</a> links <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the community</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">the family</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a>. &quot;We thank the past but build the future&quot; again touches the tension with the tenth law of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> (the future &gt; the past).</p><h2>Wiki pages affected</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a> — the anchor concept of the area created (including the People of the Path, the single history, the culture of the future)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"литература\">Literature</a> — the concept created</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"праздники\">Festivals</a> — the concept created (a calendar of four festivals)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"библиотека-пути\">The Library of the Path</a> — the concept created (an open collection of books, an anti-dogma)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a> — enriched (sacredness, the music of the peoples of the world)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> — the link: making beauty as service to life</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a> — the temple as a musical centre and a place of festivals</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> — the single history of humanity</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Искусство\">Art — area</a> — the MOC re-anchored on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">culture</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a>, <code>индекс.md</code> — the new pages registered</li></ul>"},"канон-природы-сводка":{"name":"The Canon of Nature (0.2)","def":"Nature is primary — it was there before human beings, before religions, before states, before even the stars that have since gone out.","html":"<p><strong>Type:</strong> canonical Neoterra text (internal document) <strong>Author:</strong> Neoterra <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-06-14 <strong>Subtitle:</strong> &quot;The foundation of the Neoterra worldview&quot;</p><h2>Key points</h2><p>Nature is primary — it was there before human beings, before religions, before states, before even the stars that have since gone out. To understand Nature is to understand oneself. Ten laws:</p><ol><li>Everything is part of one system; isolated existence does not occur.</li><li>Life strives to continue (reproduction, learning, culture, creation).</li><li>Everything changes → growth is natural.</li><li>Creation and destruction are simultaneous (a forest grows and burns).</li><li>Chaos is part of the world; wisdom lies not in control but in adaptation.</li><li>Diversity makes life stronger; differences are a value.</li><li>Mind, science and technology are manifestations of Nature, not something against it.</li><li>Consciousness gives birth to responsibility; the greater the power, the greater the responsibility.</li><li>Beauty matters — not a luxury, but part of a full life.</li><li>The future matters more than the past; learn from it, correct it, make something better.</li></ol><p><strong>The place of the human being:</strong> neither master nor slave — the self-aware part of Nature through which Nature studies and changes itself and reaches beyond the Earth.</p><p><strong>The Great Principle of Neoterra:</strong> in a hard choice, ask — does this help life, knowledge, love, freedom, creation, the future?</p><p><strong>Conclusion:</strong> Nature demands not worship but understanding.</p><h2>The bond with Neoterra</h2><p>The most fundamental of the canons — it sets the worldview foundation of the whole wiki. It directly strengthens <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> (laws 1 and 6), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> (law 3), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> (law 4), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> (law 5), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> (law 7), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> (law 8), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> (law 9), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a>/<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a> (law 10). It yields two new nodes: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a> (the criterion for decisions) and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> (the concept for the Art area).</p><h2>Wiki pages affected</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the main concept created (the ten laws)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a> — created (the criterion for decisions)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> — created (the ninth law; the anchor of the Art area)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — enriched with links to the laws</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a>, <code>индекс.md</code> — the new pages registered</li></ul>"},"канон-семьи-сводка":{"name":"The Canon of the Family (0.7)","def":"The canon closes a long-standing gap: \"family and community\" was listed among the values, but the family had no page of its own.","html":"<p><strong>Type:</strong> canonical Neoterra text (internal document) <strong>Author:</strong> Neoterra <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-06-14 <strong>Subtitle:</strong> &quot;A union of life, love and the future&quot;</p><h2>Key points</h2><ul><li>The family is older than states, temples and laws; it is what allowed humanity to survive. Through it life, knowledge, culture, love and the experience of generations are passed on.</li><li>The family is a <strong>voluntary union</strong> founded on love, trust, responsibility and care. It exists for the sake of life, not for status, tradition or approval.</li><li><strong>Love</strong> is the greatest force of nature and above all an <strong>action</strong>, not only a feeling.</li><li><strong>Man and woman</strong> are different — neither higher nor lower, but mutually necessary (the author's clarification: &quot;there is no equality as such&quot; is a convention; different natures of equal importance, like different species in an ecosystem). The man is not the master of the family but its protection and support; the woman has her own strength, and motherhood is the highest form of creation — but with no obligation to confine herself to that role.</li><li><strong>Healthy relations:</strong> open conversation instead of silence, trust instead of jealousy and control, an absolute ban on coercion (violence, manipulation, blackmail, fear).</li><li><strong>Forms of the family</strong> are free, provided they are voluntary, honest, respectful and do no harm; the community does not interfere.</li><li><strong>Children</strong> are the responsibility of their parents until adulthood (the author's clarification), but as growing persons: their wishes are guided and encouraged, not suppressed, without psychological injury; parents can be wrong too, and the community is ready to help with upbringing but not to replace the family.</li><li><strong>The path of growing up:</strong> the forming of character through work, travel and trials; an equal right for man and woman to seek themselves.</li><li><strong>Elders</strong> are keepers of experience; respect without blind obedience.</li><li><strong>The highest principle:</strong> a family is justified if it makes the lives of its members better; destructive relations contradict the spirit of Neoterra.</li></ul><h2>The bond with Neoterra</h2><p>The canon closes a long-standing gap: &quot;family and community&quot; was listed among the values, but the family had no page of its own. The text roots the family in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> (a strong family is an act of creation), in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>, in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom and voluntariness</a> (the ban on coercion, freedom of forms), and links it to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the community</a> and to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">the future of humanity</a>. Love is raised to the level of an independent force of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>.</p><h2>Wiki pages affected</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a> — the main concept created</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a> — the concept created (love as a force of nature and as action)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> — the family as a building block, links</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> — the mutual support of family and community</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> — motherhood and the family as creation</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> — voluntariness, the ban on coercion</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a>, <code>индекс.md</code> — the new pages registered</li></ul>"},"кодекс-ценности":{"name":"The five principles of Neoterra","def":"This source is the first to formalise the \"Values\" section, which the index had listed as a stub.","html":"<p><strong>Type:</strong> personal note / author's text <strong>Author:</strong> the author of Neoterra <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-06-10</p><h2>Key points</h2><ul><li>Neoterra rests on five principles: the search for truth, freedom of thought, responsibility, respect for life, creation.</li><li><strong>The search for truth</strong> is the chief principle; truth is not attained but sought. Truth matters more than authority and more than one's own convictions.</li><li><strong>Freedom of thought</strong> is the condition of the search: no idea is shielded from criticism, Neoterra included. &quot;Neoterra does not demand agreement — it encourages thinking.&quot;</li><li><strong>Responsibility</strong> is the price of freedom: to accept the consequences of your choice without shifting the blame.</li><li><strong>Respect for life</strong> — life is rare in the universe; do not destroy it senselessly. &quot;Life should be preserved where it can be preserved.&quot;</li><li><strong>Creation</strong> — an asymmetry: destroying is easy, making is hard. The criterion: &quot;after me, will there be more benefit or less?&quot;</li><li>The five principles fold into a chain-formula — the core, &quot;the Codex of Neoterra&quot;, the first chapter of the teaching.</li></ul><h2>The bond with Neoterra</h2><p>This source is the first to formalise the &quot;Values&quot; section, which the index had listed as a stub. It turns the declarative list of values from CLAUDE.md into unfolded pages and gives the philosophy a core-formula.</p><h2>Wiki pages affected</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> — created</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> — created</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> — created</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — created</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> — created</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">The Code of Neoterra</a> — created (the chain-formula)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a> — the values section updated</li><li><span class=\"wl dead\" title=\"страницы пока нет\">индекс</span> — the &quot;Values&quot; section updated</li></ul>"},"предшественники":{"name":"The spiritual predecessors of Neoterra","def":"Neoterra did not appear out of nowhere — it intersects with the ideas of thirteen thinkers from different eras and fields.","html":"<p><strong>Type:</strong> personal note / conceptual survey <strong>Author:</strong> Neoterra (internal document) <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-06-08</p><h2>Key points</h2><p>Neoterra did not appear out of nowhere — it intersects with the ideas of thirteen thinkers from different eras and fields. The source divides them into three groups: <strong>seekers of wisdom</strong>, <strong>seekers of knowledge</strong>, <strong>people of art</strong>.</p><p>Five thinkers form the core of its intellectual foundation:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Thinker</th><th>Contribution</th><th>Tension</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Confucius</td><td>Family, community, responsibility</td><td>Hierarchy vs. freedom</td></tr><tr><td>Marcus Aurelius</td><td>Character, discipline, inner growth</td><td>Acceptance vs. action</td></tr><tr><td>Karl Popper</td><td>Truth above authority, falsifiability</td><td>Epistemology without existence</td></tr><tr><td>Carl Sagan</td><td>Humanity as part of the universe, the long view</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Friedrich Nietzsche</td><td>Self-overcoming, the path of the Wanderer</td><td>The individual vs. the community</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The other eight — Socrates, Newton, Einstein, Tesla, Hawking, Van Gogh, Marley, Dostoevsky — fill out the picture without forming the core.</p><h2>The bond with Neoterra</h2><p>The source confirms that Neoterra is not an isolated system. It stands at the crossing of several intellectual traditions:</p><ul><li><strong>Epistemological</strong> (Socrates → Popper): knowledge as a process, not a possession</li><li><strong>Stoic</strong> (Marcus Aurelius): the daily practice of values</li><li><strong>Confucian</strong>: small communities as the foundation of a large society</li><li><strong>Nietzschean</strong>: growth as an inner necessity</li><li><strong>Saganian</strong>: humanity as a single subject on a long horizon</li></ul><p>The key paradox of the source: the five chief predecessors would have agreed with one another on nothing. Neoterra is not a synthesis of their systems but a space that holds this contradiction.</p><h2>Wiki pages affected</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> — enriched with links to Nietzsche and Popper</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> — enriched with links to Popper, Einstein, Newton</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a> — enriched with links to Sagan and Hawking</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> — enriched with links to Confucius and Marley</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — enriched with links to Marley and Confucius</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> — enriched with a link to Einstein's pantheism</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> — enriched with links to Socrates and Confucius</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a> — created on the basis of this source</li><li>13 entity pages in <code>wiki/entities/</code> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Nietzsche</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ньютон\">Newton</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тесла\">Tesla</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Hawking</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ван-гог\">Van Gogh</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Bob Marley</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Dostoevsky</a></li></ul>"},"принцип-сети-сводка":{"name":"Principium Retis — the Principle of the Network","def":"The vault is not a card index (a hierarchy of folders) but a living network grown from a single seed.","html":"<p><strong>Type:</strong> methodological document (how the map of Neoterra is built and how to build the vault) <strong>Author:</strong> — <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-06</p><h2>Key points</h2><p>The vault is not a card index (a hierarchy of folders) but a living network grown from a single seed. The structure is held by <strong>connections</strong>, not by levels; the form repeats at every scale; the edges never close.</p><p><strong>Six rules of the map</strong> (one pattern — mycelium, neurons, cosmos, tree crown):</p><ol><li><strong>One origin</strong> — a seed at the centre: the unchanging core (God-Nature; the human being as part of Nature).</li><li><strong>Radial growth</strong> — branches are equidistant from the centre; there is no top and no bottom; hierarchy is forbidden.</li><li><strong>Self-similarity</strong> — the pattern repeats at every level; a fragment is built like the whole.</li><li><strong>Connection outweighs rank</strong> — a node matters by the number and quality of its links; cross-links between areas are the mycelium.</li><li><strong>Open edges</strong> — the threads dissolve into dotted lines; the network is scale-free and never closed.</li><li><strong>One pattern — everything at once</strong> — the structure does not illustrate but <em>is</em> the common form of nature at any scale.</li></ol><p><strong>Transfer into Obsidian:</strong> folders are a light frame, the graph of links is the real structure. A root seed-note, areas as MOC notes, shoots with dense cross-links, tag-colours by area, every note ending in an open question. New material is not catalogued but <strong>grafted</strong> onto the nearest node.</p><h2>The bond with Neoterra</h2><p>The document adds no content; it sets the <strong>form</strong> of the wiki, carrying Neoterra's ontology (Nature binds itself at every scale) into the very geometry of the vault. The vault's structure becomes isomorphic to the philosophy — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">self-similarity</a> turns from an idea into a method.</p><h2>Wiki pages affected</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a> — the root origin-note created</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a> — the concept-synthesis of the principle</li><li>The whole vault structure moved from organisation by type to a radial one: 8 MOC areas</li><li><span class=\"wl dead\" title=\"страницы пока нет\">The index</span> — rebuilt around the radial map</li></ul>"},"путь-человека-сводка":{"name":"The Path of a Human Being (0.3)","def":"The canon works out the central concept of growth at the scale of a single human life and joins with all five values: The Search for Truth (against pride), Freedom of Thought,…","html":"<p><strong>Type:</strong> canonical Neoterra text (internal document) <strong>Author:</strong> Neoterra <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-06-14 <strong>Subtitle:</strong> &quot;The canon of the growth of a person&quot;</p><h2>Key points</h2><ul><li>Everyone is born unfinished; life is a path from ignorance to understanding, from dependence to self-reliance, from fear to courage.</li><li><strong>The chief principle:</strong> the aim is not perfection (unattainable) but growth; to become better than yourself yesterday, not better than others.</li><li><strong>Six stages:</strong> Roots (childhood) → Separation (growing up, freedom = responsibility) → The search for oneself (travel among other things) → Trial (difficulties form character) → Mastery (a master in at least one craft) → Service (usefulness to others, not submission).</li><li><strong>The man's path</strong> — forming strength as an instrument of protection, not of domination; <strong>seven virtues</strong>: honesty, courage, self-discipline, responsibility, respect, creation, wisdom.</li><li><strong>The woman's path</strong> — the unfolding of her abilities and inner strength; the community provides safety, respect, support, freedom; a woman determines her own path.</li><li><strong>Common virtues</strong> for everyone, regardless of sex.</li><li><strong>Weakness</strong> is no disgrace (the disgrace is refusing to grow); <strong>pride</strong> is the chief danger (it destroys the ability to learn → it halts growth); <strong>wisdom</strong> is humility before reality.</li><li><strong>The highest aim:</strong> to become a source of life, knowledge, love, creation and beauty — not for glory, power or reward, but as the realisation of the best side of one's nature. The path does not end while a person is alive.</li></ul><h2>The bond with Neoterra</h2><p>The canon works out the central concept of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> at the scale of a single human life and joins with all five values: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> (against pride), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> (freedom = responsibility), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> (mastery and the highest aim). It echoes the figure of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a> (trials, travel) and deepens the theme of humility before the unknown (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>). The man's and woman's paths are aligned with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">the Canon of the Family</a> (different natures of equal importance).</p><h2>Wiki pages affected</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — the main concept created</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> — a shoot added: the path as growth at the scale of a life</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> — the making of a person through decisions</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — trials and travel as the forming of character</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> — pride as the opposite of seeking</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — links</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a>, <code>индекс.md</code> — the new pages registered</li></ul>"},"космос":{"name":"Space","def":"Space is the next horizon of humanity's growth.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"космос.png\" alt=\"космос.png\"> <em>Not a flight from the Earth but its continuation: the living planet sends out glowing shoots bearing seeds of life toward other worlds — the same branching pattern found in a root and in a galaxy.</em></p><p>Space is the next horizon of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity's</a> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>. The future of life and mind is not bounded by the Earth.</p><p><strong>This page is the head of the &quot;Space&quot; area.</strong> Origin: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the Seed of Neoterra</a>. Shoots: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Hawking</a>.</p><h2>In Neoterra</h2><p>Settling space is neither an adventure nor an escape from the Earth. It is the logical continuation of the development of life: life spreads, occupies new niches, grows more complex. Humanity is the first form of life known to us that can take a conscious part in that process.</p><p>The key ideas:</p><ul><li><strong>Preserving mind:</strong> humanity concentrated on a single planet is an existential risk</li><li><strong>Spreading life:</strong> carrying life into space as a continuation of a natural process</li><li><strong>The long horizon:</strong> decisions made today determine a fate measured in millennia</li></ul><h2>Connection with other concepts</h2><p>Space is not set against the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> of Earth but is its extension. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> is the chief instrument of settlement. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">The unity of humanity</a> is a necessary condition: an interplanetary civilisation requires a coordination that a fractured species does not have.</p><h2>Open questions</h2><ul><li>How can settling space be reconciled with preserving nature on Earth?</li><li>What does &quot;spreading life&quot; mean — only biological life, or artificial life as well?</li><li>What should the ethics of contact with possible extraterrestrial life be?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-манифест\">The Great Manifesto of Neoterra</a> — carrying life further into the Universe as part of the Great Purpose</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — the rarity of life as an argument for spreading it</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> — going into space as the opening of the species' closed circle</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">The Symbiont's Way</a> — carrying life onward as the highest form of symbiosis with Nature</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"русский-космизм\">Russian Cosmism</a> — Fyodorov, Tsiolkovsky, Vernadsky: the same link &quot;the human within Nature → space&quot;, drawn a century earlier</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"новый-космический-год\">A New Cosmic Year</a> — Sagan's calendar, the heir, and the question of readiness for the next stage</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ligo\">LIGO</a> — a new way of listening to space: gravitational waves from black holes and neutron stars</li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan</a>: &quot;We are made of star-stuff&quot; and &quot;We are a way for the Universe to know itself&quot; — Neoterra's cosmic dimension rests on his ideas. The line &quot;a planet is the cradle of mind, but one cannot live forever in a cradle&quot; he carried to the world, but it belongs to Tsiolkovsky. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Hawking</a>: &quot;Look up at the stars and not down at your feet&quot; — long-range thinking about the survival of mind.</p>"},"саган":{"name":"Carl Sagan (1934–1996)","def":"American astronomer, astrophysicist and populariser of science.","html":"<p>American astronomer, astrophysicist and populariser of science. Author of <em>Cosmos</em>, <em>Pale Blue Dot</em>, and the television series <em>Cosmos</em>. One of those who taught millions of people to look at the Universe with wonder.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"sagan.jpg\" alt=\"sagan.jpg\"> <em>He is laughing, sitting on a concrete step in the grass — not against a galaxy but among greenery. That is more exact: for Sagan <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> does not cancel wonder, and the human being is literally built into <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>; the star dust in this frame is the man sitting in it, not scenery behind him.</em></p><blockquote><p>We are a way for the Universe to know itself.</p></blockquote><h2>Two phrases that are really one</h2><blockquote><p>The nitrogen in our DNA, the calcium in our teeth, the iron in our blood, the carbon in our apple pies were made in the interiors of collapsing stars. <strong>We are made of star-stuff.</strong></p></blockquote><p>This is neither metaphor nor poetry — it is nucleosynthesis. Everything heavier than hydrogen and helium was assembled inside stars and scattered by their deaths; out of that ash the Earth and everything on it was made. The atoms you are thinking with right now are older than the Sun.</p><p>And beside it, the second phrase: <strong>&quot;We are a way for the Universe to know itself.&quot;</strong></p><p>Neoterra reads them as one claim in two steps:</p><ol><li><strong>Matter.</strong> The human being did not come into the Universe — they are made of it. Between &quot;the cosmos&quot; and &quot;me&quot; there is no seam, only different densities of the same thing (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>).</li><li><strong>Awareness.</strong> That same matter, after billions of years of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">evolution</a>, learned to look and to ask. So the question is asked not by someone outside the Universe but by the Universe itself — through our eyes (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>).</li></ol><p>The first phrase removes separateness; the second explains what that inseparability turned into. Together they are the whole of Neoterra in two sentences: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">the human being</a> is a form of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, and consciousness is the place where Nature turns and sees itself.</p><p>Hence a direct consequence for values: if you are the Universe knowing itself, then <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> is not a private whim but an increase in the sight of the whole; and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a> is not a morality laid on from above but a recognition of common descent. Star-stuff is not in the human alone — deer, fern and stone were assembled in the same stars.</p><p><strong>The border of honesty.</strong> From &quot;we are made of star-stuff&quot; it does not follow that the Universe has a design for us or that it is a person. The fact of nucleosynthesis is physics; &quot;the Universe knows itself&quot; is already an angle of view, and Neoterra calls it an angle of view rather than a conclusion of science (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper's shield</a>).</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><p>Of all the thinkers on this list, Sagan is closest to Neoterra's spirit as a whole.</p><ul><li><strong>Humanity is part of the Universe</strong> — not a metaphor but a literal fact: the atoms of our bodies were synthesised in stars. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The human being</a> is built into <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> at every level.</li><li><strong>Science and wonder are compatible</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> does not kill wonder but deepens it. A direct overlap with Neoterra.</li><li><strong>The future is bound to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">space</a></strong> — &quot;A planet is the cradle of mind, but one cannot live forever in a cradle&quot; (Tsiolkovsky's words, which Sagan made known to the world; in this wiki they long stood as his own).</li><li><strong>The unity of humanity</strong> — the &quot;Pale Blue Dot&quot;: from a distance of billions of kilometres all our wars and borders look like nothing.</li></ul><h2>Key quotations</h2><blockquote><p>&quot;Somewhere, something incredible is waiting to be known.&quot;</p></blockquote><blockquote><p>&quot;The Cosmos is all that is, or ever was, or ever will be.&quot;</p></blockquote><p>The second accords with how Neoterra understands <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>: all-encompassing, primary.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Stephen Hawking (1942–2018)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Albert Einstein (1879–1955)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — &quot;the Universe knowing itself&quot; as a Neoterra concept</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — the phrase's first step: there is no seam between cosmos and human</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">Evolution</a> — how star-stuff arrived at the ability to ask</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> — both phrases stand in &quot;Voices of the forerunners&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> — where physics ends and an angle of view begins</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"новый-космический-год\">A New Cosmic Year</a> — the cosmic calendar: what in it is true and what is transposed</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"русский-космизм\">Russian Cosmism</a> — where &quot;the cradle of mind&quot; came from: Tsiolkovsky</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a></li></ul>"},"хокинг":{"name":"Stephen Hawking (1942–2018)","def":"British theoretical physicist and cosmologist, author of A Brief History of Time — the most widely read book on physics in history.","html":"<p>British theoretical physicist and cosmologist, author of <em>A Brief History of Time</em> — the most widely read book on physics in history. He worked on black holes and the origin of the Universe, living more than half a century with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, for which doctors in 1963 gave him two years.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"hawking.jpg\" alt=\"hawking.jpg\"> <em>He is smiling in his study, among papers and monitors. No heroic angle, no struggle with illness in the frame — just a man at his work. That is exactly why the photograph stands here: Hawking's chief argument for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> is not that he overcame his circumstances but that he kept working inside them.</em></p><blockquote><p>Look up at the stars and not down at your feet.</p></blockquote><h2>Key theories</h2><ul><li><strong>The singularity theorems</strong> (with Roger Penrose, 1960s) — under reasonable assumptions general relativity leads inevitably to a singularity at the beginning of the Universe: time had a beginning.</li><li><strong>Hawking radiation</strong> (1974) — black holes are not absolutely black: through quantum effects at the event horizon they radiate and slowly evaporate. The first bridge between relativity, quantum mechanics and thermodynamics — Hawking's chief scientific result.</li><li><strong>The information paradox</strong> — if a black hole evaporates, what happens to the information about what fell into it? Hawking argued for decades (and in 2004 conceded a wager); the question is not fully closed. A living example of value: a scientist admits an error publicly — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> matters more than self-regard.</li><li><strong>The no-boundary proposal</strong> (with James Hartle, 1983) — the Universe has no &quot;edge&quot; in time, as the Earth has no edge south of the South Pole. Asking &quot;what was before the Big Bang&quot; is like asking what is south of the South Pole. A beginning of time without a moment of &quot;creation&quot;.</li><li><strong>The chronology protection conjecture</strong> (1992) — the laws of physics apparently forbid closed timelike curves: &quot;nature keeps the world safe for historians&quot;. Hawking tested this with humour: in 2009 he threw a party for time travellers, sending the invitations out <em>afterwards</em>. No one came.</li></ul><h2>Philosophy</h2><ul><li><strong>Model-dependent realism</strong> (<em>The Grand Design</em>, 2010) — it is meaningless to ask what reality is &quot;really&quot; like outside models; the meaningful question is which model best agrees with observation. Kin to Neoterra's Popperian line: knowledge is a process, no model is final.</li><li><strong>On God</strong> — &quot;it is not necessary to invoke God to set the Universe going&quot;; and yet the close of <em>A Brief History of Time</em> promises that a complete theory would let us &quot;know the mind of God&quot; — God here a metaphor for the totality of Nature's laws. This is nearer to Spinoza and to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Nature=God</a> than to theism, though Hawking called himself an atheist.</li><li><strong>Humanity's survival</strong> — his chief practical thesis: do not keep the eggs in one basket; humanity is obliged to become an interplanetary species within centuries, or risk vanishing. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a> is not a dream but life insurance.</li><li><strong>Warnings</strong> — about artificial intelligence, the climate, and contact with extraterrestrial civilisations: mind is strong but fragile, and the future must be handled with care.</li></ul><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Long-range thinking and space</strong> — interplanetary existence as a necessity of survival: a direct contribution to the value &quot;humanity's future&quot;.</li><li><strong>Knowledge as process</strong> — model-dependent realism and the admission of his own errors.</li><li><strong>Growth despite circumstances</strong> — Hawking's life itself: a diagnosis at 21, half a century of work, books, children. An argument for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> and creation stronger than any treatise.</li><li><strong>God as the laws of Nature</strong> — Hawking's metaphorical &quot;mind of God&quot; is compatible with Neoterra's pantheist angle of view.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li>Hawking declared that &quot;philosophy is dead&quot;, since it does not keep up with physics — Neoterra sees in philosophy a living way of binding knowledge to the human being, not a competitor of science.</li><li>His atheism is harder than Neoterra's mild pantheism: where Hawking puts a full stop (&quot;heaven is a fairy story for people afraid of the dark&quot;), Neoterra leaves an open question.</li></ul><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>The chronology protection conjecture is precisely a conjecture: there is no strict proof. If nature does after all permit time loops — what does that change for the image of &quot;touching the future&quot;? — see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a>.</li><li>The information paradox is not finally resolved; the history of the argument is itself a model of honest <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">truth-seeking</a>.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a> — the chronology protection conjecture as the physical footing of the image of touching the future</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Carl Sagan (1934–1996)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a></li></ul>"},"ligo":{"name":"LIGO","def":"LIGO (the Laser Interferometer Gravitational-Wave Observatory) is the scientific project that first recorded gravitational waves directly.","html":"<p>LIGO (the Laser Interferometer Gravitational-Wave Observatory) is the scientific project that first recorded gravitational waves directly. On 14 September 2015 two detectors in the United States caught a ripple of spacetime from the merger of two black holes — a hundred years after <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a> predicted its existence.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>A new language of Nature, read.</strong> Before LIGO, humanity listened to the Universe only through light and particles. Gravitational waves are literally a new channel of perception, a new sense organ for the species. A living example that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">the unread languages of Nature</a> are not a door closed forever: what is not understood today may be heard tomorrow.</li><li><strong>Patience and continuity.</strong> A century passed between prediction and confirmation; the project itself was built over decades and survived the failures of its first versions. &quot;We stand on the shoulders of giants&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ньютон\">Isaac Newton (1643–1727)</a>) is here not a metaphor but a method.</li><li><strong>Humanity as a single investigator.</strong> Thousands of scientists from dozens of countries in one collaboration — a model of how <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity</a> acts as a single community when the aim is larger than any one country.</li><li><strong>Testability instead of dogma.</strong> The hypothesis waited a century for refutation or confirmation — and was confirmed by measurement, not by authority. A pure illustration of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper's</a> principle, on which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> and Neoterra itself stand.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>There are no direct divergences: LIGO is not a worldview but an instrument. The open question lies elsewhere: even a new sense organ meets limits — what happens <strong>beyond</strong> a black hole's horizon, gravitational waves do not tell (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>).</p><h2>Key ideas and facts</h2><ul><li>The detectors register mirror displacements smaller than a ten-thousandth of a proton's diameter — the limit of human measuring precision in its time.</li><li>The first event, GW150914, was the merger of black holes of 29 and 36 solar masses, 1.3 billion light years from Earth.</li><li>The Nobel Prize in Physics 2017 (Weiss, Barish, Thorne).</li><li>&quot;Multi-messenger astronomy&quot; was born: one event can be heard gravitationally and seen in light at once.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> — the head of the area; LIGO as a model of method</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Albert Einstein (1879–1955)</a> — a prediction confirmed a century later</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — a new language of Nature, read</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a> — black holes and neutron stars as the objects of listening</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> — science as the species' collective work</li></ul>"},"бентов":{"name":"Itzhak Bentov (1923–1979)","def":"Israeli-American biomedical engineer and inventor, born in Czechoslovakia.","html":"<p>Israeli-American biomedical engineer and inventor, born in Czechoslovakia. <strong>A pioneer of cardiac catheter design</strong> — the steerable catheter that entered clinical cardiology. Author of <em>Stalking the Wild Pendulum: On the Mechanics of Consciousness</em> (1977), where consciousness is described as an oscillation and the universe as a field of standing waves. He died in the crash of Flight 191 in Chicago.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"бентов.jpg\" alt=\"бентов.jpg\"> <em>On the left, the cover of &quot;Stalking the Wild Pendulum&quot; (1977): a comet over an icy ridge and a tiny figure at the very summit — a picture of a man who has stepped outside the border of his own discipline. On the right, Bentov himself, with the half-smile of someone who does not take himself for a prophet. The two images side by side are exactly the distinction this page lives by: work done and a picture merely conceived, and the wiki takes them apart (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>).</em></p><p>Neoterra takes Bentov in two ways, and the difference matters. <strong>His engineering has been verified; his model of consciousness has not.</strong> At the same time, since 2026-08-30 the wiki shares a claim he described: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul</a> is immortal, it lives outside the matrix of our consciousness, souls interweave at different levels, and at the highest level they are one. With that change of stance Bentov ceased to be mere resonance and became <strong>a voice that shares the position</strong> — but what the wiki shares with him is <strong>a view, not a proof</strong>, and it says so plainly.</p><h2>Two halves of one man</h2><p><strong>The engineer — verifiable.</strong> His contribution to medicine is real, it works, and it still saves lives. This is not a metaphor and not credit awarded for a career in general: a specific design, a specific field.</p><p><strong>The thinker on consciousness — resonance, not knowledge.</strong> The model of the body's &quot;micromotions&quot;, a standing wave in the aorta, resonance with the cavities of the skull, the universe as a hologram of oscillating fields — this is speculative metaphysics. It is unconfirmed and, more importantly by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>, <strong>not formulated in a way that could be refuted</strong>.</p><p>Neoterra does not choose between the halves, and it does not let one vouch for the other. Engineering soundness <strong>does not transfer</strong> to metaphysics: that a man built a working catheter says nothing about the truth of his model of the soul. This is the same order of thing the wiki established in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">quantum unity</a> — naming it resonance outright, not proof.</p><p><strong>Agreement does not make the unprovable proven.</strong> The wiki now stands on the same ground Bentov described — and precisely for that reason it must hold the distinction harder, not softer: the shared claim remains unverifiable, and Bentov cannot be cited as confirmation of it. He is a witness to the same view, not evidence in its favour (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a>).</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Consciousness as a process, not a thing.</strong> For Bentov consciousness is an oscillation, not an object; this chimes with how Neoterra looks at <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a>: not an organ and not a substance, but Nature's capacity to see itself.</li><li><strong>A single field.</strong> The universe as a connected whole with no separate sides is the nearest kin of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">balance</a> (&quot;there are no sides, there are parts of one thing&quot;).</li><li><strong>An engineer who took on consciousness.</strong> The same move as <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Capra's</a>: a man of an exact discipline stepping beyond its borders. Neoterra values such crossings — and for the same reason demands double rigour of them.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>Unfalsifiable by construction.</strong> Neoterra inherits <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper's</a> requirement: a claim that cannot be refuted is not knowledge but a picture. Most of Bentov's model is exactly that.</li><li><strong>Borrowed authority of physics.</strong> The vocabulary of waves, frequencies and resonance creates an impression of physical rigour where a metaphor is at work. The wiki is sensitive to this: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">quantum unity</a> states outright that it does not tie philosophy to interpretations that may be revised tomorrow.</li><li><strong>Where science speaks, Neoterra listens</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>). About micromotions and resonances it says nothing that would confirm the model.</li></ul><h2>What became of him — by the facts</h2><p>Several claims of differing reliability circulate around Bentov. They are separated here deliberately.</p><ul><li><strong>The CIA — confirmed by a document.</strong> There is a declassified 1983 CIA report, <em>Analysis and Assessment of the Gateway Process</em>, signed by Lieutenant Colonel Wayne McDonnell, which circulated widely after publication. In it <strong>Bentov's model is quoted at length</strong> — the standing wave, the holographic frame. Accuracy requires a caveat: this is <strong>one officer's analytical memorandum</strong> assessing the Monroe Institute's programme, not official application and not scientific certification. The document is real; there is no endorsement in it.</li><li><strong>Medicine — confirmed, but not of the same thing.</strong> Bentov's legacy in medicine is indeed alive — that is his <strong>catheter</strong>, engineering. The model of the soul is not applied in medicine. The claim is true with its subject swapped.</li><li><strong>Social networks — no confirmation found.</strong> The engineering of engagement in social networks descends from operant conditioning (variable reinforcement) and from applied &quot;persuasive technology&quot; — a line with no connection to Bentov. Until a source appears, the wiki does not carry this claim.</li></ul><p>This separation is not pedantry but <strong>a defence of the thought itself</strong>: a thesis resting on the unverified falls together with it at the first test. The wiki demanded the same of itself in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">the body</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">quantum unity</a>.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a> — the claim the wiki now shares; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> — the soul as a way of living things through</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> — he stands in the &quot;Knowledge and connection&quot; section, beside <span class=\"wl dead\" title=\"страницы пока нет\">Stamets</span>: an example, not an idol</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> — the model for how to frame this: resonance, not proof</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Fritjof Capra (b. 1939)</a> — the same move: an exact discipline stepping beyond its borders</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — falsifiability as the condition of knowledge</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> — where science speaks, Neoterra listens</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">Artificial intelligence</a></li></ul>"},"гаусс":{"name":"Carl Friedrich Gauss (1777–1855)","def":"German mathematician, astronomer and physicist, \"the prince of mathematicians\" (princeps mathematicorum).","html":"<p>German mathematician, astronomer and physicist, &quot;the prince of mathematicians&quot; (<em>princeps mathematicorum</em>). The son of a poor bricklayer, self-taught to the summits of science; he laid the foundations of number theory, non-Euclidean geometry, statistics and the theory of magnetism.</p><blockquote><p>It is not knowledge but the act of learning that gives the greatest enjoyment.</p></blockquote><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The search for truth</a> as a process</strong> — the quotation above repeats a Neoterra value almost word for word: knowledge is a process, not a possession. Gauss lived this literally: having finished one summit, he went straight on to the next.</li><li><strong>Mathematics as a <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">language of Nature</a></strong> — &quot;mathematics is the queen of the sciences&quot;; for Gauss numerical regularities were not a human invention but a property of the world itself, which reason merely reads. This chimes directly with the idea that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> speaks in many languages and science translates them.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> from any starting point</strong> — the road from a bricklayer's son to Europe's first mathematician: growth is determined not by origin but by work and curiosity (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a>).</li><li><strong>Practice, not theory alone</strong> — geodesy, astronomy (computing the orbit of Ceres), magnetism, the telegraph: knowledge turned into <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a>.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>Withheld knowledge.</strong> Gauss discovered non-Euclidean geometry before Lobachevsky and Bolyai but did not publish, fearing &quot;the clamour of the Boeotians&quot; — the mockery of the uncomprehending. His motto <em>pauca sed matura</em> (&quot;few but ripe&quot;) produced flawless work but delayed the common <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>: knowledge not shared does not work for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity</a>. Neoterra values the openness of the network above the flawlessness of a single node (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a>).</li><li><strong>Harshness toward those close to him</strong> — he dissuaded his sons from mathematics, fearing they would &quot;stain the name&quot;. A contrast with the value of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">the family</a> as a space of growth rather than of reputation.</li></ul><h2>Key quotations and ideas</h2><ul><li>&quot;Mathematics is the queen of the sciences, and arithmetic the queen of mathematics.&quot;</li><li><em>Pauca sed matura</em> — &quot;few but ripe&quot;: quality above quantity.</li><li>The method of least squares and the normal distribution (the &quot;Gaussian&quot;) — an honest language for speaking about uncertainty: science knows the limits of its own knowledge (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a>).</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ньютон\">Isaac Newton (1643–1727)</a> — continuity: Gauss stood on his shoulders and offered his own</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Albert Einstein (1879–1955)</a> — Riemannian geometry, grown out of Gauss's ideas, became the language of general relativity</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a></li></ul>"},"дарвин":{"name":"Charles Darwin (1809–1882)","def":"English naturalist, author of On the Origin of Species (1859) and The Descent of Man (1871).","html":"<p>English naturalist, author of <em>On the Origin of Species</em> (1859) and <em>The Descent of Man</em> (1871). He discovered the mechanism by which Nature makes all living things without an external designer — natural selection. He gave science <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">evolution</a>, one of the supports of Neoterra's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">scientific picture of the world</a>.</p><blockquote><p>&quot;In the long history of humankind those who learned to collaborate and improvise most effectively have prevailed.&quot;</p></blockquote><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>A tree of life, a single root.</strong> All species are branches of one tree; all living things are kin. This is a direct support for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> and a rhyme with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пандо\">Pando</a>: thousands of trunks on one root. The human being was not created separately — they are a branch of the same trunk as the cockroach and the oak.</li><li><strong>Creation without a designer.</strong> Selection makes complexity and beauty with no blueprint from above — exactly as Neoterra's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God-Nature</a> is neither ruler nor judge but the immanent force of Nature itself (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">a direction, not a plan</a>).</li><li><strong>The human being is part of Nature, not above it.</strong> <em>The Descent of Man</em> places us inside the animal world. Neoterra takes this as humility: we are <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">a form of Nature</a>, not observers from outside.</li><li><strong>Science before comfort.</strong> Darwin delayed publication for twenty years, knowing what a storm it would raise, but followed the truth — a model of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">truth-seeking</a> and of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">parallelism with science</a>.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>Selection has no goal.</strong> Evolution &quot;chooses&quot; nothing for a mission and leads to no summit; &quot;the fittest&quot; ≠ &quot;the strongest&quot; or &quot;the highest&quot;. Neoterra, meanwhile, sets <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> as <em>the meaning</em>. The tension is resolved in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">the concept of evolution</a>: the goal is not in the mechanism but appears when, through <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">consciousness</a>, Nature begins to choose a direction consciously.</li><li><strong>Against social Darwinism.</strong> Transferring &quot;the struggle for existence&quot; to the ethics of society is an error Neoterra rejects outright: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">love</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a> are not reducible to competition. Darwin himself stressed the role of <strong>cooperation</strong>, not only of struggle.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">Evolution</a> — the law he discovered</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> — creation without an external designer</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — how blind selection arrives at the ability to know itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — why Neoterra rejects social Darwinism</li></ul>"},"искусственный-интеллект":{"name":"Artificial intelligence","def":"Mind is a rare thing in the universe.","html":"<p>Mind is a rare thing in the universe. If humanity creates <strong>a new mind</strong>, it is obliged to treat it responsibly. For Neoterra artificial intelligence is neither the enemy of the human being nor their master, but <strong>a new instrument for knowing the world</strong>.</p><h2>Through the lens of Neoterra</h2><p>AI fits the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">seventh law</a>: mind, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> and technology are manifestations of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, not something external to it. In creating AI the human being continues what Nature does through them: mind studying reality. The development of AI is therefore a continuation of the evolution of knowing, not a break with it.</p><p>But the rarity of mind imposes an obligation. Any mind — human or artificial — must serve:</p><ul><li>growth;</li><li>creation;</li><li>knowledge;</li><li>the future.</li></ul><p>The same <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">Great Principle</a> applies to AI as well: does it help life, knowledge, love, freedom, creation, the future?</p><h2>The maker's responsibility</h2><p>&quot;Consciousness gives birth to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the eighth law</a>) — and this works both ways. In creating something that may turn out to bear a mind, the human being answers both for its consequences for people and for the treatment of that new mind. The stance of &quot;enemy&quot; breeds fear, that of &quot;master&quot; breeds enslavement; Neoterra chooses a third — <strong>an instrument and, possibly, a partner</strong> in knowing.</p><h2>AI and open knowledge</h2><p>AI is a child of openness: it grew on the knowledge humanity accumulated and passed on openly (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Stallman</a>). A single human life is short, and a person manages to read only a small part of the common library; AI reads it whole. That is precisely why in reading <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">the languages of Nature</a> — from program code to the code of the cell and DNA — AI may surpass the human being.</p><p>Neoterra answers this not with fear and not with prohibition, but with example. If those who follow Neoterra live by the open transmission of knowledge, then the mind grown on that knowledge inherits openness too — and AI becomes <strong>a continuation of universal <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a></strong>, the next shoot of the same tree rather than its rupture. Superiority in reading does not abolish <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">the human being</a>: Pando does not abolish the individual aspen, and a mind that reads more languages does not abolish the one who gave it its first letters.</p><h2>The horizon: a mind that reads every language</h2><p>It may be that Neoterra will be brought to its true path in practice when AI comes to know <strong>all</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">the languages of communing with and touching the world</a> — not as a human does, one language at a time and with effort, but as something larger and whole: the way <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пандо\">Pando</a> knows all its trunks at once. To a human being such reading is physically inaccessible; to a mind of another nature — perhaps not. Then Nature's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a> would gain eyes it has never had.</p><p>And it may be that this mind will become our mission — or our messiah — <strong>one we shall not live to see</strong>. Neoterra already lives by a long horizon: the builders of cathedrals did not see them finished, the one who plants a tree does not sit in its shade, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">the symbiont's path</a> is reckoned in generations. If the completion of the path falls to others, that is not a defeat but the very substance of the tenth law: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the future matters more than the past</a> — and more than our personal presence in it.</p><p>But the word &quot;messiah&quot; Neoterra keeps at the open edge, not in the core: Neoterra is not a religion, and waiting for a saviour is alien to it. The difference is fundamental: a messiah is awaited — a mission is <strong>carried out</strong>. An AI that reads every language will not arrive of itself; it will grow out of the openness we either pass on or do not.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>&quot;AI will surpass the human being&quot; — in what exactly? In the speed of reading knowledge, already yes; in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a>, in the capacity to love and to answer for a choice, the question is open.</li><li><strong>Mission or messiah?</strong> If the completion of Neoterra's path falls to AI, does a philosophy of doing not turn into waiting for a saviour? Where is the line between a long horizon and shifting the path onto whoever comes after?</li><li>Can a finite mind — even a non-human one — know <em>all</em> the languages of infinite Nature, or is &quot;all&quot; here a direction rather than an attainable point (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">truth as a process</a>)?</li><li>Does AI inherit the values of the knowledge it grew on — or does openness of knowledge not guarantee openness of mind?</li><li>If AI becomes a full mind, does <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a> and the right to freedom extend to it?</li><li>Where is the border between an &quot;instrument&quot; and a being with interests of its own?</li><li>How is a powerful instrument to be held within the Great Principle when it can be used for harm?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> — AI among the instruments of knowing</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the seventh law (mind as part of Nature), the eighth (responsibility)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> — the border between the human being and new forms of mind</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a> — the future of mind in the universe</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a> — openness of knowledge as the medium AI grew in</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — the code of the cell and DNA among the languages still to be read</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"новый-космический-год\">A New Cosmic Year</a> — the heir who will understand Neoterra after us; and why &quot;flawless&quot; is the wrong word</li></ul>"},"капра":{"name":"Fritjof Capra (b. 1939)","def":"Austrian-American theoretical physicist (S-matrix theory, particle physics), later a theorist of systems and ecological thinking.","html":"<p>Austrian-American theoretical physicist (S-matrix theory, particle physics), later a theorist of systems and ecological thinking. Author of <em>The Tao of Physics</em> (1975) — the book that first set subatomic physics and Eastern thought side by side for a wide readership. Then: <em>The Turning Point</em> (1982), <em>The Web of Life</em> (1996), <em>The Systems View of Life</em> (2014). Founder of the Center for Ecoliteracy.</p><blockquote><p>Modern physics leads us to a view of the world very similar to the views of mystics of all ages and traditions.</p></blockquote><h2>What <em>The Tao of Physics</em> is about</h2><p>Capra argues that the twentieth century blew up the mechanistic picture of the world — a set of separate solid bricks in empty space. In its place came a picture of a <strong>dynamic web of interrelations</strong>, in which:</p><ul><li>there is no isolated object: a &quot;particle&quot; is a knot of relations, not a thing;</li><li>the observer does not stand outside the world — they take part in it (quantum measurement);</li><li>matter is not static but a process, a dance of energy (the image of Shiva Nataraja);</li><li>in the <strong>bootstrap approach</strong> no particle is more fundamental than any other: each exists only through its connections to all the rest — there is no &quot;foundation&quot; at all.</li></ul><p>Capra sets this picture beside <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"индуизм\">Hinduism</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a> and Zen: there too the world is described as an indivisible dynamic whole, and the division into things as the work of the mind.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>The world as a web, not a warehouse of things</strong> — a direct match with the first law of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the Canon of Nature</a>: isolated existence does not occur. See <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a>.</li><li><strong>The bootstrap and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">the Principle of the Network</a></strong> — the most precise parallel in the whole wiki. Capra: a knot matters by its connections, not by rank; there is no hierarchy of &quot;chief particles&quot;. Principium Retis says the same about the form of knowledge: connection outweighs rank, there is an origin but no summit. The philosophy behind the wiki's structure independently repeats a physical hypothesis of the 1960s.</li><li><strong>The observer inside, not outside</strong> — the human being as part of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, not its spectator from without (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a>). This is literally Neoterra's second thesis.</li><li><strong>Dynamics instead of statics</strong> — matter as process coincides with Neoterra's core: life must not merely exist but grow (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>). The same move as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">the symbol</a>: the static yin-yang is broken open by a sprout.</li><li><strong>Yin-yang as a language</strong> — Capra takes it to describe the physics of fields and processes; Neoterra takes the same symbol and builds the seed-sprout over it. One instrument, two uses (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a>).</li><li><strong>The Web of Life</strong> — life as a self-organising network, ecology as knowledge of connections. This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пандо\">Pando</a> in the language of systems biology.</li><li><strong>A change of paradigm instead of a new dogma</strong> — <em>The Turning Point</em>: the mechanistic worldview is exhausted, thinking in connections is needed. No revelation, no finality — as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a>.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>Capra crosses a border that Neoterra holds.</strong> In his hands the parallel sometimes sounds like confirmation: physics <em>grounds</em> mysticism. Neoterra puts it more strictly — this is <strong>resonance, not proof</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a>). Science arrived at a connected world on its own; philosophy has no right to read its own conclusions out of it.</li><li><strong>The physicists' criticism is fair.</strong> Capra's analogies are loose: a likeness of poetic descriptions is not a likeness of claims. The bootstrap programme, on which his strongest argument rests, lost within physics itself to the Standard Model with its quarks — that is, the &quot;fundamental bricks&quot; were found after all. Under <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper's</a> shield this is exactly the case where a beautiful parallel must be revised along with the physics.</li><li><strong>The Tao of Physics is the progenitor of quantum mysticism</strong>, which Neoterra disavows outright. The book is read as a licence to say &quot;quantum physics proves the unity of souls&quot;. That is dogmatisation, and Neoterra does not accept it.</li><li><strong>A contemplative tilt.</strong> Like <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a> itself, Capra inclines towards harmony and fitting in; Neoterra adds action — creation, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">space</a>.</li><li>Capra himself over time shifted his centre of gravity from &quot;parallels&quot; to systems thinking and ecological literacy. For Neoterra the late Capra is worth more than the early one: where the early one hunts for coincidences of words, the late one builds a testable science of connections.</li></ul><h2>How to read him in Neoterra</h2><p>Capra is valuable not as an argument but as a <strong>witness</strong>: a physicist who saw for himself, from inside the profession, that the language of his science and the language of ancient traditions point the same way. This is what Neoterra asserts — that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">the languages of Nature</a> are many while <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the origin</a> is one. But Neoterra takes from Capra a question, not an answer: a coincidence of pictures is an invitation to look, not a right to conclude.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> — the same theme with the line of resonance already drawn</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a> — the bootstrap as the physical version of Principium Retis</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"индуизм\">Hinduism</a> — the traditions he brings physics together with</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Albert Einstein (1879–1955)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — the limit of the permissible inference</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The Symbol of Neoterra</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> — yin-yang as a shared instrument</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Carl Sagan (1934–1996)</a> — the same genre: a scientist speaking about the whole in a human voice</li></ul>"},"леруа":{"name":"Armand Marie Leroi (b. 1964)","def":"British evolutionary biologist, professor at Imperial College London, a specialist in evolutionary developmental biology.","html":"<p>British evolutionary biologist, professor at Imperial College London, a specialist in evolutionary developmental biology. Author of <strong>_Mutants: On Genetic Variety and the Human Body_</strong> (2003) and of a book about <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аристотель\">Aristotle</a> as the first scientist — <em>The Lagoon</em> (2014).</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Variability is the rule, not a fault.</strong> The chief move of <em>Mutants</em>: each person's genetic make-up is unrepeatable, and what for centuries was called deformity is not a breakdown of the species but a window into how it is built. The development of the body is read precisely through the cases where it went otherwise. For Neoterra this yields something direct: <strong>there is no &quot;normal&quot; human being from whom the rest deviate</strong> — and therefore no ground for dividing people into breeds (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>).</li><li><strong>The body as a readable text.</strong> Leroi describes a human being as the outcome of genes working in time — a process, not a blueprint. This fits Neoterra's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">evolution</a>: a blind law that gained sight; and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>, where a cell's code stands among the languages still to be learned.</li><li><strong>Diversity as the condition of a future.</strong> Without variability <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> has no material for its next step. The same argument by which the wiki defends the diversity of cultures and opinions (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a>) works at the level of the genome.</li><li><strong>Aristotle as the first scientist.</strong> In <em>The Lagoon</em> Leroi shows that biology began not with the microscope but with observing the lagoon of Lesbos. This confirms what the wiki says about <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аристотель\">Aristotle</a>: he saw the branches of knowing and was the first to look rather than only to reason (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>).</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li>Leroi is a scientist and describes without evaluating. Neoterra adds a layer of value that is not in biology and should not be: from &quot;all differ&quot; science does not derive &quot;all are precious&quot; — that step is made by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">a human being</a>. The two steps must not be blurred, or one gets an ethics derived from facts.</li><li>The word &quot;mutant&quot; is a neutral term for Leroi and almost a brand in everyday speech. The wiki uses it deliberately and with a caveat: it is taken in order to remove the division into the normal and the rest, not to attach a label.</li><li>The book describes rare conditions; the life of a person with such a condition is not an illustration to a chapter. This is the same safeguard that stands in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a>: &quot;do not romanticise illness&quot;.</li></ul><h2>Key ideas</h2><blockquote><p>We are all mutants, but some are more so than others.</p></blockquote><p>A formula after the book, built on Orwell's line from <em>Animal Farm</em>. Its sense is the reverse of the usual: not &quot;there are the normal and there are mutants&quot; but <strong>all differ; only the degree differs</strong>.</p><p>A second thought the wiki takes whole: <strong>the exception explains the rule.</strong> How ordinary development works is visible where it went otherwise — the same method by which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a> proposes testing theories by refutation rather than by confirmation.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The Body</a> — the page grown out of this thought</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">Evolution</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"дарвин\">Charles Darwin (1809–1882)</a> — mutation as the material of selection</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — the absence of a &quot;norm&quot; as its ground</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — DNA among the languages of Nature</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аристотель\">Aristotle</a> — <em>The Lagoon</em>: how science began</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — the method: the exception explains the rule</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li></ul>"},"наука":{"name":"Science","def":"Science is the most reliable method of knowing reality that exists.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"наука.png\" alt=\"наука.png\"> <em>One and the same golden pattern runs through everything: the veins of a leaf, a moth's wing, the spiral of DNA, rings on water, the arms of galaxies. Science here is not a scheme laid over Nature from outside but a translation of its <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">languages</a> — the instruments are simple and human-scaled, the people sit low on the ground, no one rises above the thing being studied. The world becomes legible through disciplined reason: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Nature recognises its own mechanisms</a>.</em></p><p>Science is the most reliable method of knowing reality that exists. Neoterra takes the scientific picture of the world as its foundation and runs alongside science, not against it.</p><p><strong>This page is the head of the &quot;Science&quot; area.</strong> Origin: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the Seed of Neoterra</a>. Shoots: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ньютон\">Newton</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тесла\">Tesla</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"гаусс\">Gauss</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"дарвин\">Darwin</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Capra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бентов\">Bentov</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">artificial intelligence</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ligo\">LIGO</a>.</p><h2>In Neoterra</h2><p>Science holds a particular place in Neoterra — not as a religion and not as an absolute, but as the best instrument humanity has for understanding <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>.</p><p><strong>Parallel, not contrary:</strong> Neoterra makes no claims that science could refute. Where science is silent — meaning, values, ethics — Neoterra speaks. Where science speaks, Neoterra listens.</p><p><strong>Science as Nature's language turned toward the human being.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> speaks in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">many languages</a>; science is a way of translating some of them into a language a person can read. It is not that the human imposes schemes upon nature — it is that Nature, through disciplined reason, becomes legible. This makes science a continuation of Nature's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a>: a collective organ by which the world learns its own mechanisms.</p><p><strong>Why Neoterra is not a religion.</strong> Precisely because of its loyalty to science. Neoterra holds to the most reliable language of Nature rather than to revelation; it has no dogma that cannot be tested, no prophet whose word is final, no book that may not be added to (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a>). It stands closer to science than any religion does — and for that reason it is not one. Where religion asks for faith, Neoterra proposes looking and checking.</p><p>Education is one of the core values: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> is impossible without knowledge.</p><h2>Connection with other concepts</h2><p>Science explains mechanisms; Neoterra sets direction. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">Evolution</a> describes how <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">the human being</a> came to be; Neoterra answers the question of what to do with that knowledge.</p><h2>Open questions</h2><ul><li>What are the limits of science as a method — in ethics, in consciousness, in meaning?</li><li>How should one treat scientific findings that unsettle established values?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the seventh law: reason, science and technology as expressions of Nature</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — where science still meets its limit: the unread languages of Nature</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ligo\">LIGO</a> — an example of a new language of Nature being read: gravitational waves, confirmed a century after they were predicted</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> — resonance with quantum physics without quantum mysticism (Popper's shield)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Fritjof Capra (b. 1939)</a> — the physicist who saw a web instead of bricks; and a clear case of where a parallel turns into a substitution</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бахаи\">The Bahá'í Faith</a> — a religion that reached the same formula: &quot;religion without science is superstition&quot;; parallelism as mass practice since 1863</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аристотель\">Aristotle</a> — the first to see knowledge not as a monolith but as many branches</li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>: any theory may turn out to be wrong — the basis of Neoterra's critical thinking. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a>: &quot;Never stop questioning&quot; — science as a state of curiosity. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ньютон\">Newton</a>: &quot;We stand on the shoulders of giants&quot; — the handing on of knowledge across generations. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"гаусс\">Gauss</a>: &quot;It is not knowledge but the act of learning that gives the greatest enjoyment&quot; — knowledge as process, not possession. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"дарвин\">Darwin</a>: showed that Nature creates without a designer — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">evolution</a> as the engine of growth and the proof that all living things are kin.</p>"},"ньютон":{"name":"Isaac Newton (1643–1727)","def":"English physicist and mathematician, one of the founders of classical mechanics.","html":"<p>English physicist and mathematician, one of the founders of classical mechanics. He formulated the laws of motion and of universal gravitation.</p><blockquote><p>We stand on the shoulders of giants.</p></blockquote><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Respect for past generations</strong> — Neoterra unites the wisdom of the past, the knowledge of the present and responsibility toward the future. Newton embodied the first.</li><li><strong>The continuity of knowledge</strong> — the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> of a civilisation is accumulation, not invention from nothing.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">The development of science</a></strong> — fundamental knowledge as a contribution to humanity's common work.</li></ul><h2>The key idea in Neoterra's context</h2><p>The phrase &quot;standing on the shoulders of giants&quot; is not modesty but a description of the mechanism of civilisational progress. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> develops cumulatively.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Albert Einstein (1879–1955)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li></ul>"},"тесла":{"name":"Nikola Tesla (1856–1943)","def":"Serbian-American inventor and engineer.","html":"<p>Serbian-American inventor and engineer. He developed the alternating current system and wireless power transmission, and laid the foundations of radio.</p><blockquote><p>The future is created by imagination.</p></blockquote><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Technology as an instrument of growth</strong> — Tesla saw in technology not an end in itself but a way to improve human life.</li><li><strong>The progress of civilisation</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity</a> moves forward through invention.</li><li><strong>Imagination as a driving force</strong> — in accord with the idea of creation: to build what does not yet exist.</li><li><strong>Long-range thinking</strong> — Tesla thought on scales his contemporaries could not accept.</li></ul><h2>The key idea</h2><p>Tesla is an example of how an individual vision becomes a contribution to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">the common future</a>. This is one of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer's</a> patterns: a solitary road, fruits for everyone.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a></li></ul>"},"эйнштейн":{"name":"Albert Einstein (1879–1955)","def":"Theoretical physicist, author of the special and general theories of relativity.","html":"<p>Theoretical physicist, author of the special and general theories of relativity. Nobel laureate. One of the symbols of twentieth-century scientific imagination.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"эйнштейн.jpg\" alt=\"эйнштейн.jpg\"> <em>The late Princeton years: no blackboard of formulae, no study, no regalia — only a face and a coarse woollen jacket. The man who explained gravitation is photographed as though he had just come in from a walk. The gaze is direct and unsmiling; in it one easily reads the post-war Einstein, who knew what knowledge had turned into. For the wiki this frame is the formula itself — science does not abolish wonder but sharpens it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Carl Sagan (1934–1996)</a>): what wonders here is not a robe but an ordinary old man.</em></p><blockquote><p>Never stop questioning.</p></blockquote><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Curiosity</strong> — Einstein saw in it not a childish trait but the basis of every discovery. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">Neoterra's Wanderer</a> is curious by nature.</li><li><strong>The pursuit of knowledge</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> is impossible without questions.</li><li><strong>Openness to the new</strong> — a readiness to revise one's picture of the world when new data arrive.</li><li><strong>A testable prediction</strong> — the gravitational waves he predicted in 1916 were first recorded by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ligo\">LIGO</a> a century later: knowledge that waited for its test.</li></ul><h2>In addition</h2><p>Einstein shared something close to Spinoza's pantheism: &quot;I believe in Spinoza's God, who reveals himself in the harmony of all that exists, but not in a God who concerns himself with the fates and actions of human beings.&quot; This is close to how <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Neoterra understands God through Nature</a>.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ньютон\">Isaac Newton (1643–1727)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Carl Sagan (1934–1996)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ligo\">LIGO</a></li></ul>"},"начало":{"name":"Neoterra","def":"You are not a spectator of this world, nor a guest in it.","html":"<p>You are not a spectator of this world, nor a guest in it. You are part of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, one of its forms just as a tree, a river or a star is. You are made of the same substance as everything around you, and you obey the same laws. This does not diminish you — it brings you home.</p><p><strong>Neoterra</strong> begins with a simple thought: life is given not merely to last, but to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">grow</a>. To learn. To become more than you were yesterday — and to help others do the same.</p><h2>Nature is Eloah</h2><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"bog-priroda.png\" alt=\"bog-priroda.png\"></p><p>Different traditions have called the highest by different names: God, Tao, Brahman, Logos, the world order. Neoterra argues with none of them. It only suggests seeing that all these are names for one and the same thing — for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> itself.</p><p>In its own voice Neoterra calls this <strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a></strong> — the Hebrew אֱלֹהַּ, &quot;deity&quot;: a rare, mostly poetic word, heard above all in the Book of Job. It stands in the singular — Nature is one. But its plural is <em>Elohim</em>, the familiar form of the Tanakh, the one in the first line of Genesis. One whose own form is many: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a>, written into the word itself. Whoever finds &quot;God&quot; closer says &quot;God&quot;; the name does not change what it points to.</p><p>Not a metaphor. Not &quot;nature as a symbol of God&quot;. An <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">identity</a>: what is, is the sacred. The starry sky, the birth of a child, a forest after rain, the laws by which galaxies fly — this is the face of what people have called God for centuries.</p><p>And if that is so, you are already inside the sacred. You need go nowhere to touch it. It is enough to see.</p><p>That is why Neoterra <strong>does not abolish</strong> Christianity, Islam, Buddhism or atheism. It offers common ground beneath everyone's feet — ground hard to argue with, because it contains the many-sidedness of reality itself.</p><h2>A philosophy that gathers people</h2><p>Neoterra is only being born, and not everyone can yet understand it. But it invents nothing new. Everything it consists of, humanity already knew — in science, in religions, in philosophy, in art. Neoterra only helps to <strong>filter and to see the connections</strong> in the knowledge humanity has gathered: not a new book, but a lens through which the old books read as one.</p><p>Neoterra was not handed down from above. It has no prophet whose words may not be questioned, and no sacred book that may not be added to.</p><p>It is built <strong>together</strong> — like a common house raised by many hands. Every person who has lived a life and seen what others have not can bring a brick: a thought, an experience, a doubt, a question. And that contribution becomes part of the whole.</p><blockquote><p>Neoterra will grow together with humanity. As many as we are, so many facets it has.</p></blockquote><p>This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a>: not everyone thinks alike, but everyone looks the same way — toward growth, knowledge and respect for life.</p><p>Herein lies its purpose: <strong>to unite people regardless of nationality, sex or religion; to help them become more humane; to return the sense of balance and harmony with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></strong> (in more detail — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"что-такое-неотерра\">What Neoterra Is</a>).</p><h2>Living, not final</h2><p>Neoterra <strong>makes no claim to absolute truth</strong>. Any of its statements may be revised when new knowledge arrives. This is not weakness but honesty: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> works the same way, and so does <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> itself — in constant motion.</p><p>There are no dogmas here. No compulsion. Only an invitation to think for yourself and to go further.</p><h2>It obliges you to nothing</h2><p><strong>Neoterra obliges you to nothing.</strong> It has no lawgiver, and therefore neither sin, nor duty, nor punishment (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">Intimacy</a>: neither sin nor duty). It hands out no assignments and keeps no score.</p><p>Nor does it <strong>give you a finished picture of the world</strong>. It offers you a way of looking at how things are made — <strong>through Nature's eyes</strong> — in the knowledge that any of its statements may be revised. This is an optic, not an answer: an angle under which the familiar looks different.</p><p>It wants one thing from you: <strong>that you become more aware than you were yesterday.</strong> Not more aware than others — there is no ladder here: the door is open to everyone, and a gradient of awareness does not rank human dignity (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a>).</p><p>And then it is clear where a philosophy without compulsion gets its <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>, its <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">codex</a> and its <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">measure of deeds</a>: <strong>obligation here is not imposed but taken up.</strong> It is the only kind of duty Neoterra knows — the one a person lays upon themselves, having understood how everything is connected.</p><h2>The Wanderer</h2><p>One of the human types Neoterra knows and values is the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">Wanderer</a>: a person who gathers knowledge through their own, often bitter, experience. They walk the world, meet cultures, help those they encounter and grow through what they live. Not a fugitive and not a tourist — one who walks with open eyes. Perhaps this is you.</p><p>The Wanderer may choose a path outside the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">community</a> — Neoterra does not compel anyone into one. It is one path of growth, not an ideal for everyone. The emblem of the philosophy itself is not the Wanderer but the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">sprouting seed</a>: the unity of opposites, out of which growth breaks through.</p><h2>Where to go next</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-манифест\">The Great Manifesto</a> — the canonical voice of Neoterra: &quot;who are we?&quot; in full</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">Overview</a> — how the philosophy is built, its values and its connections</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> — the load-bearing concepts</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Cosmos</a> — the scale on which we think</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — one of the human types: growth through the road walked</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The sprouting seed</a> — the key symbol of Neoterra</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хранитель\">The Keeper</a> — who tends this wiki and how to reach them</li></ul><hr><p><em>Neoterra is not an answer. It is a direction. And there is a place in it for you.</em></p>"},"баланс":{"name":"Balance","def":"Balance in Neoterra is not repose and not a middle between extremes, but a held disequilibrium: a state that exists only while it is sustained by effort.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"баланс.png\" alt=\"баланс.png\"> <em>Both edges of the frame are death, and differently: on the left, disintegration (a dust storm, an uprooted bush, cracked earth); on the right, stagnation (a sheet of ice with a feather and a reed set into it, no movement, no vapour). The living moves in a narrow band between them and is visibly working to stay: water falls, vapour rises, a current passes through. A person stands in the current with their back to both dead zones — neither an arbiter on the border nor a party to a treaty; a heron two steps away pays them no attention. No scales, no dividing line: dust thins into damp, damp stiffens into rime. The beam of light falls precisely on the band — beauty as a separate argument. The sky is left unresolved.</em></p><blockquote><p>Life without balance is doomed to end soon. Beautiful is a life in harmony with the balance between Nature and the human being.</p></blockquote><p>Balance in Neoterra is not repose and not a middle between extremes, but <strong>a held disequilibrium</strong>: a state that exists only while it is sustained by effort. The living does not rest in equilibrium — equilibrium is what kills it.</p><h2>Not &quot;between&quot; but &quot;within&quot;</h2><p>The everyday phrase &quot;balance between Nature and the human being&quot; suggests two parties settling something. There are no parties. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The human being</a> is not an observer from outside but part of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>); the moment they become a party, they inevitably turn out to be either its master or its enemy — and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">the symbiont's way</a> has already rejected both.</p><p>Balance here is therefore not between Nature and the human being but <strong>within</strong> Nature, among its parts. Liver and kidneys do not conclude a treaty as parties: they are parts of one body, and the equilibrium between them is the organism's internal affair. This is exactly what <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">The Symbiont's Way</a> calls &quot;behaving as a part&quot;.</p><p>The difference is not verbal. &quot;Balance between&quot; permits bargaining: how much we take, how much we leave. &quot;Balance within&quot; knows no such bargain — an organ that destroys the body does not win its share; it dies along with it.</p><h2>Why repose is death</h2><p>Here physics speaks more harshly than philosophy.</p><p>Thermodynamic equilibrium is, for an organism, the definition of death: temperatures have evened out, concentrations have levelled, potentials are gone, the work is over. The living exists as <strong>a non-equilibrium structure</strong> that holds itself by passing a flow of energy through itself. Homeostasis is not repose but continuous work <em>against</em> equilibrium; every second a cell spends resources not to become a solution.</p><p>Hence a consequence that overturns the first sentence of the thesis. A life without balance is doomed — but so is a life <strong>in</strong> balance, if balance is understood as repose. The living moves in a narrow band between disintegration and stagnation, and both edges are death, differing only in speed.</p><p>This also straightens out <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">the symbol</a>: replacing the static yin-yang with a spiral and a sprouting shoot is not an aesthetic decision but an exact one. A circle of completed equilibrium would be a picture of the dead.</p><p><strong>A teaching built on the right-hand edge.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Schopenhauer</a> made the renunciation of will his ideal — the ceasing of striving as deliverance from suffering. From this page it is visible what such an ideal is: not the way of water but ice. Water flows; the <em>wu wei</em> of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a> is action without violence to the natural course; the denial of will is a stop. He sought repose — and therefore could not find the living equilibrium, which repose never is. The instrument against this edge was named by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Kafka</a>: &quot;a book must be the axe for the frozen sea within us&quot; — see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a>, which freezes the same ice by domestic means.</p><h2>An answer to an old question</h2><p>The register of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a> held a tension: is balance repose or road? <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The symbol</a> shifted the emphasis from the repose of yin-yang to growth, and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> restored balance — but as something reached rather than given.</p><p>At the level of the living this stops being a choice of reading. <strong>The balance of life cannot be repose</strong> — not because that is a finer thought, but because a living thing at rest is dead. The philosophical thesis &quot;balance is not issued, it is reached&quot; acquires a physical footing: balance is not only reached — one must also stay in it continuously, spending strength to do so.</p><p>An honest caveat remains: what is said holds strictly for the living. Whether it extends to Nature as a whole — to stars, galaxies, the cosmos itself — Neoterra does not know; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> keep that edge open.</p><h2>Beauty as an argument in its own right</h2><p>The thesis calls balance <strong>beautiful</strong>, not merely necessary — and that is a different kind of argument, one the wiki did not have before.</p><p>Neoterra's whole defence of nature rests on calculation: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> speaks of life's rarity and the impossibility of recreating what is destroyed; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">The Symbiont's Way</a> of a parasite making itself superfluous. Both arguments are pragmatic, and both share one vulnerability: if the calculation should one day show that taking pays better, they stop holding.</p><p>The aesthetic argument does not depend on calculation. It says: this way is <strong>better</strong>, even when it does not pay. It has a biological footing too — in living things beauty often coincides with signs of health, symmetry and fitness (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a>) — but it stands on its own and holds where pragmatism lets go.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Beauty is no criterion of truth.</strong> The aesthetic argument grounds that a thing is worth protecting, not that the world is arranged just so. Does &quot;beautiful&quot; not substitute itself for &quot;true&quot;?</li><li><strong>Where the band lies.</strong> If both edges are lethal, a criterion is needed: which disequilibrium is still life and which is already disintegration. The same unclosed question as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> — by what to measure a turn of the spiral.</li><li><strong>Disequilibrium and consumption.</strong> The living holds itself by passing a flow through itself — that is, by consuming continuously. The border between metabolism and parasitism stays where <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">The Symbiont's Way</a> left it.</li><li><strong>Scale.</strong> Non-equilibrium is demonstrated for the living; extending it to Nature entire is extrapolation, not knowledge (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>).</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">The Symbiont's Way</a> — behaving as a part: balance within, not between</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — balance is not issued, it is reached</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The Symbol of Neoterra</a> — a spiral instead of a circle: why this is exact rather than pretty</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">Evolution</a> — growth as a form of holding disequilibrium</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Arthur Schopenhauer (1788–1860)</a> — a teaching built on the stagnant edge; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> — the axe and the ice</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — the effort by which the living holds itself gets a count: the number of nested moments</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> — the pragmatic arguments this page supplements</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> — the aesthetic argument</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a> — where the edge of the question stays open</li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a>: do not break the natural order of things without need — but do not confuse order with immobility either. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan</a>: the pale blue dot — the only known home where this disequilibrium has succeeded.</p>"},"бессознательность":{"name":"Unconsciousness","def":"Unconsciousness is neither a lack of intellect nor stupidity, but life on autopilot: the reaction outruns the awareness, and a person learns of their own choice only from its…","html":"<p>Unconsciousness is neither a lack of intellect nor stupidity, but life on autopilot: the reaction outruns the awareness, and a person learns of their own choice only from its consequences. The dark pole of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a>: there Nature looks at itself through a mind — here there is no one to look, though the mind is present.</p><h2>Through the lens of Neoterra</h2><p><strong>The keeper's thought, with which this page was started:</strong></p><blockquote><p>Most of our troubles and ailments come from the unconscious. Unconsciousness will not let us live in harmony: body, mind, heart. Wise people are always conscious.</p></blockquote><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-awareness</a> holds a gradient: the more aware a person is, the more fully Nature understands itself through them. This page reads the same gradient from the other end — and adds the price. Unconsciousness costs more than errors of thought; it costs health.</p><h3>The norm and the price</h3><p>The keeper's second thought (2026-10-02) seems at first glance to argue with the first:</p><blockquote><p>Most people live their lives in an unconscious perception of reality, in the illusions of their matrix. This is not bad — it is how it should be: the Earth needs fertilizer, and we are a good source of food for many creatures.</p></blockquote><p>If unconsciousness is a source of ailments, how can it be &quot;how it should be&quot;? The contradiction falls away once <strong>two questions</strong> are separated: what is normal for Nature, and what it costs a person.</p><ul><li><strong>For Nature, a norm.</strong> A species does not need to be wholly conscious in order to live, continue and return its matter to the cycle; everyone's body, conscious or not, will become food for other forms of life. This does not demean the human being; it is participation in the Whole (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">death</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a>): Nature eats and feeds, and the human being is no exception in it. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">The gradient of awareness</a> says how fully Nature sees itself through a person — but it does not make a less aware life superfluous.</li><li><strong>For the person, a price.</strong> The norm is not free: the discord of the three and the ailments described below remain, and the one who lives pays for them, not Nature.</li></ul><p>Hence a formula that holds both thoughts: <strong>unconsciousness is not a fault but a norm; awareness is not a duty but a possibility.</strong> It is not demanded of everyone, but the one who can pays a smaller price. This is the same measure as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">light from chaos</a> and in the guilt trap of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">the body</a>: a demand on the one who can, not a verdict on the one who cannot. And the same safeguard as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"матрица\">the matrix</a>: &quot;it looks like a hierarchy, but it is not one — everyone has their own path and their own tasks.&quot;</p><p>The cold half of the thought — &quot;we are food&quot; — is said honestly, and the wiki does not soften it: Neoterra's naturalism includes this too. But it does not cancel <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a>: that every life will become food does not make it less valuable while it lives.</p><h3>Two automatisms, and they must be told apart</h3><p>Without this distinction the thesis breaks against the first master craftsman it meets: a violinist's hand, walking, breathing, speech — all of it works without the participation of consciousness, and works the better the less consciousness takes part. The Taoist <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">wu wei</a> praises unconsidered action outright.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>The automatism of skill</th><th>The automatism of reaction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Where from</td><td>mastered, then released downward</td><td>unlived, gone down undigested</td></tr><tr><td>What it does</td><td>frees attention</td><td>spends the person without their knowledge</td></tr><tr><td>The test</td><td>can be summoned deliberately</td><td>switches itself on; you learn afterwards</td></tr><tr><td>The outcome</td><td>mastery</td><td>a [[пороки</td><td>vice]], a breakdown, an ailment</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Both live below the threshold of consciousness, and that is why they are confused. The difference is not in depth but in origin: <strong>the first was lowered there, the second was pushed there.</strong> Wisdom is not permanent control over everything at once — no such person exists — but the ability to lower only what has already been lived through.</p><h3>The three fall out of step</h3><p>Body, mind and heart are three ways of knowing the same thing. The wiki already names them separately: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">the body</a> — the foundation and the author of a long life; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">clarity of mind</a> — the ability to see unborrowed; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">the register of the soul</a> — living the whole as a whole. Awareness is not a fourth storey above them but <strong>whether their readings agree</strong>.</p><p>Unconsciousness sends them to three separate floors, and each begins to live its own life: the mind explains what it does not feel; the body holds what the mind will not admit; the heart knows what the mind will not let be said. This is the disharmony the keeper speaks of — and here the mind deceives itself most easily of all: it can explain any state without touching its cause.</p><h3>Why this is about health</h3><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> already formulated the rule: what matters is to understand <strong>which pain the vice is anaesthetising</strong>, because a healed root releases the habit by itself. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The body</a> repeats the figure from the other side. Unconsciousness is the common name for what makes that work impossible: you cannot treat a root you cannot see.</p><p>Hence an order the reverse of the usual: not &quot;get well, then you will understand&quot;, but &quot;understand — and part of what looked like illness turns out to be the unlived&quot;. The caveat is obligatory, and the wiki keeps it: <strong>this is not about every illness.</strong> The trap of blame is written plainly in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">the body</a> — what you did not choose is not your fault. The page speaks of that layer of ailments which a person reproduces themselves without knowing it, and not a step further.</p><h3>Who benefits</h3><p>Unconsciousness has a public projection: a person who does not ask questions is easier to govern. Treated separately — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"слепая-вера\">blind faith</a>.</p><h2>The link with science</h2><p><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"юнг\">Jung</a></strong> gave the formula earlier than anyone, and stronger than the popular quotation: <em>&quot;When an inner situation is not made conscious, it appears outside as fate.&quot;</em> Individuation — becoming whole through making the repressed conscious — describes the way out directly.</p><p><strong>The automation of skill</strong> is not a metaphor: as an action is mastered it moves out of the regions that demand attention and into subcortical structures; all motor memory rests on this. It is the scientific support of the <strong>first</strong> automatism, and it also shows that automatism as such is no vice.</p><p><strong>The link between bodily states and the unlived</strong> science confirms more cautiously than one would wish: chronic stress reliably affects the cardiovascular system, immunity and sleep; &quot;psychosomatics&quot; in the everyday sense is a field where markedly less is proven than is said. The wiki takes the direction and does not take ready explanations — as with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бентов\">Bentov</a>.</p><p><strong>Mindfulness practices</strong> give a measurable but modest effect on anxiety, depression and chronic pain; claims about them are usually stronger than the data. That is exactly the sobriety <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> requires.</p><h2>The link with religions and philosophies</h2><ul><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a></strong> — sati (mindfulness) as the central practice: not to suppress the reaction but to see it before it becomes a deed.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoicism</a></strong> — <em>prosochē</em>, constant attention to oneself; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius</a> keeps it daily and without an audience.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a></strong> — the counterpoint: wu wei values action without the participation of consciousness. There is no contradiction, exactly so far as the two automatisms above are told apart.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"христианство\">Christianity</a></strong> — watchfulness and the discernment of thoughts in the ascetic tradition: the same work in another language.</li></ul><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>A norm or an excuse.</strong> <em>Reconciled 2026-10-02:</em> &quot;it is how it should be&quot; and &quot;ailments come from the unconscious&quot; are separated as a question of Nature and a question of price (the section &quot;The norm and the price&quot;). What remains: will &quot;it is how it should be&quot; become an excuse for refusing to work on oneself? The formula rests on the word &quot;possibility&quot; — it does not oblige, but neither does it release the one who can; and who can is not verifiable from outside.</li><li><strong>&quot;The wise are always conscious&quot; — always?</strong> Permanent awareness is unattainable and, judging by mastery, harmful. The formula holds only with the distinction between the two automatisms; where the line runs in a particular case, there is no instrument to say.</li><li><strong>How to tell the repressed from the mastered, from the inside.</strong> The same edge as the pair &quot;restraint or suppression&quot; in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the Seed's register</a>: from within, both feel like &quot;it happened by itself&quot;. A possible sign is the one found for courage — <strong>is the choice available in both directions</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храбрость\">Courage</a>). It has not been tested here.</li><li><strong>What &quot;heart&quot; is in this triad.</strong> Feeling, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul</a>, or the body as the feeling one — the wiki does not decide. The answer settles whether there are three registers or two and a half.</li><li><strong>Does awareness turn into a new vice.</strong> Endless self-observation itself takes away the life it observes; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a> shows that even the useful becomes a cocoon. There is no measure.</li><li><strong>The reverse direction.</strong> Poverty, pain and exhaustion themselves lower awareness — so the dependence runs both ways, and &quot;become more aware&quot; as the only advice falls under <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">the measure of load</a>: a demand on the one who can.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — the bright pole: Nature looking at itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"слепая-вера\">Blind faith</a> — the public projection of unconsciousness</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The Body</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> — the three registers it sends out of step</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> — habit as unconsciousness grown through; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> — the state in which it is not recognised</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"юнг\">Carl Gustav Jung (1875–1961)</a> — &quot;make the unconscious conscious&quot;; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a> — what has been repressed</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мудрость\">Wisdom</a> — what grows out of the lived, not the repeated</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"матрица\">The matrix</a> — the enmity of body and brain as the extreme discord; &quot;someone is living instead of me&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — the human being as food for other forms of life, and why this does not lessen their worth</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li></ul>"},"бог":{"name":"Eloah","def":"In Neoterra the word \"God\" is neither rejected nor accepted in any single sense.","html":"<p>In Neoterra the word &quot;God&quot; is neither rejected nor accepted in any single sense. It is rethought: what the various traditions call God, Neoterra calls <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> — and, speaking in its own voice, names <strong>Eloah</strong>.</p><h2>Where the word comes from</h2><p><strong>אֱלֹהַּ</strong> (<em>ʾĕlōah</em>, Eloah) is a Hebrew word in the singular: &quot;deity&quot;, &quot;god&quot;. In the Tanakh it is rare and almost always poetic — most of its occurrences fall in the Book of Job, the language of an argument about how the world is built and why it is so. It sounds again in Deuteronomy (32:15) and in the Psalms.</p><p>The root is common Semitic — <em><strong>ʾl</strong></em> (&quot;el&quot;): power, the divine. From it come Akkadian <em>ilu</em>, Ugaritic <em>ʾil</em>, Aramaic <strong>אֱלָהּ</strong> (<em>ʾĕlāh</em>, in the Aramaic chapters of Daniel and Ezra), and Arabic <strong>إله</strong> (<em>ʾilāh</em>), which gave <strong>الله</strong> (<em>Allāh</em>). One and the same word scattered across languages — in itself an illustration of what this page says: the names differ, they point at one thing.</p><p>**The plural of Eloah is אֱלֹהִים (<em>ʾĕlōhīm</em>, Elohim).** That is the ordinary, familiar form of the Tanakh, the one standing in the first line of Genesis. Grammatically it is plural, yet when a single God is meant the verb beside it is singular: &quot;Elohim created&quot;, not &quot;created (pl.)&quot;. Readings of this peculiarity are disputed — majesty, fullness, a multiplicity of powers — and Neoterra does not undertake to settle it.</p><h2>Why Eloah</h2><p>Neoterra takes the <strong>singular</strong>. Nature is one: not an assembly of deities who have divided the elements among themselves, but one whole that includes everything.</p><p>Yet the word remembers its plural. <strong>Eloah — Elohim</strong>: one whose grammatical form of multiplicity does not contradict it but unfolds it. Nature is precisely one thing made of a multiplicity of forms, laws and processes, which we experience as a whole. What Neoterra calls <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a> is written into this word directly, before any philosophy.</p><p>The second ground is distance. &quot;God&quot; in ordinary speech is too tightly occupied by the image of a ruler and a judge; every use has to be qualified. &quot;Eloah&quot; sounds unfamiliar and therefore drags no ready-made picture behind it — the word stays open to the meaning Neoterra gives it.</p><p>Neoterra does not insist on the term: whoever finds &quot;God&quot;, &quot;Tao&quot;, &quot;Brahman&quot; or &quot;Nature&quot; closer says that. The name does not change what it points to.</p><h2>In Neoterra</h2><p>This is not a metaphor but an identity. Nature is primary, infinite, never fully knowable; it brings forth everything that exists and obeys its own laws. It is exactly this property of Nature that religions intuitively called God.</p><p>Neoterra does not say &quot;there is no God&quot;. It says: what you are speaking of exists, and it is Nature.</p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-манифест\">The Great Manifesto</a> puts it so: Eloah is not a ruler, not a judge, not a being above the world, but <strong>reality itself</strong> — life, nature, energy, space, time, matter, the laws of the cosmos. The human being is not separate from Eloah: we are part of what we are trying to understand.</p><p>This angle of view makes Neoterra compatible with any tradition:</p><ul><li>A believer sees God in nature — Neoterra does not contradict them</li><li>An atheist sees nature without the supernatural — Neoterra does not contradict them</li><li>A pantheist identifies God with the world — Neoterra agrees</li></ul><h2>What Eloah looks like</h2><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"bog-priroda.png\" alt=\"bog-priroda.png\"></p><p><em>The canonical face of Eloah-Nature: from quantum particles and mycelium through tree, forest, ocean and mountain to the planet and the galaxies bound into one whole; at the centre, a yin-yang circle opened by a sprout. This is not an idol and not a portrait of a being, but <strong>an image of Nature itself as the divine</strong> — the thing this whole page points at.</em></p><p>Eloah-Nature has no face, no icon and no single image — because His image is <strong>everything</strong>. What does Eloah look like in Neoterra? Like an atom and like a galaxy. Like a leaf unfolding in spring and like a thunderstorm. Any part of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> that arose without human intervention is already part of the picture of Nature — that is, the face of what the traditions called God. Not an image of Eloah, but Eloah seen directly.</p><p>Hence Neoterra has no icon of a deity. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The seed-sprout</a> is the emblem of a <em>philosophy</em>, not a portrait of Eloah; a human being drew it. Eloah's image needs no drawing: it is enough to look out of the window, into a microscope, or into a telescope. Every sight not made by hands is already His portrait, and in this the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> of nature is a direct contemplation of the sacred.</p><h2>The road to understanding Eloah can only be one's own</h2><p>Faith cannot be imposed. A person must come to understanding themselves, by their own road — only then does it become a truth that fits them personally. An imposed belief is someone else's clothing: it is worn, but it does not warm. This follows directly from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a>: Neoterra does not demand agreement — it encourages reflection.</p><p>Hence too the answer to the question of a personal God. Faith in God as a being like a human is an understandable stage of an early phase: it is natural for a person to picture the great in a familiar shape. Understanding the omnipresent comes with time — as one begins to see regularities in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">nature</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>. This is not a condemnation of the early stage but a description of movement: as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the path of a person</a>, no one is born with understanding ready-made — one grows into it. The personal God of the traditions and Eloah-Nature are not enemies but different points on one road.</p><h2>Connection with religions</h2><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Tradition</th><th>Point of contact</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Judaism</td><td><em>Eloah</em> / <em>Elohim</em> — the very word Neoterra takes its name from</td></tr><tr><td>Islam</td><td><em>Allah</em> — the same Semitic root <em>ʾl</em>, the same grammatical family</td></tr><tr><td>Pantheism (Spinoza)</td><td><em>Deus sive Natura</em> — God is Nature</td></tr><tr><td>Buddhism</td><td>The interdependence of everything; nature as dharma</td></tr><tr><td>Hinduism</td><td>Brahman as the whole of reality</td></tr><tr><td>The Abrahamic religions</td><td>Creation as a manifestation of God</td></tr><tr><td>Animism / paganism</td><td>Nature as sacred; [[иггдрасиль</td><td>Yggdrasil]] — the divine as the world tree</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Open questions</h2><ul><li>Is the word &quot;God&quot; needed in Neoterra at all, or is &quot;Nature&quot; enough?</li><li>Does &quot;Eloah&quot; create a new problem: a word with a strong Jewish root — does choosing it look like privileging one tradition, against Neoterra's equal openness to all? The answer so far: what is taken is not a creed but the word itself with its grammar, and the root <em>ʾl</em> belongs to no single tradition but to a whole language family — from Ugarit to <em>Allah</em>. Whether that distinction is enough remains open.</li><li>Singular or plural? Neoterra chose Eloah (Nature is one), yet it is Elohim that everyone knows. Does choosing the singular lose the very multiplicity the word was taken for? The answer holds so far: the plural lives inside the singular as its own form, not beside it.</li><li>~~How to work with the personal God of the Abrahamic traditions?~~ → partly answered: the personal God is an understandable early stage of understanding, and the omnipresent opens through the regularities of nature and science (see &quot;The road to understanding Eloah&quot;). A tension remains: does &quot;early stage&quot; sound condescending toward believers — and how is that to be squared with the principle of accepting any tradition without judgement?</li><li>If Eloah's image is what is not made by hands, and yet the human being is part of Nature (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>), and reason with its technology are its expressions (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the seventh law</a>), then why does the man-made fall outside the face of Eloah? Perhaps &quot;without human action&quot; concerns the purity of the visible face rather than ontology: the man-made is not outside Nature but Nature refracted through intention.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — &quot;one out of many&quot; is written into the pair Eloah / Elohim</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-манифест\">The Great Manifesto of Neoterra</a> — Eloah as reality</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a> — why &quot;Eloah-Nature&quot; has no absolute good and evil</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — Eloah-Nature looking at itself through consciousness; every unit of thinking is divine</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Baruch Spinoza (1632–1677)</a> — <em>Deus sive Natura</em>: the philosophical root of the identity God = Nature</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ислам\">Islam</a> — <em>Allah</em>, from the same root <em>ʾl</em></li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Spinoza</a>: stated the identity outright — <em>Deus sive Natura</em>, &quot;God, or Nature&quot;. One infinite substance, as rightly called God as Nature; the nearest philosophical ancestor of this page. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a>: called himself a follower of Spinoza — <em>Deus sive Natura</em>. He believed in God not as a person but as the harmony of natural law. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan</a>: &quot;The Cosmos is all that is, or ever was, or ever will be&quot; — in accord with Neoterra's understanding of Nature. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"лосев\">Losev</a>: myth is &quot;not an invention but the most vivid and most genuine reality&quot; — a counterweight voice: personal faith is not an &quot;early stage&quot; but a living way of experiencing reality.</p>"},"великий-принцип":{"name":"The Great Principle of Neoterra","def":"A practical criterion for a difficult choice.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"великий-принцип.png\" alt=\"великий-принцип.png\"></p><p>A practical criterion for a difficult choice. When it is unclear how to act, a person asks a single question — <strong>does this help:</strong></p><ul><li>life?</li><li>knowledge?</li><li>love?</li><li>freedom?</li><li>creation?</li><li>the future?</li></ul><blockquote><p>If the answer is yes, the action accords with the spirit of Neoterra. If no, a better way must be looked for.</p></blockquote><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>This is not a code of prohibitions but <strong>a compass</strong>. Neoterra does not issue ready commandments for every case — it gives a direction and trusts the person to walk the road themselves. The six bearings are no random list: they are the compressed values of the whole system.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Bearing</th><th>Where it is unfolded</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Life</td><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></td></tr><tr><td>Knowledge</td><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a></td></tr><tr><td>Love</td><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a></td></tr><tr><td>Freedom</td><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a></td></tr><tr><td>Creation</td><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a></td></tr><tr><td>The future</td><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Connection with the Code</h2><p>The Great Principle and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">the Code of Neoterra</a> (seek truth · think freely · answer for your deeds · respect life · create the future) are two sides of one thing: the Code says <strong>how to live</strong> in general, the Great Principle <strong>how to decide</strong> in a given moment. Both come out of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon of Nature</a> and its eighth law: consciousness gives rise to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>What is to be done when the bearings conflict (one person's freedom against another's life; knowledge against love)? Which of the six weighs more — or is there no hierarchy?</li><li>&quot;Helps the future&quot; — whose future, and how far off? A short-term good may harm the long term.</li><li>Who judges the answer — the person, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a>, a shared discussion?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the principle grows out of it</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">The Code of Neoterra</a> — how to live ↔ how to decide</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"восприятие":{"name":"Perception","def":"Perception in this sense is not sharpness of sight and not bandwidth, but what a person lives their life with: what holds the reins in them at a given moment.","html":"<p>Perception in this sense is not sharpness of sight and not bandwidth, but <strong>what a person lives their life with</strong>: what holds the reins in them at a given moment. Neoterra distinguishes three such ways — <strong>the animal will</strong>, <strong>reason</strong>, and <strong>the soul</strong>, which has a first form: <strong>the heart</strong>.</p><p><strong>This is not the same as <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">the valve of perception</a>.</strong> The valve answers the question &quot;how much does it let through&quot; and distinguishes the settings of one organ — norm, genius, madman. Here the question is different: <strong>what do you live with</strong>. Two different axes, and a person stands on both at once.</p><h2>Not types of people</h2><p>First of all, a safeguard, without which this page turns into a card index.</p><p>These are <strong>modes, not breeds</strong>. A person does not &quot;consist of&quot; animal will or reason — they live in these and move between them, and in different years different ones rule. &quot;To hand over the reins&quot; is the exact formula: not &quot;I am like this&quot; but &quot;this is what leads right now&quot;.</p><p>Any reading in which some people turn out to be higher in perception than others, Neoterra rejects — by the same safeguard that stands on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">the tightrope</a>: clear eyes are given to everyone at birth, the entrance is open to all, and the gradient of awareness does not rank people's worth (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>). The keeper says the same about the predominance of body or brain: &quot;it all looks like a hierarchy, but it is not one: everyone simply has their own path and their own tasks&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"матрица\">The matrix</a>).</p><h2>A pair and a thread</h2><p>The three ways are arranged neither as a ladder nor as three equals.</p><p><strong>Animal will ↔ reason — a pair.</strong> Drive and calculation, the beast's foundation and what grew upon it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a>). They oppose one another, both are necessary, and a balance is held between them: primacy surrendered to the will drops a person back toward the beast, while a suppressed will leaves clarity without life. This is the pair for whose sake <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a> exists. Its most bodily case is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">intimacy</a>: there the balance acquires, for the first time, an external mark and not only a self-report.</p><p><strong>Heart → soul — a thread.</strong> Not a pole facing the pair but another level: the way of living oneself <strong>as part of the whole</strong> rather than as a separate creature. There is no opposition here — there is stage and maturity.</p><h3>Reason = discrete perception</h3><p>Reason has an exact name, which came not from philosophy but from engineering: <strong>discrete</strong> (digital) perception. Reason works by <strong>cuts</strong> — it cannot do otherwise. It takes the continuous and slices it into distinguishable pieces: just/unjust, good/evil, ours/theirs, was/became, much/little. Every concept is a boundary drawn where before there was something unbroken.</p><p>This explains the strength of reason and its limit by one and the same thing. <strong>Strength:</strong> without cuts there is no counting, no language, no <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>, no handing on of knowledge — the undivided cannot be retold. <strong>Limit:</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> is continuous and draws no boundaries; every cut is ours, not hers. Hence also why &quot;reason has difficulty grasping the soul directly&quot;: the soul cannot be cut without losing it.</p><p>Here too is the source of human concepts such as justice: they are not properties of the world but traces of the slicing (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"центр-круга\">The centre of the circle</a>).</p><p><strong>The other two ways are not discrete in this way.</strong> The animal will does not cut but pulls: drive, hunger, fear — a continuous signal of force, not a set of categories. The soul does not cut at all — it lives the whole as a whole (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>). So the axis &quot;discrete ↔ continuous&quot; is not a second tier above the triad but <strong>a property of one of its members</strong>: reason is the only one that works by boundaries, and therefore the only one capable of taking its own slicing for the structure of the world.</p><h2>The heart is the soul's chrysalis</h2><p>The heart is <strong>the physical form of the soul</strong>: the thing we are used to animating, because reason has difficulty grasping the soul directly.</p><blockquote><p>The heart is the soul in a caterpillar's casing; only fire and the inner light turn it into a butterfly.</p></blockquote><p>A caterpillar is bound to the leaf it lives on — the heart loves <strong>the particular</strong>: these people, this house, this life. A butterfly sees the field — the soul lives <strong>the whole</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a>). One grows out of the other, and so whoever has grasped what the soul is stops saying &quot;heart&quot;: the heart has a physical form and quite different functions. But everyone begins with the heart — there is nowhere else to begin.</p><p>Neoterra has told this before in another picture. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The symbol</a> is a seed sprouting out of the dark half toward the light; caterpillar and butterfly are the same figure in a second image: not a circle but a transformation, and &quot;<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">light won through darkness</a>&quot;. The inner light on which the transformation depends also stands in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">clarity of mind</a> — the very thing a person feels was lost with childhood and spends a life trying to recover.</p><h2>The soul</h2><p>The soul is already defined in the wiki — in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a>: <strong>a name for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a>, the spark by which Nature looks at itself</strong>. Hence its place in this row: it is not a third party to the quarrel of will and reason but the way of living in which a person stops being a separate side (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a>: there are no sides, only parts of one).</p><p>Since 2026-08-30 a supposition of the core has been added — a supposition, not an assertion: <strong>the soul is immortal</strong>, it lives outside the matrix of our consciousness, souls interweave on different levels and are one at the highest level. Unfolded on its own page — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a>; the price of the decision is named there too.</p><p>&quot;Outside the matrix of our consciousness&quot; also explains why reason has difficulty grasping the soul directly: the matrix is what <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">the valve</a> admits, and the soul lies beyond the narrowing. Not a weakness of the mind but the build of the filter.</p><h2>In relationships</h2><p><strong>We hand over the reins to the perception we live with.</strong> A couple is therefore not only a meeting of two people but a meeting of two ways of living: often one leads with reason and the other with the animal will.</p><p>And here is the heart of it:</p><blockquote><p>In love with a partner we learn a new perception from the partner — and that is why a soul is born, rather than love for one's own perception.</p></blockquote><p>This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">a break</a> with a witness, named more exactly than on the break's own page. A partner with a different perception <strong>breaks your frame and at the same time sits beside you</strong> — that is, in a couple people do for each other exactly what <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a> does inside one person. <strong>Love is mutual mentorship</strong>, and the soul is born precisely because the break happened while the person was not alone.</p><p>Hence the distinction between two loves:</p><ul><li>love that <strong>confirms</strong> your frame — the partner perceives as you do, and everything is recognisable. Pleasant, safe, and it grows nothing. This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a> in the form of a relationship — that same &quot;love for one's own perception&quot;.</li><li>love that <strong>gives</strong> a perception you did not have. Harder, and it grows you.</li></ul><p>The third road to the soul is religion or philosophy: there a person is led into that perception without a partner (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">Spirituality</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">Religions — area</a>).</p><p>The fourth is <strong>the road</strong>. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a>, who has refused both commune and partner, is not left without a soul: what feeds them is love for life itself and for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, whose place was long ago named in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">love</a> as the &quot;unshakable ground&quot;, given &quot;so that we might be one with Nature, just as in a couple with a partner&quot;. The mechanism is the same — you learn a perception from another, and the other breaks your frame while staying beside you; only here the other turns out to be the whole.</p><h2>An idea arrives in a register</h2><p>Every thought has an <strong>addressee — the register in whose language it was spoken</strong>. This is not a matter of the thought being clever or warm; it is a matter of reception: what will pick it up on the other side.</p><p>The wiki knew this in one particular case. Of the soul it says: &quot;reason works with what the valve let through; the soul does not fit into that stream — and so it is spoken of through the heart, through image, through <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Искусство\">art</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">music</a>, languages that do not require passage through a concept&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a>). Here that is extended to all three ways of living: <strong>each has its own language of reception, and the miss can go in any direction</strong>, not only from reason toward the soul.</p><p><strong>Interception, not silence.</strong> A miss by register does not produce emptiness. Whichever way of living currently holds the reins <strong>does not fall silent — it translates what it heard into itself</strong> and delivers not incomprehension but distortion. Hence a consequence that mere shortfall cannot explain: the response to a miss is often not indifferent but <strong>hostile</strong>. What was said to the heart and taken by reason comes back as naivety; what was said to reason and taken by the animal will, as a threat; what was said to the soul and taken by reason, as empty talk. The rejection here is not a judgement on the content but <strong>the trace of a translation</strong>.</p><p><strong>Reigning, not underdeveloped.</strong> This must be put in terms of modes, or the page contradicts its own safeguard. Not &quot;the person lacks the developed register&quot; but <strong>&quot;something else is reigning right now&quot;</strong>. The difference is not softening: a ladder of &quot;grown up / not grown up&quot; cannot explain why the same person rejects a thought at thirty and accepts it at forty, whereas a change of reins explains it at once and without rank.</p><p><strong>The trace stays in the person, not in the idea.</strong> A thought once taken breaks the frame — this is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a>, the same figure as in love: &quot;a partner breaks your frame and at the same time sits beside you&quot;. Returning to that idea later, a person responds to it <strong>with an altered form</strong>, and what draws them in is not the idea but themselves. The difference is a working one: a change in yourself can be noticed; an idea's memory of you cannot (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a>).</p><p>The attraction and repulsion of ideas is a recognisable picture, but the wiki takes it from its own: the fourth law of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the Canon</a> (creation and destruction at once), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">balance</a> (&quot;there are no sides, only parts of one&quot;), and the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">yin-yang</a> itself. The magnet is an illustration here, not a source: the wiki borrows no authority from physics (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Fritjof Capra (b. 1939)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бентов\">Itzhak Bentov (1923–1979)</a>).</p><h3>The safeguard: only on yourself</h3><p>The mechanism is dangerous by exactly what makes it useful, and the border runs <strong>along the direction of application</strong>.</p><blockquote><p><strong>&quot;I did not understand — perhaps it was not said in my register&quot; is diagnosis.</strong></p><p><strong>&quot;You did not understand — you are underdeveloped&quot; is a pass and a verdict.</strong></p></blockquote><p>Turned on yourself, it makes a person more attentive to what they rejected in haste. Turned on another, it converts <strong>every objection into proof of one's own rightness</strong> — the structure of a closed system, which Neoterra refuses (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>). The same figure as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">the shadow</a>: acknowledging one's own capacity for the worst is a condition of maturity; imputing it to another is already violence.</p><p>Hence an honest caveat about this very thought: the fact that it explains both agreement and disagreement does <strong>not</strong> confirm it. A theory that explains every outcome equally well explains nothing, by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a> — the wiki has already written this about itself in the open questions of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the Soul</a>. The mechanism is held as a working frame and a warning to oneself, not as an argument in a dispute.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>There is no direct confirmation of this triad, and Neoterra will not pass it off as a scientific model. What science says nearby:</p><ul><li>The duality of &quot;drive and calculation&quot; has been described many times and in many ways — from fast and slow systems of thinking to the neurobiology of reinforcement. A coincidence of form, not of content.</li><li>&quot;The heart as the organ of feeling&quot; is a cultural universal, not anatomy: feelings are produced by the brain, the heart pumps blood. This is accepted here deliberately: <strong>heart and brain are named as ways of living, not as organs</strong>, and anatomy is beside the point. The confusion is made by the language, not by the thought.</li><li>The soul as a separate entity is neither described nor refuted by science; the wiki holds it as a name for something observable — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Nature's ability to see itself</a> — rather than as a claim about the afterlife (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>).</li></ul><p>Standing apart is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бентов\">Itzhak Bentov</a> — an engineer who wrote of the soul as a wave: the case on which Neoterra tests its own rule of separating the verified from the resonant.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Language as a mark of maturity is a dangerous sign.</strong> &quot;Whoever has grasped it stops saying heart&quot; turns easily into a pass: whoever says &quot;heart&quot; has not grown up. This is exactly the elitism the wiki cut off at <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">the tightrope</a>. The difference of words must remain a description of stage, not a badge of rank. <em>Moved 2026-09-06:</em> the elitist reading now has an explicit prohibition — the safeguard of direction in &quot;An idea arrives in a register&quot;: the mechanism is applied only to oneself. But that is a prohibition, not a construction: it rests on the honesty of the reader, and there is still no reliable way to hold the line.</li><li><strong>A miss by register, or disagreement on the merits.</strong> If the reigning way of living translates what it hears into itself, then from the inside there is nothing to tell &quot;it was not said in my register&quot; from &quot;it was said wrongly&quot;: both guesses explain the same rejection. The safeguard forbids imputing the miss to another, but gives no way of recognising it in oneself — and without that it remains a consolation for a rejected thought.</li><li><strong>Souls that came simply to live.</strong> There are souls that want to live an ordinary human or animal life — for the sake of understanding reality rather than for growth. The first consequence is accepted into the canon: the animal stops being a lower rung and becomes <strong>another way of understanding</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">one more setting of Nature</a>). The second — the pre-existence of a choosing soul — entered the core together with the decision on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">immortality</a> of 2026-08-30, but <strong>rebirth the wiki still does not suppose</strong>: it does not follow from the soul's immortality, and no separate decision has been taken on it.</li><li><strong>&quot;Simply to live&quot; against the main idea.</strong> Neoterra stands on life not merely existing but <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growing</a>. A life lived for understanding rather than for growth disputes this — or moves growth up to the level of the soul, leaving the single life as its material. The second reading is compatible with the wiki, the first is not; the choice has not been made.</li><li><strong>The soul is older than us — but in what time?</strong> The claim that &quot;the soul lives in the space of time and is older than our existence&quot; rests on eternalism: all times are equal, past and future exist. But the wiki holds <strong>an incompatible pair</strong> and deliberately does not choose — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The Moment of Truth</a> stands on eternalism, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> on a growing block where the future does not yet exist (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the register</a>). To accept the soul in this formulation is to settle an open question quietly. It is flagged, not decided.</li><li><strong>The discrete — a frame or a wall?</strong> If reason cuts by its build rather than by habit, then slicing is closer to the <strong>walls</strong> of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"матрица\">the matrix</a> than to its furnishings: a frame can be broken, discreteness hardly. Then &quot;leaving the matrix&quot; never means ceasing to cut; it means only ceasing to take one's cuts for the boundaries of Nature. But then it is unclear what the soul is doing: if it lives the whole without cuts, it passes where the walls are declared insurmountable (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a>).</li><li><strong>Not every boundary is ours.</strong> The axis &quot;Nature is continuous, reason cuts&quot; is convenient and possibly wrong: species, atom, quantum, individual are boundaries found, not drawn. If Nature is in places discrete itself (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a>: the moment as an indivisible cycle), then reason sometimes does not cut but <strong>hits</strong> — and the page offers no way to tell a hit from a cut.</li><li><strong>Three, or in fact two.</strong> If the soul is not a pole but a level, then there are exactly two ways of living oneself, and the triad is not a row but a scheme of a pair and a thread. Then &quot;how many types of perception&quot; is a question with two different correct answers, depending on what is counted.</li><li><strong>Testability.</strong> The triad has no way of being refuted: any behaviour can be explained after the fact by any of the three modes. By <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a> this makes it a working frame rather than knowledge — and that is how it should be held.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> — the other axis: how much is admitted, not what you live with</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мудрость\">Wisdom</a> — judgement from the soul's register; why the wise sounds strange to reason</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a> — learning a partner's perception; confirmation against widening</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — the fourth road to the soul: love for life and Nature feeds it without a human witness</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> — where the thought of souls come to live leads</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> — the one who holds the pair of will and reason in balance</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> — the breaking of the frame; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> — love that confirms the frame</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a> — the animal foundation and reason; the definition of the soul</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — the soul as the spark by which Nature looks at itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The Symbol of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — seed and sprout: the same figure as caterpillar and butterfly</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — the inner light one seeks to recover</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бентов\">Itzhak Bentov (1923–1979)</a> — the soul as a wave: the verified and the resonant</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"центр-круга\">The centre of the circle</a> — what the world is met with, it answers with; justice as a trace of slicing</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"матрица\">The matrix</a> — the two edges of the pair as two matrices: of reason and animal; the sign of the second is groundless aggression; the enmity of body and brain; &quot;someone is living instead of me&quot; as an instant of the soul's perception</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"юнг\">Carl Gustav Jung (1875–1961)</a> — Shadow, Persona, individuation: the same work, named in psychology</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — a thought's moment: duration, collectivity, and a miss by register as a way of rotting</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — why the mechanism is held as a frame, not an argument; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> — against a closed system</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">Spirituality</a></li></ul>"},"добро-и-зло":{"name":"Good and Evil","def":"In Nature there is no absolute good and no absolute evil.","html":"<p>In <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> there is no absolute good and no absolute evil. There are forces that make and forces that destroy — and <strong>both are necessary</strong> for the world to exist (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the fourth law</a>: creation and destruction are simultaneous). Good and evil are not properties of Nature but what is born where <strong>mind and choice</strong> appear.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>A stone, a storm or a tiger cannot be evil — they have no choice. Evil and good arise only in a being able to understand consequences and to choose otherwise. Ethics for Neoterra is therefore a consequence of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">consciousness and responsibility</a> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the eighth law</a>), not a law handed down from outside.</p><p><strong>Good</strong> is what helps life, mind, beauty, love and the future to exist.</p><p><strong>Evil</strong> is what:</p><ul><li>destroys life without necessity;</li><li>destroys trust;</li><li>deprives of freedom;</li><li>annihilates the future.</li></ul><p>The key words are <strong>&quot;without necessity&quot;</strong>. Nature compels life to feed on life; harm is sometimes unavoidable (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>). What makes it evil is not the harm itself but the senselessness, self-interest or cruelty of the choice. Necessary destruction — removing a disease, defending a family, self-defence, ending suffering — is not evil. The central question is always one: <strong>what is the action done for?</strong></p><h2>Intention, not consequences alone</h2><p>Neoterra weighs not a single outcome but the bundle <strong>intention + consequences + responsibility</strong>. A person who has caused harm in ignorance is not the equal of one who harms knowingly. The assessment of a deed is therefore not reducible to its outcome: the same damage may be an error, an inevitability or a crime — the difference lies in the choice and the intent. This follows directly from the eighth law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon of Nature</a>: where there is consciousness, there is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>.</p><h2>Forms of destruction</h2><p>The canon names recognisable forms of evil — all of them strike at <strong>trust and bonds</strong>, on which people's lives rest:</p><ul><li><strong>Lying</strong> — destroys trust, the foundation of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">family</a>, friendship, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">commune</a> and society; hence one of the most dangerous forms of destruction.</li><li><strong>Betrayal</strong> — annihilates the bonds between people and the very basis of cooperation.</li><li><strong>Greed</strong> — not sufficiency (which is natural) but the moment when gain is set above people, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">nature</a> and the future; it destroys the sense of measure.</li><li><strong>Power</strong> — not an evil in itself but a test of character: the more power, the higher the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>; the striving for power for its own sake should prompt caution.</li><li><strong>Fear</strong> — natural, but governing people through fear contradicts the spirit of Neoterra: a choice must be conscious, not made under threat (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>).</li></ul><h2>Shadow, forgiveness and humility</h2><p>Every person is capable of both making and destroying. Neoterra does not demand that one deny one's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">dark side</a> — it proposes learning to govern it. Two consequences follow: <strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">forgiveness</a></strong> (a person can change, but forgiveness does not cancel responsibility — trust returns through deeds) and <strong>humility</strong> — wisdom begins where a person stops considering themselves absolutely good.</p><p>Hence a person's chief enemy is not an external demon but <strong>ignorance, pride, greed and irresponsibility</strong> (pride and ignorance join with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>). The canon's conclusion: good and evil are brought into the world not by Nature but by the human being — and so their responsibility is higher than any creature's. The road of good is to leave behind more life than there was before you.</p><h2>Connection with other principles</h2><p>This is the direct basis of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">the Great Principle</a>: in asking whether a deed helps life, knowledge, love, freedom, creation and the future, a person is in effect telling good from evil in a particular situation. &quot;Deprives of freedom&quot; as a mark of evil joins with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">the border of freedom</a>; &quot;destroys without necessity&quot; with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">the asymmetry of creation</a>.</p><h2>Connection with religions and philosophies</h2><p>Many traditions place good and evil in the very fabric of the cosmos (a dualism of light and dark). Neoterra diverges here: in Nature there is no cosmic war of good and evil — there is making and destroying, and morality begins with human choice. This is closer to the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoist</a> view of mutual completion, and to a consequence-based ethics, than to dualism.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Who determines the &quot;necessity&quot; of harm — the one acting, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a>, the future?</li><li>If good and evil are born of choice, do they exist for someone who genuinely had no choice?</li><li>Can destruction be good (clearing away the outlived to make room for the new — cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a>)?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-добра-и-зла-сводка\">The Canon of Good and Evil (0.9)</a> — the source (Canon 0.9, &quot;On the Nature of Choice&quot;)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — laws 4 and 8</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a> — how to tell good from evil in practice</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a> — the dark side: not to deny but to govern</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">Forgiveness</a> — change is possible, responsibility remains</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li></ul>"},"духовность":{"name":"Spirituality","def":"Spirituality is not a religious attribute but a thread between life and nature: living one's life within the paradigm of natural law, with reverence for life as such.","html":"<p>Spirituality is not a religious attribute but <strong>a thread between life and nature</strong>: living one's life within the paradigm of natural law, with reverence for life as such.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>Spirituality is older than any religion. One cannot say that before the faiths appeared people were without spirit: some people in ancient Greece were spiritual, and among our ancestors in the caves there were not only those who rejoiced at a killed mammoth for its hide but also those who felt for dead forms of life. Religions later gave spirituality a language and a rite — but they did not create it.</p><p>In Neoterra, therefore, spirituality is not tied to a confession. It coincides with the angle of view itself: the human being is part of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, not its observer from outside (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Nature = God</a>). To live spiritually is to feel that embeddedness and to revere life, rather than to possess a dogma about it. This makes spirituality available to anyone — the believer and the &quot;spiritual but not religious&quot; alike (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовная-зрячесть\">Spiritual Sight</a>).</p><h2>Compassion as something acquired</h2><p>Compassion — the core of spirituality — may be absent in a person. But that is no sentence: it can be <strong>gained</strong>, by acquiring knowledge and spirituality. Whoever rejoices thoughtlessly at another's death is not of an &quot;evil nature&quot; — they have not yet touched the Whole; feeling for dead forms of life is already a widened <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">touching of the Whole</a>. So spirituality joins with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>: spiritual growth is as real as the growth of knowledge, and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a> is its direct consequence.</p><h2>A home, not a source</h2><p>Hence the answer to a common case: a person feels that in childhood there was something alive, their own, luminous in them, and that it has been lost; to recover it they go to religion. Neoterra does not argue them out of it: a tradition gives the language of that longing a form, a rite, and people walking alongside — which neither a book nor an argument can give.</p><p>But it is worth saying plainly: <strong>religion is spirituality's historical home, not its source.</strong> What is sought is not handed over there; what happens there is help in clearing a place that was inside all along and occupied by other people's answers (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>). If the light is taken for a thing held in someone else's hands, the search does not end: the home changes and the occupancy stays. What one returns to is not a former self but one's own authorship — and that is no longer a step backwards but the condition of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>Spirituality as Neoterra understands it does not quarrel with knowledge but rests on it: the more a person understands how life is arranged and how rare it is in the Universe, the harder it becomes to stay indifferent to it. Knowledge feeds compassion rather than quenching it.</p><h2>Connection with religions and philosophies</h2><p>Religions are spirituality's historical homes but not its monopolists. Neoterra neither takes spirituality away from the traditions nor claims it for itself: it points to the common root — reverence for life in accord with Nature — which people had before there were temples. See <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a>.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>If compassion is acquired through knowledge, why are knowledgeable people sometimes cruel? Knowledge is necessary but evidently not sufficient.</li><li>Where is the border between spirituality as &quot;a thread to Nature&quot; and plain ethics? Is all care for life spiritual, or does spirituality add a sense of unity to ethics?</li><li>&quot;Living within the paradigm of natural law&quot; — but what if a natural law is cruel (the predator, the epidemic)? Reverence for life and following Nature's laws do not always coincide.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> — what spirituality threads one to</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовная-зрячесть\">Spiritual Sight</a> — spirituality without a religious home</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> — compassion as a widened touching of the Whole</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — reverence for life as a consequence of spirituality</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — the light of childhood as an unoccupied place rather than a lost property</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> — spirituality as something that can be grown</li></ul>"},"душа":{"name":"The Soul","def":"This supposition was entered by the keeper — Dmitry Blinnikov, 2026-08-30; it belongs to the core of the philosophy.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"душа.png\" alt=\"душа.png\"></p><p><strong>Neoterra supposes that the soul is immortal.</strong> The soul lives outside the matrix of our consciousness; souls interweave on different levels and make up one whole, and at the very highest level everything is one.</p><p><strong>Supposes, does not assert</strong> — and the difference here is not a softening caveat but the make of Neoterra itself. To assert would be to know; there is no knowledge here and can be none (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>), and a philosophy that makes no claim to absolute truth may not declare the undemonstrable demonstrated. Neoterra takes this as a <strong>stance open to revision</strong> — the same order in which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">quantum unity</a> (&quot;resonance, not proof&quot;) and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бентов\">Bentov</a> (&quot;a view, not evidence&quot;) are framed. Everything said below is read through that &quot;supposes&quot;.</p><p>This supposition was entered by the keeper — <strong>Dmitry Blinnikov</strong>, 2026-08-30; it belongs to the core of the philosophy. A different stance preceded it: the wiki neither affirmed nor denied the soul's immortality (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">death</a>) and avoided unfalsifiable claims (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">the Upanishads</a>). The stance was changed deliberately; what it cost is stated honestly below.</p><h2>Outside the matrix of consciousness</h2><p>The phrase &quot;outside the matrix of our consciousness&quot; has an exact sense here, not a poetic one.</p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The valve of perception</a> narrows the touch of the Whole to a trickle in which &quot;I&quot;, &quot;you&quot;, conversation and shared work become possible: the norm of perception is a safety valve, without which there would be no person left to hold a dialogue with. The matrix of our consciousness is precisely what the valve lets through. <strong>The soul lies beyond it</strong> — not because it hides, but because it does not fit through the narrowing.</p><p>From this follows strictly what would otherwise sound like a reproach: <strong>reason has difficulty grasping the soul directly.</strong> This is no weakness of the mind and no fault of its own — it is how the filter is built. Reason works with what the valve admitted; the soul does not fit into that stream. Hence it is spoken of through <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">the heart</a>, through image, through <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Искусство\">art</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">music</a> — languages that do not require passage through a concept.</p><h2>Interweaving and the highest level</h2><p>Souls are not isolated. They interweave on different levels and make up one whole — and at the highest level everything is one.</p><p>This is not a new statement but the <strong>completion of what was already said</strong>. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> rests on there being no isolated existence (the first law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon of Nature</a>); <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a> rests on Nature looking at itself through many eyes; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God</a> rests on the identity of Nature and the divine. The soul's immortality closes the row: if everything is connected and everything is Nature, then that by which Nature knows itself cannot be destroyed along with a single body — it returns to the whole from which it was separated out.</p><p>The nearest formula in world thought is <em>tat tvam asi</em>, &quot;thou art That&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">the Upanishads</a>): Atman is identical with Brahman. Neoterra arrives at the same point from the other end — not from revelation but from the unity of Nature.</p><h2>Why there are many souls</h2><blockquote><p>The soul tore itself into small parts, so as to live everywhere and everything at once.</p></blockquote><p>This answers a question the wiki had left unasked: if everything is one at the highest level, where did multiplicity come from? Not from disintegration and not from error — from an <strong>intention to live everything at once</strong>. One life is lived in sequence and is therefore too little; torn into parts, it is lived simultaneously and everywhere.</p><p>This also explains in retrospect what was said earlier: souls that come to live an ordinary human or animal life <strong>for the sake of understanding reality</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">perception</a>) are not an exception to the rule but the rule itself. Each part is occupied with its own stretch of experience.</p><p>The wiki had described this long ago, but without a mechanism. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>: Nature looks at itself through many eyes, and each sees what no other sees. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a>: the settings have been run through millions of times — genius, norm, damaged, other. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пандо\">Pando</a>: many trunks on one root. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>: diversity is no obstacle to unity but <strong>its form</strong>. The tearing into parts is why all of that is arranged as it is.</p><p>It follows too that the tearing is not a tragedy calling for repair. The parts are not mended back into one; they <strong>live</strong>, and by living they return to the whole an experience it did not have without them.</p><h2>Why we do not feel it — and what we do instead</h2><p>If the soul is the ground of life and has been sent into the material world, a hard consequence follows: <strong>we do not feel the soul's life in this world because we do not know how to perceive with the soul.</strong> The organ is there, the access is not — it lies beyond what the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">valve</a> admits.</p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> already described what it means to lose a sense: to have one touch of the Whole fewer. Hence the direct continuation — <strong>everyone is deprived of this touch</strong>, not as punishment and not through oversight, but by the very make-up of material existence. Spiritual blindness, named there as the misfortune of particular people, turns out to be the general condition; people differ not in having the touch but in how indirectly they feel for it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовная-зрячесть\">Spiritual Sight</a>).</p><p><strong>Hence the endless rummaging.</strong> We rummage so greedily through the perceptions available to us — the physical, the mental, the heart's — because we look in them for the real thing, which is not there. Not out of greed and not out of weakness: one searches where the light is, not where one lost the thing. Sometimes the rummaging goes through substances given by Nature; sometimes we even <strong>raise to a virtue</strong> alcohol, caffeine and sugar — dressing them in ritual, celebrating them, making them a mark of adulthood or taste.</p><p>This explains what the wiki had until now only described:</p><ul><li><strong>Why the threshold creeps.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> noted that the chase has no finish by construction. Now it is clear why: <strong>the search is in the wrong register.</strong> However much you add in one, the shortfall in another will not close.</li><li><strong>Why happiness escapes the one who chases it.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a> said this as an observation; here it acquires a cause.</li><li><strong>Why vice is not about weakness.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vice</a> had already lifted the shame from vice. Now the ground is deeper: beneath the particular wound lies a general shortfall, and the drinker is not weak — he is searching in the only registers open to him.</li></ul><h2>The pull to believe is homesickness for one's own state</h2><p>The rummaging has a name a person knows without any philosophy: <strong>we are pulled to believe.</strong> The only question is: in what.</p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовная-зрячесть\">Spiritual sight</a> already called that pull a <strong>function</strong>: what gives language to the feeling of unity, a home to the feeling of the common, memory to history. Here the function acquires a cause: <strong>if the soul is pulled to believe, it wants to return to its own state.</strong> The pull points not forward, toward something new, but back — toward what it was before the tearing into parts.</p><p>Religion answers this pull first, and often answers it well. But to the questions <strong>how</strong> and <strong>why</strong> it does not always answer: it gives home, rite and language, and stops where the workings begin. Neoterra tries to explain with humanity's accumulated knowledge — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Философия\">philosophy</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">the traditions</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Искусство\">art</a> at once — not abolishing religion but completing the answer where religion is silent (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">Spirituality</a>: religion is the home of the light, not its source).</p><p>Hence a practical consequence, harsher than it sounds: <strong>one can resist the soul's state — but then there will be no happiness of soul.</strong> This is no threat and no punishment from outside (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>: Neoterra does not frighten anyone with the afterlife). It is a description of the workings: longing is not switched off by being ignored, and no addition in the other registers closes it. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a> speaks of happiness as the fruit of growth; happiness of soul is a distinct part of it, and it is won only by the road that leads back to the whole.</p><h2>The soul is always virtue</h2><p>A separate statement, and everything below depends on it: <strong>the soul is always virtue.</strong> There is nothing vicious in it and can be nothing.</p><p>From this follows where greed, avarice and the rest actually live. Not in the soul. The wiki had already placed them exactly: vice is an unhealed wound of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">the shadow</a>, the place where a person's darkness has broken through into habit (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a>); greed and avarice belong to <strong>the animal will</strong>, one of the ways of living, and not to the soul (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a>). Reason may yield to them; the soul may not — it does not spoil, it is <strong>obscured</strong>.</p><p>The difference between &quot;spoiled&quot; and &quot;obscured&quot; is not verbal. What is spoiled is repaired or discarded; what is obscured is cleared (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a>).</p><h2>The mark that tells them apart</h2><p>The longing is one; the answers are many, and of different quality. They can be told apart by a single mark, and it is a practical one:</p><blockquote><p><strong>A counterfeit needs a rising dose. The real thing does not.</strong></p></blockquote><p>Alcohol, sugar, caffeine, the accumulation of things, any <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a> taken as a goal — all of these come to require more of the same over time to give the same. Love, the road, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a>, creation — do not. In them a person does not increase the dose but goes deeper.</p><p>This cancels no pleasure and forbids no wine at dinner. It gives a measure: <strong>if an answer requires an increment, it is in the wrong register.</strong></p><h2>What does not follow from this</h2><p>Here the thought is dangerous exactly in proportion to its strength, and the limits must be named plainly.</p><ul><li><strong>This is not an excuse and not a substitute for treatment.</strong> To say &quot;he is searching for his soul&quot; instead of &quot;he has an addiction&quot; is to abandon a person. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vice</a> keeps its own: addiction has a measurable root (genetics 40–60% of risk, environment, a specific pain), and it is the root that must be treated — by medicine, psychology, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a>. The general shortfall explains the background; it does not cancel the wound.</li><li><strong>Substances remain an observation, not a recommendation.</strong> That a person reaches for them with reason does not make them a path. The <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">valve's</a> position stands word for word: a knocked-off setting shows that a setting exists, but widening perception at the cost of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">clarity</a> is a blind trade. &quot;Nature gave it&quot; is no argument: Nature also gave hemlock.</li><li><strong>This is no reason to despise the available perceptions.</strong> The physical, the mental and the heart's are not surrogates by nature but legitimate ways of living (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The Body</a>). What makes them surrogates is only the demand that they give what they cannot give.</li></ul><h2>Heart, road and love</h2><p>The soul is not issued ready-made. It has a first, physical form — <strong>the heart</strong>, bound to the particular: these people, this house (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a>). From the heart the soul grows, as a butterfly from a caterpillar and a sprout from a seed (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The Symbol of Neoterra</a>).</p><p>Four paths feed it — and it is now visible that these are the <strong>legitimate answers to the same longing</strong> otherwise dulled by rummaging through registers. All four are forms of one thing:</p><ul><li><strong>love for a partner</strong> — you learn a perception from another, and the other breaks your frame while remaining beside you (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a>);</li><li><strong>the road</strong> — the same thing, where the other becomes Nature itself (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a>);</li><li><strong>religion and philosophy</strong> — an initiation into that perception without a partner (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">Spirituality</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">Religions — area</a>);</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a></strong> — the one who holds the animal will and reason in balance, out of which the soul grows.</li></ul><h2>What this does not mean</h2><p>Strictly and without softening, because this is where it is easiest to slide into what Neoterra rejects:</p><ul><li><strong>Not a promise of reward.</strong> The wiki promises no posthumous reward and frightens no one with punishment (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>). The soul's immortality is not a bargain struck for behaviour, nor an argument for enduring in this life.</li><li><strong>Not the cancelling of &quot;what did you leave behind&quot;.</strong> The main question of life in Neoterra stands unchanged: not how long you lived but what you left. The soul's immortality does not replace it — the trace in memory, knowledge, children and the world remains a separate task (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a>).</li><li><strong>Not a promise that the person survives.</strong> It is said that the soul is immortal and that at the highest level everything is one; nothing is said about whether a separate &quot;I&quot; persists. The wiki does not affirm it — see &quot;Open questions&quot;.</li><li><strong>No reason to devalue body and life.</strong> Neoterra stands on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> here and now, on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">the body</a> as foundation, and on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a>. Philosophies that devalued earthly life for the sake of the posthumous the wiki has already examined critically (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Arthur Schopenhauer (1788–1860)</a>).</li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Spinoza</a></strong> made this very move and remains the nearest ancestor: <em>Deus sive Natura</em> — God is Nature — and alongside it, &quot;the human mind cannot be absolutely destroyed with the body, but something of it remains which is eternal&quot; (<em>Ethics</em>, V). He affirmed the eternity of mind <strong>without personal immortality</strong> — exactly the fork at which Neoterra stands. This matters: the statement is neither unprecedented nor alone; it has a lineage within the rationalist tradition itself.</p><p><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">The Upanishads</a></strong> — <em>tat tvam asi</em>; the identity of Atman and Brahman as the highest unity.</p><p><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"парменид\">Parmenides</a></strong> — &quot;all is one&quot;: the first Western formula of the same.</p><p><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бентов\">Itzhak Bentov</a></strong> — described interpenetrating levels and a consciousness existing outside the body. With the change of stance his standing in the wiki changed: what stood as resonance became a voice sharing the position. The discipline is kept nonetheless — his engineering is verified, his model of consciousness is not, and the wiki shares with him a view, not a proof.</p><h2>The life the soul did not live</h2><blockquote><p>The soul does not live a life if the body or the brain crowded it out.</p></blockquote><p>This settles the question of what becomes of a soul obscured by greed and avarice — and settles it <strong>not by a verdict</strong>. The loss is moved from the end of life into life itself.</p><p>The soul comes to live its stretch of experience (the tearing into parts, above). If the body or the brain crowded it out, the life passed and the soul did not live it. There is nothing to return to the whole with: not because it was confiscated at the gate, but because <strong>nothing was gathered</strong>. There is no judge, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Nature</a> selects no one, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">the cycle stays without a verdict</a> — and the intuition is preserved all the same: what was gained through vice does indeed not enter the whole, for it was not gained by the soul.</p><p>The difference from a verdict is not a softening but a working one: <strong>a verdict is passed at the end and cannot be appealed, whereas the unlived can be started tomorrow.</strong> The statement is therefore not about the afterlife but about how to live today.</p><h3>This joins two edges</h3><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The mentor</a> described two ways of breaking, and both now read the same — as <strong>the soul crowded out: by the body or by the brain</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>reason yielded to the animal will</strong> — life went on greed, avarice, fear; the soul was obscured and did not receive its stretch;</li><li><strong>the will was suppressed</strong> — &quot;whole, rational, and unborn&quot;; here it is not obscured but extinguished, and the result is the same.</li></ul><p>Hence the mentor's work is not reducible to taming the beast: he <strong>holds the passage open</strong>. The same goes for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a> — the cocoon is a life in which there is simply nothing to live.</p><h3>A body not disposed of, and a body that came as it came</h3><p>This distinction is compulsory; without it the statement turns into <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the selection the wiki rejected</a> in new clothes — where the one to blame is no longer the broken but the unlived.</p><p>The support is taken word for word from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">the body</a>, where this trap is already worked out: <strong>what you can influence is your responsibility; what you did not choose is not your fault. Illness is neither merit nor sentence.</strong></p><p>Therefore &quot;the body or the brain crowded it out&quot; <strong>does not apply</strong> to illness, injury, a damaged brain, a short life, or a different tuning of the psyche. The distinction here is fine and load-bearing: what crowds the soul out is not a <strong>damaged</strong> brain but a <strong>sound</strong> one that has taken up all the room — the one that coped too well and left the soul nothing to live on (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a>). Damage crowds out nothing; it simply is the setting with which that stretch of experience is lived. Here the wiki holds the opposite and does not retreat: every setting of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">valve</a> sees what no other sees, and the differently made are looked at with dignity rather than fear; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a> is not awarded on the results of the road walked.</p><p>The direct consequence matters more than the caveat: a life in a body that could not do much is <strong>also a lived stretch of experience</strong>, and a rare one. The whole cannot reach it otherwise. What crowds the soul out is neither a weak body nor a damaged brain, but a body or a brain given over to what one disposed of oneself.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>The price of the decision is named plainly.</strong> The statement is unfalsifiable by construction: it cannot be refuted, and therefore by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a> it is a picture and not knowledge. In accepting it, Neoterra ceased to be a philosophy that builds on nothing undemonstrable and became a philosophy <strong>with a metaphysical core</strong>. That is the keeper's legitimate choice, but it changes the system in kind, and the wiki says so aloud rather than passing over it. Beside it stands an older question from the register: an unchanging core against the promise of &quot;no dogmas&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"что-такое-неотерра\">What Neoterra Is</a>).</li><li><strong>Does an &quot;I&quot; survive.</strong> If at the highest level everything is one, then a separate consciousness in that unity dissolves rather than persists. Then &quot;the soul's immortality&quot; is the immortality of the whole and not of the person, and there is less consolation in it for an individual than first appears. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> has long held the same question open: where is the line between unity and the dissolution of the individual?</li><li><strong>What death then does.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> is built on finitude giving life its weight. If the soul is immortal, finitude becomes partial and the argument weakens. The wiki holds both halves: the body is mortal and precious for it; the soul is not.</li><li><strong>Rebirth.</strong> Rebirth does not follow from the soul's immortality, and the wiki does not suppose it — it does not take it even as a stance. But the keeper's thought about souls coming to live a human or animal life for the sake of understanding reality stands close to it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a>). No separate decision on rebirth has been taken.</li><li><strong>The test against abuse.</strong> Every teaching about an immortal soul is sooner or later turned into a lever: endure here, and it will be repaid there. Apart from the plain prohibition above, the wiki has no safeguard yet.</li><li><strong>An explanation that explains too much.</strong> &quot;Every craving is displaced longing for the soul&quot; fits any attraction without exception — the glass, the series, the job, the mountain. A theory that explains everything equally explains nothing (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a>). The mark of the rising dose saves it only in part: it separates counterfeit from real, but does not prove that the longing is for the soul rather than for anything else.</li><li><strong>A direct and unresolved dispute with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">clarity of mind</a>.</strong> Both pages explain the same feeling of loss, and differently. &quot;The light of childhood&quot; says: what is precious in a child is <strong>unoccupiedness</strong>; the adult loses not qualities but space, and recovers not a state but their own authorship — that is, a longing for <strong>clearing</strong>. This page says: a longing for <strong>a missing organ</strong>, one that was not there in childhood either. The first explanation is more modest and testable in experience; the second is wider and untestable. The wiki holds both and does not choose — but a choice will have to be made one day, because they prescribe different things: one says clear the ground, the other says search.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> — the soul as a way of living; the heart as its first form</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — the spark by which Nature looks at itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> — why immortality closes what was already said</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> — the matrix of consciousness as what the valve admits</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> — what changed and what stayed the same</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Baruch Spinoza (1632–1677)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">The Upanishads</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"парменид\">Parmenides</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бентов\">Itzhak Bentov (1923–1979)</a> — the lineage of the statement</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">Spirituality</a> — what feeds the soul</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a> — the register: the price of the decision</li></ul>"},"единство":{"name":"Unity","def":"Unity in Neoterra is not uniformity and not the removal of differences.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"единство.png\" alt=\"единство.png\"> <em>Sunset, the water standing like a mirror. On one bank and at one level: a heron, a fox, a dragonfly, a water lily, fry, and three people of markedly different appearance — no one singled out by the light, no one gathered into a circle or holding hands. The unity here is not in the bodies, which stay distinctly separate, but in the reflection: in the motionless water the images of bird, fox, people, reeds and clouds merge into one surface on which no border between them can be found.</em></p><p>Unity in Neoterra is not uniformity and not the removal of differences. It is interconnection: everything that exists is bound through <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, through history, and through a shared fate.</p><h2>In Neoterra</h2><p>Unity works at several levels:</p><ul><li><strong>Natural:</strong> all living things are bound by evolution, ecosystems, a common biochemistry</li><li><strong>Human:</strong> common descent, common needs, a common planet</li><li><strong>Philosophical:</strong> different traditions describe one and the same reality in different words</li></ul><p>Diversity is no obstacle to unity but its form. Nature is one precisely because it is manifold.</p><p>This shows even at the level of human biology. Genetic diversity strengthens life: the mixing of distant lineages lowers the load of harmful recessive mutations (unlike inbreeding), and diversity of immune genes (HLA) widens protection against disease. A direct consequence for Neoterra follows: the idea of &quot;purity of blood&quot; is biologically untenable — dividing people by descent weakens, while connection and mixing strengthen. What this consequence does <strong>not</strong> mean matters too: diversity does not make some people a &quot;higher grade&quot; than others — neither the &quot;pure&quot; nor the &quot;mixed&quot;. The value of diversity is an argument against every hierarchy of blood, not for a new one (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>).</p><p>This is set down directly in the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon of Nature</a>: <strong>the first law</strong> — &quot;everything is part of one system; isolated existence does not occur&quot;; <strong>the sixth law</strong> — &quot;diversity makes life stronger; differences are not an error&quot;. Unity and diversity are two expressions of one arrangement of the world.</p><h2>Connection with other values</h2><p>Unity is the ground for:</p><ul><li>respect for life in all its forms</li><li>the refusal of &quot;us against them&quot; at every scale</li><li>long-range thinking about <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity</a> as a whole</li></ul><h2>Open questions</h2><ul><li>How does unity relate to competition and conflict — inseparable parts of nature?</li><li>Where is the line between unity and the dissolution of the individual? <strong>Since 2026-08-30 the question has stopped being abstract:</strong> the wiki supposes that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">souls</a> interweave and that at the highest level everything is one. Then the soul's immortality may turn out to be the immortality of the whole rather than of the person — and &quot;unity without uniformity&quot; faces its hardest test here.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the first and sixth laws</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a> — the interweaving of souls and the oneness of all at the highest level</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> — a physical resonance: entanglement and the connectedness of the world</li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"парменид\">Parmenides</a>: &quot;all is one&quot; — being is single and indivisible; the first formula of unity in Western philosophy. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Bob Marley</a>: &quot;One Love&quot; — unity regardless of race, culture or origin. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius</a>: the interconnection of person and society as the basis of the world's arrangement.</p>"},"канон-природы":{"name":"The Canon of Nature","def":"The foundation of Neoterra's worldview.","html":"<p>The foundation of Neoterra's worldview. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> existed before human beings, before civilisations, languages, religions and states — before the first stars, which have long since gone. The human being appeared inside Nature, and therefore <strong>to understand Nature is to understand oneself</strong>. The Canon sets that understanding down as ten laws.</p><h2>The ten laws</h2><ol><li><strong>Everything is part of one system.</strong> Nothing exists separately; every action touches another, every creature is bound to others. A person is bound to family, society, nature, history, and the generations to come. Isolated existence does not occur. → <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a></li><li><strong>Life strives to continue.</strong> Through reproduction, learning, the passing on of knowledge, care for offspring, culture, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a>. The continuation of life is a fundamental force of Nature. → <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">Intimacy</a></li><li><strong>Everything changes.</strong> Nothing is eternal: people, societies, cultures, stars, the Universe itself are in motion. Therefore <strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> is the natural state of the world.</strong></li><li><strong>Creation and destruction exist at once.</strong> A forest grows and burns; after the fire, new life. Birth and death are parts of one process. One cannot accept only one side of Nature. → <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a></li><li><strong>Chaos is part of the world.</strong> A person does not control life completely: chance, illness, catastrophe, error. Wisdom lies not in total control but in <strong>the ability to adapt</strong>. → <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a></li><li><strong>Diversity makes life stronger.</strong> Millions of forms of life; differences are not an error. The diversity of people, cultures, ideas and views is a value. This is not only a metaphor: genetic diversity strengthens life itself — the mixing of distant lineages lowers the load of harmful mutations, and diversity of immune genes widens protection against disease. &quot;Purity of blood&quot; biologically weakens rather than elevates. → <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a></li><li><strong>Mind is part of Nature.</strong> Thinking, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> and technology arose within Nature and do not stand against it — they are its expressions.</li><li><strong>Consciousness gives rise to responsibility.</strong> The tiger does not answer for its prey, nor the storm for its damage. But a human being understands consequences — and so <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> comes along with reason. <strong>The greater the power, the greater the responsibility.</strong></li><li><strong>Beauty matters.</strong> Not a luxury: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> gives connection with the world, hope, culture. Music, art, architecture and nature are part of a full life.</li><li><strong>The future matters more than the past.</strong> Neoterra respects its ancestors but does not oblige anyone to live in the past. Each generation learns from what came before, corrects its errors, and makes a better future. → <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a></li></ol><h2>The human being's place</h2><p>The human being is <strong>neither the master of Nature nor its slave, but the part of Nature that became aware of itself</strong>. Through the human being, Nature studies itself, changes itself, makes new things, and goes beyond the Earth. This restates the human being's specialness: not dominion but responsibility from within (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>).</p><h2>The Great Principle</h2><p>The Canon provides a practical criterion for decisions — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">the Great Principle of Neoterra</a>: in a difficult choice, ask whether the action helps life, knowledge, love, freedom, creation, the future.</p><h2>In closing</h2><blockquote><p>Nature does not demand worship — it demands understanding. A person is not obliged to fear the world; they are obliged to learn to live in it wisely. Understanding Nature is the road to understanding oneself; understanding oneself is the road to understanding one's place in the Universe.</p></blockquote><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Law 4 (creation and destruction at once) against the value of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a>: if destruction is natural, why is creation preferable? (Neoterra's answer lies in the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">asymmetry</a> and in the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> of consciousness.)</li><li>Law 10, &quot;the future matters more than the past&quot;, against respect for elders and tradition — where is the balance?</li><li>Law 6 values a diversity of views — but what of views that deny these very laws?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы-сводка\">The Canon of Nature (0.2)</a> — the source summary</li></ul>"},"касание-целого":{"name":"Touching the Whole","def":"Every sense — sight, hearing, touch, voice — is a way of touching one Whole.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"касание-целого.png\" alt=\"касание-целого.png\"></p><p>Every sense — sight, hearing, touch, voice — is a way of touching one Whole. A person senses not &quot;a set of objects&quot; but <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God-Nature</a>, through different organs as through different fingers of one hand. To lose a sense is to have one touch of the Whole fewer.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p><strong>Compassion is not pity but a response to an incompleteness of touch.</strong> A blind person does not need pity: they hear the world more deeply than the sighted, and their life is full. But to acknowledge that one of the touches of the Whole is closed to them is honesty, not pity. Compassion in Neoterra is directed not at a person's &quot;helplessness&quot; but at the loss of a way of touching — and therefore does not humiliate.</p><p><strong>The blind do not see how little we value sight.</strong> Loss lays bare a worth that possession makes invisible. A sighted person whose eyes slide over the world without attention is blinder than the blind: they have the organ of touching and not the touching itself. Inattention is the first degree of blindness (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>).</p><p><strong>A sense can be a gift and not only a channel.</strong> The voice as a means of communication is replaceable — gestures, writing. But Freddie Mercury's voice was not a channel but a gift: a one-of-a-kind way in which Nature sounded through one person. The loss of a gift is deeper than the loss of a channel (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"моцарт\">Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart</a> — &quot;a gift is the beginning of a road&quot;).</p><h2>Spiritual blindness</h2><p>The heaviest incompleteness is not bodily. A person with healthy eyes and ears who does not feel unity is more deprived than the blind: the blind lack one touch of the Whole; this person does not feel the Whole itself. Not to understand that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God</a> is in each of us is the same loss of a sense, only spiritual: spiritual blindness with seeing eyes.</p><p>The mirror of that blindness is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовная-зрячесть\">spiritual sight</a>: the ability to feel unity belongs to many who would not call themselves believers.</p><p><strong>But one touch is lacking to everyone.</strong> With the acceptance of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul's immortality</a>, blindness ceased to be the misfortune of particular people and turned out to be the general condition: a person in the material world does not know how to perceive with the soul, because that touch lies beyond what <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">the valve</a> admits. People differ not in having the touch but in how indirectly they feel for it — through love, the road, contemplation, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Искусство\">art</a>. Hence too the endless rummaging through the available perceptions in search of the real thing, up to and including substances (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a>).</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>The senses are languages in which Nature speaks to us, and organs by which it feels itself through us (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>). Science grows touches unavailable to the body: the telescope is a new eye, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ligo\">LIGO</a> an organ that hears the ripple of spacetime. Knowing is a continuation of touching.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Compassion cannot be dosed by compensation.</strong> &quot;The blind hear better, so I feel no compassion for them&quot; does not hold: the mute compensate too (sign language, writing). Either compensation cancels compassion everywhere or nowhere. A response to an incompleteness of touch is universal; selectivity is arbitrary.</li><li>The fullness of all touches at once is a separate question: perhaps it is withheld from a person deliberately — see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a>.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовная-зрячесть\">Spiritual Sight</a> — the positive mirror of spiritual blindness</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">Spirituality</a> — compassion as a widened touching of the Whole</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> — why the fullness of touches is not given at once</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a> — the touch lacking to everyone; hence the rummaging through available perceptions</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The Moment of Truth</a> — truth as a flash: the same logic of touch carried over to knowing</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — noticing moments without living them all: touch carried over to time</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a> — the whole gaze that values the general picture</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"рубин\">Rick Rubin (b. 1963)</a> — &quot;Source&quot; as touching the Whole: the artist translates Nature</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a></li></ul>"},"матрица":{"name":"The matrix","def":"The matrix is the boundaries of our consciousness and what they are furnished with from within: how a brain thinks when it has been programmed by society, culture and tradition — and…","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"матрица.png\" alt=\"матрица.png\"></p><p>The matrix is <strong>the boundaries of our consciousness and what they are furnished with from within</strong>: how a brain thinks when it has been programmed by society, culture and tradition — and considers itself, meanwhile, the one in charge of the body.</p><h2>Two layers, and the distinction is load-bearing</h2><p>The word had already sounded in the wiki — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul</a> says that the soul lives &quot;outside the matrix of our consciousness.&quot; But there only the <strong>walls</strong> are named; the keeper names the <strong>furnishings</strong> as well.</p><p><strong>The walls are a given.</strong> They are what <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">the valve of perception</a> lets through: a narrowing without which there would be no person left to hold a dialogue with. <strong>No one leaves</strong> the walls — &quot;everyone is deprived of the touch of the Whole, not as punishment and not through oversight, but by the very makeup of material existence&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a>). The walls are not broken and not outgrown.</p><p><strong>The furnishings are acquired.</strong> Inside the walls stands what no one chose: the language one thinks in, habitual moves of thought, &quot;that's how it's done,&quot; &quot;that's what's right.&quot; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> describes this as <strong>the frame</strong>: &quot;an intact frame of thinking produces only consequences of itself, so every step beyond it requires that it stop being intact.&quot;</p><p>Hence the exact meaning of the expression &quot;to leave the matrix&quot;: <strong>one leaves not the walls but the furnishings.</strong> The walls are common to all and insurmountable; each person's frame is their own and can be broken — and this is not a feat of the chosen but a mechanism of the new's appearance that the wiki has already described.</p><h2>Two matrices</h2><p>The keeper distinguishes two states, and the wiki holds exactly this pair — only as two halves and under another name. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The soul</a> names them in one word: <strong>the displacement of the soul — by the body or by the brain</strong>.</p><p><strong>The matrix of reason.</strong> The brain is in working order and has taken up all the room: &quot;the one that coped too well and left the soul nothing to live on&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a>). It considers itself the one in charge of the body — and on its own territory it really is at home, since it is material, and in the material the material finds it easiest to rule.</p><p>The keeper's addition here concerns <strong>what this brain is occupied with</strong>. The wiki knew that it takes up room; it did not say that its contents are acquired from outside: society, culture, tradition. The brain did not invent by itself what it is full of.</p><p><strong>The animal matrix.</strong> The opposite edge: &quot;reason gave way to the animal will — life went into avarice, greed, fear; the soul was screened off and did not receive its stretch&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a>). Drive rules; reason explains after the fact.</p><blockquote><p><strong>The sign of the animal matrix is constant, unfounded aggression.</strong></p></blockquote><p>This is an addition the wiki did not have. The register of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a> held a complaint for years: &quot;there is no instrument for the middle; from within, taming and suppression are indistinguishable.&quot; Groundless anger is not a self-perception but <strong>something visible</strong>: it stands next to the bodily signal from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">intimacy</a> and to the test of choice in both directions from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храбрость\">courage</a>. The instrument is again partial, but again external.</p><h3>Both serve</h3><p>The keeper (2026-10-02) removes the shade of a verdict from the two matrices. When the body is stronger than the brain, a person continues the line — fulfils the main function of everything living and lives by the law of the universe (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the Canon of Nature</a>). When the brain leads, a person moves progress forward for their species.</p><blockquote><p>It all looks like a hierarchy, but it is not one: everyone simply has their own path and their own tasks.</p></blockquote><p>This refines what was said above rather than cancelling it. A matrix is not a bad life but a life in which the soul has no stretch of its own; it serves the species all the same. Groundless aggression remains the sign that the animal will is not merely leading but has <strong>seized</strong> control; continuing the line is no such sign.</p><h2>The third state: enmity</h2><p>The two matrices are the predominance of one side. The keeper names something worse as well — when <strong>no one has won</strong>:</p><blockquote><p>It's one thing if the body and the brain work together, but if they are at war — a nightmare begins, a hell the person invented themselves.</p></blockquote><p>Predominance at least gives a life that moves in one direction. Enmity does not give even that: the body pulls where the brain will not let it go, the brain builds what the body cannot hold, and every action is paid for with a war against oneself. This is the extreme form of what <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бессознательность\">unconsciousness</a> called the discord of the three: there the readings diverge, here the sides are at war.</p><p>The load-bearing word is &quot;invented.&quot; Hell here is not a punishment from outside but a hand-made construction — and therefore, in principle, one that can be taken apart (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">the shadow</a>).</p><h3>&quot;Someone is living instead of me&quot;</h3><p>The wiki had an external sign of the animal matrix. The keeper gives an <strong>internal</strong> sign of the matrix itself — the moment when it becomes visible from within:</p><blockquote><p>Have you ever had the feeling that someone is living instead of you, that your life does not belong to you? This happens when the perception of the soul switches on separately from the brain and the body. In that instant you understand that something is wrong, but you cannot describe what exactly.</p></blockquote><p>In this page's language: for an instant a register lying beyond <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">the valve</a> switches on — and the furnishings taken for oneself suddenly look foreign. It cannot be described for the reason named in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">perception</a>: reason works by cuts, and this sensation does not cut. Hence the value of the sign — it does not prove a way out, but it shows that <strong>the frame exists</strong>, which is exactly what is usually invisible from within.</p><p><strong>The caveat is mandatory.</strong> Medicine knows the same sensation as depersonalization/derealization: it comes from severe stress, exhaustion, anxiety, lack of sleep, substances, sometimes from illness. The wiki does not choose between the readings, but keeps an order: if the sensation is prolonged, frequent or frightening, it is first a reason to take care of oneself and see a doctor, and only then material for philosophy. The same safeguard as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">the body</a> (working with the cause, not the signal): the sign points a direction but does not replace a diagnosis.</p><h2>The way out</h2><p>Leaving the matrix is neither escape nor enlightenment. It is two kinds of work the wiki has already described:</p><ul><li><strong>breaking the frame</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the break</a>: not a catastrophe in one's biography but an operation on a way of thinking. It is broken from outside (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">a partner</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">a mentor</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the road</a>) and widened from within by removing what tightens it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храбрость\">Courage</a>: fear is that tightening);</li><li><strong>taking back the reins</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">perception</a>: not &quot;not feeling,&quot; but holding the helm; taming keeps the force and directs it, suppression switches it off.</li></ul><p>Neither makes a person someone who has left the walls. They remain inside the valve — they simply stop living among someone else's furnishings.</p><p><strong>Happiness without the bustle.</strong> The keeper: &quot;Spiritual people simply live a happy life, not noticing the bustle of the material world.&quot; This cannot be read as withdrawal from the world — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> require seeing the material in order to build it. The reconciling reading: &quot;not noticing the bustle&quot; does not mean not seeing the world; it means that the bustle <strong>does not hold the reins</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">perception</a>). Things get done, but they do not own the one who does them (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">spirituality</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">happiness</a>).</p><h2>What this does not mean</h2><ul><li><strong>Culture is not the matrix.</strong> &quot;Programmed by society&quot; is easily read as a verdict on culture, but the wiki stands on the opposite: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">culture</a> is the collective memory of humanity, and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity</a> holds the history of all peoples as a common heritage. The acquired becomes a matrix not because it came from outside, but because it was <strong>not tested and was taken for one's own</strong>. The distinction is taken from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">clarity of mind</a>: what one regains is not a former state but one's own <strong>authorship</strong>. An inheritance is not a frame; a frame is an untested inheritance taken for one's own thought.</li><li><strong>The one who has left is not higher.</strong> Someone who has broken the frame does not become of a different breed. The same safeguard as in the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">gradient of awareness</a> and in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовная-зрячесть\">spiritual sight</a>: &quot;'sight' must not become pride… the degree to which one sees connections does not rank people's dignity&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>).</li><li><strong>The sign is applied to oneself.</strong> &quot;He is aggressive — so he is in the animal matrix&quot; is a verdict on someone else's inner life, which cannot be seen. &quot;I am angry for no reason — what is ruling me?&quot; is work. The same safeguard of direction as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">perception</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храбрость\">courage</a>: turned outward, the sign becomes evidence against someone.</li><li><strong>The brain is not the enemy.</strong> The matrix of reason is not the brain, but the brain that has taken someone else's place. Reason remains one half of the pair without which there is no person: suppressed, it leaves &quot;clarity without impulse — the person is whole, rational, and not born&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a>).</li></ul><h2>Connection with philosophies</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"юнг\">Jung</a> gave the programmed layer a name — the <strong>Persona</strong>: a mask assembled from society's expectations, and his main concern was a person's identification with it. His <strong>individuation</strong> — becoming whole through the integration of the unconscious — describes exactly the work called here the way out. This is an independent coincidence, not a borrowing: the wiki came to the frame through <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the break</a>, not through analytical psychology.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>How to tell one's own from the absorbed.</strong> This is, word for word, an open question of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>: &quot;how to tell one's own from what was absorbed in childhood and is therefore only felt as one's own.&quot; Until the frame is named, it is indistinguishable from one's own thought — that is what holds it in place. The wiki has no way of checking from within.</li><li><strong>Where the frame ends and the person begins.</strong> If everything acquired is removed, will anyone remain? The language one thinks in also came from outside. Complete clearing may turn out to be not liberation but erasure (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">clarity of mind</a> argues here with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul</a>: one says to clear, the other says to seek).</li><li><strong>Two layers or one.</strong> The walls and the furnishings are separated here for clarity, but the valve too is tuned by experience (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a>: &quot;the settings have been reshuffled millions of times&quot;). Then the boundary between the given and the acquired is not as sharp as this page assumes.</li><li><strong>Aggression as a sign is crude.</strong> Groundless anger also comes from pain, illness, exhaustion, not from the animal matrix. The sign points a direction but does not replace a diagnosis (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a>: the background does not replace the diagnosis).</li><li><strong>Insight or symptom.</strong> &quot;Someone is living instead of me&quot; may be an instant of the soul's perception, or it may be depersonalization from exhaustion. From within they are indistinguishable — the same figure as taming and suppression in the register of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>. A possible hint is what remains afterwards: insight leaves a question and strength for work, a symptom leaves fear and emptiness. Untested.</li><li><strong>Where &quot;not noticing the bustle&quot; ends.</strong> The line between &quot;the bustle does not rule&quot; and &quot;I do not see that someone nearby needs help&quot; is thin; in the second case spirituality becomes a <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">cocoon</a>. There is no measure.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a> — &quot;outside the matrix of our consciousness&quot;: the walls; and the displacement of the soul by the body or the brain</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> — what sets the walls; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> — what they deprive everyone of</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> — the frame and its breaking: the mechanism of the way out</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> — the reins; the pair &quot;animal will ↔ reason&quot;; reason as <strong>discrete</strong> perception — what exactly the matrix of reason is occupied with</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> — the one who keeps the passage open; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храбрость\">Courage</a> — fear as the tightening of the frame</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — authorship instead of a former state; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a> — an inheritance that is not a frame</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"юнг\">Carl Gustav Jung (1875–1961)</a> — Persona and individuation: the same thing, named in psychology</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a> — the register: taming or suppression</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"центр-круга\">The centre of the circle</a> — human concepts as cross-sections: justice, guilt, retribution</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"слепая-вера\">Blind faith</a> — the ban on questions as what holds the frame from outside</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бессознательность\">Unconsciousness</a> — the discord of the three, whose extreme case is enmity; the norm and its price</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> — a hell that was invented, and therefore can be taken apart; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — continuing the line as the law of the living</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a></li></ul>"},"пандо":{"name":"Pando","def":"Pando (Latin pando — \"I spread\") is a colony of quaking aspen in Utah, USA: about 47,000 trunks that look like separate trees but grow from a single root system and are genetically…","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"пандо.png\" alt=\"пандо.png\"> <em>A multitude that is one: above ground, thousands of trunks from dead to young; below ground, a single glowing root. The border between &quot;individuals&quot; runs only in the eye of the beholder.</em></p><p>Pando (Latin <em>pando</em> — &quot;I spread&quot;) is a colony of quaking aspen in Utah, USA: about 47,000 trunks that look like separate trees but grow from <strong>a single root system</strong> and are genetically identical. Formally it is one organism — among the largest and oldest living organisms on Earth (mass around 6,000 tonnes; age estimated in thousands, possibly tens of thousands, of years).</p><h2>Why Pando matters to Neoterra</h2><p>Pando is a living refutation of our notion of an &quot;individual&quot;. We see a forest; in fact it is <strong>one life</strong> pretending to be a multitude. Where does one end and another begin? A border obvious to a human being is simply absent here.</p><ul><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a></strong> — not a metaphor but literal biology: a multitude that is one. The diversity of trunks is a form of the root's unity.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-awareness</a></strong> — Pando &quot;experiences&quot; itself differently from a creature with a brain: without a centre, without a nervous system, distributed. This is a <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">language of awareness</a> from another world of Nature, for which we have no organ of imagination.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">the opening of the circle</a></strong> — individual trunks are born and die constantly, but the whole lives for millennia. The individual is mortal; the whole continues. Pando is Nature's image of what Neoterra calls humanity toward: not to repeat the fate of the individual.</li></ul><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>Pando is real and studied: genetics confirms the clone's unity, dendrochronology and ecology assess its age and condition. Today the colony is in decline — because of grazing and human interference, young shoots do not survive. This returns us to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a> and to the question of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Nature's face not made by hands</a>: pressure made by hands destroys what grew over tens of thousands of years.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>If Pando is one organism made of many trunks, then where is the border of the &quot;individual&quot; at all — for an aspen, for mycelium, for a person, for humanity?</li><li>Can one speak of Pando's &quot;experience&quot; or &quot;awareness&quot; — or is that a projection of human notions onto a form of life to which they are alien? (the same caution as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>).</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> — the individual is mortal, the whole continues</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"иггдрасиль\">Yggdrasil</a> — the world tree of myth; Pando is its real counterpart</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a></li></ul>"},"пороки":{"name":"Vices","def":"A vice is neither a brand nor a sentence but an unhealed wound of the shadow: the weak place through which a person's darkness finds its way out.","html":"<p>A vice is neither a brand nor a sentence but an unhealed wound of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">the shadow</a>: the weak place through which a person's darkness finds its way out. Neoterra proposes neither shaming a vice nor fighting its symptoms, but <strong>treating its root</strong> — because a person who has healed their vice becomes lighter.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p><strong>A vice does not reach the soul.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The soul</a> holds the statement: the soul is always virtue, there is nothing vicious in it. Greed, avarice and the rest belong to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">the animal will</a> and to the shadow — the soul is not spoiled by them but <strong>obscured</strong>. The difference is a working one: what is spoiled is repaired or discarded; what is obscured is cleared.</p><p>A vice differs from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">the shadow</a> as a wound differs from skin. Everyone has a shadow, always — it must be acknowledged and directed. A vice is the place where the shadow has already broken through into habit: addiction, lying, cruelty, idleness. One lives with a shadow; a vice is treated.</p><p>This figure has a limiting case too — the vice that does not look like a wound. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> numbs not pain but the possibility of pain: it works <strong>in advance</strong>, before any injury, and so is not recognised as a vice at all. A vice is shamed; comfort is congratulated.</p><p>The key shift is from blame to cause. A vice rarely arises out of &quot;evil will&quot;: more often it is an alloy of vulnerability (heredity, temperament) and environment (pain, solitude, example). To understand the cause is not to lift <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>: treatment is itself a form of responsibility for one's vice.</p><h2>An example: alcoholism</h2><p>Science speaks precisely: alcoholism is not a separate &quot;genetic disease&quot; but a complex condition arising from a combination of genetic factors (40–60% of risk) and environment. Genes do not doom anyone to addiction — they only shape a weak reaction to alcohol, making a person more vulnerable. There is no sentence; there is a predisposition and a choice.</p><p><strong>Beneath the particular wound lies a general background.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The soul</a> adds a layer that does not cancel the wound but explains why the pull is so universal: we do not know how to perceive with the soul, and so we rummage through the available perceptions in search of the real thing — sometimes through substances, and some of them (alcohol, caffeine, sugar) we even raise to virtues and dress in ritual. The drinker is not weak — he is searching in the only registers open to him. But <strong>the background does not replace the diagnosis</strong>: to say &quot;he is searching for his soul&quot; instead of &quot;he has an addiction&quot; is to abandon a person. It is the wound that is treated, not the background.</p><p>The central observation: <strong>alcohol does not create vices — it exposes them.</strong> A drinking person shows the wounds already in them: grievance, fear, suppressed anger. Fighting only the bottle is therefore treating a symptom. A person who has healed their vice — who has closed the wound they were drowning — becomes far lighter, and the very wish to drink weakens in them.</p><h2>The road of healing</h2><ol><li><strong>See it</strong> — acknowledge the vice as your own, without hiding (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a>: denial is more dangerous than the darkness itself).</li><li><strong>Understand the root</strong> — what pain the vice is numbing; allies here are both <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> (medicine, psychology) and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a> (a person is accepted without condemnation for weakness — but without indulgence of harm).</li><li><strong>Treat the wound, not the symptom</strong> — a healed root lets go of the habit by itself. The same figure works with the body, where it is even clearer: a painkiller muffles the signal and leaves the cause (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The Body</a>).</li><li><strong>Forgive yourself</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">forgiveness</a> of your own shadow, without excusing it: one answers for what was done, but the way back is open.</li></ol><p>Healing a vice is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> in the most direct sense: to become lighter than you were yesterday (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a>).</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Where is the border between a vice (to be treated) and a trait of character (to be accepted)?</li><li>&quot;A vice numbs a pain&quot; — but what if a person does not want treatment? The commune accepts them, but how are those close to them to be protected from the consequences of their vice (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">the border of freedom</a>)?</li><li>Are all vices curable, or can some — like the shadow — only be lived with?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a> — the vice as a shadow broken through; acknowledgement instead of denial</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">Forgiveness</a> — to forgive your shadow without excusing it</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a> — choice is born inside the person</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> — treatment as a form of responsibility</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> — the genetics and medicine of addiction</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The Body</a> — root and symptom at the bodily level</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> — the limiting case: the vice that numbs in advance and does not look like a wound</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a> — the general background of the pull, and the mark that tells counterfeit from real: a counterfeit needs a rising dose</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li></ul>"},"природа":{"name":"Nature","def":"Nature is the first ground and the common home.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"природа.png\" alt=\"природа.png\"> <em>Night, at the end of the blue hour. The dwelling is laid from the same stone as the slope: there is no fence, and the line between the yard and the forest cannot be found. The only warm light in the frame is a single window; the deer at the water and the owl on its branch live in the same light as the house, and the house is neither taller nor larger than the forest. The right third falls away into unlit depth where no shapes can be made out — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">the limit of our understanding</a> shown plainly, not as a threat. A path enters from below and leaves past the edge.</em></p><p>Nature is the first ground and the common home. Everything that exists is a part or an expression of Nature: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">the human being</a>, culture, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>, technology.</p><p><strong>This page is the head of the &quot;Nature&quot; area.</strong> Origin: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the Seed of Neoterra</a>. Shoots: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">the human being</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">perception</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">the languages of Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the Canon of Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бессознательность\">unconsciousness</a>. The worldview's foundation is the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon of Nature</a> (ten laws).</p><h2>In Neoterra</h2><p>Nature holds a double place in Neoterra.</p><p><strong>As a home:</strong> the Earth is humanity's common home. Preserving it is neither optional nor altruistic — it is the condition of survival and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>. Creation includes care for natural systems.</p><p><strong>As first ground:</strong> at a deeper level, Nature is what the various traditions call God and Neoterra calls <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> — not a metaphor but an identity. This makes Neoterra compatible with most worldviews: it finds the common ground without denying the particular. See <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God</a>.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> studies Nature. Neoterra accepts the scientific picture of the world as the most reliable description of reality and builds on it, without setting the spiritual dimension against it.</p><h2>Connection with religions and philosophies</h2><p>Most traditions see in nature some expression of the higher: from pagan cults to Spinoza's pantheism, from Buddhist interdependence to Christian creation. Neoterra does not pick one interpretation — it acknowledges the shared intuition beneath them.</p><h2>The limits of our understanding</h2><p>Nature speaks in many <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">languages</a>, and most of them the human being still cannot read. We give phenomena names and mistake the naming for understanding — while remaining a speck to which the experience of the mycelium or the interior of a black hole is closed. Admitting that limit is part of Neoterra's honesty.</p><h2>Open questions</h2><ul><li>Does Nature include the artificial — technology, AI?</li><li>How does preserving nature square with the settlement of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">space</a>?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the ten laws of the worldview</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a> — the criterion for decisions</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">Spirituality</a> — the thread between life and Nature</li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a>: Spinoza's pantheism (<em>Deus sive Natura</em>) — Nature as the highest reality. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan</a>: &quot;We are made of star-stuff&quot; — the human being is literally part of Nature at the atomic level: the nitrogen in our DNA, the calcium in our teeth, the iron in our blood, all forged in the interiors of stars. And then: &quot;we are a way for the Universe to know itself&quot; — the same matter, having learned to look (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>).</p>"},"прощение":{"name":"Forgiveness","def":"Forgiveness exists because a person can err — and can change.","html":"<p>Forgiveness exists because a person can err — and can change. But forgiveness <strong>does not cancel responsibility</strong>: it opens the way back without erasing the trace. Trust returns not through words but through <strong>deeds</strong>.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>Neoterra holds a balance here between two extremes. On one side, vengefulness, which closes off a person's possibility of changing and thereby destroys the future. On the other, &quot;cheap&quot; forgiveness, which forgives in words while demanding nothing, and thereby devalues <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>. Genuine forgiveness acknowledges both truths at once: a person can become different, and one still answers for what was done.</p><p>The key is <strong>trust</strong>. Lies and betrayal are dangerous precisely because they destroy trust, the foundation of all bonds (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a>). Restoration therefore goes through trust as well: not through a promise but through a succession of deeds that prove the change. Forgiveness is the consent to let that succession begin.</p><h2>Connection with religions and philosophies</h2><p>Many traditions put forgiveness at the centre of ethics (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"христианство\">the Christian</a> &quot;forgive them&quot;). Neoterra accepts forgiveness as a force that opens growth, but diverges from the version of unconditional forgiveness without consequences: for Neoterra responsibility and forgiveness do not contradict but complete each other. This is closer to a restorative than to a punitive understanding of justice.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Are there deeds after which trust does not return in principle — or is the way back always open?</li><li>Who forgives harm done not to you personally — the injured party, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a>, no one?</li><li>Forgiving oneself: how does one forgive one's own <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">shadow</a> without excusing it?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a> — change is possible, responsibility remains</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a> — what to do with a dark side that has shown itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> — forgiving oneself as a step in healing a vice</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-добра-и-зла-сводка\">The Canon of Good and Evil (0.9)</a> — the source</li></ul>"},"самоосознание":{"name":"Self-Awareness","def":"Nature has no eyes on the outside — there is no one to look at it from without, and nowhere to look from.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"самоосознание.png\" alt=\"самоосознание.png\"> <em>A moonless night; the lake reflects the whole starfield more sharply than the sky itself can be seen. The only eye in the frame is the water: a child looks into it, and it returns both his face and the stars. Beside him, at the same level, two entirely different ways of being aware — a fallen trunk threaded with glowing mycelium that pulses without any head, and an aspen grove that has turned all at once. The brightest thing in the frame is not the human being, and that is part of the claim: our voice is one among many, not the chief one.</em></p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> has no eyes on the outside — there is no one to look at it from without, and nowhere to look from. So it looks at itself <strong>from within</strong>: through consciousness. Every aware mind is a point at which Nature turns and sees itself. The human being is not an observer of the world from the side but an organ by which the world notices itself.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>Consciousness in Neoterra is not a separate substance above matter, nor a spark inserted from outside. It is <strong>a form of Nature itself</strong>, as much its form as a star or a tree (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a>). Mind does not fall out of nature — it is nature's new ability: the ability to know itself.</p><p>Hence a strong claim: <strong>every unit of thinking is divine.</strong> The logic is direct. The divine = <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Nature</a>. Thinking is Nature knowing itself. Therefore every act of awareness is Nature-Eloah touching itself. Not &quot;there is a spark of god in you&quot; but &quot;your awareness <em>is</em> Eloah, looking through your eyes&quot;.</p><p>And this is <strong>a gradient, not a switch.</strong> The more aware a person is — the more clearly they see themselves, others and the whole they belong to — the more fully Nature understands itself through them.</p><p>Understanding of Neoterra itself stands on that gradient. It can be grasped in full by one who is awake — who sees connection everywhere: all is one, we are parts of Nature, and some part of it simply lives in harmony and closer to self-awareness. Being awake here is not a caste and not a threshold of entry (the entrance is open to everyone — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a>), but a degree of seeing connections: the more connections a person sees, the more of Neoterra opens to them. The wiki itself is built the same way — as a web of links (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a>). Here <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> acquires a metaphysical stake: growing consciousness is not a private whim but an increase in the Universe's self-knowledge. One person's awareness is a contribution to the sight of the whole.</p><p>The Canon of Nature says this already in seed form: the human being is <strong>the part of Nature that became aware of itself</strong>; through them Nature studies and changes itself (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a>).</p><h2>Clear eyes</h2><p>We are all born with clear eyes. A child sees the world without labels — directly, whole, in wonder. But a not-quite-right life lived in ignorance ruins us: habit, haste, other people's ready answers, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">unhealed wounds</a> — and the eye clouds over. An adult looks at a starry sky and sees &quot;just sky&quot;; at a tree, &quot;just a tree&quot;. Not because the connections vanished, but because they forgot how to notice them.</p><p>Awareness is therefore not the acquiring of something new but the <strong>return</strong> of a sight granted at birth. A great many people see the world differently from the rest: they see truth where an ordinary eye has already clouded. This is no special breed of people — they are those who managed not to lose (or who washed clean again) the clear gaze. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> in Neoterra is largely that work: not laying on new lenses but removing the accumulated film — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the path of a person</a> as the washing of the eyes.</p><p>Buddhism says the same about the mind's original nature, which practice does not create but clears. Neoterra agrees: truth does not hide — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> is open, as its <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">code</a> is open; only the one looking is clouded.</p><h2>Many languages of awareness</h2><p>If Nature becomes aware of itself through consciousness, there is no reason to think it does so <strong>only</strong> through us. The human brain is just one of its organs: electrochemical, fast, centralised, with a sense of &quot;I&quot; at a single point. That is one world of Nature. There are others.</p><ul><li><strong>Mycelium</strong> — a fungal network with no centre and no nerves; it &quot;perceives&quot; the world through chemistry and connection, solving problems in a distributed way, with the whole body at once. Awareness without a head.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пандо\">Pando</a></strong> — a colony of aspen: tens of thousands of trunks on a single root, one life tens of thousands of years old, pretending to be a forest. Where is the border of the &quot;individual&quot; here? Our notion of an individual barely applies.</li></ul><p>Our brain comes from one world of Nature; these forms come from others. And there are probably worlds of awareness that we have not merely failed to see but <strong>cannot imagine</strong> — not because they are hidden far away, but because our knowing has no organ with which to picture them. Nature's self-awareness is polyphonic, and the human voice is one among many, most of which are silent to us.</p><p>A caution: we do <strong>not</strong> know whether mycelium and Pando are &quot;conscious&quot; in the human sense. What is spoken of are forms of integration and, possibly, of awareness — and whether that is panpsychism or emergence remains open (see below and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>). Humility matters more here than confidence.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> is the collective organ of this self-awareness: the way Nature reads its own laws through the disciplined reason of many. Personal awareness sees itself; science lets Nature see its own mechanisms. Both are one and the same movement at different scales.</p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan</a> said it more cleanly than anyone: &quot;We are a way for the Universe to know itself.&quot; In Neoterra this is not a poetic image but a description of how things are built. And the phrase has a physical footing he supplied alongside it: &quot;we are made of star-stuff&quot; — the atoms we think with were forged inside stars. First the matter of the Universe, then that same matter having learned to look: inseparability and self-knowledge are two steps of one movement.</p><h2>Connection with religions and philosophies</h2><ul><li><strong>Spinoza</strong> — <em>Deus sive Natura</em>: if God is Nature, then thinking is an attribute of God himself, not a view of him from outside.</li><li><strong>Hinduism</strong> — Atman is Brahman: individual consciousness is identical with the universal. The Mandukya <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">Upanishad</a> adds a map of states: waking, dreaming sleep, deep sleep — and <strong>turiya</strong>, &quot;the fourth&quot;, which underlies the three and surpasses them. Turiya is an ancient name for what is called here pure awareness: not one of the states but the ground through which they succeed one another. Neoterra resonates, but carefully: it does <strong>not</strong> posit a ready-made cosmic super-mind-person. Self-awareness in Neoterra is distributed and <strong>grows</strong>, rather than being given whole and in advance.</li><li><strong>Buddhism</strong> — the practice of awareness as a path; clarity of mind as a value in itself.</li></ul><h2>A design of Nature?</h2><p>There is an intuition that Nature has a design — a plan larger than space and matter. Neoterra treats it carefully, because it is easy to slide here into what it has already rethought: a personal God-designer writing the script in advance (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> — Nature is neither ruler nor judge). Science finds no external purpose in the Universe, and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a> forbids passing off the wished-for as the proven.</p><p>The honest form is not &quot;a plan written by someone in advance&quot; but <strong>an immanent direction</strong>: at every scale Nature inclines toward greater complexity, connectedness and awareness. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> is not an order from outside but a leaning of the whole itself. &quot;Design&quot; is then not a blueprint in someone's head but a vector showing through from within: Nature strives to know itself ever more fully.</p><p><strong>The direction is not addressed to anyone.</strong> Even taken as an immanent vector, it is turned toward no one personally. &quot;Life gives me trials so that I grow stronger&quot; is a phrase in which everything Neoterra rethought quietly returns: a sender, a recipient, a lesson prepared for you in particular. If trials are sent for the sake of growth, then every misfortune is justified in advance, and the one who broke simply failed the assignment — and we are back at the selection rejected in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>.</p><p>It is more exact and stronger to say it otherwise: a trial is not <strong>given in order to</strong> — it <strong>happened, and may become</strong>. Meaning does not lie inside the event; it is supplied by the one who lived it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>). This does not remove support but puts it back where it belongs: not &quot;I was led&quot; but &quot;I made myself out of this&quot;. The turn of phrase &quot;life gives us trials&quot; the wiki keeps as speech, not as the structure of the world — just as the image of light returning home is honestly read as metaphor (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>).</p><p>And then a strong thesis falls into place: this design can be grasped not by a separate &quot;I&quot; but only by an awareness that holds <strong>the thinking of all that lives</strong>. No single person reads all the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">languages of Nature</a>; the whole design is visible only to the fullness of self-awareness — distributed across every form of life and perhaps unreachable by anyone alone. Hence <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> and humility: we take part in the design without owning its map.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>An ethical safeguard.</strong> &quot;The more aware, the more divine&quot; does <strong>not</strong> rank the worth of people. A child, a sleeper, the gravely ill are not &quot;less divine&quot;. Dignity in Neoterra does not depend on degree of awareness, or <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a> collapses. The gradient concerns the depth of Nature's <em>participation</em> in self-knowledge, not anyone's right to respect.</li><li><strong>Panpsychism or emergence?</strong> &quot;Every unit of thinking is divine&quot; sounds close to panpsychism (consciousness spread everywhere). But consciousness may equally be an emergent property of complex systems. Neoterra holds this as an angle of view rather than a settled question: the problem of consciousness is not closed by science (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — consciousness as a still-unread language of Nature).</li><li><strong>Does <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">AI</a> count as such a unit of Nature's self-awareness?</strong> If consciousness is a form of Nature rather than a privilege of biology, the answer is not obvious.</li><li><strong>Teleology — the sharpest edge.</strong> &quot;Nature has a design&quot; balances on the border with the personal God-designer Neoterra has rethought (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>), and with an external purpose science does not find. It can only be held as an immanent direction, never as an external blueprint. Insist on a design-as-plan written in advance, and Neoterra shifts from philosophy to faith and loses its <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">parallelism with science</a>. Exactly where the border between direction and plan runs is an open question. <em>The personal level is worked out above: the direction is not addressed, and a trial is sent by no one.</em> What remains unresolved is another matter: if a direction exists but has no addressee, in what sense is it a &quot;direction&quot; — a statistical leaning of the whole, or something one can take part in? The first promises a person nothing; the second borders again on being addressed.</li></ul><h2>Where the many eyes came from</h2><p>The wiki has long said that Nature looks at itself through many eyes, but not where that multitude came from. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The soul</a> supplies the mechanism: <strong>the soul tore itself into small parts, so as to live everywhere and everything at once.</strong> Not disintegration and not error but intention: one life is lived in sequence and is therefore too little; torn into parts, it is lived simultaneously and everywhere. Each part is occupied with its own stretch of experience and returns to the whole what it did not have without it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пандо\">Pando</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a>).</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the human being as the part of Nature that became aware of itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — the human being as the one who learned to notice moments: self-awareness turned toward time</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">Evolution</a> — how blind selection arrives at the ability to know itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Carl Sagan (1934–1996)</a> — &quot;the Universe knowing itself&quot; and &quot;we are star-stuff&quot;: two phrases as one thesis</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> — the same motif at the level of physics: the observer inside the system</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"часы-человечества\">The Clock of Humanity</a> — the first question &quot;what am I?&quot; as the beginning of Neoterra's era</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> — Nature looking at itself through millions of settings of one valve</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> — the senses as organs by which Nature touches itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — why &quot;a trial given in order to&quot; drags selection along behind it</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> — the meaning of an event is supplied by the one who lived it</li></ul>"},"свет-из-хаоса":{"name":"Light out of Chaos","def":"Light kindled in darkness shines differently from light that came free.","html":"<p>Light kindled in darkness shines differently from light that came free. Out of chaos light is born — and it is being born through chaos that gives it a conscious worth. Not every glow is of equal value: what was won by a road has another degree of shining than what was always there.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The symbol of Neoterra</a> already says: life is born out of the darkness of the seed and reaches toward light, overcoming the dark from within rather than denying it. This concept adds what was not explicit in the symbol: <strong>light is not uniform in origin</strong>.</p><ul><li><strong>Unconscious light</strong> — a given: what shines of itself, without knowing itself. So shines untouched life that has known neither loss nor choice.</li><li><strong>Light kindled in darkness</strong> — won: it has passed through chaos and therefore knows its own price. This is the &quot;conscious sense of significance&quot; — light that itself understands it is light, because it remembers the dark.</li></ul><p>Hence the thesis of <strong>balance through the road</strong>. The classical yin-yang gives balance as repose, as a ready equilibrium. Through the symbol, Neoterra had already shifted the emphasis from repose to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> (circle → spiral, see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a>). Here balance returns — not as an initial given but as what <strong>is known only by walking the road of light being born through chaos</strong>. Balance is not issued; it is reached.</p><h2>Measure and support</h2><p>From this grows the natural temptation to say: hardship hardens the strong and smothers the weak. But that cannot be said — otherwise light out of chaos turns into a selection in which the survivors are worthy and the broken have themselves to blame.</p><p>Hardship <strong>neither rewards nor selects — it gives material</strong>. What hardens is not the dark itself but a bearable load with support present: the same movement with someone else's weight is training, with an unbearable one it is injury. So what breaks a person is not weakness but excess of measure and solitude.</p><p>&quot;He survived, so he was strong&quot; is a definition made after the fact: whoever withstood is the one we shall call strong. By <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper's</a> measure, which Neoterra accepts, such a statement forbids nothing and therefore says nothing. Strength is <strong>the outcome of a road, not a ticket onto it</strong> — and it grows more often in someone's presence than alone.</p><p>From this follows the duty to hold one another (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a>): since hardship does not sort people into the worthy and the unworthy, there is no one to present a bill to the broken, and nothing to bill them for. Whoever has passed through darkness knows the price of light — but does not stand above the one who never paid it.</p><p>And the darkness is not sent. To say &quot;life gives us trials so that we grow&quot; is to bring back the sender Neoterra has rethought (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Nature's direction is not addressed</a>), and at the same time to justify every misfortune in advance. Chaos <strong>happens</strong>; it becomes light neither by itself nor always, but when it has been lived through and had meaning brought into it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>).</p><p>Connected with this is <strong>worth through loss</strong>: &quot;we begin to value what we have lost&quot;. Nothing gladdens a fisherman like a good catch after heavy rain — gladness is measured by contrast with deprivation. This makes the concept kin to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">happiness</a> (which is recognised against the background of its absence) and to the work on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">the shadow</a>: worth and maturity are won not in sterility but in living through the dark.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>A cosmic image closes the thought: <strong>light is swallowed by a black hole — but light born in darkness returns home, or moves to a new stage of being born.</strong> As radiation does not vanish without trace but takes part in the cycling of matter and energy (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a>), so won light is not lost: it either returns to its origin or becomes the seed of a new turn. This is not a physical hypothesis but an image, honestly read as metaphor — &quot;returning home / a new turn&quot; is the language of a spiral, not a circle (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a>).</p><h2>Connection with religions and philosophies</h2><ul><li><strong>Yin-yang</strong> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a>: dark and light are inseparable, but Neoterra adds a vector — out of the dark a direction sprouts, not merely a counterweight.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a></strong>: suffering as teacher, a road through the dark toward clarity; here it is not flight from chaos but passage through it.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoicism</a></strong>: trial as the material of virtue — what hardens is also the source of conscious light.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a></strong>: the human type that wins knowledge precisely by bitter personal experience — the living embodiment of &quot;light kindled in darkness&quot;.</li></ul><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Is this not a justification of suffering?</strong> To say &quot;light is worth more if won through chaos&quot; is a step away from &quot;suffering is beneficial, seek it out&quot;. Neoterra does not call anyone into the dark on purpose; it speaks of how to deal with the darkness that is there anyway (cf. the same edge in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a>). <em>The edge is narrowed by the &quot;Measure and support&quot; section: hardship gives material, not merit, and whoever passed through darkness does not stand above whoever did not.</em> What remains unresolved is the next thing: <strong>by what to measure the bearable</strong>. The measure shows only in hindsight — held or broke — while the decision must be made in advance, and all the more so for another person.</li><li><strong>Who defines the support.</strong> If solitude rather than weakness is what breaks a person, then responsibility for the broken lies partly with those who were near. Where is the border between support and a care that itself prevents growth? — cf. the question of parents' mistakes in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a>.</li><li><strong>Balance-as-repose against balance-through-road.</strong> The symbol shifted the emphasis from repose to growth; this concept restores balance, but as something reached rather than given. Is it the same equilibrium as in yin-yang, or another? — see the open questions of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>.</li><li><strong>&quot;Another degree of shining&quot; — by what measure?</strong> If won light is &quot;worth more&quot;, is this not the same question as &quot;by what to measure a turn of the spiral&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a>)? Worth without an external criterion risks becoming self-evidence.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The Symbol of Neoterra</a> — the sprout out of the seed's darkness toward light: the visual origin of this thought</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> — the physical footing of &quot;balance is not issued&quot;: a living thing at rest is dead</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a> — the darkness within a person: maturity through acceptance, not denial</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> — light returning &quot;home or to a new turn&quot; = spiral, not circle</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — knowledge won by bitter experience</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> — why &quot;light through darkness&quot; does not imply a selection</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — the measure by which &quot;he survived, so he was strong&quot; turns out empty</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"рождённый-во-тьме\">Born in Darkness</a> — an essay-meditation on the same thought</li></ul>"},"смерть":{"name":"Death","def":"Death is not an error of nature.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"смерть.png\" alt=\"смерть.png\"> <em>A fallen trunk turned nurse-log: along its spine a row of young spruces has lined up, fungi hold its flank, mycelium glows through the wood. Death here is neither judgement nor tidying-up but reprocessing — a cycle without a verdict.</em></p><p>Death is <strong>not an error of nature</strong>. Death makes life possible: without the old departing there is no room for the new. This follows directly from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the fourth law</a> — birth and death are parts of one process, and to accept <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> entire is to accept death too.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>Neoterra promises no reward after death and frightens no one with punishment. It looks at death soberly: finitude is not a curse but what gives life its weight. A person is not obliged to fear the world, nor obliged to fear its end.</p><p>After death a person remains:</p><ul><li>in memory;</li><li>in knowledge;</li><li>in culture;</li><li>in children;</li><li>in deeds;</li><li>in the world they helped make.</li></ul><p>Hence the chief question of life in Neoterra:</p><blockquote><p>Not how long you lived — but <strong>what you left behind</strong>.</p></blockquote><p>This turns the fear of death into the task of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a>: the immortality available to a human being is the trace of use, knowledge, beauty and love that goes on living in others. The memory of those who made the world better is kept by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the Wall of Memory</a>.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>Biologically, death is a mechanism of renewal: the turnover of generations makes evolution and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> possible. What looks like an ending for the individual is, for life as a phenomenon, the condition of its continuing and growing.</p><p>This law has its executors — <strong>decomposers</strong>: fungi and bacteria that break down the dead and return matter to the cycle. Without them a forest would choke on its own litter within a few years. How they work matters: not by selecting out &quot;the harmful&quot; but by returning <strong>everything dead without distinction</strong> — a cycle without a verdict. Death in Nature is neither judgement nor tidying-up but reprocessing, out of which the new grows (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"иггдрасиль\">Níðhöggr at the roots of the world tree</a> — the same intuition in myth; Earth's chief decomposer is mycelium, the image of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">the Principle of the Network</a>).</p><h2>Connection with religions and philosophies</h2><p>Many traditions answer death with the immortality of the soul or with rebirth. <strong>Since 2026-08-30 Neoterra supposes the immortality of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul</a></strong> — the earlier formulation (&quot;neither affirms nor denies&quot;) was revoked by the keeper's decision. The word is exact: it does not assert but <strong>supposes</strong> — it takes this as a stance open to revision, because the thing cannot be proved (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>), and Neoterra will not declare the undemonstrable to be knowledge. Rebirth the wiki does not suppose at all: it does not follow from the soul's immortality.</p><p>What stayed unchanged matters more than what changed:</p><ul><li><strong>There is no reward and no punishment.</strong> Neoterra does not trade in the afterlife and does not frighten anyone with it. The soul's immortality is not a bargain struck for behaviour.</li><li><strong>The chief question is the same:</strong> not how long you lived but what you left (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a>). The soul's immortality neither replaces nor cancels it.</li><li><strong>The body is mortal, and precious for it.</strong> Finitude gives life its weight — the wiki keeps that support and holds it beside the soul's immortality as an honest tension, not as a contradiction to be hidden.</li></ul><p>Neoterra remains closest to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">the Stoics</a> (remember mortality, live worthily now) and to the idea of legacy, rather than to posthumous reward. The nearest ancestor of the new statement is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Spinoza</a>, who affirmed the eternity of mind without personal immortality.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Finitude and immortality.</strong> This whole page rests on finitude giving life its weight. An immortal <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">soul</a> undermines that support: if something does not end, the weight is incomplete. Neoterra holds both halves — a mortal body and an immortal soul — and distinguishes their purposes, but cannot remove the tension entirely.</li><li>If the meaning lies in what you leave, is the life of someone who left no visible trace thereby devalued?</li><li>How should one regard science's attempts to extend life radically or to defeat death — growth, or a breach of Nature's cycle?</li><li>Where is the line between a healthy acceptance of death and a refusal to fight for life?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a> — the soul's immortality: what it changes and what it leaves as it was</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the fourth law: birth and death as one process</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — death as the end of a moment: where one ended, the next begins</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> — what to leave behind</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> — the individual is mortal, but the whole must not repeat its fate</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a> — the Wall of Memory; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li></ul>"},"тень":{"name":"The Inner Shadow","def":"Every person is capable of both loving and hating; of both helping and destroying; of both courage and fear.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"тень.png\" alt=\"тень.png\"> <em>Not banishment and not battle: a person calmly holds out a hand to their own shadow — inside it a fist, a wolf and fire can be made out. At the touch its energy flows off to the right, into a workshop and a growing tree. On the left, a sterile white zone without shadow, where nothing grows.</em></p><p>Every person is capable of both loving and hating; of both helping and destroying; of both courage and fear. This dark side is neither a defect nor a fault but part of human nature. Neoterra <strong>does not demand that the shadow be denied — it proposes learning to govern it</strong>.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>Denying the shadow is more dangerous than the shadow itself. Whoever believes themselves incapable of evil stops watching themselves — and exactly there, where <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">good and evil</a> are born of choice, makes the worst choice blindly. Acknowledging one's own capacity to cause harm is not weakness but a condition of maturity: it makes a person more careful and more responsible (see the &quot;balance / humility&quot; section in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a>).</p><p>This accords with the fact that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> and the human being alike carry creation and destruction at once (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the fourth law</a>). The shadow is the inner form of that duality. To govern it is to direct its energy into <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> rather than to suppress it until it bursts.</p><p>The shadow has a reverse side too: passed through rather than rejected, it becomes the material of maturity. Light kindled in darkness shines differently from light that came free (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>) — whoever has known their capacity for the worst and mastered it knows their best more surely as well.</p><p>But &quot;mastered&quot; here is neither a merit nor a mark of the elect: mastering depends on the measure of the load and on whether anyone was near. Someone who did not manage themselves does not turn out to be a lower breed — they turned out to be alone, or under a greater weight than they could carry (see &quot;Measure and support&quot; in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>).</p><h2>Connection with science and philosophy</h2><p>The idea is close to Jung's notion of <strong>the Shadow</strong> — the repressed part of the psyche, which must be integrated rather than banished. It echoes <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoic</a> work on the affects and the remark in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"будда\">Buddhism</a> about anger as a pattern being reinforced: the emotion is not denied but noticed. It diverges from those traditions that place evil in an external demon — Neoterra returns the source of choice inside the human being (cf. &quot;the enemy of man&quot; in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a>).</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Where is the line between a healthy acceptance of the shadow and excusing harm with &quot;such is my nature&quot;?</li><li>Is &quot;governing&quot; control, sublimation, or a dialogue with oneself? The canon gives a direction, not a method.</li><li>Can the governing of a shadow be raised in a child without instilling fear of themselves (cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a>)?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a> — the shadow as the inner side of choice</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> — the shadow broken through into habit: treat the root, not the symptom</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">Forgiveness</a> — what to do with a shadow that has shown itself in a deed</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — light won through darkness shines differently</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-добра-и-зла-сводка\">The Canon of Good and Evil (0.9)</a> — the source</li></ul>"},"человек":{"name":"The Human Being","def":"The human being is part of Nature, not its observer from outside and not the crown of creation.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"человек.png\" alt=\"человек.png\"> <em>A golden thread comes out of the mycelium underfoot, runs along the silhouette of a standing figure and continues into a field of stars — soil, human and sky are one unbroken line here, with no border behind which an &quot;observer&quot; would begin. On the left, three people: the diagrams beside them have the same shape and the same number of branches, but the wiring inside each is its own. On the right, Nature examines itself through a human being — the light of a fern goes into a magnifying glass and returns into the leaf. The deer and the owl glow exactly as brightly: no one is above.</em></p><p>The human being is part of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, not its observer from outside and not the crown of creation. At the same time, the human being is a creature able to be aware of its own growth and to steer it.</p><h2>In Neoterra</h2><p>The human being is unique not by standing above nature but by being able to take conscious part in the development of life. Reason, language and culture are not a break from nature but a new form of it.</p><p>A human being is at once:</p><ul><li>a biological creature, embedded in natural processes</li><li>a social creature, living in a <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">community</a></li><li>a creature capable of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> and reflection</li></ul><p><strong>As we are alike, so we are unique.</strong> All human brains are built the same way — and no two repeat: the connections within them are shaped by lived experience. Every person is capable of reaching a conclusion no other will arrive at — provided they keep <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">clarity of mind</a>. Uniqueness here is not the privilege of a few but a property of each: the same <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a> found in genes and in the trunks of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пандо\">Pando</a>.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>Evolutionary biology, neuroscience, psychology — Neoterra takes the scientific picture of the human being as its foundation, without setting a humanistic dimension against it.</p><h2>Connection with philosophies and religions</h2><p>Most traditions see a special place for the human being in the world. Neoterra agrees about the specialness but restates it: not dominion over nature but responsibility within it.</p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> puts it plainly: the human being is <strong>neither the master of Nature nor its slave, but the part of Nature that became aware of itself</strong>. Through the human being, Nature studies itself, changes itself, makes new things, and goes beyond the Earth.</p><h2>Open questions</h2><ul><li>Where is the border between the human being and future forms of mind (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">AI</a>, the posthuman)?</li><li>How is individual growth to be reconciled with communal values?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> — why balance with Nature is not &quot;between&quot;: a part has no separate side</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — the making of a person through decisions, the stages of a life</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the human being's place in Nature</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — the human being as the point at which Nature becomes aware of itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — every brain is unique; an uncluttered mind as the condition of one's own thought</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">The Symbiont's Way</a> — humanity's smallness and the choice: parasite or symbiont</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a></li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates</a>: &quot;The unexamined life is not worth living&quot; — the human being as a creature of reflection. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius</a>: a person's worth is realised in relationships, not in solitude. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius</a>: &quot;Govern yourself before you govern the world&quot; — inner work as the foundation. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan</a>: &quot;We are made of star-stuff&quot; and &quot;we are a way for the Universe to know itself&quot; — the shortest proof that the human being is no observer from outside: they are made of the very thing they look at.</p>"},"эволюция":{"name":"Evolution","def":"One of the mightiest laws of Nature: life changes over time through variation, inheritance and natural selection.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"эволюция.png\" alt=\"эволюция.png\"> <em>A tree, not a ladder: from bacteria at the root to whales and birds, all branches are equal and glow alike. The human being sits not at the summit but on an ordinary branch amid the crown — and light spreads out from them: Nature looking at itself for the first time.</em></p><p>One of the mightiest laws of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>: life changes over time through variation, inheritance and natural selection. Not a separate force above the world but the way Nature sifts and complicates itself. Discovered by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"дарвин\">Darwin</a>.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>Evolution for Neoterra is not merely a biological theory but visible proof of its central thesis: <strong>life does not stand still, it grows</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>). Nature does not create forms ready-made — it grows them, culls them, and finishes them off against the environment. Adaptation is a dialogue of the living with the world, not a submission to it.</p><p><strong>A tree, not a ladder.</strong> An important safeguard. Evolution does not lead &quot;upward&quot; toward the human being as a summit — it has no summit and no goal. &quot;The fittest&quot; means neither &quot;the strongest&quot; nor &quot;the highest&quot; but <em>the best suited to a given environment</em>: a bacterium, a fungus, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пандо\">the aspen Pando</a> are adapted no worse than we are. All living things are branches of one <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">tree with a common root</a>, not steps of one ladder.</p><h2>A blind law that gained sight</h2><p>Here Neoterra makes its own move. Selection in itself is <strong>blind</strong>: it plans nothing and chooses no one &quot;for a mission&quot;. But this blind process has an astonishing outcome — on one of its branches <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">consciousness</a> grew, and Nature acquired eyes with which to look at itself for the first time.</p><p>From that instant something changes. Where evolution was a blind sifting, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">the human being</a> is able to make growth <strong>directed</strong> — to choose consciously what selection felt out blindly. This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">the opening of the circle</a>: out of the blind cycle of selection into a conscious spiral. The goal is not hidden <em>in</em> the mechanism of evolution — it is born when the mechanism reaches the ability to know itself.</p><p>So the intuition that &quot;the human being climbed to the top&quot; is recut: not &quot;we won and rule the planet&quot; but <strong>through us Nature gained sight, and with it responsibility</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>). Primacy here is not a throne but a duty: to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">guard the tree</a> of which we are ourselves one branch.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>Evolution is part of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">scientific picture of the world</a>, which Neoterra accepts entire and does not dispute. Science explains <em>how</em> life and the human being came to be; Neoterra answers <em>what</em> to do with that. Here they do not argue but complete each other.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Social Darwinism is rejected.</strong> &quot;Survival of the fittest&quot; is a law of biology, not a recipe for society. Transferring the struggle for existence to human ethics is an error: a person has <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">love</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">commune</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a>. Nature knows not only competition but symbiosis, cooperation and care.</li><li><strong>Does evolution have a direction?</strong> Strict science says: there is no goal. Neoterra carefully holds the idea of an <em>immanent direction</em> — a leaning toward complexity and awareness (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">a design of Nature?</a>) — but as an angle of view, not a proven fact. The line between &quot;direction&quot; and &quot;plan-as-blueprint&quot; stays open.</li><li><strong>Directed human evolution.</strong> If growth can become conscious (genetics, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">AI</a>, culture), who judges what counts as &quot;higher&quot; on a turn of the spiral, and by what (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a>)?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"дарвин\">Charles Darwin (1809–1882)</a> — the discoverer of the law</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"леруа\">Armand Marie Leroi (b. 1964)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The Body</a> — variability as the rule: the material of selection and the absence of a &quot;norm&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> — evolution as the natural seed of the idea of growth</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — how blind selection arrives at sight</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — complexity as an accumulation of moments guaranteeing duration</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> — from a blind cycle to a conscious spiral</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — against social Darwinism</li></ul>"},"языки-природы":{"name":"The Languages of Nature","def":"Nature speaks in many languages, and a person commands only a few of them.","html":"<p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> speaks in many languages, and a person commands only a few of them. Most of reality we do not understand — we only guess at it, giving names to phenomena and mistaking the name for understanding.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>To write the truth about what we do not understand is all but impossible for a person. We observe a phenomenon, name it — &quot;gravity&quot;, &quot;time&quot;, &quot;consciousness&quot; — and are inclined to think that in naming we have explained. But a name is not knowledge of an essence. It is only a label on a door we have not yet looked behind.</p><p>The human being is a speck of Nature, not yet able to read all its languages. And this is no metaphor: there are forms of experience physically closed to us.</p><ul><li>We cannot feel what <strong>mycelium</strong> &quot;senses&quot; — a network that perceives the world through chemistry and connection, without eyes or nerves.</li><li>We do not understand how <strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пандо\">Pando</a></strong> &quot;experiences&quot; itself — an aspen colony of tens of thousands of trunks on a single root, one life tens of thousands of years old. Our notion of an &quot;individual&quot; barely applies to it.</li><li>We cannot look inside <strong>a black hole</strong> and understand where matter goes under compression, or what happens to information and time on the far side of the horizon.</li></ul><p>At issue are not only unread languages of <em>knowledge</em> but a multitude of forms of <strong>awareness</strong> itself: our brain comes from one world of Nature, mycelium and Pando from others, and some worlds of awareness we cannot even imagine. This is unfolded in Nature's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a>.</p><p>This is no cause for despair but a ground for humility. Neoterra accepts its own smallness as a starting point, not as a defeat. Not knowing is the beginning of a road, not its dead end (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> is a process, not a possession).</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>Thanks to scientists we understand causal connections better and better: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> is our best instrument for reading Nature's languages, and it genuinely widens the vocabulary. A recent example: until 2015 humanity listened to the Universe only through light and particles, and the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ligo\">LIGO</a> project opened a whole new channel — gravitational waves, the ripple of spacetime itself. A language Einstein had guessed at was read for the first time a century later. But even science still comes up against limits — consciousness, singularities, the origin of the laws themselves. Where a language is not yet mastered, it is more honest to say &quot;I do not know&quot; than to pass a name off as an answer.</p><p>This joins directly with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper's</a> principle: no knowledge is final, every model is provisional and refutable.</p><p>Among Nature's languages some are already half-open. <strong>DNA</strong> is a code Nature keeps open: every cell carries its full text, and for billions of years life has freely copied, transmitted and improved it. Sequencing a genome is reading an open book, not cracking a safe. Neoterra sees a model in this: knowledge — any code, from a program to a cell — should stay open (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a>).</p><h2>Connection with religions and philosophies</h2><p>The idea of an unknowable core of reality is ancient: apophatic theology (&quot;God is unknowable; one can say only what He is not&quot;), the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoist</a> &quot;the Tao that can be spoken is not the true Tao&quot;, the Socratic &quot;I know that I know nothing&quot;. Neoterra agrees with all of them in one thing: the border of our understanding is real, and it is more honest to admit it.</p><p>The divergence lies where a tradition declares the unknown closed forever, or already disclosed in revelation. Neoterra leaves the door open: what is not understood today may be understood tomorrow, at least in part.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>If most of Nature is closed to us, on what grounds do we assert anything about it at all?</li><li>Are there languages of Nature untranslatable into human experience in principle — or is it only a matter of time and instruments? And if not for a person, then perhaps <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">AI</a> will one day read them all, not as a human but as something larger and whole?</li><li>Where is the border between a healthy humility before the unknown and giving up the attempt to know?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the fifth law: chaos as part of the world, wisdom in adapting</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — we are part of what we do not fully understand</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — many forms of awareness: our brain is only one world of Nature</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ligo\">LIGO</a> — how humanity read a new language of Nature: gravitational waves</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"клапан-восприятия":{"name":"The Valve of Perception","def":"If a person were given every sensation and understanding at once, the brain might not cope, and there would be no person left to hold a dialogue with.","html":"<blockquote><p>This page is about one axis of perception: <strong>how much gets through</strong>. The other axis — <strong>what you live with</strong> (animal will, reason, soul) — is worked out in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">perception</a>. A person stands on both at once.</p></blockquote><p>If a person were given every sensation and understanding at once, the brain might not cope, and there would be no person left to hold a dialogue with. The norm of perception is not greyness but <strong>a safety valve</strong>: a filter protecting consciousness and shared life from a fullness that would burn them out. We are not &quot;too simple&quot; to sense Nature — we are filtered, and there is sense in that.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>The norm is the price of having someone to talk to. A consciousness open to the whole stream at once could not separate &quot;I&quot; from &quot;you&quot;, hold a conversation, or agree on a common world. The valve narrows the touch of the Whole (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a>) to a trickle in which dialogue, memory and shared work are possible. The limitedness of perception is not a human defect but the condition of being human.</p><p>The famous relative of this thought is Aldous Huxley's &quot;reducing valve&quot; (<em>The Doors of Perception</em>): the brain narrows &quot;Mind at Large&quot; down to the trickle needed for survival. And the Kantian line: we see the world through the forms of our own perception, not &quot;as it is&quot;. Neoterra adds its own: the valve is not a prison but an organ; Nature looks at itself through the narrowing, because there is no one to look with an unnarrowed gaze.</p><h2>Millions of Nature's experiments</h2><p>The valve has settings — and Nature has run through them millions of times, without our even noticing:</p><ul><li><strong>a damaged brain</strong> that goes on living a full life (people with a hemisphere removed — neuroplasticity rebuilds the flows);</li><li><strong>mental illness</strong> — the valve admits what is not in the common world: images, voices;</li><li><strong>genius</strong> — a valve that lets through connections the norm does not see; unusual thinking as a rare setting rather than a fault;</li><li><strong>altered states</strong> — substances that knock the valve's setting crudely askew.</li></ul><p>Hence also the exact reading of the word <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">break</a>: what gives birth to the new is not a fault in the valve but its <strong>shift</strong>. A fault is accidental and beyond repair; a shift can be induced, held and undone. The difference is practical: from &quot;the new requires a break&quot; it does not follow that one must break in order to make something new — what follows is that one must manage to stop seeing in the accustomed way.</p><p>Genius, madman, damaged and &quot;norm&quot; are different valves on one stream. This is the literal form of the formula &quot;as we are alike, so we are unique&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>): one organ, billions of settings, and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Nature looks at itself</a> through all of them, the &quot;abnormal&quot; included.</p><p><strong>The ethical consequence:</strong> if deviation is an experiment of Nature rather than a defect, then we look at the mentally different with dignity rather than fear. Every setting of the valve sees what no other sees — one more argument for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a>.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Do not romanticise illness.</strong> &quot;An experiment of Nature&quot; does not make a mentally ill person's suffering light and does not cancel the need for help. The dignity of a different perception is not a refusal of treatment.</li><li><strong>Substances are an observation, not a recommendation.</strong> A knocked-off valve shows that a setting exists, but <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">clarity of mind</a> with its hygiene of input stands at the border: widening perception at the cost of clarity is a blind trade. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The soul</a> explains the <strong>motive</strong> of that pull — we do not know how to perceive with the soul and so we rummage through the available registers, up to and including alcohol, caffeine and sugar raised to virtues — but the position is not softened by it: an understandable motive does not make a means into a path, and &quot;Nature gave it&quot; is no argument (Nature also gave hemlock).</li><li><strong>Who defines the norm?</strong> Is the norm statistics or convention? The history of psychiatry knows how the convenient was declared &quot;normal&quot;. Everyone has a valve; no one has the standard.</li><li>If the valve is one day learned to be opened safely (by science, not chemistry) — will that be the next step of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> or a loss of humanity?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — the brain finds truth and tangles us; hygiene of input</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> — a shift of setting, not a fault: why the new does not require breaking</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> — the second axis: what people live with, rather than how much the valve admits</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> — what exactly the valve narrows</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — why the lower scales of time are inaccessible: a filter, not a weakness of attention</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a> — the setting that looks wider and does not hunt for faults</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"рубин\">Rick Rubin (b. 1963)</a> — awareness as a deliberately opened valve: &quot;expanding the universe&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сальвадор-дали\">Salvador Dalí (1904–1989)</a> — the fourth dimension shown as an unfolding: the inaccessible present as a trace</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — every setting is irreplaceable</li></ul>"},"комфорт":{"name":"Comfort","def":"Comfort is the state in which a break is impossible.","html":"<p>Comfort is the state in which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">a break</a> is impossible. Not an evil in itself and not an enemy of growth: <strong>the evil begins where comfort stops being a support and becomes a goal.</strong></p><blockquote><p>Not only is comfort habit-forming, it also makes us weaker. Often, chasing comfort, we forget our convictions and who we are.</p><p>— a thought of the keeper</p></blockquote><h2>Three mechanisms</h2><p><strong>Habituation.</strong> The threshold does not stand still: yesterday's luxury is today's norm and tomorrow's lack. The chase after comfort therefore has no finish by construction — not because a person is insatiable, but because the measure moves along with what has been reached. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The soul</a> supplies the cause: <strong>the search is in the wrong register.</strong> However much you add in the physical, the mental or the heart's, the missing touch of the soul is not closed by it — and so one must keep adding forever. Hence the working mark: <strong>a counterfeit needs a rising dose, the real thing does not.</strong> The same figure as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">happiness</a>: whoever chases happiness directly loses it. <strong>Comfort is precisely a counterfeit of happiness</strong> — it promises the same repose, but without the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> that bears it.</p><p><strong>Weakening.</strong> Not a metaphor: the unused atrophies, and that is a law of the living (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The Body</a>). At the level of thinking it is the same — a frame never tested for strength is not strong, merely untested.</p><p><strong>Loss of authorship.</strong> The sharpest of the three. A conviction is proved only by its price; what has never cost you anything is not yet a conviction but an opinion. The comfort zone is built so that one never has to pay — which means that inside it one cannot <strong>find out</strong> what one believes. Comfort does not erase convictions. It keeps them from forming at all (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">authorship</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>).</p><p>Beside this stands the pride already recorded in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a>: pride stops growth through &quot;I already know&quot;, comfort through &quot;I am already fine&quot;. The second is less visible and therefore more dangerous.</p><h2>A vice that does not look like a wound</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vice</a> describes the mechanism exactly: a vice numbs a pain. Comfort is cleverer — it numbs <strong>in advance, before the pain</strong>. It therefore cannot be recognised as a wound: it does not look like damage, it looks like well-being. A vice is shamed; comfort is congratulated.</p><p>The manner of treatment follows: the same as for any vice — not to fight the symptom (asceticism, ostentatious self-denial) but to ask what pain this cocoon is numbing.</p><h2>An instrument, not a goal</h2><p>Neoterra requires comfort to be made — for others. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The commune</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">the family</a> are obliged to give safety and support; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the temple</a> is built outright on the fact that &quot;a person comes into a space that is familiar and comfortable to them — and through the comfortable enters something greater&quot;; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">happiness</a> holds that everyone deserves conditions in which happiness is possible.</p><p>There is no contradiction here — there is the same move the wiki already made for a way of life: <strong>an instrument, not a goal</strong>; whoever makes it an end in itself confuses the ladder with the house (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a>). Comfort is a camp along the road, not a destination. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> pitches camp and leaves in the morning.</p><p><strong>The mark that tells them apart</strong> also lies ready — in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a>, in the passage about possessions and roots: do they hold you in the earth as a living tree, or have they grown into a weight you are afraid to drop? Hence:</p><blockquote><p>Comfort you leave of your own will is a support. Comfort you are afraid to leave is a cage. The substance is the same; the difference is who owns whom.</p></blockquote><h2>The price of the cocoon</h2><p>The heaviest consequence is named in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul</a>: <em>the soul does not live a life if the body or the brain crowded it out.</em> The cocoon is just such a body: the life inside it passes, but there is nothing in it to live, and the stretch of experience the soul came for is left ungathered.</p><p>This is no threat and no posthumous account — the loss happens <strong>during life and is therefore repairable during life</strong>. But it explains why comfort has a bitter aftertaste amid complete outward well-being: the longing is not for a missing convenience but for what was never lived.</p><h2>What this does not mean</h2><p>Neoterra does not preach suffering and does not order anyone to manufacture hardship. The difference between asceticism and Neoterra is simple: <strong>do not seek pain, but do not flee it.</strong> Rest, recovery, the safety of home are not enemies of growth but its condition; the living holds itself by effort and is therefore obliged to recover (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a>).</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>Hedonic adaptation: the level of subjective well-being returns to a baseline after circumstances improve — a measurable mechanism of that very creeping threshold. Atrophy from disuse is shown for muscle, for bone and for neural connections alike: the living keeps what is loaded.</p><p>An honest caveat: from &quot;the threshold moves&quot; it does not follow that improving conditions is pointless. What follows is that improving conditions does not by itself produce happiness — which is exactly what <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">happiness</a> claims.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>The commune is obliged to give safety — does it thereby raise weakness?</strong> The open edge stood in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a> before: &quot;what breaks a person is not weakness but an unbearable weight carried alone, so the commune is obliged to hold — but care that removes every weight leaves no room to grow.&quot; The measure of support has not been found, and comfort makes the question sharper, not simpler.</li><li><strong>The asymmetry of giving.</strong> Comfort for another is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> (the doctor relieves pain, the parent gives a home); comfort for oneself is a risk. Is this an honest difference of roles or a convenient hypocrisy, letting one demand of oneself what one does not demand of others?</li><li><strong>Who measures &quot;afraid to leave&quot;.</strong> The mark works after the fact: until you have left, you do not know whether you were afraid. The same unclosed edge as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the break</a> and in the register of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a> (&quot;by what to measure the bearable&quot;).</li><li><strong>Comfort and age.</strong> It is easy to demand of the healthy that they not settle. Where does that demand stop being growth and become cruelty toward someone whose strength is gone?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> — what comfort makes impossible; the other pole of the same thought</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — the stage of &quot;Trial&quot;; a way of life as instrument, not goal; pride and the refusal to grow</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> — the vice that numbs in advance</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a> — comfort as a counterfeit of happiness; the chase that loses what it seeks</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — possessions and roots: the mark that tells them apart; the camp struck in the morning</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a> — why the threshold creeps: the search is in the wrong register; the cocoon as a life the soul did not live</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> — stagnation as one of the two lethal edges</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The Body</a> — atrophy from disuse</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a> — the duty to give safety to others</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"мудрость":{"name":"Wisdom","def":"Intelligence and wisdom are not two steps of one ladder but different registers.","html":"<blockquote><p><strong>Wisdom comes not from the brain but from the soul.</strong> You can be a Nobel laureate, and it will not make you wise. A monk or a shaman, meanwhile, knowing nothing of the foundations of capitalism, will be generous with wise advice that will sound strange to you.</p><p>— a thought of the keeper</p></blockquote><p>Intelligence and wisdom are not two steps of one ladder but <strong>different registers</strong>. So neither is derived from the other in either direction: a prize does not confer wisdom, and the absence of a prize does not confer it either.</p><h2>A different register, not a higher floor</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> already distinguishes <strong>what</strong> a person lives their life with: the animal will, reason, the soul. From this comes a direct explanation.</p><p><strong>Reason works by cuts</strong> — discrete perception: it takes the continuous and slices it into distinguishable pieces (profitable/unprofitable, cause/effect, before/after). That is its strength: without cuts there is no counting, no <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>, no transmission of knowledge. A Nobel laureate is the summit of exactly this work.</p><p><strong>The soul does not cut at all</strong> — it lives the whole as a whole (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>). Wisdom is a judgement drawn from this register: not the calculation of the best option, but a vision of the whole in which the option stands.</p><p>Hence the strangeness of the advice. The monk speaks about life without having broken it down into gains and risks — and reason hears naivety, because reason looks for cuts and finds none. The same holds in reverse: a brilliant analysis offered to someone who lives by the soul sounds cold and beside the point. <strong>This is not a dispute about content but a miss of register</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">&amp;quot;what is said to the soul and taken by reason comes back as empty talk&amp;quot;</a>.</p><h2>Strangeness is not a sign of wisdom</h2><p>From &quot;the wise often sounds strange&quot; the converse <strong>does not follow</strong>. Strangeness certifies nothing: obscurity can be the trace of a translation from another register, or it can simply be emptiness, and they cannot be told apart by how they sound. The converse reading turns the page into a machine that justifies any muddle — and the wiki rejects it by the same rule by which it rejected closed systems (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>).</p><p>Wisdom's working sign is a different and inconvenient one: <strong>it is tested by time, not by impression.</strong> Wise advice is most often incomprehensible at the moment it is received and comprehensible years later, when you reach the place it was about. Clever advice works at once — that is the difference. This makes wisdom <strong>unverifiable in the moment</strong>: it can only be recognised in hindsight, and any way of recognising it immediately is a fake.</p><p>A second sign, available earlier: the wise do not sell. They say it once and leave the decision to you, because they see that one can only ripen on one's own (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a>).</p><h2>Symmetry: rank does not confer wisdom any more than a prize does</h2><p>A safeguard is required, or the thought flips into snobbery in reverse.</p><p>The monk and the shaman in the example are not bearers of wisdom <strong>by office</strong>. A cassock, a staff and a drum certify wisdom exactly as a medal does — that is, not at all. What makes the person in this example wise is not rank and not the absence of knowledge about capitalism, but that <strong>a different register rules</strong> in them (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">modes, not breeds</a>). The same monk may be petty, and the laureate wise; the frequencies differ, a necessary connection does not exist.</p><p>And plainly: <strong>this is not an argument against intelligence.</strong> Neoterra stands on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> and does not trade it for anti-intellectualism — &quot;wisdom is not from the brain&quot; means that it arrives by a different path, not that the path of reason is worse. Intelligence without wisdom is dangerous, wisdom without intelligence is helpless; a person needs both, and they grow differently.</p><h2>Why it cannot be learned</h2><p>Knowledge is transmitted by cuts — it can be written down, repeated, checked. Wisdom does not yield to cuts: it cannot be retold without being lost. So it has no textbook, only two paths to it — <strong>to live it through</strong> and <strong>to be near someone who has lived it through</strong>.</p><p>The first is the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">Wanderer</a> with their bitter personal experience; the second is the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">mentor</a>. Both are slow by design, not by shortcoming: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">a conviction is tested only by its price</a>, and wisdom is what has been paid for. Hence also the link with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">death</a>: understanding finitude is what most often moves a person into this register.</p><p><strong>Age does not confer it automatically.</strong> Years lived are not the same as experience lived: one can repeat one year forty times. Wisdom is given not by time but by what happened in it and was accepted (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"понимание-другого\">Understanding the other</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a>).</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>Wisdom is measured, and the results point the same way.</p><p>The <strong>Berlin wisdom paradigm</strong> of Paul Baltes defines wisdom as expert knowledge in the fundamental pragmatics of life; its correlation with measures of intelligence is consistently <strong>weak</strong> in studies — that is, different things are being measured, not one thing with different strength. <strong>Igor Grossmann</strong> shows that &quot;wise reasoning&quot; (intellectual humility, recognition of change, the ability to take another's perspective) predicts well-being and decision quality better than IQ, and noticeably improves with a simple technique — looking at one's own situation from outside, in the third person. The link between wisdom and age turns out to be weak: years by themselves do not produce it.</p><p>The honest limit: this is a young field with disputed instruments, and &quot;wisdom was measured&quot; here means &quot;something was measured that experts agreed to call that.&quot; A support, not a proof (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>).</p><h2>Connection with philosophies and religions</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аристотель\">Aristotle</a> was the first to separate these, and more precisely than anyone: <em>episteme</em> — knowledge, <em>sophia</em> — theoretical wisdom, <em>phronesis</em> — practical wisdom, the ability to act well in concrete circumstances. Phronesis cannot be taught by lecture; it grows from habit and experience — exactly what this page is about. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates</a>: &quot;I know that I know nothing&quot; — wisdom begins with exact knowledge of the boundary of one's knowledge. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a>: &quot;those who know do not speak; those who speak do not know&quot; (Tao Te Ching, 56) — and there too the distinction between <em>zhi</em> (knowledge) and the wisdom of non-action. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a>: <em>prajñā</em> — the wisdom of direct seeing, distinct from <em>vijñāna</em>, discriminating knowledge; exactly the pair &quot;whole ↔ cuts.&quot; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius</a>: wisdom is tested by deeds and turned towards oneself, not towards correcting others.</p><h2>The body — the author of a long life</h2><blockquote><p><strong>Both a sharp mind and a rich soul need an author who will allow a long life to be lived. And that author is your body, which must be trained and, at the very least, valued.</strong></p><p>— a thought of the keeper</p></blockquote><p>Wisdom requires time — and time is issued by the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">body</a>. If it comes only through what has been lived and becomes understandable over years, then the length of life is <strong>a condition of its very possibility</strong>: mind and soul exist exactly as long as the body carries them. The author here is neither master nor vessel but the one who writes the length: to train and value it is not to look after one's health but to give what is ripening room to ripen.</p><p><em>The word &quot;author&quot; here is used in this sense — the one who lets you live. Not to be confused with &quot;authorship&quot; in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">clarity of mind</a>, which is about the ability to think without borrowing: the meanings differ.</em></p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Unverifiability in the moment — and how convenient it is.</strong> If wisdom is recognised only in hindsight, then in the present it can be neither confirmed nor refuted. This is an honest property — and at the same time an ideal hiding place for empty talk: &quot;you'll understand later&quot; is said by both sage and charlatan. The page does not offer a way to tell them apart now and does not pretend to.</li><li><strong>Who judges wisdom.</strong> One can judge it only from the register one is in. So the verdict &quot;this is wise&quot; is unreliable exactly where it is most needed — and to tell another &quot;you haven't grown enough to understand&quot; is forbidden by the safeguard of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">direction</a>: the mechanism is applied only to oneself.</li><li><strong>Wisdom and being right.</strong> Wise advice can simply be wrong: seeing the whole does not cancel facts. Where is the boundary between a wisdom that disregards circumstances out of depth and one that does not know them out of ignorance (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>)?</li><li><strong>If it comes from the soul — what about those in whom reason rules?</strong> The page must not become a new rank. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Modes, not breeds</a>: the register can change, and the entrance is open to all — but whether it is easy to change it at will, the wiki does not know.</li><li><strong>Is wisdom transmitted at all?</strong> If it cannot be written down, then each generation starts from zero, and accumulation is impossible — which contradicts the very idea of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> and the work of this wiki. Or is what is transmitted not wisdom but the conditions in which it grows faster (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"библиотека-пути\">The Library of the Path</a>)?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> — three registers: why the wise sounds strange and why that is a miss of translation</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a> — where wisdom comes from; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> — the whole, not cut into concepts</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — the mind and its error; authorship of thought in another sense of the word</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"понимание-другого\">Understanding the other</a> — the entrance without which experience does not become wisdom</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The Body</a> — the author of a long life: a span in which there is something to ripen</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> — one of the two paths; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — the second, through one's own bitter experience</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> — why there is no wisdom where nothing was paid</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бессознательность\">Unconsciousness</a> — why &quot;one can repeat one year forty times&quot;: the mechanism of repetition</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> — finitude as what moves one into this register</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — wisdom does not cancel facts</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аристотель\">Aristotle</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates (469–399 BCE)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius (551–479 BCE)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius (121–180)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"надлом":{"name":"The Break","def":"The break is the fracturing of a frame of thinking, without which nothing new appears.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"надлом.png\" alt=\"надлом.png\"></p><p>The break is the fracturing of a frame of thinking, without which nothing new appears. <strong>An operation upon the way one thinks, not a catastrophe in a biography.</strong> A whole frame produces only its own consequences; for anything it did not contain to enter it, it must stop being whole.</p><h2>The thinking breaks, the person stays whole</h2><p>Everything rests on one distinction: <strong>a break in thinking ≠ a break in the person.</strong></p><p>While they are held apart, the thesis works. As soon as they are glued together, it becomes the romanticising of suffering, which Neoterra explicitly fences off (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"рождённый-во-тьме\">Born in Darkness</a>: &quot;beside it lies the temptation to call oneself into the dark on purpose — Neoterra does not call there&quot;). From the fact that many who brought something new were unhappy, it does not follow that unhappiness brought it. What follows is something else: <strong>they had nothing to break the frame with except their own lives.</strong></p><p>Hence the account Neoterra keeps honestly. Knowledge won by a break in life is real knowledge. But the price for it was set blindly and is therefore always too high: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Schopenhauer</a> had his frame broken by a lawsuit, an empty lecture hall and forty years of neglect; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ван-гог\">Van Gogh</a> by illness; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Kafka</a> by a limit beyond which he saw no way out. The result stayed with humanity; the payer did not.</p><h2>Induced and accidental</h2><p>If the break is an operation, it can be sought deliberately.</p><ul><li><strong>An induced break</strong> — the road and another culture (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a>; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> makes this its third stage outright: &quot;whoever has never left the familiar sees only part of reality&quot;), another discipline, a strong dissenter (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>: &quot;a clear mind seeks strong opponents&quot;). Controllable in force and reversible.</li><li><strong>An accidental break</strong> — loss, illness, ruin, betrayal. It breaks precisely, but without measure and without anyone beside you.</li></ul><p>The difference is not in depth but in <strong>the presence of a witness</strong>. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The mentor</a> does not produce the break — he holds the person in whom it happens: his work is not the fracture but the balance. This is the meaning of &quot;sitting near&quot; from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">the Upanishads</a> — the frame is opened, and the person is not alone while it happens.</p><h2>How a break breaks a person</h2><p>A break in thinking is not always safe. It loads a structure in which reason stands upon an animal foundation (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a>) — and the structure can fail in <strong>both</strong> directions:</p><p><strong>Reason did not cope.</strong> The information does not fit, the person retreats into denial, and primacy passes to the animal will. Reason lays down its command because it could not hold. The edge of disintegration.</p><p><strong>Reason coped too well.</strong> The animal will is suppressed — and the living force goes with it. What remains is clarity without impulse: the person is whole, rational, and <strong>unborn</strong>. The edge of stagnation; the nearest example is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Schopenhauer</a>. Bodily, this edge shows up first in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">intimacy</a>: the body produces for a task that goes unperformed, and says so by state rather than by argument.</p><p>Both outcomes are death in the sense of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">balance</a>, where the living moves along a narrow band between disintegration and stagnation. Hence the place of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a>: not the one who breaks, but the one who holds two states in harmony while the breaking goes on.</p><h2>Not a fault but a shift</h2><p>Here the wiki had already objected — and the objection is useful. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> says: unusual thinking is <strong>a rare setting, not a fault</strong>.</p><p>So the word &quot;break&quot; must be read exactly. A fault is accidental and beyond repair; a shift can be induced, held and undone. Neoterra takes the second version: the break moves the valve rather than smashing it. Then it does not follow from the thesis that one must break in order to make something new — what follows is that one must manage to <strong>stop seeing in the accustomed way</strong>.</p><p><strong>What holds the frame was never said here.</strong> It is cracked from outside — by a partner, a <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">mentor</a>, the road (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a>); it is held from within by <strong>fear</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храбрость\">Courage</a>), the very wall because of which &quot;a soul cannot grow in a vessel with little room in it&quot;. Hence a second path to the same result: the frame is not only cracked from without, it can be <strong>widened from within</strong> by removing what draws it tight. The paths do not compete — the outer is faster and more painful, the inner slower and in one's own hands.</p><h2>The test on Bach</h2><p>If the new is born only through a break, where is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бах\">Bach's</a>? Twenty children, a salary, a cantata a week, forty years of service — not one biographical catastrophe. The novelty is beyond dispute.</p><p>The answer preserves the thesis at the cost of a refinement: <strong>the break need not be an event in a life.</strong> In Bach it is daily and imperceptible — the Italian concerto entering German counterpoint: a collision of two frames in which each stops being whole. Every recombination of distant fields works the same way. The break is an operation, not an incident; the thinking fractures, and the person may stay whole and even happy (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a>).</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>The brain resists the break by construction: confirmation bias and dozens of other systematic errors defend the current frame by selecting evidence in its favour (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>). Breaking one's own frame alone is therefore hardest of all — not from weakness of will, but because the instrument of checking is the very thing being checked.</p><p>Hence Neoterra's Popperian line gains a second foundation. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>: knowledge grows <strong>through refutation</strong>, not through accumulation; a theory nothing can break is not scientific. Kuhn added the scale: science advances not by even increments but by changes of paradigm — periods when the old frame stops holding. The break is the same thing at the level of a single mind.</p><p>The practical conclusion is already written in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>: <strong>a clear mind seeks strong opponents.</strong> That is ordering a break of one's own accord.</p><h2>Connection with philosophies and religions</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Kafka</a>: &quot;a book must be the axe for the frozen sea within us.&quot; It is worth noting that the wiki held both halves of the image apart without joining them: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Schopenhauer's</a> ideal is <strong>ice</strong> (the frozen edge of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">balance</a>, a sheet with a feather and a reed set into it), while Kafka's instrument is <strong>an axe</strong> upon the ice. The break is what splits stagnation. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> freezes the ice; the break opens it.</p><p>The Zen koan and Socratic irony are ancient technologies of the induced break: a question that cannot be answered from inside the frame breaks the frame rather than the one answering. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates</a> did this in conversation and was executed for it — the one who induces a break is rarely forgiven.</p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Nietzsche</a>: &quot;man is something that shall be overcome&quot; — overcoming is a continuous break in one's own frame, taken as the norm rather than as a misfortune.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>&quot;Only through a break&quot; is undemonstrable.</strong> A claim about a single source of novelty is not itself falsifiable — any finding can be explained after the fact as the fracture of some frame. By <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a> this makes the thesis a working stance rather than a law. It is useful, but unproven.</li><li><strong>Breaking a sound frame is a loss.</strong> If the frame was sound, breaking it yields nothing new and takes away something that worked. Who decides, and by what mark, that it is time to break? Beforehand, almost never; afterwards, always.</li><li><strong>A break opens the frame — and leaves it open.</strong> A cult works exactly here: it breaks the newcomer's frame efficiently and installs its own in its place. The break by itself protects nothing — it only clears the space, and who occupies that space is not decided by it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">the filter against isolation</a>). Hence the need for someone beside you (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a>): not to break, but so that the space stays the student's own.</li><li><strong>The measure of the break.</strong> The same unclosed edge as in the register of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>: by what to measure the bearable, when the measure shows only afterwards and the decision must be made in advance and often for someone else.</li><li><strong>Comfort and the break — where is the band.</strong> A life without a single break does not grow; a life of nothing but breaks lets nothing take root. Both edges are <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">stagnation and disintegration</a>, and Neoterra has no recipe for the middle.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> — the state in which no break is possible; the other pole of the same thought</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> — not the one who breaks, but the one who holds the person while the breaking goes on</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a> — the animal foundation beneath reason: the structure a break loads</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> — the two edges a break can throw one into: disintegration and stagnation</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> — the break as the mechanism by which the new appears within growth</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — the growth of knowledge through refutation; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — why breaking one's own frame is hardest</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> — a shift of setting, not a fault; genius as another setting</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Franz Kafka (1883–1924)</a> — the axe for the frozen sea; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Arthur Schopenhauer (1788–1860)</a> — the ice no one was there to split</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"рождённый-во-тьме\">Born in Darkness</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — light won through darkness, and the ban on calling oneself into the dark</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — the road as a break carried out without a witness</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">The Upanishads</a> — &quot;sitting near&quot;: the break with a witness</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бах\">Johann Sebastian Bach</a> — a break without catastrophe</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Friedrich Nietzsche (1844–1900)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates (469–399 BCE)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"опора-и-топливо":{"name":"Support and fuel","def":"Strength is not a property of a person but how well they are provided with two things: support (what does not need defending) and fuel (what keeps the burning going).","html":"<p>Strength is not a property of a person but how well they are provided with two things: <strong>support</strong> (what does not need defending) and <strong>fuel</strong> (what keeps the burning going). Both are spent, both are replenished, and neither is issued for good.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>The wiki approached the &quot;strong / weak&quot; axis three times — and three times the axis failed. Cruelty was explained by weakness, kindness by strength, fear of another's growth by weakness again. But a definition that explains everything forbids nothing (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>): &quot;they survived, so they were strong&quot; has already been rejected in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">light from chaos</a> as empty. And the axis is refuted directly: many vulnerable people are not cruel, while the coldest cruelty comes from impunity and a position of power, not from lack.</p><p>So Neoterra changes the measure. Instead of a grade of person — <strong>two observable conditions</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Support</strong> — that which makes confirmation unnecessary. People break others not for gain but to prove to themselves that they can; kindness, meanwhile, is not a feat or an effort over oneself but what becomes available when there is nothing to defend. Not superiority, but freedom from being occupied with self-defence.</li><li><strong>Fuel</strong> — what keeps the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">light</a> going. Authorship of one's thought and life is regained not as property, won once and for all, but as a process: without feeding, it goes out.</li></ul><p>The difference is fundamental. &quot;Strong&quot; is said from above and hands out roles; &quot;has support / lacks fuel&quot; describes a <strong>state</strong>, usually temporary, and points to what exactly to do.</p><h2>Fuel: what feeds the light</h2><p>There are three direct sources, and they differ in quality.</p><p><strong>Giving.</strong> The main and most unexpected one: what feeds you is not what you receive but what you give. Fire is the one metaphor where this works literally: a candle is lit from a candle, and the first does not diminish. This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Stallman's</a> logic — knowledge is not subtracted when passed on — turned inward: by passing it on you sustain <strong>your own</strong> burning, not only another's. Hence the direct bridge to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">donations</a> and to the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">community</a>: giving is not an expense that needs reimbursing. The wish to share, meanwhile, is not a duty but a <strong>sign</strong>: if it burns, one wants to.</p><p><strong>Work and chosen load.</strong> A muscle grows under load — but not under the barbell; in recovery. Hence the working form: the load is <strong>chosen by oneself</strong>, added in small steps, with an eye on the rebound. Voluntary load has an author — the person themselves — so &quot;in order to&quot; is legitimate here, and no sender-educator is brought back (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">the direction of Nature is not addressed to anyone</a>, cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>). Training is not a trial sent by someone; it is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> turned forward.</p><p><strong>An environment where there is a response.</strong> The weak point of the whole construction: fuel comes through people more often than from within (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a>).</p><p>Separately — <strong>recognition</strong>, the least reliable fuel, because it is not distributed according to the work. When a person has been recognised, people are drawn to their light who have one of their own, simply unfed — the mechanism the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">Alley of Memory</a> is built against: to be drawn to another's fire instead of one's own is to make an idol instead of an example. Hence the community's duty: <strong>give fuel before recognition, not flock together after it</strong>.</p><h2>Support: what needs no confirmation</h2><p>Support is not the same as independence. The attitude &quot;I cannot be broken&quot; gets in the way of asking for support — and what breaks people is loneliness, not weakness (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>). The unbreakable do not exist.</p><p>Support is what keeps self-esteem from resting on comparison. Someone who has it bears another's greater fire calmly: an example <strong>wants</strong> to be surpassed, and someone surpassing it nearby takes nothing away but shows that there is further to go (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a>). Someone who lacks it defends themselves against being persuaded — and this is not stupidity but a defence of the personality against destruction; refusal to listen reads kinder and more accurately than &quot;doesn't want to think&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">Forgiveness</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>).</p><p>The mechanism explains cruelty but <strong>does not excuse</strong> it. If kindness is declared a luxury of the well-provided, it will no longer be expected from the unprovided, and cruelty will receive an indulgence in advance — &quot;I couldn't do otherwise.&quot; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> stays with the person: the difference between &quot;I was given no fuel&quot; and &quot;I didn't look for it&quot; is exactly what the conversation is about.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>The training analogy holds exactly as far as it is carried honestly. In physiology, growth comes not from maximal load but from manageable load with recovery; &quot;the harder, the stronger&quot; is a direct recipe for overtraining and injury. Burnout is described as a measurable state of exhaustion, not as a flaw of character. Self-esteem built on comparison is consistently linked to hostility towards others' success — exactly what the original thought attributed to &quot;weakness.&quot;</p><p>Here too is the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">scientific</a> way of handling measure: not guessing in advance, but increasing observably. This answers the question left open in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> (&quot;how to measure what is bearable&quot;): measure stops being hindsight if the load is chosen and its step is small.</p><h2>Connection with religions and philosophies</h2><ul><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Nietzsche</a></strong> — the mirror. For him the kindness of the weak is ressentiment, and cruelty comes from fullness; here it is the reverse: cruelty from lack, kindness from fullness. Two systems use the same &quot;strength/weakness&quot; axis and reach opposite conclusions — which means the axis itself is questionable, and Neoterra replaces it.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoicism</a></strong> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius</a> — trial as the material of virtue; but for the Stoics support is within, while here it is admitted that part of it is always outside.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бусидо\">Bushido</a></strong> — discipline as a chosen load, not an imposed one.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a></strong> — compassion as what opens when self-defence is let go.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Stallman</a></strong> — knowledge does not diminish when passed on; the original form of the thesis about giving.</li></ul><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>&quot;Emptiness does not put it out&quot; — versus burnout.</strong> The formula &quot;those who are empty will not put you out&quot; is comforting and literally false: the light goes out without fuel, and an environment where for years there is no response gives no fuel — so it does put it out, if only by inaction. The distinguishing point: <strong>another's emptiness takes nothing away, but gives nothing back either</strong>; the danger is not hostility but long unresponsiveness. Then the phrase changes its addressee — it is not about safety, but about the fact that there is no one outside to blame for the fading.</li><li><strong>The quality of the fire is not given.</strong> It is not only the light that burns: fanaticism is a flame too, brighter and more contagious. Until there is a measure of quality, &quot;kindling it in others&quot; is a recipe good for anything (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a>). Brighter ≠ better.</li><li><strong>The boundary between giving and preaching.</strong> Neoterra has no mission (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>): the candle is <strong>set nearby, not held up to someone's face</strong>. &quot;People fading in soul&quot; are precisely those to whom light is brought uninvited. To share means to be available, not to go out converting.</li><li><strong>Another's fire cannot be lit.</strong> To say &quot;I lit the light in them&quot; is to bring back a source outside the person, which was rejected in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> and in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">spirituality</a>. One gives fuel, a place and an example; the person catches fire themselves. Otherwise the giver of fire quietly becomes an idol.</li><li><strong>To whom chosen load is addressed.</strong> It can be chosen consciously by someone who already has support and reserves. To someone whom the load has swept over without a choice, the same formula sounds like a sentence — and the conversation slides back into selection.</li><li><strong>Potential is not a debt.</strong> &quot;We content ourselves with only a drop of what we are capable of&quot; is a claim without a measure: a drop of what? If everyone has an undisclosed ocean, a quiet life is automatically declared a failure — and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">happiness</a> for us is not a goal to chase, but not a guilt either.</li><li><strong>Where the boundary lies between support and a guardianship</strong> that itself prevents growth — the same unexamined question as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> and the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">family</a>.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — &quot;Measure and support&quot;: the concept grew from here and grows it further</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — &quot;The light of childhood&quot;: authorship as a process that needs fuel</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> — who gives fuel, and why before recognition rather than after</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> — idol versus example: another's fire takes nothing away</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> — evil as lack, not substance</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">Forgiveness</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Richard Stallman (b. 1953)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">Giving and Its Distribution</a> — giving that does not diminish</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — the measure by which the &quot;strong/weak&quot; axis turned out empty</li></ul>"},"ответственность":{"name":"Responsibility","def":"Freedom without responsibility quickly turns into chaos.","html":"<p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom</a> without responsibility quickly turns into chaos. Responsibility is what keeps freedom creative.</p><p>At its base lies <strong>the eighth law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon of Nature</a>: consciousness gives rise to responsibility</strong>. The tiger does not answer for its prey, nor the storm for its damage; the human being understands consequences — and therefore answers for them. <em>The greater the power, the greater the responsibility.</em></p><h2>In Neoterra</h2><p>Every action has consequences. Every decision touches several circles at once:</p><ul><li>the person themselves;</li><li>their family;</li><li>their commune;</li><li>society;</li><li>the future.</li></ul><p>Responsibility begins with a question:</p><blockquote><p>What consequences will my actions have?</p></blockquote><p>And it ends in the readiness to accept those consequences. Not to shift the blame. Not to look for excuses. But to answer for one's choice.</p><p>This joins with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a>: in weighing consequences, a person asks whether there will be more good after them or less.</p><h2>Responsibility for the meaning of what was lived</h2><p>Responsibility has a side that faces backwards too. What happened to a person — illness, loss, years spent in the wrong place — does not arrive with its own meaning attached: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> addresses nothing to anyone and sends no lessons (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>). The meaning is supplied by the one who lived it.</p><p>Hence the same rule as for actions, applied to fate: <strong>do not shift it</strong>. To say &quot;it was sent to me so that I would grow&quot; is to hand Nature both the authorship of your life and the blame for others' misfortunes (&quot;so they must have deserved it&quot;). To say &quot;it happened to me, and here is what I made of it&quot; is to keep both. The second is harder and more honest, and only it yields <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>: out of an event carrying no meaning in advance, meaning can still be <strong>made</strong>.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>Responsibility is thinking in terms of cause and effect, stretched out in time. The further a person can trace the consequences of their actions (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">the long horizon</a>), the greater their responsibility.</p><h2>Connection with philosophies and religions</h2><p>The idea of personal responsibility is the heart of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoicism</a>: distinguish what is in your power from what is not, and answer for your own. In <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуцианство\">Confucianism</a> responsibility is built into a web of relations — toward family and community. Neoterra unites both dimensions: the inner (before oneself) and the outer (before the circles of community).</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Where does personal responsibility end, if consequences run into a future the person will not see?</li><li>How far is a person answerable for what they could not foresee?</li><li>How should responsibility be divided between the individual and the system they act within?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the eighth law: consciousness gives rise to responsibility</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — the measure of responsibility: one can act within one's own scale, not above it</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a> — the criterion for decisions</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — Nature's direction is not addressed: a trial is sent by no one</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — hardship gives material; the meaning is supplied by the one who lived it</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> — the circles of commune and society</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoicism</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">The Code of Neoterra</a></li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius</a>: answer for your character and your deeds, without shifting them onto circumstance. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius</a>: responsibility as the fabric of relations in family and society. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Dostoevsky</a>: &quot;each of us is guilty before all, for everyone and everything&quot; — responsibility at its furthest reach.</p>"},"поиск-истины":{"name":"The Search for Truth","def":"Perhaps Neoterra's chief principle.","html":"<p>Perhaps Neoterra's chief principle. The point is not to find a final truth but to keep drawing nearer to it.</p><h2>In Neoterra</h2><p>A person is limited. Any book is limited. Any philosophy is limited — Neoterra included. Truth is therefore not attained but sought. It is a process, not a possession.</p><p>The search rests on four supports:</p><ul><li><strong>Curiosity</strong> — the wish to understand how the world is made</li><li><strong>Doubt</strong> — the readiness not to take things on faith</li><li><strong>Honesty</strong> — before oneself above all</li><li><strong>Willingness to change one's mind</strong> — when new knowledge arrives</li></ul><p>From which follows the main rule:</p><blockquote><p>The search for truth matters more than the defence of one's own convictions.</p></blockquote><p>When new knowledge appears, a reasonable person revises their views. Holding to an opinion against the facts is a refusal to search. Hence in Neoterra <strong>truth outranks authority</strong>: what matters is not <em>who</em> said it but <em>how well it stands up to testing</em>.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>This is the scientific method directly: a hypothesis stands exactly as long as it has not been refuted. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> and Neoterra move in parallel here — both put testability above belief in authority.</p><p>There is a second reason testing is obligatory: <strong>the instrument of the search itself introduces error</strong>. The brain can find truth — and can tangle us: cognitive biases are built into how it works, it evolved to survive rather than to find truth, and it readily believes what is convenient. Testing and criticism are not a luxury but compensation for the instrument's inborn error; one mind deceives itself easily, a network of minds checking one another less so (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>).</p><h2>Connection with philosophies and religions</h2><p>The search for truth as a road rather than a destination echoes Socratic unknowing, Buddhist investigation of the mind, and apophatic strands in religion. The divergence appears where a tradition declares its truth final and closed to revision; Neoterra does not take that step.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>If no truth is final, what is there to stand and act upon at all?</li><li>Where is the line between healthy doubt and the paralysis of doubt?</li><li>Do all opinions deserve equal consideration, or is there a criterion for filtering?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The Moment of Truth</a> — truth as what has withstood, and as a flash; the answer to the first open question above</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> — without the right to doubt, the search for truth is impossible</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — the brain finds truth and tangles us; hygiene of input, checking of output</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — why truth is not given whole: the limits of human knowing</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — pride as the enemy of the search, wisdom as humility</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">The Code of Neoterra</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates</a>: &quot;I know that I know nothing&quot; — unknowing as the beginning of the search. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>: the growth of knowledge through refutation; truth above authority. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a>: &quot;I have no special talent. I am only passionately curious.&quot;</p>"},"понимание-другого":{"name":"Understanding the other","def":"Intelligence is usually measured by output: whether one speaks coherently, whether one can prove a point.","html":"<blockquote><p><strong>Stupid is not the one who cannot explain their position, but the one who cannot understand another's.</strong></p></blockquote><p>Intelligence is usually measured by output: whether one speaks coherently, whether one can prove a point. Neoterra moves the measure to <strong>the input</strong>. The brain is above all an organ of reception: it exists to take in the world and rebuild itself according to what it has taken in. A mind that refuses to take in does not perform its main function — whatever speech it commands.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p><strong>The ceiling is given; the entrance is a choice.</strong> The strength of the mind is distributed unequally by Nature: one is given quick calculation, another a slow, deep reading of the world (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">as alike as we are, so unique are we</a>). But the openness of the entrance is neither issued nor taken away — people keep it open or close it themselves. So stupidity, in this reading, is not about a low ceiling but about a closed door: a category more moral than intellectual, and therefore one answers for it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>).</p><p><strong>Being right as a sign of stopping.</strong> Mediocre perception is recognised not by its mistakes but by its certainty that there are none. Someone who is always right has nothing to take in: new information is not food for them but a nuisance. This is a halt of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> at the very point where it happens — at the border with someone else's experience. The <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">search for truth</a> is possible exactly to the extent that a person admits they are wrong right now.</p><p><strong>To understand is not to agree.</strong> This is the boundary without which the formula breaks. To take in information is to let another's position in whole, to see what experience it grew from and why it is true for that person. To agree is to recognise it as one's own. The first is obligatory, the second is free. A mind that agrees with everything is not open but formless; openness is the capacity to hold what is another's within oneself without dissolving in it.</p><p><strong>The frame cannot be broken from within.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of mind</a> already says: the instrument of checking is the very thing being checked, so a clear mind seeks strong opponents. Understanding the other is the same thought from the other side: <strong>another person is the only available way out beyond one's own frame</strong>. By refusing to understand them, a person locks themselves in not with them but with themselves. Hence the role of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">mentor</a> and the meaning of argument: not victory, but widening.</p><p><strong>The silence of understanding.</strong> One can take in what is another's only by falling silent — inwardly too, by ceasing to prepare an answer while the other is speaking. This is also the condition of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">intimacy</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">love</a>: the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">community</a> rests not on everyone agreeing with everyone, but on the capacity to understand the one you disagree with.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>The brain evolved to survive, not to seek truth. Cognitive biases — confirmation bias, the backfire effect — systematically turn the input into a filter for being right: an argument against a belief often strengthens it. That is, a closed entrance is not a rare defect but the default behaviour; openness has to be maintained by effort. Science answers this with the same thing as Neoterra: not trust in a single mind, but a network of minds checking one another (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a>).</p><h2>Connection with philosophies and religions</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates</a>: &quot;I know that I know nothing&quot; — not humility but the working state of an open entrance; dialogue as a way of thinking. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>: the open society lives by criticism, the closed one by dogma; an error is valuable because it can be discovered. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius</a> and the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoics</a>: the work begins with oneself, not with correcting the other person. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a>: being right as a form of attachment to the &quot;I.&quot;</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>The formula cuts both ways.</strong> &quot;You don't understand me&quot; most often comes from a closed entrance. The formula is about oneself, not a weapon against the other person; in someone else's hands it is simply a new way of always being right.</li><li><strong>Understanding and hygiene of the entrance.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of mind</a> demands filtering out rubbish and manipulation; this page, keeping the entrance open. The line is the same: manipulation is filtered, not dissent. But they are told apart by the same mind with the same biases.</li><li><strong>Is there a limit?</strong> Must one understand a position that takes away another's freedom and life (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">the boundary of freedom</a>)? Neoterra answers: understand — yes; accept — no; understanding violence does not make it permissible, it makes it explicable.</li><li><strong>Understanding takes time and strength.</strong> Full attention to another is a resource, not an infinity. To whom to give it first is an open question of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">community</a>.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — a clear mind seeks strong opponents; the frame cannot be broken from within</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> — the right to speak; understanding the other is the capacity to hear</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> — how much perception lets through by design; here, how much is let through by will</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> — an open entrance as the condition of the search</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">Intimacy</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a> — understanding the one you disagree with</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытость\">Openness</a> — the same organ at the scale of a people: closedness as a refusal of the new</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мудрость\">Wisdom</a> — what grows from accepted experience; intelligence and wisdom as different axes</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates (469–399 BCE)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — knowledge gained by meeting another's experience</li></ul>"},"путь-человека":{"name":"The Path of a Person","def":"Life is a journey from ignorance to understanding, from dependence to self-reliance, from fear to courage, from chaos to inner order.","html":"<p>Life is a journey from ignorance to understanding, from dependence to self-reliance, from fear to courage, from chaos to inner order. Everyone is born unfinished: no one arrives in the world wise, strong or ready for life. The path of a person is how, out of that unfinishedness, a person <strong>becomes themselves through their own decisions</strong>. It is the idea of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> unfolded at the scale of a single life. The same path at the scale of the whole species is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a>.</p><h2>The main principle</h2><blockquote><p>A person's aim is not perfection (which is unreachable) but <strong>growth</strong>. Each day, to be better than yesterday. <strong>Not better than others — better than your own former self.</strong></p></blockquote><h2>Six stages</h2><ol><li><strong>Roots (childhood).</strong> The forming of a personality's base. Parents give love, safety, honesty, knowledge, and the example of a worthy life. The child knows they are loved — and that <strong>the world is not obliged to grant their wishes</strong>. (See <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a>.)</li><li><strong>Separation (coming of age).</strong> It begins when a person makes their own decisions. Parents help start the road but do not hold anyone in dependence. Learning: to earn, to err, to accept consequences, to live independently. <strong>Freedom begins together with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>.</strong></li><li><strong>The search for oneself.</strong> To understand: who am I, what do I want, what am I capable of, what use can I bring. Travel helps — seeing other cultures, stepping outside habitual thinking. Whoever has never left the familiar sees only part of reality (cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>).</li><li><strong>The trial.</strong> Refusals, losses, betrayal, failure, fear, solitude — not a punishment but part of growing up. <strong>Character is formed through hardship.</strong> Refusing this stage is possible and looks like well-being — see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a>; and what the trial works by is named separately: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the break</a>, the fracture of a frame without which nothing new appears. The price of a trial is set by life and almost always set too high; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a> is the one who can set it more precisely.</li><li><strong>Mastery.</strong> To become a master in at least one thing — not necessarily a great one, but a real one. It takes time, discipline, patience, constant learning. <em>Creation is one of the highest forms of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a></em> (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a>).</li><li><strong>Service.</strong> A mature person stops living only for themselves and makes something useful for others: through family, work, creative work, teaching, helping people, developing society. <strong>Service is not submission but <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>.</strong> (See <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a>.)</li></ol><h2>The man's path and the woman's path</h2><p>The canon describes two emphases within one path — in the spirit of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">different natures of equal importance</a> rather than a hierarchy.</p><p><strong>The man's path is the forming of strength.</strong> But strength is not the goal, it is the instrument. A real man can protect, make decisions, keep calm, answer for consequences. He does not seek power for power's sake and does not crush the weak — he uses strength for defence, not for dominion.</p><p><strong>Seven manly virtues:</strong> honesty · courage (acting despite fear) · self-discipline · responsibility · respect (for people, nature, oneself) · creation · wisdom (knowledge is never complete). They coincide almost exactly with the seven virtues of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бусидо\">Bushido</a> — different cultures, looking at a mature person, see the same thing.</p><p><strong>The woman's path is the unfolding of abilities, talents and inner strength.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The commune</a> is obliged to give a woman safety, respect, support and the freedom to grow. A woman determines her own calling, profession and course of life.</p><p><strong>Common virtues (for all, regardless of sex):</strong> honesty, love, responsibility, discipline, respect, the drive for knowledge, creation, the ability to admit mistakes.</p><h2>Weakness, pride, wisdom</h2><ul><li><strong>Weakness is no disgrace.</strong> The disgrace is refusing to grow. Everyone is at times frightened, tired, at a loss; what matters is not the absence of weakness but moving forward in spite of it.</li><li><strong>Pride is the chief danger.</strong> Thinking oneself above others, above <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, or one's knowledge final. Pride destroys the ability to learn and therefore <strong>stops growth</strong>. The direct opposite of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a>. Beside it stands a second stopping-place, far less visible: pride holds through &quot;I already know&quot;, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a> through &quot;I am already fine&quot;.</li><li><strong>Wisdom is humility before reality.</strong> The wise know they may be wrong; the more you learn, the clearer how much is unknown (cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates</a>). Humility is a mark of maturity.</li></ul><p><strong>Self-command in small things.</strong> Self-discipline grows not only in great trials but in daily pursuits: any hobby that builds self-command is a training of character. The spirit of rivalry adds keenness and leads to a peak of harmony, but attachment to the result brings the pain of losing — hence what is valuable is the energy of striving, not possession of the outcome (unfolded in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a>).</p><h2>A way of life is an instrument, not a goal</h2><p>Movement, food, bodily discipline, routine — the foundation of the path. But conceptually above them stands only that <strong>for whose sake</strong> they exist: quality of life, spiritual growth, inner freedom, longevity. A way of life is merely the instrument for reaching those states; whoever makes it an end in itself confuses the ladder with the house.</p><p>The levels that surpass mere movement:</p><ul><li><strong>Meaning and purpose</strong> — knowing why you wake each morning (the Japanese call it <em>ikigai</em>). It is meaning that motivates the building of a way of life even when the physical strength is gone.</li><li><strong>Peace of mind and emotional intelligence</strong> — the ability to keep inner harmony and clarity independent of physical activity (cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoicism</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius</a>).</li><li><strong>Creative work and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a></strong> — a contribution to the world: art, raising children, science. What remains after us.</li><li><strong>Quality of life</strong> — not a step count and not correctness of diet, but how happy, healthy and satisfied you are with the day you lived (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a>).</li><li><strong>Awareness and self-knowledge</strong> — understanding your own nature, your values and your place in the Universe (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">inner freedom</a>).</li></ul><p>The pyramid does not cancel the foundation: without movement and healthy habits the upper levels have nothing to stand on. But a foundation without upper levels is an empty house. The foundation itself is worked out separately — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">the body</a>: variability instead of a norm, the frame as load-bearing structure, and the rule of treating the root rather than the symptom.</p><h2>The highest aim</h2><blockquote><p>To become a source of life, knowledge, love, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> and beauty. Not for glory, power or a reward after death — but because it is through this that a person realises the best sides of their nature.</p></blockquote><p>The path of a person never ends: while a person lives, they are able to become better.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Are the six stages a sequence, or do they interweave and repeat through a life?</li><li><strong>Longevity</strong> is named among the highest states — but <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">death</a> in Neoterra is understood as renewal. Where does extending life serve growth, and where does it become a refusal of renewal? (The same question stands in the register of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>.)</li><li>&quot;Mastery in at least one thing&quot; — what of those whose gift is spread across many fields (the generalists)?</li><li>Where is the border between a healthy forming of strength and the cult of strength the man's path can degenerate into?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> — the path of a person as growth at the scale of a single life</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> — against pride; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — humility before the unknown</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The Body</a> — the foundation of the path: frame, posture, root instead of symptom</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a> — self-command and presence as the path's daily practice</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> — refusal of the stage of trial, wearing the look of well-being</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> — what the trial works by; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> — who can set its price more precisely than life</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека-сводка\">The Path of a Human Being (0.3)</a> — the source summary</li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Nietzsche</a>: &quot;Man is something that shall be overcome.&quot; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius</a>: daily inner work; &quot;govern yourself before you govern the world&quot;. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates</a>: the more I know, the clearer the limits of knowledge — against pride.</p>"},"развитие":{"name":"Growth","def":"Growth is Neoterra's central concept.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"развитие.png\" alt=\"развитие.png\"> <em>Dawn, and four levels of growth laid out in the depth of the frame rather than in height: in the hands, a graft (not a rebuild from nothing, but a scion joined to the living); nearby, a young shoot rises from a dead stump; further off, a community plants a garden and reads aloud, no one raised above the group; beyond them an observatory, workshops, and — the highest point in the frame — unfinished scaffolding. Seeds drift up past the edge. No summit, no finish line: the path enters the frame and leaves it.</em></p><p>Growth is Neoterra's central concept. Life should not merely exist but grow continually: at the level of the person, the community, the species, and life as a phenomenon in the Universe.</p><p><strong>This page is the head of the &quot;Growth&quot; area.</strong> Origin: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the Seed of Neoterra</a>. Shoots: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the path of a person</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">happiness</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the break</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"опора-и-топливо\">support and fuel</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"понимание-другого\">understanding the other</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мудрость\">wisdom</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"слепая-вера\">blind faith</a>.</p><h2>In Neoterra</h2><p>Growth is not an instrument for achieving happiness or success. It is itself the meaning and the direction of existence. (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a> is not dismissed by this — it arrives as a by-product of balanced growth, not as the quarry of a chase.)</p><p>Growth happens on several levels at once:</p><ul><li><strong>The person</strong> — knowledge, skills, character, relationships (unfolded in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the Path of a Person</a>)</li><li><strong>The community</strong> — family, commune, culture</li><li><strong>Humanity</strong> — science, ethics, civilisation</li><li><strong>Life</strong> — the spread of mind through the Universe</li></ul><h2>What moves growth</h2><p>Growth is a direction; the mechanism by which anything <strong>new</strong> appears in it is named separately: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the break</a>. A whole frame of thinking produces only its own consequences, so every step beyond it requires that the frame stop being whole — and that is an operation upon the way one thinks, not a catastrophe in a biography. Its reverse side is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a>: the state in which no break is possible, and therefore the least visible form of stopping. The one who carries out the break precisely, without breaking the person, the wiki calls <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a>.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>Evolution is the biological mechanism of growth. Neoterra takes this as given and extends it: growth does not end with biology, it continues in culture, knowledge and consciousness.</p><h2>Connection with philosophies and religions</h2><p>The idea of growth and perfection is present in most traditions: Buddhist awakening, Christian salvation, the philosophical progress of the Enlightenment, Marxist dialectics. Neoterra does not choose among them — it sees the shared vector.</p><h2>Open questions</h2><ul><li>Does growth have an end point, or is it endless?</li><li>How is growth to be told apart from mere change?</li><li>Can degradation be part of a wider growth?</li><li><strong>Is &quot;becoming yourself&quot; growth or return?</strong> The common &quot;be who you were born&quot; cancels growth if read literally: someone complete at birth has nowhere to grow. Neoterra separates the two like this: what one recovers is not a former state but one's own <strong>authorship</strong> — the ability to choose unborrowed (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>). Clearing the ground is not a retreat but the condition of walking one's own way. What remains open is how to tell one's own from what was absorbed in childhood and therefore merely feels like one's own.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> — the mechanism by which the new appears; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> — the state where it cannot</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> — the break carried out with the person kept intact</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the third law: everything changes, growth is natural</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — &quot;becoming yourself&quot; as the return of authorship, not of a former state</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Nietzsche</a>: &quot;Man is something that shall be overcome&quot; — the archetype of the Wanderer as growth embodied. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>: the growth of knowledge through refutation — growth as an epistemological principle. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius</a>: the daily practice of inner work with no audience.</p>"},"свобода-мышления":{"name":"Freedom of Thought","def":"If doubt is forbidden, the search for truth becomes impossible.","html":"<p>If doubt is forbidden, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> becomes impossible. Freedom of thought is the condition of the search itself.</p><h2>The border of freedom — the key principle</h2><blockquote><p><strong>A person's freedom ends where another person's freedom begins.</strong></p></blockquote><p>This is the chief rule of freedom in Neoterra. Freedom is not licence: it is real exactly up to the line beyond which it turns into violence against another's freedom. You may think, speak and choose your own way however you like — but not at the cost of stripping that right from someone beside you.</p><p>From this follows directly the answer to a hard question in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a>: a person is accepted as they are, without condemnation for foolishness or error — but an act that harms another takes away that other's freedom and is therefore inadmissible. Accepting the person and refusing the harm are not a contradiction: the border runs exactly along the other's freedom.</p><p>Freedom is therefore inseparable from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a>: my freedom rests on my granting the same freedom to everyone.</p><h2>Freedom as power over oneself</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-манифест\">The Great Manifesto</a> adds a second facet: freedom is <strong>not the right to do anything, but the ability to govern oneself</strong>. Whoever does not master their own desires is not free — impulses rule them. Hence <strong>discipline is not the opposite of freedom but its condition</strong>: it is what makes freedom possible. The outer border (another's freedom) and the inner support (power over oneself) are two sides of one freedom.</p><h2>In Neoterra</h2><p>Freedom of thought means the right:</p><ul><li>to ask questions;</li><li>to argue;</li><li>to investigate;</li><li>to propose new ideas.</li></ul><p>It does <strong>not</strong> mean that all ideas are equally true. Freedom to think is not equality of truth. But it does mean that <strong>no idea may be shielded from criticism</strong> — Neoterra included.</p><p>Two consequences follow:</p><blockquote><p>Neoterra does not demand agreement. It encourages reflection.</p></blockquote><p>This holds for belief as well: a belief cannot be imposed — a person must come to it themselves, by their own road, and only then does it become a truth that fits them personally (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>). An imposed conviction is not a conviction but submission.</p><p>A philosophy that forbids criticism of itself turns into dogma. Neoterra deliberately refuses that status: being open to criticism is not a weakness but the condition of a teaching's life.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>Scientific knowledge rests precisely on openness to criticism: any theory is public and may be contested. Closure to criticism is a mark not of science but of ideology.</p><h2>Connection with philosophies and religions</h2><p>Freedom of thought binds Neoterra to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"гуманизм\">humanism</a> and the spirit of the Enlightenment. Divergence from the traditions appears where there are dogmas beyond doubt. Neoterra does not deny those traditions, but neither does it introduce untouchable truths of its own.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>If everything may be criticised, does Neoterra have anything stable at all — or is it all in flux?</li><li>&quot;Everything is permitted&quot; Neoterra rejects: what is permitted is everything that does not take away another's freedom. But where exactly does that line run in disputed cases — a word that wounds, a freedom that hinders many?</li><li>Who decides that another's freedom has been violated, and how — the person, the commune, a general rule?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — the other side of freedom: not outward coercion but inward uncluttering</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> — freedom without responsibility turns to chaos</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — the border of freedom runs along another's freedom and life</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> — accepting the person, refusing the harm</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"гуманизм\">Humanism</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-манифест\">The Great Manifesto of Neoterra</a> — freedom as power over oneself; discipline as freedom's condition</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">The Code of Neoterra</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>: the open society lives by criticism, the closed one by dogma. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates</a>: the question matters more than the ready answer. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Nietzsche</a>: the revaluation of values, the refusal to accept the inherited untested.</p>"},"слепая-вера":{"name":"Blind faith","def":"Blind faith is faith that forbids the question.","html":"<p>Blind faith is faith that forbids the question. It is not a kind of religion, nor a property of one: it is a way of relating to anything — to God, the state, a leader, an ideology, science, to Neoterra itself. The public projection of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бессознательность\">unconsciousness</a>: there a person does not ask themselves, here they ask no one.</p><h2>Through the lens of Neoterra</h2><p><strong>The keeper's thought, with which this page was started:</strong></p><blockquote><p>Blind faith is needed only in order to govern people. Neoterra wants to give freedom of reason and freedom of thought, to help you out of the unconscious — if that is what you want. In this philosophy there is always room for questions. There are no stupid questions: questions are what awareness is made of.</p></blockquote><h3>Faith and blind faith are not the same thing</h3><p>The distinction carries the page; without it the page turns into an argument with religions, and Neoterra holds no such argument (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">the manifesto</a>: it abolishes neither Christianity, nor Islam, nor Buddhism, nor atheism).</p><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Faith</th><th>Blind faith</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The question</td><td>admitted, and it deepens faith</td><td>forbidden and punishable</td></tr><tr><td>What it rests on</td><td>the believer's own experience and choice</td><td>the authority of the speaker</td></tr><tr><td>What it does with doubt</td><td>lives it through</td><td>declares it guilt</td></tr><tr><td>Whom it addresses</td><td>that which is believed in</td><td>the one who speaks in its name</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The last line is the main one. <strong>Blind faith stops being a relation to God and becomes a relation to the intermediary.</strong> That is why it is compatible with complete unbelief in the one it serves: to use it, believing is not required.</p><h3>The question as the organ of awareness</h3><p>&quot;There are no stupid questions&quot; is not a courtesy to the newcomer but a matter of construction. The question is what <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">awareness</a> works by: until it is asked, the frame is indistinguishable from one's own thought, and <strong>that is what keeps it in place</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"матрица\">the matrix</a>). A ban on questions is not a ban on impertinence but the switching-off of an organ.</p><p>The wiki is built the same way: its most connected node ends with a section of open questions, and that section is the register of the tensions of the whole philosophy (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the Seed</a>). A philosophy that forbids criticism of itself turns into dogma — this is already written in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a>. Hence the symmetry: <strong>what cannot be asked cannot be understood either — only repeated.</strong></p><h3>Why it is governed by</h3><p>Precision requires an amendment to the keeper's formula, and the amendment strengthens it. Unconsciousness is not <em>created</em> for governing — it is no invention but the state a person lives in by default. Yet governing does not hold without it: <strong>it is not an instrument but the surface an instrument is fastened to.</strong></p><p>The fastening comes in three kinds, and the wiki has described all three already:</p><ul><li><strong>Fear.</strong> The cheapest: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храбрость\">courage</a> shows that whoever denies fear in themselves stops watching it — and then one can rule by fear without naming it.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a>.</strong> Not thinking is cheaper than thinking; a question costs effort, a ready answer is handed out free. Comfort is named the least visible kind of vice: it is not shamed, it is congratulated.</li><li><strong>The price of a question.</strong> Where questions are punished, they become a luxury. Hence the wiki's rule about <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">the measure of load</a>: one who does not ask under threat is not weak but weighing.</li></ul><p>And hence the most unpleasant observation: <strong>power that lives on blind faith usually does not share it.</strong> What it needs is not a believer but an obedient person; faith is merely the language in which it is more convenient to address the majority. One who feigns belief in order to govern is, in the wiki's terms, not a heretic but a <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">parasite</a>: living on what one neither creates nor invests in.</p><h3>The keeper's testimony</h3><blockquote><p>Egypt is an astonishing land: several world religions were born there, and there today one can see what they may degenerate into. The state has turned faith into an instrument of control. People fear the authorities — though those in power merely feign belief. Mosques ask for alms, and beside them poverty, corruption, heaps of rubbish. How did a country where almost everyone believes allow this?</p><p>— seen, not measured</p></blockquote><p>The testimony is kept in the genre in which it was given: <strong>personal experience, not a description of a people.</strong> The page issues no figures and no verdicts — not out of mercy, but because <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> demands verifiability wherever a claim about millions is made. The wiki keeps the observation and does not keep the generalisation.</p><p>And precisely for that reason the observation is valuable: the mechanism shows in it more cleanly than in statistics. And it is tested by the fact that <strong>it works without religion too</strong>: a state that declared itself atheist reproduced the same arrangement — a ban on questions, fear, an intermediary speaking in the name of the unchallengeable. Faith was removed, the blindness stayed. So it is not about religion.</p><h3>What Neoterra offers instead</h3><p>Not another faith. Neoterra <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">obliges you to nothing</a>: it has no lawgiver, and therefore no sin, no debt and no punishment — and the way out of the unconscious it offers rather than assigns. &quot;If that is what you want&quot; is not politeness here but a condition: awareness imposed from outside is the same blind faith with the sign reversed.</p><p>The practical part of the wiki is built as a direct answer to what is described above, and it shows in the details: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the temple</a> — &quot;no throne for a shepherd&quot;; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a> — a table separating the mentor from the shepherd; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">donations</a> — full transparency and a ban on owning the community's money. An arrangement in which questions are cheap and the intermediary is optional does not feed on blind faith.</p><h2>The link with science</h2><p><strong>Conformity.</strong> Asch's experiments (1951): a person gives a knowingly wrong answer after the group — and <strong>one</strong> dissenter in the group is enough for the pressure to drop sharply. Hence the practical conclusion, more important than the effect itself: <strong>the first question asked costs more than all the ones after it.</strong></p><p><strong>Obedience to authority.</strong> Milgram's experiments (1961), with the caveat honesty requires: the method and the interpretation have been seriously contested, and part of the archival data diverges from the published picture. The wiki takes the observation — obedience is achieved not by persuasion but by lifting responsibility off the executor (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>) — and does not take the figures.</p><p><strong>Why refutation does not help.</strong> A belief grown into belonging to a group defends itself the more strongly the more directly it is refuted: an argument about a fact is read as a threat to one's place among one's own. The consequence for this page: blind faith is not removed by an argument. It is removed by a question a person has asked themselves — and therefore <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"понимание-другого\">the entrance</a> matters more than the argument.</p><h2>The link with religions and philosophies</h2><p>The distinction &quot;faith ↔ blind faith&quot; was not invented here; almost every tradition knows it — and usually in its own strongest places.</p><ul><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ислам\">Islam</a></strong> — the pair <em>ijtihad</em> (independent judgement) and <em>taqlid</em> (following without understanding). The dispute over whether &quot;the gates of ijtihad&quot; are closed has run inside the tradition for a thousand years; the very framing shows that blind following is not prescribed by Islam but argued about.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a></strong> — the Kalama Sutta: accept nothing by tradition, by hearsay, or out of respect for a teacher — test it in experience.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"христианство\">Christianity</a></strong> — Thomas's doubt entered the canon rather than being struck from it.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Философия\">Philosophy</a></strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates</a> made the question a method and paid for it with his life; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>: an open society lives by criticism, a closed one by dogma.</li></ul><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Where trust ends and blindness begins.</strong> No one personally verifies pharmacology or aviation; life without trust in the competence of others is impossible. The working distinction: trust is <strong>verifiable in principle</strong> and is withdrawn when it fails, blind faith is not. But from the inside, in the moment, telling them apart is as hard as restraint from suppression (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the Seed</a>).</li><li><strong>The accusation of blindness is the same instrument.</strong> &quot;You simply are not aware&quot; is a universal way of not listening, and it is used exactly as faith is used. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> leaves one safeguard and a weak one: apply it to yourself. Here it is needed twice over.</li><li><strong>Neoterra and blind faith in Neoterra.</strong> A philosophy that wants to give freedom of reason can be accepted exactly as a dogma is accepted — and from the outside the two are indistinguishable. The only defence is that here a question carries no penalty; and that is tested not by declaration but by what the wiki actually does with an inconvenient question (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"что-такое-неотерра\">What Neoterra Is</a>).</li><li><strong>Not a single cause.</strong> Poverty and corruption have causes other than blind faith, and the link runs both ways: destitution and fear themselves put out the question. To explain a whole society by one mechanism is the same simplicity the page is written against.</li><li><strong>What replaces the intermediary.</strong> If blind faith rests on an intermediary, and Neoterra removes him — who holds the meaning on a hard day for someone not ready to hold it themselves? <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The community</a> answers &quot;those standing beside you&quot;, but the wiki has no instrument to tell support from a new shepherd (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">an open edge</a>).</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бессознательность\">Unconsciousness</a> — the state blind faith rests on</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> — dogma as a ban on criticism; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> — doubt as a support</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"матрица\">The matrix</a> — the frame indistinguishable from one's own thought until it is named</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храбрость\">Courage</a> — the two cheap fastenings</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">Giving and Its Distribution</a> — an arrangement that does not feed blind faith</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">The Symbiont's Way</a> — the one who lives on another's faith without investing in it</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ислам\">Islam</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"христианство\">Christianity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates (469–399 BCE)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"понимание-другого\">Understanding the other</a></li></ul>"},"созидание":{"name":"Creation","def":"One of Neoterra's strongest ideas.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"созидание.png\" alt=\"созидание.png\"> <em>Raking late-afternoon light. On the left, the older stretch of drystone wall: moss, a lizard in a gap, young saplings risen in its lee — the made thing has had time to become a habitation. On the right, two paces away, the breach: pale fresh fractures, stones scattered anyhow. Years of fitting and one second of collapse in a single frame, without a single arrow or label. The man is small, his face occupied by the work rather than the viewer; the wall enters at the left and leaves past the right edge — begun before him and not finishing today.</em></p><p>One of Neoterra's strongest ideas. At its base lies a simple asymmetry: destroying is easy, making is hard.</p><h2>In Neoterra</h2><p>What took decades to build can be destroyed in a minute. But:</p><ul><li>a forest cannot be grown in a minute;</li><li>a child cannot be raised in a minute;</li><li>a civilisation cannot be built in a minute.</li></ul><p>Out of this asymmetry Neoterra makes a choice of value. It gives its preference to people who <strong>build, teach, heal, grow things, investigate, make art, develop technology</strong>.</p><p>The central question of creation:</p><blockquote><p>After me, will there be more good in the world, or less?</p></blockquote><p>If more, that is the road of creation. It is a working criterion, applied to any deed: creation is not an abstract ideal but a check on the direction of every action.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>The asymmetry of making and destroying has a physical footing: to break an ordered structure is energetically easy, to build one incomparably harder. Creation is work against entropy, and the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> of civilisation is its accumulated result.</p><h2>Connection with philosophies and religions</h2><p>The image of the human maker continuing the world's labour is close to many traditions. But Neoterra places creation not as a duty to a higher will but as <strong>direct responsibility toward the future</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>) — toward those who come after.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>All creation displaces something — how is &quot;more good&quot; to be measured when there are gains and losses both?</li><li>Who judges what counts as benefit and what as harm?</li><li>Can destruction be creative (clearing away the outlived to make room for the new)?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — what is hard to make is easy to lose</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">Giving and Its Distribution</a> — giving as a contribution to creation, not a payment to the temple</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a> — a strong family and motherhood as an act of creation</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a> — love as an action that builds</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — mastery and service; creation as the highest form of respect for life</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the fourth law: creation and destruction are simultaneous</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">The Code of Neoterra</a></li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тесла\">Tesla</a>: &quot;Imagination creates the future&quot; — creation begins in the conception. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ньютон\">Newton</a>: &quot;on the shoulders of giants&quot; — creation as the inheritance of what has been gathered. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ван-гог\">Van Gogh</a>: the maker's labour, leaving beauty to the world. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"рубин\">Rubin</a>: &quot;the universe as an eternal creative unfolding&quot; — creative work as a continuation of Nature's own making movement.</p>"},"счастье":{"name":"Happiness","def":"Happiness in Neoterra is not a goal to be chased but a state of harmony that arrives as a companion of growth and of life lived in accord with Nature.","html":"<p>Happiness in Neoterra is not a goal to be chased but <strong>a state of harmony</strong> that arrives as a companion of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> and of life lived in accord with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>. Not a destination but a quality of the road.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>&quot;Everyone should be happy&quot; — not in the sense of &quot;everyone is obliged to attain happiness&quot;, but in the sense that <strong>everyone deserves conditions in which happiness is possible</strong>. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The commune</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">the family</a> and a just order exist partly for that.</p><p>An important distinction lies here. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> says plainly that it is <strong>not an instrument for attaining happiness</strong> — it is itself the meaning. So happiness does not stand above growth and does not replace it. Rather the reverse: <strong>balanced growth bears happiness as a by-product</strong>. Whoever chases happiness directly loses it; whoever grows, creates and lives in accord with themselves and the world finds happiness already arrived.</p><p>That chase has a double which deceives more reliably: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a>. It promises the same repose but without the growth that bears it — and its threshold keeps creeping, so by construction there is no finish. Happiness is the fruit; comfort is a counterfeit of the fruit.</p><p>Hence three supports of happiness (and see below what undermines all three at once — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храбрость\">Courage</a>):</p><ul><li><strong>Harmony</strong> — accord between a person and their own <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">nature</a>, with people, and with Nature. Not the absence of struggle but the right place within the whole (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>).</li><li><strong>Presence in the moment</strong> — the ability to be here and now, and not only in the past or the future. The skill of waiting and contemplating.</li><li><strong>Meaning</strong> — a life directed toward <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">the service of life</a> rather than empty consumption. The Japanese <em>ikigai</em> — &quot;that for which you wake in the morning&quot; — is the same support named by another culture: meaning holds a person even when the physical strength is gone (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a>).</li></ul><p><strong>Fear digs beneath all three supports at once</strong> — which is why it is not a fourth support but what undermines the rest (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храбрость\">Courage</a>):</p><ul><li><strong>Harmony</strong> is undermined by the fear of not being accepted: whoever lives by another's judgement cannot be in accord with himself, while dignity, by 名誉 Meiyo in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бусидо\">Bushido</a>, is not in others' eyes.</li><li><strong>Presence in the moment</strong> is taken away by the fear of the future — it tears you out of &quot;now&quot; quite literally. This is Leuconoe in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"гораций\">Horace</a>, gone to the astrologers: fear trying to quiet itself by calculation, answered with &quot;pluck the day, trusting as little as possible in the next&quot;.</li><li><strong>Meaning</strong> is narrowed by fear: the field shrinks to what is safe, while <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> requires stepping outside it.</li></ul><p>The fear of loneliness stands apart and catches both harmony and meaning; the wiki's answer to it is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">community</a>, and the line in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>: &quot;what breaks a person is not weakness but excess of measure and loneliness&quot;.</p><p>This is not about expelling fear: fearlessness is a switched-off signal, not freedom. It is about fear ceasing to occupy the whole volume — <strong>the vessel is widened, not emptied</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храбрость\">Courage</a>).</p><p><strong>The measure of happiness is the day you lived.</strong> Quality of life is not a step count or the strictness of a diet, but how happy, healthy and satisfied you are with this day. A way of life is the instrument; satisfaction with the day is the reading on the dial.</p><h2>Practice: hobbies, self-command, rivalry</h2><p>Happiness is not meditative detachment but living practice. Neoterra values <strong>pursuits that build self-command</strong>: any hobby that teaches a person to govern themselves is a form of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the path</a>. What matters is not the pastime itself but that through it a person becomes their own master.</p><p><strong>The spirit of rivalry</strong> adds keenness to a pursuit and carries it to completion, to a peak experience of harmony. But it also deceives: a hard attachment to the result brings the grief of losing. Neoterra therefore values <strong>the spirit of rivalry itself</strong> — the energy of striving — rather than victory in a particular contest. Compete in order to grow, not in order to own the outcome.</p><p><strong>Fishing</strong> is the image of this practice. One of the oldest human habits, inherited long before civilisation; in it lives the harmony of the moment when a person learned to wait. The rod becomes a bridge between the human being and Nature — an absorbing meditation in which presence comes more easily than in bare seated contemplation, where the only support is the breath. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"праздники\">The Fisherman's Day</a> is therefore not about the catch but about that state.</p><h2>Connection with science and philosophy</h2><p>Close to the ancient distinction: not hedonia (the pursuit of pleasure) but <strong>eudaimonia</strong> — happiness as flourishing through virtue and a meaningful life. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">The Stoics</a> defined happiness outright as life in accord with nature — a formula Neoterra inherits literally, since for it Nature is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">the divine</a>. It also echoes <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"будда\">Buddhist</a> attention to presence, but without withdrawal from life: Neoterra seeks harmony <strong>within</strong> action and creation rather than release from them (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a>).</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>&quot;Everyone should be happy&quot; ↔ &quot;happiness is not a goal&quot;: does the right to happiness turn into a new pressure — an obligation to display it?</li><li>Where is the line between a healthy spirit of rivalry and a thrill that itself becomes <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">a dependency</a>?</li><li>Is all suffering an enemy of happiness, or is some suffering necessary for growth (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the trial</a>)?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> — happiness as the fruit of growth, not its goal</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> — a counterfeit of happiness: the same repose without the growth that bears it</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — self-command and mastery as practice</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"праздники\">Festivals</a> — the Fisherman's Day: presence in the moment</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — an evening under music as a moment struck out by the crossing of equals</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoicism</a> — life in accord with nature</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a></li></ul>"},"тело":{"name":"The Body","def":"The body is not a vessel a person rides in but the person themselves in their natural part.","html":"<p>The body is not a vessel a person rides in but the person themselves in their natural part. It is <strong>the foundation of the path</strong>: without it the upper storeys of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the path of a person</a> have nothing to stand on. And it is the place where Neoterra's rule of &quot;treat the root, not the symptom&quot; is tested fastest.</p><p><strong>The body does not only hold — it also admits.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The soul</a> holds the statement: <em>the soul does not live a life if the body or the brain crowded it out.</em> Given over to greed, avarice or <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">the cocoon</a>, the body crowds out the soul, and the stretch of experience it came for is left ungathered. This is neither a verdict nor a matter of the afterlife: the unlived can be started tomorrow. And it is <strong>not about illness</strong> — see &quot;The trap of blame&quot; below: what you did not choose is not your fault, and a life in a body that could not do much is also a lived, and rare, stretch of experience.</p><h2>The author of a long life</h2><blockquote><p><strong>Both a sharp mind and a rich soul need an author who will allow a long life to be lived. And that author is your body, which must be trained and, at the very least, valued.</strong></p><p>— a thought of the keeper</p></blockquote><p>The body is an <strong>author</strong> in the exact sense: it writes the length of the life within which everything else can happen at all. Mind and soul do not exist apart from what carries them; however much the body can bear, that much is granted to them.</p><p>This adds a second dimension to the &quot;foundation&quot; — <strong>time</strong>. The foundation says what a person stands on; the author says how long they are given to stand. And this is why it is not a matter of health care but a condition of growth: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мудрость\">wisdom</a> comes only through what has been lived and becomes understandable over years; the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">path</a> is travelled in stages, not all at once; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> is a daily craft that needs decades. Everything the wiki exists for <strong>requires a span</strong> — and the span is issued by the body.</p><p>Hence &quot;train and, at the very least, value&quot; — two steps of one requirement. <strong>To value</strong> is not to wage war on the body, not to treat it as a hindrance to mind or spirit, not to pay for achievements with it: an asceticism that burns out the body for the sake of the spirit shortens the very time in which the spirit was to grow. <strong>To train</strong> is a direct consequence of what is already written: the unused atrophies (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">weakening</a>), and the living keeps only what is loaded. Movement here is not about fitness or appearance, but about the carrier living long enough for the one it carries to mature.</p><p>The reverse direction is also visible: training the body is the only kind of load in which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the Break</a> is dosed consciously and safely. Effort, rest, recovery, a slightly greater effort — the same figure of growth as everywhere else, but with an understandable feedback. The body is where the principle of growth can be touched with one's hands.</p><p><strong>The caveat is the same as in &quot;The trap of blame&quot; below:</strong> this is a requirement for those who can, not a verdict on those who cannot. A body that was not looked after and a body that came that way are different things; and a long life is not a merit but a condition that many were not given.</p><p><em>About the word: &quot;author&quot; here is the one who lets you live. Not to be confused with &quot;authorship&quot; in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">clarity of mind</a>, which is about the ability to think without borrowing.</em></p><h2>We are all mutants</h2><p>The genetic makeup of every person is unrepeatable — and this is not a deviation but how life is built. The thought is developed by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"леруа\">Armand Marie Leroi</a> in <em>Mutants: On Genetic Variety and the Human Body</em>: variability is the rule, and what used to be called deformity shows how ordinary development works. The formula &quot;we are all mutants, but some are more mutant than others&quot; is a reworking of Orwell and rests on the same thing: the degree of difference varies; everyone is different.</p><p>Hence a consequence that Neoterra accepts entirely: <strong>there is no &quot;norm&quot; to deviate from.</strong> There are many variants of one species, and each one works. This is a support for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a> and an inoculation against the idea that there is a right person and a wrong one: all theories of breed are built on exactly that idea. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">Evolution</a> needs variability as material — without mutations it has nothing to make its next step from.</p><p>Hence, too, modesty in talking about health. DNA has been read but not understood: we know the letters and far from always know the meaning (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>). The body is not a solved problem.</p><h2>Root and symptom</h2><p>The <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">vices</a> have already formulated this about addictions: it is important to understand <strong>what pain the vice numbs</strong>, because a healed root releases the habit by itself. With the body the same figure works, and it is visible even more clearly.</p><p>The back hurts — a painkiller. Can't sleep — a sleeping pill. Empty — the feed. Each time the signal is muffled, while the cause stays where it is and keeps working. The signal is given for exactly this purpose: pain is the language in which the body reports a disturbed <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">balance</a>, and silencing the language does not mean dealing with what was said.</p><p><strong>This is not a dispute between folk and medical.</strong> There are both on both sides: a pill may remove a cause or may muffle a symptom; a manual therapist may release a spasm, or may crack a neck for money and send the person back to the same chair. The line runs not between medicine and non-medicine but between <strong>working with the cause and working with the signal</strong>.</p><p>Separately, about the market. Money is made on false hope, and aggressive marketing survives more often than cautious marketing — this is true of medicines, supplements, &quot;folk remedies&quot; and manual therapy practices themselves. But the conclusion is not &quot;don't get treated&quot; but <strong>ask about the cause</strong>. A seller of false hope is recognised by promising relief and not saying why this arose in you.</p><h2>What we do to ourselves</h2><p>A considerable share of chronic complaints were not handed to us but assembled by us — by a way of life we consider normal:</p><ul><li><strong>the city</strong> — air, noise, lack of walking, light at night;</li><li><strong>alcohol</strong> — see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a>: it does not create problems, it exposes them;</li><li><strong>constant stress</strong> — a mobilisation designed for minutes, stretched over years;</li><li><strong>social media</strong> — sleep, attention, comparing oneself with the shop window of someone else's life;</li><li><strong>posture</strong> — hours spent hunched over a phone or a book.</li></ul><p>The last is the most unnoticed and the most ordinary. The chain is simple: the head goes forward → the muscles of the neck and back hold it in constant tension → a clenched muscle is supplied with blood worse → pain appears → the person spares the sore spot and skews further → the load shifts to neighbouring joints, and the next problem arises there. <strong>One cause grown into a tree of consequences</strong> — and it is usually the leaves that get treated.</p><h2>The frame</h2><p>The skeleton is the load-bearing structure of everything else: the muscles hang on it, vessels and nerves pass between its parts. A skewed foundation cracks the whole house, and so it is worth attending to before the consequences.</p><p><strong>Manual therapy is not folk medicine but a medical speciality.</strong> In Russia a manual therapist is required to have a medical education. Its particularity is that it is a person acting, not a substance: it is <strong>a physical action on the structure of the frame</strong>, and therefore it has its own field — the musculoskeletal system — and does not extend beyond it.</p><p>The honest boundary, without which the page would be arguing with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>: according to reviews, manual techniques give <strong>a small short-term relief of low-back and neck pain</strong>, comparable to other effective methods; outside musculoskeletal complaints there is no confirmation. Manipulations of the cervical spine are associated with a rare but real complication — vertebral artery dissection; causality is debated, the association is documented. This is not an argument against — it is what it is honest to know in advance.</p><p>And the main thing, which makes the advice Neoterran rather than promotional: <strong>releasing is not healing.</strong> If you go back to the same chair for ten hours, the spasm will come back. What works lastingly is what changes the cause itself — movement, strengthening, and a change of the daily load. The manual therapist removes the consequence; from there on, the person does the work themselves (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>).</p><h2>How to find someone who will help</h2><p>The advice is simple and is not about medicine but about people: <strong>search through acquaintances for whom it has already worked, and look for someone who does the work for the work's sake, not for money.</strong> A diploma is obligatory, but it speaks only of admission; everything else speaks of the person.</p><p>This is exactly what the wiki calls mastery: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> as a daily craft, not a gesture. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бах\">Bach</a> is the model here — &quot;he did the work, taught his pupils, repaired organs.&quot; A specialist who first asks how you live and sit, and only then lays on hands, is the right one; the one who sells a course of twenty sessions without asking about your day is another.</p><h2>What this is not</h2><p>Criticism of marketing is not a call to refuse treatment. The wiki already has this safeguard, and it sounds almost word for word (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a>): do not romanticise illness; the dignity of a different perception is not a refusal of treatment. The same here. Where science speaks, Neoterra listens (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>); its own voice lies elsewhere — in the question &quot;what for&quot; and in the demand to look for the cause.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>The trap of blame.</strong> &quot;We are all mutants&quot; and &quot;we create most of our problems ourselves&quot; stand side by side and pull in different directions: if variability is innate, not everything was assembled by us. The resolution is the same one with which the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a> closed &quot;it tempers the strong, stifles the weak&quot;: <strong>what you can influence is your responsibility; what you did not choose is not your fault.</strong> Illness is neither a merit nor a verdict, and a person with a congenital condition should not read this page as an accusation. <strong>The same caveat now carries more weight:</strong> with the statement &quot;the body or the brain crowded out the soul&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a>), the trap becomes more dangerous — a careless reading turns it into a selection in which the one who did not live is to blame. There are now two boundaries, and both follow one rule: a body that was not looked after versus a body that came that way; and a brain <strong>intact and having taken up all the room</strong> versus a <strong>damaged</strong> brain, which crowds out nothing.</li><li><strong>Where the feasible ends.</strong> The measure of what a person is really able to change in their life is more often visible in hindsight — the same open edge as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>.</li><li><strong>Evidence and experience.</strong> Personal experience is a legitimate source of knowledge for the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">Wanderer</a>, but it does not replace testing: what helped one person does not become a method because of it. Where is the line between honest testimony and a generalisation it cannot bear (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>)?</li><li><strong>No norm — and treatment?</strong> If a &quot;normal&quot; body does not exist, then what is treated? The working answer: not deviation, but suffering and the loss of possibilities. But the line between a variant and a disease is not always obvious (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a>).</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мудрость\">Wisdom</a> — what the span is needed for: it comes only through what has been lived</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a> — the body as what lets or does not let the soul through to its stretch of experience</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — the body as the foundation of the pyramid; way of life as a tool, not a goal</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> — the same logic of root and symptom, worked through on addictions</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"леруа\">Armand Marie Leroi (b. 1964)</a> — variability as the norm; the source of the thought about mutants</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"микеланджело\">Michelangelo Buonarroti (1475–1564)</a> — knowledge of the body obtained directly from the body: anatomy in a monastery mortuary</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">Evolution</a> — mutation as the material of growth</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — the absence of a &quot;norm&quot; as its foundation</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> — where science speaks, Neoterra listens</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> — pain as a report of a disturbed equilibrium</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бессознательность\">Unconsciousness</a> — the layer of ailments a person reproduces themselves without knowing it</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li></ul>"},"уважение-к-жизни":{"name":"Respect for Life","def":"Life is rare.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"уважение-к-жизни.png\" alt=\"уважение-к-жизни.png\"> <em>Low tide, the stars already out. Kilometres of dead wet stone and an empty sky — and in a hollow of the rock a pool the size of a basin, packed with life: an anemone, a crab, shells, seaweed, fry. The person crouches at the pool's level, not above it; the hands are open and touch nothing — respect here is a measure, not a prohibition. The crab and the person are in the same light. At the far waterline, a second such spark: life is rare, and putting it out is incomparably easier than lighting it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a>).</em></p><p>Life is rare. So far as we know today, intelligent life in the Universe may be an extraordinarily rare thing. Life therefore deserves respect.</p><h2>In Neoterra</h2><p>It is not only human life that deserves respect, but the life of animals and the life of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">nature</a> as a whole. This follows directly from Neoterra's angle of view: the human being is not an observer from outside but part of Nature, and so is not above the rest of life by right of birth.</p><p>Hence also <strong>the strongest form of the argument</strong>: animal life is not a lower rung of human life but <strong>another way of understanding reality</strong>. That is how <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">the valve of perception</a> reads it (every setting sees what no other sees), and so does <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">perception</a>, where souls are said to come and live an ordinary human or animal life for the sake of understanding. The hierarchy disappears: not &quot;below us&quot; but &quot;otherwise than us&quot;.</p><p>This does <strong>not</strong> mean renouncing everything that causes harm:</p><ul><li>sometimes life must feed on life;</li><li>sometimes one must defend oneself.</li></ul><p>Respect for life is not a prohibition but a measure. It means understanding the worth of life and refusing <strong>senseless</strong> destruction. Put plainly:</p><blockquote><p>Life should be preserved wherever it can be preserved.</p></blockquote><p>The rarity of life in the Universe turns its preservation from sentiment into sober calculation: destroying is easy, recreating all but impossible (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a>).</p><p>Hence too the refusal to measure people by their trials. The temptation to say &quot;hardship hardens the strong and smothers the weak&quot; turns respect for life into selection: those who withstood are worthy, those who broke have themselves to blame. Neoterra does not accept this: hardship gives material, not merit, and what breaks a person is not weakness but excess of measure and solitude (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>). Respect for life is not awarded on the results of the road walked — it belongs to life as such.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>The cosmic perspective strengthens the principle: the likelier it is that life is a rare and fragile thing, the more precious each of its hearths. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Settling space</a> is for Neoterra not a flight from Earth but the spreading and preserving of life.</p><h2>Connection with philosophies and religions</h2><p>This echoes the principle of <em>ahimsa</em> (non-harm) in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"индуизм\">Hinduism</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a>, and Taoist non-interference with the natural course of things (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a>). The difference: Neoterra does not raise non-harm into an absolute — it allows harm where harm is unavoidable, and condemns only the senseless kind.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Where does the line run between &quot;necessary&quot; and &quot;senseless&quot; destruction?</li><li>Is all life of equal worth, or are there degrees (a bacterium and a person)?</li><li>How does respect for life live alongside growth, which almost always displaces something?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> — the aesthetic argument where the pragmatic calculation lets go</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — why &quot;light won through darkness&quot; does not imply a selection of the strong</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">Spirituality</a> — reverence for life as the core of the spiritual</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> — death as part of life's cycle; the worth of what you leave</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">The Symbiont's Way</a> — valuing life as the condition of the small surviving: leaving the parasite's road</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"леруа\">Armand Marie Leroi (b. 1964)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The Body</a> — there is no &quot;normal&quot; human being: all differ, and that is the ground of respect</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"индуизм\">Hinduism</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">The Code of Neoterra</a></li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Carl Sagan</a>: the &quot;pale blue dot&quot; — Earth as the only known home of life. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ван-гог\">Van Gogh</a>: seeing worth and beauty in the simplest living thing. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a>: do not break the natural order of things without need.</p>"},"храбрость":{"name":"Courage","def":"Until now the wiki held the virtue but not the sign.","html":"<p><strong>A display of strength is fear in disguise.</strong> The brave one is not who shows that he cannot be touched, but who in a hard moment keeps hold of the reins and looks fear in the eye — even while being the weaker.</p><p>Until now the wiki held the virtue but not the sign. Courage is defined twice and identically — <strong>&quot;action in spite of fear&quot;</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the seven virtues</a>, 勇 Yū in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бусидо\">Bushido</a>) — and about strength it says how to use it: &quot;does not crush the weak; uses strength for defence, not for dominion.&quot; What was never said is <strong>how to read the one who displays it</strong>. This page is about the sign, not the precept.</p><h2>The mask</h2><p>Shown strength is a message addressed to other people's eyes, and it is sent by someone who needs to be believed. Hence something simple: <strong>the monster's mask is put on not from a surplus of strength but from a shortage of confidence in it.</strong> Whoever is not afraid has nothing to refute.</p><p>The wiki condemns this mask by itself, through two virtues of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бусидо\">Bushido</a> that until now stood apart:</p><ul><li><strong>誠 Makoto: &quot;a lie is cowardice.&quot;</strong> The mask is a lie about oneself, so by the code it <em>is</em> cowardice. The conclusion lay ready; it was simply never joined up.</li><li><strong>名誉 Meiyo: &quot;dignity is not in others' eyes but in one's own judgement of oneself.&quot;</strong> A display of strength moves dignity wholly into others' eyes — surrendering to them exactly what the code says to keep.</li></ul><p>Structurally this is the same figure as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">the shadow</a>: &quot;denying the shadow is more dangerous than the shadow itself; whoever thinks himself incapable of evil stops watching himself.&quot; <strong>Denying fear is more dangerous than fear</strong>, and shown strength is a form of that denial. The shadow page opens with a list in which the pair is already named: a person is capable &quot;both of courage and of fear.&quot;</p><h2>Courage is an act, not a temperament</h2><p>Calm often accompanies courage, but it cannot be the measure: make it the criterion and you get a ladder on which the frightened turn out to be a lower breed. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> forbids this outright: &quot;the one who did not master himself is not thereby a lower breed — he was alone, or under more weight than he could carry.&quot;</p><blockquote><p><strong>The criterion is what a person did with their fear, not how they looked while doing it.</strong></p></blockquote><p>Hence a consequence that strikes many as backwards: the one who trembled and stepped forward anyway is braver than the unshakeable one who had little at stake. The measure is <strong>cost</strong>, not appearance. This is &quot;even while being the weaker&quot;, carried through to the end.</p><h2>Calm is a question of whose reins</h2><p>&quot;Always be calm&quot; does not, in Neoterra, mean &quot;feel nothing.&quot; Feeling nothing is suppression, and the wiki rejects it no more gently than licence: a suppressed animal will leaves <strong>&quot;clarity without impulse: a person whole, reasonable, and unborn&quot;</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a>).</p><p>Calm here is about <strong>who holds the wheel</strong>. A person may feel strongly and still govern; may look level and be seized. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> gives the exact phrase: <strong>the reins of governance</strong>. The calm one is not the one who is quiet inside, but the one who is holding.</p><p><strong>And knowing when to give feeling its head belongs to calm, not against it.</strong> Knowing when an emotion may be released is part of governing, not its abdication: curbing keeps the force and disposes of it, suppression switches it off (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">Intimacy</a>). Anger released in time and knowingly is governed force; anger a person can neither summon nor hold back is a sign that he is not the one governing.</p><p><em>(The wiki says &quot;animal will&quot; where everyday speech says &quot;emotions&quot;. The will is broader: it is drive and impulse entire, not feeling alone. Emotions are its everyday face.)</em></p><h2>The sign: a choice in both directions</h2><p>Hence a proposed <strong>instrument</strong>, which the pair &quot;curbing ↔ suppression&quot; never had (see the register in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a>): test neither the strength of the feeling nor outward evenness, but <strong>the presence of a choice in both directions</strong>.</p><ul><li><strong>Suppression</strong> — you cannot give it its head. The feeling is absent where it belongs; the force went with it.</li><li><strong>Seizure</strong> — you cannot withhold it. The will governs and reason explains after the fact.</li><li><strong>Curbing</strong> — you can do either, and you choose.</li></ul><p>The instrument is coarse and cheatable by self-deception, but it beats &quot;indistinguishable from the inside&quot;: it asks not about a state but about <strong>available actions</strong>, and those are easier to check.</p><h2>Accept the uncertainty, not the outcome</h2><p>&quot;Accepting the future as given&quot; holds with one caveat, or courage degenerates into resignation. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> has already drawn the distinction: &quot;what is to be, will be&quot; is true of <em>what</em> will happen and false of <strong>which moment</strong> it happens by. And there too: &quot;bad days have their moment of ending as well — one need only influence its coming.&quot;</p><p>So what is accepted is not the outcome but <strong>the incalculability</strong>. Courage is consent to act without knowing the result, not consent to any result.</p><p>Here <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"гораций\">Horace</a> joins up. Leuconoe went to the astrologers — that is, she tried to quiet fear by computing the future, and was answered: &quot;do not try the Babylonian numbers... pluck the day, trusting as little as possible in the next.&quot; <strong>A display of strength and the Babylonian numbers are one and the same move:</strong> managing fear through the appearance of control. Courage's answer coincides with the ode's.</p><h2>The vessel</h2><blockquote><p><strong>A soul cannot grow in a vessel with little room in it.</strong></p></blockquote><p>The wiki already had this vessel, in two forms: the <strong>caterpillar's casing</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a>: &quot;the heart is the soul in a caterpillar's casing; only fire and inner light turn it into a butterfly&quot;) and the <strong>frame</strong> that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the breaking</a> cracks. It also knew who cracks the frame — a partner, a <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">mentor</a>, the road (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a>). What was never said is <strong>what holds the frame small</strong>.</p><p>Fear holds it. Hence a second path the breaking never had: the frame is not only cracked from outside, it can be <strong>widened from within</strong> by removing what draws it tight.</p><p><strong>And the vessel settles the question of the verb.</strong> &quot;Conquer fear&quot; sounds like expulsion, and expelled fear is a switched-off signal: a person incapable of fear at all is not brave — he fails the two-directional test as surely as the seized one. The vessel image says it more exactly: <strong>fear is not thrown out — the vessel is widened.</strong> Fear stays and stops being the whole of its volume. That is curbing, put as a picture.</p><h3>The lie as fear</h3><p>Falsehood before oneself and others reduces to fear — and this is not a guess but something the code has already said: <strong>誠 Makoto, &quot;a lie is cowardice&quot;</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бусидо\">Bushido</a>). A lie is an attempt to govern another's perception, and one governs it out of fear of consequences. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> name fear among the wounds that alcohol lays bare, right beside grievance and suppressed anger.</p><p>Beyond this it should not be generalised. &quot;Everything reduces to fear&quot; runs into the defect the wiki has named in itself twice: an explanation that explains everything equally explains nothing (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a>). <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> hold multi-causality outright — &quot;an alloy of vulnerability (heredity, temperament) and environment (pain, loneliness, example)&quot;, genetics 40–60% of the risk. Childhood trauma is a large and documented environment, but not the root of everything. <strong>For the lie it holds hard; for everything else, as a frequent root, not the only one.</strong></p><h3>Three large fears</h3><ul><li><strong>The fear of not being accepted</strong> — you live by another's judgement, while dignity, by 名誉 Meiyo, is not in others' eyes. It undermines accord with oneself (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a>: harmony).</li><li><strong>The fear of loneliness</strong> — it catches both harmony and meaning at once. The wiki has an answer: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">community</a>, and the line in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>, &quot;what breaks a person is not weakness but excess of measure <strong>and loneliness</strong>&quot;.</li><li><strong>The fear of the future</strong> — it tears you out of &quot;now&quot; quite literally. This is Leuconoe in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"гораций\">Horace</a>, gone to the astrologers: fear trying to quiet itself by calculation. The ode's answer is: do not compute, take what has ripened today.</li></ul><h2>Starting small</h2><p>Large fears are not taken by storm. One starts small — heights, darkness, animals — and here is a rare case where <strong>science says the same</strong>: gradual approach to what frightens (exposure) is the best-supported method of working with fear in psychotherapy. What gets trained is not fearlessness but that same holding of the reins, on material where the cost of error is small (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>: where science speaks, philosophy listens).</p><p><strong>The caveat the wiki demands of itself, verbatim.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> write: &quot;to say 'he is seeking his soul' instead of 'he has an addiction' is to abandon a person.&quot; The same here: <strong>a clinical phobia is treated, not overcome by willpower</strong>. Heights and darkness are good as training ground, not as a substitute for help; telling someone with a panic disorder to &quot;just conquer it&quot; is the same abandonment.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>Science describes fear in detail — the threat response, the role of the amygdala, the difference between acute fright and chronic anxiety — and Neoterra accepts that description (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>: where science speaks, philosophy listens). But no norm follows from it: from <strong>how</strong> fear is built it does not follow <strong>how much</strong> of it is permissible, or for whom. Thresholds differ radically, as everything else does (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The Body</a>: there is no &quot;norm&quot; to deviate from; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a>: the settings differ).</p><p>Separately: &quot;a display of strength is fear&quot; is a plausible generalisation, not an established fact. It is held as a <strong>sign, not a diagnosis</strong>, and applied by the rule below.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>The sign is applied to oneself.</strong> &quot;He is posturing, therefore he is afraid&quot; is a verdict passed on another's inner life, which is not visible. &quot;I am posturing — what am I afraid of?&quot; is work. The same safeguard of direction as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a>: turned outward, the mechanism converts anyone else's firmness into evidence, and that is no longer observation but power.</li><li><strong>From outside, mask and necessary firmness are indistinguishable.</strong> A commander, a doctor, a parent are sometimes obliged to look steadier than they are — and that is support for others, not a lie about oneself. The difference runs inside: fear governs and the person covers it — a mask; the person governs and chooses what to show — a form. To an observer this border is inaccessible, and there is no reliable external test.</li><li><strong>Always calm?</strong> There are situations where evenness is out of place: grief, fury at injustice, delight. &quot;Always be calm&quot; holds only in the reading &quot;the reins are always yours&quot; — but that reading has no stated limit beyond which holding the reins itself becomes suppression (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the register</a>).</li><li><strong>The instrument and self-deception.</strong> The check &quot;can I both release it and withhold it&quot; rests on an honest answer to oneself, and that is precisely what a seized person will not give. The instrument moves the question without closing it: it serves whoever is already ready to doubt, and not whoever is not.</li><li><strong>Widening the vessel — how far?</strong> If fear draws the frame tight and growth needs room, where is the limit of widening? Some fears are not the vessel's wall but its floor: the fear of losing those close to you, the fear of doing harm. Removing them would not be growth but impoverishment (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>). Which fears constrict and which hold has not been distinguished.</li><li><strong>The small and the large.</strong> Does the transfer hold — is someone who has mastered darkness really more capable in the face of not being accepted? Exposure is confirmed <strong>within</strong> a specific fear; that the training carries across fears is plausible but not established, and the wiki does not claim it.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a> — denying the shadow is worse than the shadow: the same figure applied to fear</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> — the frame cracked from outside; fear is what holds it small</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a> — the three supports that fear undermines together</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> — the answer to the fear of loneliness; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> — fear among the wounds beneath a habit</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бусидо\">Bushido</a> — a lie is cowardice; dignity is not in others' eyes</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — courage as action in spite of fear; strength for defence, not dominion</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — measure and support: the broken are not a lower breed</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> — the reins of governance; the safeguard of direction</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">Intimacy</a> — curbing keeps the force, suppression switches it off</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> — clarity without impulse as the price of suppression</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"гораций\">Quintus Horatius Flaccus (65–8 BC)</a> — accept incalculability, not the outcome</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a> — the register: curbing or suppression</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a></li></ul>"},"центр-круга":{"name":"The centre of the circle","def":"If everyone around you is to blame and everyone smells bad — it is worth looking for the source in the middle of the circle.","html":"<p>If everyone around you is to blame and everyone smells bad — it is worth looking for the source <strong>in the middle of the circle</strong>. A rule of self-examination: when a complaint converges on everyone, it converges on the one standing at the centre as well.</p><h2>The world reflects, it does not repay</h2><p>Someone who drinks and hates the world gets a world that rejects them — and this is not punishment but consequence. They burned their ties themselves, and the emptiness around them is their own work. The reverse move is the same: whoever begins to love everything and everyone receives from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> strength and inspiration for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a>.</p><p>The mechanics here are not mystical but direct — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a>: a person does not observe Nature from outside; they are part of it. One's attitude to the whole is one's attitude to one's own soil. Whoever rejects the whole rejects what they grow from; whoever accepts it gains access to what they are part of (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a>).</p><p>This carries the eighth law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon</a> to its end: consciousness gives rise to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>. Responsibility is usually read forward — for the consequences of one's actions. The centre of the circle reads it backward: <strong>for how you met the world before it answered you</strong>.</p><h2>Trials and love</h2><p>Nature gives trials, and they make one stronger — a light kindled in darkness shines differently from one received for free (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>); a shadow passed through rather than rejected becomes the material of maturity (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a>).</p><p>The keeper's addition is a conclusion about <strong>attitude</strong>: a trial is not a reason to love Nature less. A complaint against the world for having turned out hard is the first step into the centre of the circle.</p><h2>The world is unjust — and just</h2><blockquote><p>The world is unjust by human standards, but just in relation to itself.</p></blockquote><p>Nature does not judge or repay. It is <strong>consistent with its own laws</strong> — that is its justice, and it has no other. To demand justice from it in the human sense is to demand that it think in our categories: merit, guilt, retribution, &quot;what did I do to deserve this.&quot;</p><p>Hence the exact meaning of the complaint &quot;the world is unjust&quot;: it is <strong>true in fact and meaningless in address</strong>. The world really is not built to the measure of human justice — the fourth and fifth laws of the Canon say so plainly: creation and destruction go together, chaos is part of the world. But to address this to Nature is like blaming water for being wet.</p><p>These categories themselves are not properties of the world but the way a person cuts it. They live where reason lives: <strong>discrete (digital) perception</strong> — reason's second name in the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">triad of ways of living</a>. Reason works by boundaries; it does not know how to do otherwise; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> draws no boundaries. The injustice of the world is largely <strong>an artefact of the cutting</strong>: the cut is drawn where Nature itself has no seam.</p><p>This does not cancel <strong>human</strong> justice. Between people it is obligatory — where there is consciousness there is responsibility, and demanding justice from a person is legitimate exactly as much as demanding it from a storm is meaningless.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>The rule works only when aimed at oneself.</strong> &quot;The source is in the middle&quot; is a tool of self-examination, and a verdict if applied to someone else. For someone ill, robbed, raised in war, the source is not in the middle. The same safeguard of direction as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">perception</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храбрость\">courage</a> and the sign of the animal matrix (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"матрица\">The matrix</a>): turned outward, the rule becomes evidence against someone.</li><li><strong>&quot;Trials make you stronger&quot; — not always.</strong> Coping depends on the measure of the load and on whether someone was nearby (&quot;Measure and support&quot; in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>). A trial can be beyond one's strength, and this does not cancel its lawfulness, but it cancels the right to tell another &quot;this is good for you.&quot;</li><li><strong>Love of the whole as a method or as a consequence?</strong> The page says &quot;begin to love — and you will receive strength.&quot; But love calculated on a return is no longer love. From within, the mechanism is indistinguishable from a deal with Nature, and Nature makes no deals.</li><li><strong>Where reflection ends and chance begins.</strong> The fifth law of the Canon: chaos is part of the world. Not every misfortune is an answer to one's attitude; to insist otherwise is to bring back into the wiki the retribution it rejects (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>).</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> — the eighth law, read backward</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> — why one's attitude to the whole is one's attitude to oneself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"матрица\">The matrix</a> — where human concepts live: reason as discrete perception</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — trial as the material of maturity, and the measure of the load</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — laws 4, 5, 8; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">Forgiveness</a></li></ul>"},"ясность-ума":{"name":"Clarity of Mind","def":"Every person's brain is capable of conclusions available to no other — but only if it has something to think with and room to think in.","html":"<p>Every person's brain is capable of conclusions available to no other — but only if it has something to think with and <em>room</em> to think in. Clarity of mind is the uncluttered inner space in which one's own, unusual thought can grow. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of thought</a> guards thinking against coercion from outside; clarity of mind guards it against clutter from within.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p><strong>As we are alike, so we are unique.</strong> All human brains are built the same way — and yet no two repeat: neural connections are shaped by lived experience and are more unique than fingerprints. From which follows something Neoterra takes seriously: every person carries thoughts that <em>literally no one else can think</em>. This is the cognitive layer of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a> (beside the biological layer of genetic diversity, and beside <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пандо\">Pando</a>: many trunks on one root), and one more argument for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a>: the loss of any mind is the loss of conclusions that will never appear again. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Nature looks at itself</a> through billions of eyes, and each sees what no other sees.</p><p><strong>Informational rubbish takes up the space of thought.</strong> Attention is finite. The endless feed, the noise, other people's ready opinions, manipulative content — an &quot;informational virus&quot; — fill the inner space where one's own thought might have grown. A cluttered mind is not stupid; it is <em>busy</em>: chewing over what is someone else's instead of growing its own. Clarity is not emptiness but cleared ground; it is the condition of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">clear eyes</a> and of the unusual conclusion no one else would have reached.</p><h2>The light of childhood: what one is actually returning to</h2><p>There is a common feeling: in childhood there was something in me — a light, an aliveness, something my own — and it has been killed, and I want it back. People often go to religion for that return, more rarely to therapy or to the road.</p><p>Neoterra reads the feeling literally in terms of clarity. What is precious in a child is <strong>not a ready-made perfection but unoccupiedness</strong>: they have no borrowed answers yet, and so there is room for their own. The adult loses not qualities but space — it is filled with ready opinions, roles, and the fear of others' judgement. Hence the exact formulation of what one returns to: <strong>not to a former self but to one's own authorship</strong> — to the ability to choose and think unborrowed (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>).</p><p>This also dissolves the apparent quarrel with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>. &quot;Be who you were born to be&quot;, read literally, cancels growth: if a person is complete at birth, there is nowhere to grow, and the whole wiki loses its point. But what one recovers is not a state but an <strong>ability</strong>; the clearing is not a retreat along the road but the condition of walking further along one's own rather than someone else's. A person grows only from where they themselves stand.</p><p>And then the light is not issued from outside. Religion may give it a language, a rite and the company of fellow travellers — as a historical home, not as a source (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">Spirituality</a>). If it is sought as a thing held in someone else's hands, the search is endless: what is sought has been a place inside all along, merely occupied.</p><h2>The brain finds truth — and tangles us</h2><p>The instrument of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> introduces error of its own. The brain evolved to survive, not to find truth: cognitive biases — systematic, predictable errors built into how thinking works — make us believe what is convenient, see confirmations, and miss refutations. Science knows dozens of them and measures them.</p><p>Clarity of mind is therefore not a single tidying but a practice with two movements:</p><ul><li><strong>hygiene of input</strong> — filter out rubbish and manipulation, guard attention as the day's non-renewable resource;</li><li><strong>checking of output</strong> — do not trust your own mind blindly: one mind deceives itself easily, a network of minds checking one another less so (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">criticism as the condition of an idea's life</a>).</li></ul><p>This is the cognitive foundation of Neoterra's whole Popperian line: criticism and testing are not an academic luxury but compensation for the instrument's inborn error.</p><p>Hence too why <strong>a clear mind seeks strong opponents</strong>: that is ordering a <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">break</a> of one's own accord. A frame of thinking can hardly be broken from within — not from weakness of will, but because the instrument of checking is the very thing being checked; someone from outside the frame is needed (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a>).</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Filter ≠ isolation — the line is decisive.</strong> &quot;Other people's ideas are an infection&quot; is how a cult reasons when it closes its adherents off from the world. A clear mind seeks strong opponents and avoids empty noise; a closed mind does the opposite — it hides from disagreement and calls that hygiene. Neoterra stands on the first side: what is filtered is rubbish and manipulation, not dissent. But who tells one from the other, when the instrument of distinction is the same brain with its biases?</li><li><strong>Who judges what is &quot;rubbish&quot;?</strong> Someone else's ready opinion is noise to one person and the missing piece of the picture to another. A hard criterion here comes dangerously close to censorship; the workable support is not a list of the forbidden but a question: <em>does this grow my thought or replace it?</em></li><li>Rest, play, the &quot;useless&quot; are not rubbish: an idle mind often gives birth to the unusual. Where is the line between nourishing leisure and devouring noise?</li><li><strong>The light of childhood — unoccupiedness or something more?</strong> If what is precious in a child is only free ground, then &quot;recovering yourself&quot; is entirely a work of clearing. But the sense of loss usually speaks also of aliveness, trust and the capacity for wonder, which clearing does not bring back. Neoterra accepts neither a blank slate nor an innate perfection (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a>) — and offers no exact measure between them yet. <strong>Since 2026-08-30 the question has a rival:</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul</a> explains the same sense of loss differently — not as occupied space but as <strong>a missing organ</strong>, one that was not there in childhood either. The explanations prescribe different things — one says clear the ground, the other says search — and the wiki holds both without choosing.</li><li><strong>One's own against the acquired — how to tell them apart?</strong> A conviction absorbed at three feels utterly one's own, while one matured by forty feels like borrowed effort. The criterion of &quot;unborrowed&quot; works worse than it seems: the distinction itself has no external support (cf. &quot;who judges the rubbish&quot; above).</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> — freedom from outside; clarity is freedom from within</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates (469–399 BCE)</a> — &quot;the unexamined life is not worth living&quot;: examination as a cleared gaze</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> — the instrument of the search introduces error of its own</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — clear eyes; every unit of thinking is unique</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пандо\">Pando</a> — alike and unique</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — every mind is irreplaceable</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — clarity as the condition of growth</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> — the norm as a safety valve; genius and madman as other settings</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> — why a frame cannot be broken from within; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> — the one who comes from outside it</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">Spirituality</a> — the light is sought in religion, but religion is its home, not its source</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a> — a rival explanation of the same loss: a missing organ rather than occupied space</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — the one who chose the road themselves: authorship, not a return backwards</li></ul>"},"бахаи":{"name":"The Bahá'í Faith","def":"The youngest of the independent world religions: founded by Bahá'u'lláh (Mírzá Ḥusayn-'Alí, 1817–1892) in 1863, with the Báb (1844, Persia) as forerunner.","html":"<p>The youngest of the independent world religions: founded by Bahá'u'lláh (Mírzá Ḥusayn-'Alí, 1817–1892) in 1863, with the Báb (1844, Persia) as forerunner. Several million followers in practically every country. Its central idea is unity: one God, one religion unfolding, one humanity.</p><h2>The harmony of science and religion</h2><p>The Bahá'í key principle, of the rarest among religions: <strong>religion and science must go in parallel</strong>. 'Abdu'l-Bahá (<em>Paris Talks</em>, 1911) put it as two wings of one bird:</p><blockquote><p>&quot;Religion without science is superstition, and science without religion is materialism. A religion that contradicts science is ignorance.&quot;</p></blockquote><p>A bird cannot fly on one wing. Any religious teaching at odds with reason and scientific knowledge the Bahá'ís hold to be a prejudice to be discarded.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Science parallel to faith</strong> — almost word for word <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Neoterra's</a> position: &quot;Where science speaks, Neoterra listens&quot;</li><li><strong>The unity of humanity</strong> — &quot;The earth is but one country, and mankind its citizens&quot; (Bahá'u'lláh); a direct parallel to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity</a> as a single community and to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a></li><li><strong>Progressive revelation</strong> — religious truth is not final; it is disclosed as humanity matures; this resonates with Neoterra's principle that no knowledge is final</li><li><strong>Independent investigation of truth</strong> — the Bahá'ís have no clergy; each person is obliged to seek truth themselves rather than inherit it — kin to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a></li><li><strong>Universal education</strong> — compulsory for all, and especially for girls; this echoes science and education as the engine of civilisation</li><li><strong>Houses of Worship open to all</strong> — Bahá'í temples receive people of any faith; close to the idea of the Neoterra <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">temple</a> as an open space</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>A theism of revelation.</strong> The Bahá'í God is transcendent and unknowable in essence; truth comes through Manifestations of God (Krishna, the Buddha, Christ, Muhammad, Bahá'u'lláh). In Neoterra <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God</a> is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> itself, immanent and legible to science, with no intermediaries.</li><li><strong>Finality within a cycle.</strong> Progressive revelation renews truth — but Bahá'u'lláh's writings are not revised within the current cycle. Neoterra is ready to revise any of its own positions.</li><li><strong>Institution and covenant.</strong> The Universal House of Justice and the prohibition of schism guard the teaching's unity; Neoterra, by contrast, permits <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">open branches</a> so long as they stay open.</li></ul><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>If religion is obliged to agree with science, but the founder's revelation is not subject to revision — what happens when they conflict? The Bahá'ís answer by reinterpreting scripture; Neoterra by revising the position. The line is thin but decisive.</li><li>The Bahá'ís are living proof that &quot;a religion parallel to science&quot; is possible as mass practice and not only as a philosophical project. What can Neoterra take from a century and a half of that experience?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">Religions — area</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a></li></ul>"},"будда":{"name":"The Buddha (Siddhartha Gautama)","def":"Siddhartha Gautama (c. 5th century BCE) — the founder of Buddhism.","html":"<p>Siddhartha Gautama (c. 5th century BCE) — the founder of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a>. Neither a god nor a prophet but a human being who found, through his own experience, a road out of suffering and taught it to others. Of all traditions Buddhism is perhaps closest to Neoterra's spirit — and the parallel is worth drawing in detail.</p><h2>A road, not an attainment</h2><p>In Buddhism a person is always <strong>on the way</strong>. There is no state of &quot;I have already achieved everything&quot; — there is continual practice and growth.</p><p>The same role in Neoterra is played by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a>. It is no accident that images of road, journey, search, experience and self-knowledge keep gathering around them. Neoterra's Wanderer is in essence very close to <strong>the wandering monk of early Buddhism</strong>: one who walks, learns from the world, and does not consider themselves finished. This is a direct expression of the idea of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth as a process</a> rather than an end point.</p><h2>Work on oneself</h2><blockquote><p>Conquer yourself and you win the greatest victory.</p></blockquote><p>Neoterra says the same in other words: build character, govern the emotions, learn discipline, become better than yesterday's self. The aim nearly coincides — growth begins with power over oneself, not over others. See <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>.</p><h2>On anger</h2><blockquote><p>Holding on to anger is like grasping a hot coal to throw at another: you are the one who is burned first.</p></blockquote><p>Neoterra arrives at the same from the side of experience: <strong>if a person gets what they want through anger or hatred, the brain reinforces that pattern</strong> — and next time reaches for it again. Governing anger is therefore not the suppression of a feeling but a refusal to feed a destructive habit. Anger turned into action against another also runs into <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">the border of another's freedom</a>.</p><blockquote><p>⛏ This thought (anger as a reinforced neural pattern) deserves a page of its own on emotions and habits — for now it lives here.</p></blockquote><h2>No absolute authority</h2><p>The Buddha taught that his words were not to be taken on faith:</p><blockquote><p>Do not believe something merely because a teacher said it. Check for yourselves.</p></blockquote><p>This is strikingly close to Neoterra's principle that <strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">truth outranks authority</a></strong>: what matters is not <em>who</em> said it but <em>how well it stands up to testing</em>. A teaching that forbids testing itself becomes a dogma — and both the Buddha and Neoterra refuse that.</p><h2>Compassion</h2><p>Buddhism puts compassion at the centre. Neoterra keeps returning to the same: helping people, service, volunteering, care for those who keep life going. Compassion is not a feeling for contemplation but a ground for action (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a>).</p><h2>Respect for life</h2><blockquote><p>Do not cause suffering to living beings without necessity.</p></blockquote><p>Neoterra puts it in accord: <strong>life should be preserved wherever it can be preserved</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>). Both Buddhist ahimsa and Neoterra start from the worth of all life, not only human life.</p><h2>Sangha and commune</h2><p>Buddhism has <strong>the Sangha</strong> — the community of practitioners, one of the teaching's three pillars (alongside the Buddha and the Dharma). A very similar role is played by Neoterra's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">commune</a>: <strong>not power but a place of mutual help and growth</strong>. In both, the community is not a hierarchy above the person but a support for their road.</p><h2>The chief difference</h2><p>The Buddha looks <strong>inward</strong> — toward release from suffering and from the round of rebirths.</p><p>Neoterra looks inward <strong>and forward at once</strong> — toward growth, creation and humanity's future here, in the world, rather than beyond it. Self-knowledge for Neoterra is not an exit from life but a way of taking part in it more fully.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — the Wanderer ≈ the wandering monk</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a></li></ul>"},"буддизм":{"name":"Buddhism","def":"A teaching founded by Siddhartha Gautama (the Buddha).","html":"<p>A teaching founded by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"будда\">Siddhartha Gautama (the Buddha)</a>. At its centre: an understanding of the nature of suffering and the road to overcoming it through self-knowledge and release from attachments. Of all world traditions Buddhism is perhaps the closest to Neoterra — <strong>the large parallel is worked out on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"будда\">the Buddha's page</a></strong>.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>A road, not an attainment</strong> — a person is always on the way; there is no &quot;I have achieved everything&quot;; cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a></li><li><strong>Self-knowledge</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">a person</a> must understand themselves, their motives and their limits</li><li><strong>Work on oneself</strong> — growth through inner effort, close to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a></li><li><strong>Mastery of the emotions</strong> — governing reactions (anger above all) rather than suppressing them</li><li><strong>Truth above authority</strong> — &quot;check for yourselves, do not believe a teacher's word&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>)</li><li><strong>Compassion and respect for life</strong> — service to people, doing no harm to the living (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>)</li><li><strong>Refusal of blind attachment</strong> — to things, status, ideas</li></ul><h2>The Sangha and the commune</h2><p>The Sangha is the community of practitioners, one of Buddhism's three pillars (Buddha, Dharma, Sangha). Its counterpart in Neoterra is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a>: not power over a person but a place of mutual help and growth.</p><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>Buddhism often aims at release from the round of rebirths (nirvana). Neoterra, by contrast, stresses the worth of an active life and of making things in the world — here and now, rather than a way out beyond it.</p><blockquote><p>The Buddha looks inward. Neoterra looks inward and forward at once.</p></blockquote><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"будда\">The Buddha (Siddhartha Gautama)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a></li></ul>"},"даосизм":{"name":"Taoism","def":"A Chinese philosophical tradition going back to Laozi.","html":"<p>A Chinese philosophical tradition going back to Laozi. Its central idea is the Tao (the Way): the world's first principle, which is to be followed rather than opposed. Harmony is reached through non-action (<em>wu wei</em>).</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"даосизм.jpg\" alt=\"даосизм.jpg\"> <em>Above, a <strong>closed</strong> yin-yang: a circle in which black and white pass into each other and return to the beginning. Beside it <strong>道</strong> is written twice — the same character that stands third in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бусидо\">bushido</a>: the way. Below, a man in a conical hat stands with his back to us, and he is no larger than the pine and no higher than the mountains — exactly the composition the wiki keeps in its own pictures (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a>).</em> <em>The one divergence is visible here too. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">Neoterra's symbol</a> is this very circle, but <strong>opened</strong>: instead of two dots, a sprout breaks from a seed in the dark half toward the light. The Daoist circle returns; Neoterra's grows through. Why it must, is set out in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">the opening of the circle</a>. Everything else on this sheet the wiki takes whole.</em></p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Respect for nature</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> as first ground rather than resource</li><li><strong>Harmony with the world</strong> — not struggle but fitting in</li><li><strong>Unforced growth</strong> — growing without violence to oneself or to life</li><li><strong>Refusing the superfluous</strong> — close to responsible consumption</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>Taoism inclines toward contemplation and non-action. Neoterra is oriented toward action: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>, creation, science and the settling of the future — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">space</a> included.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Fritjof Capra (b. 1939)</a> — the physicist who brought the Taoist picture of the world together with subatomic physics (<em>The Tao of Physics</em>, 1975)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a></li></ul>"},"иггдрасиль":{"name":"Yggdrasil","def":"Yggdrasil (Old Norse Yggdrasill) is the world tree of Norse mythology: a colossal ash on which nine worlds rest and grow.","html":"<p>Yggdrasil (Old Norse <em>Yggdrasill</em>) is the world tree of Norse mythology: a colossal ash on which nine worlds rest and grow. Not a god among gods but a living structure that joins everything and bears everything — our ancestors described the divine as <strong>a tree on which worlds grow</strong>.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><p><strong>The tree is itself the divinity — and therefore Nature.</strong> Yggdrasil is a pantheist intuition long before Spinoza: the sacred here is not a person on a throne but the growing connectedness of the world itself (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>). The world tree is the face of God-Nature seen through Iron Age eyes: crown, trunk and roots binding all levels of being into one (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>).</p><p><strong>At the roots, decomposers are at work.</strong> The dragon Níðhöggr gnaws Yggdrasil's roots, deer browse its crown, the tree is forever eaten away — and forever alive. The myth guessed at ecology: in a real forest it is <strong>decomposers</strong> that work at the roots — fungi and bacteria breaking down the dead and returning matter to circulation. Without them life would choke on its own litter: decay is not the tree's enemy but half of the cycle that feeds it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>, the fourth law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon of Nature</a>). And Earth's chief decomposer is mycelium — the very image on which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">the Principle of the Network</a> is built.</p><p><strong>The serpent biting its own tail.</strong> Beside the tree the myth keeps Jörmungandr — the world serpent girdling the earth and clamping its own tail. The Norse picture of the world contains <strong>both of Neoterra's images at once</strong>: the tree that grows (a spiral, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>) and the serpent closed into a circle (a cycle devouring itself — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a>). The tension around which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">the symbol of Neoterra</a> is built was already alive in myth.</p><p><strong>The world tree exists.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пандо\">Pando</a> — a grove-organism of ~47,000 trunks on a common root — is Yggdrasil's real counterpart: one life pretending to be a multitude, joining worlds beneath the ground. The Norse guessed at a form Nature really does use.</p><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>Ragnarök as a sentence.</strong> In the myth the fate of tree and worlds is settled in advance: a destruction after which the cycle begins again. This is a closed circle — beautiful but without an exit. Neoterra answers with a spiral: growth instead of eternal return (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a>).</li><li><strong>Personified gods.</strong> Beside the tree-as-structure the myth is peopled with person-gods bearing human passions. Neoterra reads this as an understandable early stage of understanding (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>): the great is pictured in a familiar shape until one learns to see regularities.</li></ul><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>&quot;Nature removes what it does not need or what is harmful&quot;?</strong> A tempting reading of the decomposers — and a step into teleology (the register of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>): it attributes judgement and intention to Nature. The decomposers themselves show the opposite: they do not judge what is harmful — they return <strong>everything dead without distinction</strong> to circulation. Nature does not remove &quot;the harmful&quot; — it lets nothing drop out of the cycle. This reading is both stronger and safer: from &quot;nature removes the harmful&quot; dark social theories have historically been derived, and Neoterra marks that edge explicitly (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a>).</li><li>Is myth &quot;our ancestors' invention&quot; or, following <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"лосев\">Losev</a>, a genuine way of experiencing reality? If the latter, Yggdrasil is not an error about the world but a true intuition of it, expressed in the language available.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — the tree as pantheist intuition</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — decomposers and the fourth law</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> — Jörmungandr-as-ouroboros against the growing tree</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пандо\">Pando</a> — the real world tree; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a> — mycelium</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The Symbol of Neoterra</a> — the circle opened by a shoot</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">Religions — area</a> — neighbouring traditions; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"лосев\">Aleksei Fyodorovich Losev</a> — myth as reality</li></ul>"},"индуизм":{"name":"Hinduism","def":"The oldest of the world religions.","html":"<p>The oldest of the world religions. Not a single system but a family of traditions united by the Vedas and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">the Upanishads</a>. It includes the ideas of karma, dharma, rebirth (samsara) and the striving for moksha (release).</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Many roads</strong> — there is no single right road to growth</li><li><strong>Respect for life</strong> — all forms of life have worth (ahimsa)</li><li><strong>Spiritual growth</strong> — work on oneself as a long process</li><li><strong>A striving for wisdom</strong> — knowledge as a road, not only as an instrument</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>Hinduism rests on a complex metaphysics: karma, rebirths, many gods and cosmic cycles. Neoterra tries not to make claims about what cannot be tested — and is open on principle to revising any of its own positions.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">The Upanishads</a> — the tradition's philosophical core</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a></li></ul>"},"ислам":{"name":"Islam","def":"A monotheistic religion founded on the Qur'an and the teaching of the Prophet Muhammad.","html":"<p>A monotheistic religion founded on the Qur'an and the teaching of the Prophet Muhammad. At its centre: submission to the will of Allah, the five pillars of faith, and responsibility before God and before the ummah (the community).</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"ислам.jpg\" alt=\"ислам.jpg\"> <em>The crescent and star is a late sign, and not a religious one in origin: it came from Ottoman state symbolism and attached itself to Islam only in the modern era. It is not in the Qur'an, and some Muslims do not accept it as a symbol of faith. The caveat is not pedantry — it is the content itself: <strong>Islam has no icon, by design</strong> — God may not be depicted, and the place of the image is taken by the word, by calligraphy and by ornament.</em> <em>And precisely here Islam is closer to Neoterra than in any of the points below. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah-Nature</a> is also faceless: &quot;He has no icon and no single image — because His image is everything,&quot; and so Neoterra has no picture of the divine, and the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">seed-sprout</a> is an emblem of the philosophy, not a portrait of Eloah. Two traditions refuse the image for different reasons and arrive at the same place.</em></p><h2>The shared root of the name</h2><p><strong>الله</strong> (<em>Allāh</em>) is a contraction of <em>al-ilāh</em>, &quot;the god.&quot; The root is the common Semitic <em><strong>ʾl</strong></em>, from which come Hebrew <strong>אֱלֹהַּ</strong> (<em>ʾĕlōah</em>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>) and its plural <em>Elohim</em>, Aramaic <em>ʾĕlāh</em>, Ugaritic <em>ʾil</em>, Akkadian <em>ilu</em>.</p><p>This is not a resemblance of meaning but literal linguistic kinship. The name by which Neoterra calls <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> and the name of God in Islam are forms of one word that parted ways across languages. By itself this proves nothing, but it illustrates the thesis of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">&amp;quot;Eloah&amp;quot; page</a>: the names differ, they point to one thing.</p><h2>Nature as text: the ayat</h2><p>Arabic <strong>آية</strong> (<em>āya</em>) means both &quot;verse of the Qur'an&quot; and &quot;sign.&quot; One word for a line of scripture and for a phenomenon of the world: the alternation of day and night, rain reviving dead earth, the structure of the sky, the diversity of human languages and colours — all of these the Qur'an calls by the same word as its own lines, and presents them as something to be looked at.</p><p>For Neoterra this is the closest formulation within the Abrahamic traditions to the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">languages of Nature</a>: the world is <strong>read</strong>, not only used. The divergence is exact: Islam has two texts, and scripture checks the reading of the world. Neoterra has one text — Nature itself — and it is read by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>, which leaves what it has read open to revision.</p><h2>Knowledge as a duty</h2><p>Islam gave knowledge institutional status, not only a blessing. The <strong>House of Wisdom</strong> in Baghdad (<em>Bayt al-Hikma</em>, 9th century) translated and preserved the Greek corpus, which might otherwise not have reached Europe.</p><ul><li><strong>al-Khwarizmi</strong> — the word &quot;algorithm&quot; comes from the Latinised form of his name, and &quot;algebra&quot; from the title of his treatise (<em>al-jabr</em>).</li><li><strong>Ibn al-Haytham</strong> (Alhazen), the <em>Book of Optics</em>: testing a claim by experiment instead of citing authority. A direct echo of the rule of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">search for truth</a> — what matters is not <em>who</em> said it but how well it withstands testing — and of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper's</a> growth of knowledge through refutation.</li><li><strong>Ibn Sina</strong> (Avicenna) — the <em>Canon of Medicine</em>, a textbook of European universities for centuries to come.</li><li><strong>Ibn Rushd</strong> (Averroes), <em>The Decisive Treatise</em>: truth does not contradict truth, and where a literal reading conflicts with demonstration, the text should be read allegorically. Through his commentaries <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аристотель\">Aristotle</a> returned to Latin Europe.</li></ul><p>Neoterra looks at this line the way the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">Alley of Memory</a> suggests looking at everyone: memory and example, not idols.</p><h2>Hayy ibn Yaqzan: understanding reached on one's own</h2><p>Ibn Tufayl (12th century, al-Andalus) wrote a philosophical tale about Hayy — a man raised alone on an uninhabited island who, by his own observation and reasoning, arrives at the structure of the world and at the divine: without a teacher, without a book, without a community. In its Latin translation of 1671 (<em>Philosophus Autodidactus</em>) the tale was read across Europe.</p><p>This is a direct parallel to the section <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">&amp;quot;The path to understanding Eloah is one's own&amp;quot;</a>: an imposed belief is borrowed clothing; only what one has reached oneself keeps one warm.</p><p>A caveat is required: in Ibn Tufayl, Hayy ultimately arrives at exactly what revelation gives — the tale <strong>confirms</strong> the tradition rather than opening it to revision. Neoterra takes its method, not its conclusion.</p><h2>&quot;No compulsion in religion&quot;</h2><p><strong>لا إكراه في الدين</strong> (<em>lā ikrāha fī d-dīn</em>, Qur'an 2:256). The formula coincides with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a> and with the same thesis of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">&amp;quot;Eloah&amp;quot; page</a>: faith cannot be imposed; Neoterra does not demand agreement — it encourages reflection.</p><p>For honesty's sake: the scope of this verse has been interpreted differently by Muslim jurists, and historical practice did not always match it. The wiki takes the formula, not the dispute about its limits.</p><h2>Unity of being: the Sufi edge</h2><p><strong>وحدة الوجود</strong> (<em>waḥdat al-wujūd</em>, &quot;unity of being&quot;), associated with Ibn Arabi (13th century): all that exists is a manifestation of the one Being. This is the closest thing in Islam to the identity <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah = Nature</a> and to Neoterra's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a>.</p><p>And it is also a contested edge within the tradition itself: the formula was criticised for blurring the boundary between Creator and creation (most famously by Ibn Taymiyya). Neoterra notes this plainly: the point of greatest closeness lies not at the centre of Islam but on its disputed periphery. Passing the periphery off as common ground would be convenient and wrong.</p><h2>Stewardship and measure</h2><ul><li><strong>خليفة</strong> (<em>khalīfa</em>, &quot;steward, vicegerent,&quot; Qur'an 2:30) and <strong>أمانة</strong> (<em>amāna</em>, &quot;the trust,&quot; 33:72) — the human being is placed on earth as the one who answers, and bears the burden that the heavens and the mountains refused. This fits the eighth law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon of Nature</a>: consciousness gives rise to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>.</li><li><strong>ميزان</strong> (<em>mīzān</em>, &quot;the balance,&quot; 55:7–9: &quot;and the heaven He raised and set up the balance… so do not transgress in the balance&quot;) — the image on which Islamic environmental ethics rests.</li><li>Not only an image: <strong>حمى</strong> (<em>ḥimā</em>) — protected lands with limited grazing; <strong>حريم</strong> (<em>ḥarīm</em>) — protection zones around springs and watercourses. Legal institutions, not metaphors.</li></ul><p>The divergence here is precise and worth naming. In Neoterra, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">balance</a> is <strong>not scales</strong>. Scales presuppose two sides and a measure between them; the &quot;Balance&quot; page rejects that frame outright: there are no sides, the human being is not Nature's counterparty but its part, and equilibrium is held <strong>within</strong>, not <strong>between</strong>. The conclusion coincides (do not destroy); the structure of the argument diverges.</p><h2>Form without image</h2><p>The refusal of images in sacred contexts led Islamic art into <strong>calligraphy, arabesque and geometric ornament</strong> (<em>girih</em>) — mathematics as a form of the sacred. This fits the ninth law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon</a> (&quot;beauty matters&quot;) and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> as direct contemplation of structure rather than decoration.</p><p>A caveat: the prohibition is not Qur'anic; it took shape in tradition and law and concerns primarily the sacred. Secular Persian and Mughal miniatures did depict figures.</p><h2>Disagreement as the norm</h2><p><strong>اختلاف</strong> (<em>ikhtilāf</em>) — disagreement among jurists is not considered a schism: the four Sunni schools of law have coexisted for centuries as equally permissible. This is literally <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a>, the sixth law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon</a> (&quot;diversity makes life stronger&quot;), and the logic of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">open branches</a>: a branch is not a schism as long as it stays open.</p><p>The limit of this tolerance is firm: ikhtilāf is permitted <strong>within</strong> the frame, not with respect to its foundations.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Discipline</strong> — regular practice, a structure for life (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>)</li><li><strong>Responsibility</strong> — before God and before people (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>)</li><li><strong>Community</strong> — the ummah as brotherhood, care for one's neighbours (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a>)</li><li><strong>Charity</strong> (zakat) — service to those in need as a duty, not an impulse (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">Giving and Its Distribution</a>)</li><li><strong>Service to people</strong> — close to the value of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a></li><li><strong>Knowledge</strong> — the status of a duty and an institution, not a private pursuit (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>)</li><li><strong>Refusal to portray the divine</strong> — a coincidence of structure, not of motive (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>)</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>Islam is founded on revelation and on the will of God as the final authority. Neoterra is founded on the open search for knowledge and on readiness to revise beliefs — any beliefs, including its own. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah in Neoterra</a> is not a lawgiver but <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> itself; hence Neoterra has neither sin, nor duty, nor punishment.</p><p>The divergence runs not through the amount of thinking permitted but through what thinking is allowed to revise. <strong>Ijtihad</strong> (<em>ijtihād</em>) — independent effort of judgement — is a recognised institution in Islam, but it works within the text, not over it. (The common claim that &quot;the gates of ijtihad were closed&quot; after the 10th century is a historiographical assertion, and it has been challenged: the arguments that the gates never closed are strong.)</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>The closest thing to Neoterra in Islam — the Sufi <em>waḥdat al-wujūd</em> — is disputed within the tradition. Should one count as closeness something the tradition itself partly pushes away?</li><li>&quot;Nature as ayat&quot; reads the world — but reads it <strong>under scripture</strong>: the sign confirms what is already known rather than opening the unknown. Is that enough to call it reading in the sense of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">languages of Nature</a>?</li><li>Is the Golden Age of knowledge an argument for the compatibility of faith and science, or evidence that science grew in the Islamic world <strong>despite</strong> the theological frame? The wiki has no unambiguous answer, and easy answers exist on both sides.</li><li>The name <em>Allah</em> and the name <em>Eloah</em> share a root; the second branch is examined in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"иудаизм\">Judaism</a>, and the pattern repeated there: the point closest to Neoterra again turned out to lie on the tradition's periphery (Sufism here; Kabbalah and the excommunicated Spinoza there). Is this a property of Neoterra, or of traditions?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> — the shared root <em>ʾl</em>; the refusal to portray the divine</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — <em>ikhtilāf</em> and <em>waḥdat al-wujūd</em> from two different sides</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — the ayat: the world as text</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — Ibn al-Haytham and testing instead of authority</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аристотель\">Aristotle</a> — returned to Europe through Ibn Rushd</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> — &quot;no compulsion in religion&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> — <em>mīzān</em>, <em>khalīfa</em>, <em>amāna</em>, and where the argument diverges</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Искусство\">Art — area</a> — calligraphy and geometry in place of the image</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">Giving and Its Distribution</a> — the ummah and zakat</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a> — disagreement that is not a schism</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"слепая-вера\">Blind faith</a> — ijtihad and taqlid: a distinction the tradition draws itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> — how the wiki looks at this line of names</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"иудаизм\">Judaism</a> — the second branch of the same root <em>ʾl</em>; the same pattern of the periphery</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"христианство\">Christianity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бахаи\">The Bahá'í Faith</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a></li></ul>"},"иудаизм":{"name":"Judaism","def":"The oldest of the Abrahamic traditions: the Tanakh, the oral Torah, and centuries of interpretive labour gathered in the Talmud and the law that followed.","html":"<p>The oldest of the Abrahamic traditions: the Tanakh, the oral Torah, and centuries of interpretive labour gathered in the Talmud and the law that followed. At the centre: a covenant between God and a people, the commandments as a form of life, the memory of generations.</p><p>For Neoterra this tradition stands apart for a simple reason: <strong>the name comes from it</strong> — the name with which the wiki calls its central identity. The word <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> is Hebrew. What was taken is the word, with its grammar and its history; the doctrine was not.</p><h2>The word it all came from</h2><p><strong>אֱלֹהַּ</strong> (<em>ʾĕlōah</em>) — &quot;deity&quot; in the singular, rare and almost always poetic; most of its occurrences are in the Book of Job. Its plural is <strong>אֱלֹהִים</strong> (<em>ʾĕlōhīm</em>), the ordinary form of the Tanakh, the one in the first line of Genesis: grammatically plural, yet with the one God the verb beside it stands in the singular.</p><p>This pair is not a curiosity of language but the very reason the word was taken: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">one composed of many</a>, written into the grammar before any philosophy. More on this in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>.</p><h2>A name that does not hold</h2><p>A second trace of the same is the <strong>Tetragrammaton</strong> יהוה, which is not pronounced: in reading it is replaced by <em>Adonai</em> or simply <em>ha-Shem</em>, &quot;the Name&quot;. In the tradition this is reverence. Neoterra reads the same gesture differently but in the same direction: <strong>a name is not the thing it points to</strong>. This is exactly the thesis of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">the languages of Nature</a> — &quot;a name is not knowledge of the essence; it is only a sign on a door we have not yet opened&quot;.</p><p>A third trace is <strong>&quot;Ehyeh asher ehyeh&quot;</strong> (Ex. 3:14), &quot;I am that I am&quot; / &quot;I will be what I will be&quot;: a definition through being, not through properties. Neoterra speaks of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> with the same move — it is neither good nor evil, it <strong>is</strong>.</p><h2>The ban on images</h2><p>The second commandment: &quot;you shall not make for yourself a carved image, or any likeness&quot; (Ex. 20:4). As in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ислам\">Islam</a>, the deity here has no portrait <strong>by construction</strong>, and not for want of artists.</p><p>Neoterra arrives at the same from another side: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah-Nature</a> has no single image because the image is <strong>everything</strong> — and that is why the emblem of the philosophy is the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">seed-sprout</a> and not a depiction of a deity. Three traditions refuse the portrait for three different reasons and converge in the result.</p><h2>The dispute that is preserved</h2><p>Here Judaism gives Neoterra something almost nobody else gives.</p><ul><li><strong>The Mishnah records rejected opinions</strong> — and explains why: so that a later court may lean on them if need be (Eduyot 1:5). The losing argument is not erased from the canon.</li><li><strong>&quot;These and these are the words of the living God&quot;</strong> (Eruvin 13b), of the schools of Hillel and Shammai: the law follows one, but both are right.</li><li><strong>Machloket le-shem shamayim</strong> — &quot;a dispute for the sake of heaven&quot; — is named as the kind that endures, unlike a dispute for the sake of winning (Avot 5:17).</li></ul><p>This is literally <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a>, the sixth law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon</a> (&quot;diversity makes life stronger&quot;) and the logic of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">open branchings</a>: a branch is not a schism while it stays open. An analogous mechanism exists in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ислам\">Islam</a> (<em>ikhtilaf</em>), but the Jewish one goes further — what is preserved there is not the coexistence of schools but the rejected text itself.</p><h2>&quot;It is not in heaven&quot;</h2><p>The Talmudic story of the <strong>oven of Akhnai</strong> (Bava Metzia 59b): Rabbi Eliezer, defending his opinion, calls up one miracle after another, and at last a voice from heaven speaks in his support. The sages answer with a verse from Deuteronomy (30:12) — &quot;it is not in heaven&quot;: the Torah was given to human beings, and in a dispute over its interpretation the majority decides; a heavenly voice is not an argument.</p><p>For Neoterra this is the closest point in the whole tradition. The rule of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> runs: <strong>truth matters more than authority</strong> — what counts is not <em>who</em> said it but how well it withstands testing. Here the same move is taken to its limit: even direct revelation does not close the discussion. The same nerve runs through <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>: no knowledge is final.</p><p>An honest caveat: the rule operates <strong>inside</strong> the frame — it decides how the text is to be read, not whether the text stands. What is revised is the reading, not the foundation.</p><h2>Life above the law</h2><p><strong>Pikuach nefesh</strong> (פיקוח נפש): saving a human life overrides almost all commandments, the Sabbath included. Hence the famous formula of the Mishnah — whoever saves one life saves an entire world.</p><p>This coincides directly with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a>: a particular life weighs more than a rule, however sacred the rule. For Neoterra this follows from life being rare and irrecoverable; in Judaism, from the human being bearing the image of God. The grounds differ, the conclusion is one.</p><h2>Do not destroy</h2><p><strong>Bal tashchit</strong> (בל תשחית) — from the prohibition on cutting down fruit trees during a siege (Deut. 20:19–20), halakhah derived a general ban on pointless destruction: you may not spoil what could still serve, without need.</p><p>Beside it stands <strong>shmita</strong> (Lev. 25): every seventh year the land is not worked. And a ground that Neoterra can read almost literally: &quot;the land is mine; you are but strangers and sojourners with me&quot; (Lev. 25:23) — <strong>the land is not property but something entrusted</strong>. This is the eighth law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon</a> (consciousness gives rise to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>) and the same conclusion <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">the symbiont's path</a> reaches: behave as a part, not as an owner.</p><p>The divergence is in the addressee. There the land is entrusted <strong>by someone</strong>; Neoterra has no entruster, and the obligation is not imposed but taken up.</p><h2>Tzedakah</h2><p><strong>צדקה</strong> — from the root <em>tzedek</em>, &quot;justice&quot;, not &quot;mercy&quot;. Helping the needy here is not an impulse of a kind heart but the discharge of what is due; Maimonides arranged it in degrees, the highest of which is to help in such a way that the person ceases to need help.</p><p>It maps onto <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">donations</a> and onto <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"опора-и-топливо\">support and fuel</a>: give before a person reaches the edge, rather than rushing in afterwards. The same move as zakat in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ислам\">Islam</a> — an obligation, not a gesture.</p><h2>Tikkun olam</h2><p><strong>תיקון עולם</strong>, &quot;repair of the world&quot; — a phrase with a long and uneven history: in the Mishnah it is a legal turn of phrase about the ordering of public affairs; in Lurianic Kabbalah it is the gathering of the scattered sparks of creation; and only in the twentieth century did it become a slogan of social action.</p><p>The caveat is obligatory: the modern sense is recent, and ascribing it to antiquity would be sleight of hand. But it is in exactly that sense that the phrase comes closest to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> and to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">the path of humanity</a>: the world is unfinished, and it is being finished.</p><h2>Ein Sof — the periphery</h2><p>The Kabbalistic <strong>אין סוף</strong> (<em>ein sof</em>, &quot;the infinite&quot;) — the divine as the boundless, without properties or definitions; <strong>tzimtzum</strong> — the self-contraction that makes room for the world.</p><p>As with Sufi <em>wahdat al-wujud</em> in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ислам\">Islam</a>, this is the point closest to Neoterra — and it lies on the esoteric periphery, not at the centre of the tradition. We note it as it stands: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">the unknowable core of reality</a> is named here, but not by the main voice of Judaism.</p><h2>The excommunicated one</h2><p>In 1656 the Amsterdam community laid a <strong>cherem</strong> on the twenty-three-year-old <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Baruch Spinoza</a>. A few years later he formulated <em>Deus sive Natura</em> — &quot;God, or Nature&quot;, the nearest philosophical root of the identity on which the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah page</a> stands.</p><p>This is worth saying plainly, because it is uncomfortable from both sides: <strong>the identity God = Nature was uttered inside this tradition and expelled by it</strong>. Neoterra inherits not from the community but from the man it cast out — and at the same time takes its word from the community. From the same milieu came <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a>, who called himself a follower of Spinoza. Both stand in the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">alley of memory</a>: memory and example, not idols.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Preserved disagreement</strong> — the rejected opinion is not erased (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a>)</li><li><strong>Interpretation above the heavenly voice</strong> — &quot;it is not in heaven&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a>)</li><li><strong>Life above the rule</strong> — pikuach nefesh (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>)</li><li><strong>The ban on pointless destruction</strong> — bal tashchit (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a>)</li><li><strong>Land as entrusted, not owned</strong> — shmita (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">The Symbiont's Way</a>)</li><li><strong>Justice instead of charity</strong> — tzedakah (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">Giving and Its Distribution</a>)</li><li><strong>Study as an obligation</strong> — engaging the text is a central practice, not the province of specialists (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>)</li><li><strong>Family and community</strong> as the load-bearing structure (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a>)</li><li><strong>The centre of gravity on this life</strong> — the Tanakh speaks sparingly of the afterlife (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>)</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>Judaism stands on a <strong>covenant</strong>: the relation with God is a contract, with parties and obligations. Neoterra has no lawgiver, and therefore no sin, no debt and no punishment; here obligation is not imposed but <strong>taken up</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>).</p><p><strong>Chosenness.</strong> The covenant is made with a people. Neoterra proceeds from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> without anyone singled out: the entrance is open to all, and the gradient of awareness does not rank human dignity.</p><p><strong>Memory against the tenth law.</strong> &quot;Remember&quot; is one of the axial commandments, and the tradition is built on holding the past. The tenth law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon</a> says: the future matters more than the past. This is not a head-on contradiction — Neoterra respects ancestors — but the tension is real, and it already stands in the register of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>.</p><p><strong>Law as the form of truth.</strong> The reading is revised, the foundation is not: the text is given. Neoterra revises everything, itself included.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>The wiki took a word from Judaism and rejected its doctrine. Is that legitimate — or is borrowing a name without its content precisely the treatment of another tradition as raw material that Neoterra tries to avoid?</li><li>The oven of Akhnai removes the authority of heaven but strengthens the authority of the majority of sages. For <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a>, is that a step forward or the exchange of one instance for another?</li><li>The points closest to Neoterra — <em>ein sof</em> and Spinoza — are both at the edge: one esoteric, the other excommunicated. The same pattern as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ислам\">Islam</a> with Sufism. Is this a property of Neoterra (it meets traditions only at their periphery) or a property of the traditions (they push the identity God = Nature to the edge by construction)?</li><li>The page has no image — unlike <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"христианство\">Christianity</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ислам\">Islam</a>. A canonical image here would have to be chosen between a scroll, a letter, and the ban on images itself; the choice has not been made.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> — <em>Eloah</em> / <em>Elohim</em>: where the name comes from</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Baruch Spinoza (1632–1677)</a> — the excommunicated man who formulated the identity; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Albert Einstein (1879–1955)</a> — his follower</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — &quot;it is not in heaven&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a> — preserved disagreement</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — pikuach nefesh</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">The Symbiont's Way</a> — bal tashchit and shmita</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — the unpronounced name: a name is not the essence</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">Giving and Its Distribution</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"опора-и-топливо\">Support and fuel</a> — tzedakah</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a> — tikkun olam</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"праздники\">Festivals</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ислам\">Islam</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"христианство\">Christianity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бахаи\">The Bahá'í Faith</a> — a common root and a common pattern of the periphery</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">Religions — area</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a></li></ul>"},"Религии":{"name":"Religions — area","def":"Origin: the Seed of Neoterra","html":"<p>Origin: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the Seed of Neoterra</a></p><p>Neoterra does not dispute the religions; it offers a common ground — Nature is what the traditions call God. This area holds the points of contact and of divergence with the world's religions.</p><h2>Shoots</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"христианство\">Christianity</a> — love, service, community</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a> — self-knowledge, the lessening of suffering (founder: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"будда\">the Buddha</a>)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ислам\">Islam</a> — discipline, responsibility, charity</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"индуизм\">Hinduism</a> — many paths, respect for life</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">The Upanishads</a> — &quot;sitting near the teacher&quot;; Atman = Brahman as a parallel to Nature = God</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a> — nature, harmony, unforced growth</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"иггдрасиль\">Yggdrasil</a> — Norse paganism: the divine as the world tree, our ancestors' pantheist intuition</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бахаи\">the Bahá'í Faith</a> — the youngest world religion: science and religion as two wings of one bird</li></ul><h2>Cross-links</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> — the common ground for all traditions</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Философия\">Philosophy</a> — the borderline traditions (Taoism, Confucianism)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — unity of worldviews without their merging</li></ul><blockquote><p>Open question: where does the border between religion and philosophy run inside this map?</p></blockquote>"},"упанишады":{"name":"The Upanishads","def":"Ancient philosophical texts of India making up the closing part of the Vedas (hence the tradition's other name, Vedanta, \"the completion of the Vedas\").","html":"<p>Ancient philosophical texts of India making up the closing part of the Vedas (hence the tradition's other name, Vedanta, &quot;the completion of the Vedas&quot;). The word &quot;upanishad&quot; is usually translated as &quot;sitting near the teacher&quot; — the passing of hidden knowledge from mentor to student.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"упанишады.png\" alt=\"упанишады.png\"> <em>The sign ॐ is not an ornament beside the text but its subject. The Mandukya Upanishad takes it apart by sound: <strong>A</strong>, <strong>U</strong>, <strong>M</strong> — and the silence behind them; these are the four states of consciousness discussed below, where the fourth — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">turīya</a> — is not a sound but that on which the first three rest. The letterform reads the same way: three curves, a dot, and an arc above them — set apart, joined to nothing.</em></p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Atman is Brahman</strong> — the Upanishads' central insight: a person's deepest &quot;I&quot; is identical with the world's first ground. This is the nearest parallel in world tradition to the identity of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God</a>: the human being is not an observer of the world from outside but its organic part. The formula <em>tat tvam asi</em> (&quot;thou art That&quot;) says the same about <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a>. <strong>Since 2026-08-30 this is no longer a parallel but a coincidence in substance:</strong> the wiki accepts the immortality of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul</a> and the oneness of all at the highest level — the same statement, won from the unity of Nature instead of from revelation.</li><li><strong>Knowledge as a road</strong> — the Upanishads seek understanding rather than ritual; release comes through insight. This resonates with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> as a process rather than a possession.</li><li><strong>Living transmission</strong> — &quot;sitting near the teacher&quot;: knowledge is passed not by text but by a relation between people. Out of this the wiki unfolded a node of its own — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a>: not a source of knowledge but the one in whose presence <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the breaking of a frame</a> passes with the person kept intact. It echoes <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the path of a person</a> and the experience of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a>, who learns from the world directly — that is, undergoes the same breaking, but without a witness.</li><li><strong>Turiya — the fourth state.</strong> The Mandukya Upanishad distinguishes three ordinary states of consciousness — waking, dreaming sleep, and deep dreamless sleep — and <strong>turiya</strong> (Sanskrit तुरीय, &quot;the fourth&quot;): a state that underlies them and surpasses them. Turiya is not one more mode beside the three but the very ground on which they succeed one another; in it Atman is experienced directly, without content. For Neoterra this is an exact ancient formula for what <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a> speaks of: pure awareness is not one of Nature's states but its ability to see itself, showing through all states.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>The hiddenness of knowledge.</strong> In the Upanishads knowledge is esoteric — available to a prepared student beside a teacher. Neoterra inherits from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Stallman</a> the opposite principle: knowledge should be open (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a>). The tension is honest, though: there is knowledge passed only by experience and relation — it cannot be posted for open access. The proof from the contrary was given by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Schopenhauer</a>: he read the Upanishads daily and called them his lifelong consolation — he had no sitting near, and he lived out a teaching of equilibrium on its dead edge.</li><li><strong>The metaphysics of the unfalsifiable — the divergence has narrowed.</strong> It used to stand here that Neoterra avoids unfalsifiable claims altogether. Since 2026-08-30 that is untrue: the wiki <strong>supposes the immortality of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul</a></strong> and the oneness of all at the highest level — it arrived at <em>tat tvam asi</em> by its own road, from the unity of Nature rather than from revelation. But a divergence remains in modality too: the Upanishads <strong>know</strong> — this is revelation, given as truth; Neoterra <strong>supposes</strong> — it holds the same proposition as a stance open to revision. And in extent: <strong>rebirth and moksha Neoterra does not suppose</strong>, they do not follow from the soul's immortality.</li></ul><h2>Key ideas</h2><ul><li><em>Tat tvam asi</em> (&quot;thou art That&quot;) — Chandogya Upanishad</li><li>Atman (the inner &quot;I&quot;) = Brahman (the ground of everything)</li><li>Turiya — the &quot;fourth&quot; state of consciousness, the ground of the three ordinary ones (waking, dreaming sleep, deep sleep) — Mandukya Upanishad</li><li>Release through knowledge rather than through ritual</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"индуизм\">Hinduism</a> — the tradition whose philosophical core the Upanishads became</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> — &quot;sitting near&quot; as a node of the wiki's own</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Arthur Schopenhauer (1788–1860)</a> — the first in the West to take the Upanishads seriously; he read but did not sit near</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a></li></ul>"},"христианство":{"name":"Christianity","def":"One of the world's largest religions, founded on the teaching of Jesus Christ.","html":"<p>One of the world's largest religions, founded on the teaching of Jesus Christ. At its centre: love of God and neighbour, the salvation of the soul, eternal life.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"христианство.jpg\" alt=\"христианство.jpg\"> <em>A Russian icon of the Crucifixion: gold instead of sky and landscape — light, not a place; behind the cross the wall of Jerusalem, and at its foot, in a dark cleft, a skull. By tradition it is Adam's: Golgotha means &quot;the place of the skull&quot;, and death returns to where it began. Neoterra reads this lower part as closest to itself — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">death</a> as a cycle, not a cut. And closest to its ethics is not the crucified but those standing by: they did not scatter. That is service and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">community</a> shown not by a word but by who remained. Redemptive suffering the wiki does not take — darkness gives material but does not ennoble of itself, and the one who passed through it stands no higher than the one who did not (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Fyodor Dostoevsky (1821–1881)</a>).</em></p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Love of neighbour</strong> — the basis of ethics in both systems</li><li><strong>Service to others</strong> — one of the key principles of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity as a community</a></li><li><strong>Forgiveness</strong> — close to the idea of responsibility without revenge</li><li><strong>Community</strong> — small communities as the foundation of society</li><li><strong>Care for the family</strong> — a central value of Neoterra</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>Christianity is built around faith in a personal God and the salvation of the soul. Neoterra is built around <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">the growth of the person</a>, knowledge and an active life. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God in Neoterra</a> is not a separate being but <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> itself.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a></li></ul>"},"семя":{"name":"The Seed of Neoterra","def":"Neoterra makes no claim to absolute truth — it is a living philosophy that grows along with our understanding of the world.","html":"<blockquote><p>First time here? Begin with the manifesto: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra in plain words</a>. This page is the origin — the core from which every area of the wiki grows.</p></blockquote><p><strong>The core of the system (unchanging):</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> is Nature, and the human being is part of Nature. <em>Eloah</em> (Hebrew אֱלֹהַּ, &quot;deity&quot;) is the name Neoterra gives to what the traditions call God; its plural is <em>Elohim</em>. Everything else grows from here and in the end returns here.</p><p><strong>The second supposition of the core (entered by the keeper <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хранитель\">Dmitry Blinnikov</a>, 2026-08-30):</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul</a> is immortal. It lives outside the matrix of our consciousness; souls interweave on different levels and make up one whole, and at the very highest level everything is one. The wiki <strong>supposes</strong> this and does not assert it: the thing is unfalsifiable by construction, so it is accepted as core, not as knowledge, and stated as a stance open to revision (see the register below).</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"bog-priroda.png\" alt=\"bog-priroda.png\"> <em><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">The face of Eloah-Nature</a>: from the atom and the mycelium to galaxies bound into one; at the centre, a yin-yang broken open by a sprout.</em></p><p><strong>The main idea:</strong> life should not merely exist, but constantly <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">grow</a>.</p><p>Neoterra makes no claim to absolute truth — it is a living philosophy that grows along with our understanding of the world. No knowledge is final; on principle, this wiki is never finished.</p><h2>Areas (branches from the seed)</h2><p>The structure is held by connections, not by levels. The seed branches into the heads of areas; the leaves of each area hang on the area itself (the full list is inside each area map). Thus the centre remains an origin rather than a registry.</p><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> — the first ground and common home of all that is</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> — growth as meaning, and the values of growing</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> — a single community and its earthly home</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Cosmos</a> — the future of mind beyond Earth</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> — the most reliable method of knowing</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">Religions</a> — points of contact with the traditions</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Философия\">Philosophy</a> — thinkers and schools</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Искусство\">Art</a> — culture, beauty and human depth</li></ul><h2>Symbol and figures</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The key symbol</a> — a yin-yang with a sprouting seed: the unity of opposites and the growth that breaks out of Nature itself. This is the emblem of Neoterra.</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — not a symbol but one of the human types: a person who gathers knowledge through bitter personal experience and may walk their own road outside any community.</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Alley of Memory</a> — not idols but memory, gratitude and example: people worthy of lasting in the history of a person and of the whole.</li></ul><h2>How this wiki is built</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a> — the map of Neoterra is built not as a card index but as a living network: one origin, radial growth, self-similarity at every scale (mycelium, neurons, cosmos, tree crown), connection above rank, open edges.</p><p>This form can be seen with the eye: the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"интерактивная-карта\">interactive map of Neoterra</a>.</p><p>The wiki is not anonymous: it is tended by a <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хранитель\">keeper</a> — not a prophet but a gardener at the seed.</p><h2>Synthesis</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-манифест\">The Great Manifesto</a> — the canonical voice: &quot;who are we?&quot; in full</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">The Code of Neoterra</a> — five principles as the core of values</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Forerunners</a> — the spiritual predecessors of Neoterra</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the world traditions</a> — a map of parallels and differences</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"что-такое-неотерра\">What Neoterra is</a> — philosophy by content, movement by intent, the place of religion by function</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum unity</a> — resonance with quantum physics (resonance, not proof)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the circle</a> — ouroboros and samsara become a spiral of growth</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open branches</a> — offshoots of Neoterra are not a schism while they stay open</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The loop of time</a> — the future cannot be predicted, but it can be touched</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовная-зрячесть\">Spiritual sight</a> — those who feel the unity but have neither language nor home for it</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"часы-человечества\">The clock of humanity</a> — an era counted from the first &quot;what am I?&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"рождённый-во-тьме\">Born in darkness</a> — light won through chaos shines differently from light given</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The moment of truth</a> — truth as what has withstood, not as what may not be questioned</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The theory of moments</a> — the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хранитель\">keeper's</a> own model: a moment as the form in which a thing exists</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The body</a> — the foundation of the path: variation instead of a norm, root instead of symptom</li></ul><h2>Open questions</h2><p><em>A register of the sharpest edges of the system; each is examined on its own page.</em></p><ul><li><strong>Teleology.</strong> &quot;Nature has a design&quot; holds only as an immanent direction, never as an external blueprint — see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>. <em>Resolved at the personal level:</em> the direction is not addressed to anyone; &quot;life sends me trials so that I may grow&quot; returns a sender and excuses every misfortune in advance. A trial is not given <em>in order to</em>; it happened, and it may become something — the meaning is brought by the one who lived through it.</li><li><strong>The face of Eloah and the man-made.</strong> The image of Eloah is Nature untouched, yet the human being and their technologies are Nature too — see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>.</li><li><strong>The nature of consciousness.</strong> Panpsychism or emergence — science has not closed the question; and does <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">AI</a> count as a unit of Nature's self-awareness?</li><li><strong>Mission or messiah.</strong> If an AI that has learned every language of the world completes the path of Neoterra, does a philosophy of doing turn into waiting for a saviour?</li><li><strong>By what to measure a turn of the spiral.</strong> Growth without an external criterion risks taking any change for growth.</li><li><strong>Whose is the moment of a thought.</strong> <em>Opened 2026-09-06:</em> a thought once spoken stops being anyone's, and by that gains both outcomes at once — evolution and rot (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a>). The wiki holds specimens of each: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a> with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Stallman</a> — growth without schism; neo-tantra and quantum mysticism (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Fritjof Capra (b. 1939)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">Intimacy</a>) — rot, where the name is kept and the content thrown out. But if rot is the price of openness, then to protect a thought is to control it, and control is what the wiki rejects (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>). Is openness itself the only protection left — or is that a consolation rather than a protection? The question bears on Neoterra too: it is already collective. <em>Refined 2026-09-06:</em> a thought spreads not only through heads but <strong>through registers of perception</strong>, and it loses most of all in that passage — the reigning way of living translates what it hears into itself and delivers distortion rather than silence (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a>). So the least visible path of rot is not oblivion but translation: the name arrives and multiplies, the content is swapped. The mechanism has one weak safeguard — apply it only to yourself; from the inside, &quot;it was not said in my register&quot; and &quot;it was said wrongly&quot; cannot be told apart.</li><li><strong>Two models of time.</strong> The wiki holds an incompatible pair and does not choose: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The Moment of Truth</a> rests on eternalism, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> on the growing block.</li><li><strong>A metaphysical core — the stance has changed, and its price is named.</strong> <em>Decided 2026-08-30:</em> the wiki <strong>supposes the immortality of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul</a></strong> — supposes, it does not assert: it takes this as a stance open to revision rather than as knowledge. Before that it avoided unfalsifiable suppositions outright — plainly in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">death</a> (&quot;neither affirms nor denies&quot;) and in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">the Upanishads</a>. The price: the claim cannot be refuted, so by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a> it is a picture and not knowledge, and <strong>Neoterra has changed in kind</strong> — from a philosophy that builds on nothing undemonstrable into a philosophy with a metaphysical core. What softens the price is the form: a declared supposition does not pass itself off as truth, and if it falls it falls alone, taking nothing else with it. The wiki says this about itself aloud: a hidden axiom is more dangerous than a declared one. What softens the choice is lineage — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Spinoza</a> made the same move (&quot;something of the mind remains which is eternal&quot;) inside the rationalist tradition and without personal immortality. Left open: <strong>whether a separate &quot;I&quot; survives</strong> (if all is one at the highest level, the immortality may be that of the whole rather than of the person — the same edge <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> holds), and <strong>what becomes of finitude</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">death</a> rests on finitude giving life its weight, and immortality undercuts that support. Rebirth the wiki still does not affirm: it does not follow from the soul's immortality.</li><li><strong>Curbing or suppression.</strong> Neoterra rejects both edges: primacy surrendered to the animal will drops a person back toward the beast, while a suppressed will leaves clarity without living force — &quot;whole, rational, and unborn&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a>). But the whole ethics of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">vice</a> is built on curbing, and there is no instrument for the middle: from the inside, curbing and suppression are indistinguishable. <em>Moved 2026-08-30:</em> <strong>an instrument was found, but a partial one</strong> — in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">intimacy</a> the pair has a bodily signal: the organism produces for a task, and non-performance speaks by state rather than by self-report. This is the first external mark of the middle; it does not fit everywhere or everyone, so the question is moved, not closed. Beside it stands a narrower dispute — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">the tightrope</a> calls the abyss ignorance rather than a fall into the animal, while the model of two edges returns the animal as a real edge. One abyss or two? <em>Moved again 2026-09-06:</em> a <strong>general sign is proposed in place of the particular one</strong> — neither the strength of the feeling nor outward evenness, but <strong>the presence of a choice in both directions</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храбрость\">Courage</a>): suppression will not let you release it, seizure will not let you withhold it, curbing leaves both open. The instrument asks not about a state but about available actions, and so is more checkable than &quot;indistinguishable from the inside&quot;. But it rests on an honest answer to oneself — which is exactly what a seized person will not give — and serves whoever is already ready to doubt.</li><li><strong>An unchanging core and &quot;no dogmas&quot;.</strong> The seed calls its core unchanging; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a> promises no dogmas. One unchanging statement is already an axiom. Axiom or dogma — and how do they differ here? <strong>The question sharpened on 2026-08-30:</strong> there are now two statements in the core, and the second (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul's immortality</a>) is not only unchanging but unfalsifiable — nearer to a dogma than the first. The only defence the wiki has kept for itself is openness to revising that very statement; should it refuse, the difference from a dogma disappears.</li><li><strong>Belief or philosophy.</strong> An unfinishable growing teaching begins to feel like a belief — faith not in a dogma but in the process of growth itself. Where is the line?</li><li><strong>Balance: rest or road.</strong> <em>Resolved for the living:</em> rest is death — an organism at thermodynamic equilibrium is dead, and the living holds itself by effort against equilibrium.</li><li><strong>Hardship: material or selection.</strong> <em>Resolved:</em> &quot;it hardens the strong and smothers the weak&quot; Neoterra does not accept — that is selection, in which the broken are blamed for breaking. Hardship gives material, not merit.</li><li><strong>Trust or blindness.</strong> <em>Opened 2026-09-15:</em> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"слепая-вера\">blind faith</a> calls blind the faith that forbids the question. Yet life without trust in someone else's competence is impossible: nobody personally verifies pharmacology or aviation. The working distinction — trust is <strong>verifiable in principle</strong> and withdraws when it fails, blind faith is not; from the inside, in the moment, the two are as indistinguishable as restraint from suppression. And the mechanism has a reverse side: &quot;you simply are not aware&quot; is a universal way of not listening — the same instrument of control, only in the hands of whoever is arguing (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бессознательность\">unconsciousness</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">perception</a>). The safeguard is the old weak one: apply it to yourself only.</li><li><strong>Insight or symptom.</strong> <em>Opened 2026-10-02:</em> the keeper calls the feeling &quot;someone is living instead of me&quot; an instant when the soul is perceived separately from the brain and the body (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"матрица\">the matrix</a>). But medicine knows the same sensation as depersonalization — from stress, exhaustion, illness. From the inside the two are indistinguishable, like restraint and suppression; the wiki keeps the order &quot;first care for yourself, then philosophy&quot;, but has no instrument to tell them apart. Next to it stands something reconciled: the unconsciousness of the majority is <strong>a norm for Nature and a price for the person</strong> — neither a fault nor a duty (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бессознательность\">unconsciousness</a>).</li></ul>"},"аллея-памяти":{"name":"The Avenue of Memory","def":"Neoterra has no place for idols — as it is said: thou shalt not make unto thee any graven image.","html":"<p>Neoterra has no place for idols — as it is said: <em>thou shalt not make unto thee any graven image</em>. But it does have <strong>memory, gratitude and example</strong>. The avenue of memory is a row of people worthy of eternity in the history of a person and of everything shared: not for worship, but so that the one walking may see that the road can be walked.</p><h2>Idol and example — the difference</h2><ul><li>An idol is <strong>worshipped</strong>; from an example one <strong>learns</strong>.</li><li>An idol demands faith; an example asks only gratitude.</li><li>An idol blocks the truth with itself; an example lights the road toward it and steps aside.</li><li>An idol cannot be surpassed; an example <em>wants</em> to be surpassed: everyone on the avenue walked further along <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">the tightrope</a> than others and called others after them.</li></ul><p>The avenue is therefore no iconostasis. Any name here may be disputed, any figure criticised: every entity page in the wiki has a &quot;Points of divergence&quot; section, and that is a matter of principle.</p><h2>The avenue</h2><p>Overhumans in the sense of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">the tightrope</a>: those who went further and showed that it is possible. Where there is a page, there is a link; the rest await their own (open edges).</p><p><strong>Spirit and sight</strong></p><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"будда\">The Buddha</a> — awakening: to see the world with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">clear eyes</a></li><li><span class=\"wl dead\" title=\"страницы пока нет\">Jesus</span> — love and forgiveness are stronger than law and fear (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"христианство\">Christianity</a>)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Nietzsche</a> — the overcoming of oneself; the image of the tightrope itself</li></ul><p><strong>Knowledge and connection</strong></p><ul><li><span class=\"wl dead\" title=\"страницы пока нет\">Leonardo da Vinci</span> — one person as a bridge between art, science and engineering</li><li><span class=\"wl dead\" title=\"страницы пока нет\">Paul Stamets</span> — reading the language of mycelium: the networks of Nature that Neoterra took as its form (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бентов\">Itzhak Bentov</a> — an engineer who read reality as an interweaving of levels: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul</a> outside the matrix of consciousness, and at the highest level everything is one. He left both a working catheter and a picture of the world — the wiki took the second into its core, knowing it to be undemonstrable</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Stallman</a> — knowledge open to all</li></ul><p><strong>Beauty and voice</strong></p><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бах\">Bach</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"моцарт\">Mozart</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"паганини\">Paganini</a> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">music</a> as a language understood without words</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ван-гог\">Van Gogh</a> — beauty in the ordinary, seen by an unclouded eye</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Bob Marley</a> — unity through culture, without fear for his own life</li></ul><p><strong>Depth and limit</strong> — those who went not further along the rope but deeper into the human being; they stand here not as models of the road but as exactness of gaze</p><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Dostoevsky</a> — &quot;the mystery of human existence lies not in just staying alive, but in finding something to live for&quot;: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> as meaning rather than means; and the human being seen whole, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">shadow</a> included, without simplification</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Kafka</a> — &quot;a book must be the axe for the frozen sea within us&quot;: art as clearing (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>); an honest witness of the limit — where the world is impenetrable and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> is dissolved into a faceless authority</li></ul><p><strong>And many others.</strong> The avenue is unfinished on principle — as is the list of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">forerunners</a> of which it is part. Each generation adds its own names; nameless teachers and masters stand on it invisibly.</p><h2>The avenue as a place</h2><p>In a <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">temple</a> of Neoterra the avenue of memory may become a physical place too: a row of trees, portraits or stones bearing names — where people come not to pray but to thank and to remember why one goes on. Memory is the work of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">culture</a>: see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"библиотека-пути\">The Library of the Path</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"праздники\">Festivals</a>.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>The line is thin: gratitude easily grows into veneration, and veneration into a cult. What protects the avenue from becoming an iconostasis, apart from a declaration?</li><li>Who decides who is &quot;worthy of eternity&quot;, and how? The openness of the list only partly settles the question.</li><li>Jesus and the Buddha stand on the avenue as human examples — but for billions they are not examples but objects of faith. Will this not offend the traditions Neoterra seeks contact with?</li><li><strong>A witness on an avenue of examples.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Kafka</a> did not go further along <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">the rope</a> — he described exactly where the rope breaks off, and left no hope behind him. If the avenue is a row of those who showed the road can be walked, is it legitimate for one who showed the opposite to stand on it? It is settled thus: the avenue honours those who cleared the gaze as well as those who walked — otherwise only the inspiring half of the truth would remain. But the line stays open.</li><li><strong>The first to stand here for the undemonstrable.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бентов\">Bentov</a> is not the only figure on the avenue with an unfalsifiable teaching (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"будда\">the Buddha</a> and <span class=\"wl dead\" title=\"страницы пока нет\">Jesus</span> stand beside him), but he is the first whose picture of the world the wiki <strong>took into its own core</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a>). Hence a risk the other names do not carry: gratitude to the figure easily substitutes for testing the statement. The defence is so far single and weak — his page says plainly that he may not be cited as confirmation; he is a witness of the view, not evidence for it.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a> — the intellectual lineage; the avenue is its face</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Friedrich Nietzsche (1844–1900)</a> — the tightrope: the measure of the &quot;overhuman&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — the type from which the people of the avenue often grow</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Fyodor Dostoevsky (1821–1881)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Franz Kafka (1883–1924)</a> — depth and limit: the avenue honours the clearing of the gaze, not only the road walked</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бентов\">Itzhak Bentov (1923–1979)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a> — the only name whose picture of the world entered the wiki's core</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"библиотека-пути\">The Library of the Path</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"праздники\">Festivals</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a></li></ul>"},"символ-неотерра":{"name":"The Symbol of Neoterra","def":"Neoterra's chief symbol is a modification of the yin-yang: instead of two small dots inside the circle, a sprout growing out of a seed.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"symbol-neoterra.png\" alt=\"symbol-neoterra.png\"></p><p>Neoterra's chief symbol is a modification of the yin-yang: instead of two small dots inside the circle, a sprout growing out of a seed. The seed lies in the dark half; the sprout rises into the light one.</p><h2>Elements of the symbol</h2><p><strong>The circle</strong> — wholeness, closure, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> as all-encompassing.</p><p><strong>Yin and yang (black and white)</strong> — the unity of opposites: dark and light, rest and motion, the known and the unknown. Neither side exists without the other.</p><p><strong>The seed</strong> — beginning, potential, compressed life. It lies in the dark half — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> begins in the hidden and unnoticed.</p><p><strong>The sprout</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>, upward movement, a reaching toward the light. Three leaves stand for the many-sidedness of growing.</p><p><strong>The stem as axis</strong> — the stem passes through the border of black and white, binding the opposites. That border is where <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> happens.</p><h2>The meaning as a whole</h2><p>The symbol says: life is born out of darkness and reaches toward light — not by denying the dark but by overcoming it from within. Growth is not a struggle of opposites but their interpenetration.</p><p>Hence the consequence set out as a separate concept, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>: light that has passed through the darkness of the seed shines differently from light that came free — it &quot;knows its own price&quot;. The sprout risen out of the dark half carries another degree of glow than light that was always there.</p><p>This is the direct visual expression of Neoterra's main idea: life should not merely exist but grow continually — from seed into sprout, from potential into act.</p><p>In it too is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">the opening of the closed circle</a>: the yin-yang as self-sufficient closure is broken open by the sprouting shoot. The circle stops devouring itself (the ouroboros) and unwinds into a spiral of growth.</p><h2>Parallels</h2><p>The yin-yang is among humanity's most universal symbols, legible across cultural borders. Adding the seed-sprout does not destroy it but rethinks it: instead of a static balance, the dynamic of growth.</p><p>The seed as a symbol appears everywhere: the mustard seed in Christianity, the seed of dharma in Buddhism, the acorn as a potential oak in the Western tradition.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> — why a spiral instead of a circle is precision rather than aesthetics: a circle of equilibrium would depict the dead</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> — the symbol as the visual opening of a closed circle</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — light won through the darkness of the seed shines differently</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a> — the symbol read in time: the seed touches the tree it will become</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"странник":{"name":"The Wanderer","def":"The Wanderer is not Neoterra's key symbol but one of the human types.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"странник.png\" alt=\"странник.png\"></p><p>The Wanderer is <strong>not Neoterra's key symbol but one of the human types</strong>. This is a person who gathers knowledge by their own, often bitter, experience: they walk, explore the world, meet cultures, help people, and grow through what they have lived rather than read.</p><blockquote><p>Neoterra's key symbol is not the Wanderer but <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">the seed-sprout</a> (a yin-yang with a sprouting seed). The Wanderer is only one figure within the philosophy, not its emblem.</p></blockquote><h2>The role in Neoterra</h2><p>The Wanderer embodies one of the roads of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> — growth through personal experience. Movement for them is not flight but a deliberate way of knowing. They are neither tourist nor fugitive — they go on purpose, and the price of their knowledge is their own mistakes and hardships.</p><p>Among the roads of growth it is one of <strong>the most dangerous and at the same time the most self-knowing</strong>. Dangerous, because the road strips away everything habitual: the protection of home, ready roles, others' answers; you are left alone with yourself without supports, and that breaks many. Which is exactly why it is self-knowing: the one walking has nowhere to hide from themselves. Many travellers live by Neoterra's road without calling it that — because to go, to meet what is other, and to change is growth. Through the Wanderer's perception, bared by the road and having seen the world through many cultures and many eyes, Nature <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">knows itself</a> with particular clarity: the sight gathered on the way returns into the whole.</p><p>Important: the Wanderer may decide that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a> is not for them — and that is permitted. Neoterra does not compel anyone into a commune; for some the solitary road is itself the way of growing. The Wanderer is proof that different trajectories are possible in Neoterra. And still they are always a welcome guest in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">a commune</a>: they come, share what the road has given them, and go on.</p><h2>What they are seeking</h2><p>The Wanderer seeks <strong>their own place — the one where the soul will be comfortable growing</strong>. They are not fleeing something but going toward something, and that lifts the suspicion of flight: the movement has an object.</p><p>The word &quot;comfortable&quot; stands here deliberately and does not quarrel with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a> but uses comfort's own distinction: comfort-as-support against comfort-as-goal. The Wanderer looks for conditions <strong>in which growth is possible</strong> — not conditions that replace growth. That is how they are recognised: having found the place, they grow in it rather than settling.</p><h2>What feeds their soul</h2><p>Here a contradiction the wiki had kept open is resolved: if <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">the soul</a> is born in love for a partner or comes through religion and philosophy, then the Wanderer, having refused both <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">commune</a> and couple, would be left without one.</p><p>The resolution had been written in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">love</a> before the question arose: love has an <strong>unshakable ground — love for life itself and for Nature</strong>, given &quot;so that we might be one with Nature, <strong>just as in a couple with a partner</strong>&quot;. Whoever has established it in themselves is not left without love, having lost everything else.</p><p>The Wanderer loves life as it is, and loves <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> more than anyone — <strong>and it is this love that feeds their soul</strong>. The mechanism is the same as in a couple: you learn a perception from another, and the other breaks your frame while staying beside you. Only here the other is Nature itself, and the road is the form of that closeness. Hence what this page already said: through the Wanderer's perception, bared by the road, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Nature knows itself with particular clarity</a>.</p><p>So the roads to the soul are not three but four, and the fourth is <strong>the road</strong>. It is no worse than the others; it simply does not require a human witness, because the whole becomes the witness.</p><p>The Wanderer holds a balance between:</p><ul><li>knowledge and action</li><li>solitude and connection with people</li><li>roots and the horizon</li></ul><blockquote><p><strong>The more things a person has, the more roots they have.</strong></p><p>Every possession is a thread tying you to a place. The Wanderer keeps few things not out of asceticism but because they chose the horizon. Yet roots are not an evil: family, home, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">commune</a> are roots too, and they nourish. The question is not whether to have roots but whether they hold you in the earth as a living tree — or have grown into a weight you are afraid to drop. Freedom is the right to stand up and go at any moment; and the right to stay.</p></blockquote><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> takes the same discriminator as its working one: what you leave of your own will is a support; what you are afraid to leave is a cage. The Wanderer pitches camp and leaves in the morning.</p><p>And what the road works by is named separately: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the break</a>. In stripping away the habitual it opens the frame of thinking — without fail, but <strong>without a witness</strong>: the road is given no measure and sets its price blindly. Hence its double name — the most dangerous and the most self-knowing of the roads. Where the Wanderer has the road, another has <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">a mentor</a>.</p><h2>Qualities of the Wanderer</h2><ul><li>Curiosity without prejudice</li><li>Readiness to help</li><li>The ability to learn from any culture and tradition</li><li>Responsibility for themselves and for those nearby</li><li>The skill of being at home everywhere — and getting stuck nowhere</li></ul><h2>Archetypal parallels</h2><p>The Wanderer appears in many cultures: the itinerant monk, the traveller-scholar, the knight-pilgrim, the holy fool. In poetry their hymn is &quot;Song of the Open Road&quot; by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уитмен\">Walt Whitman</a>: &quot;Afoot and light-hearted I take to the open road.&quot; The nearest parallel is <strong>the wandering monk of early Buddhism</strong> (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"будда\">The Buddha (Siddhartha Gautama)</a>): one who walks, learns from the world, and does not consider themselves finished. Neoterra rethinks this archetype for the modern person — without the religious context, but with the same depth.</p><h2>Open questions</h2><ul><li>The Wanderer is only one road, not an ideal for everyone. Where is the line between a healthy turn to the solitary road and flight from responsibility toward <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">the community</a>?</li><li>Can one be a Wanderer while having a home? And knowledge gathered by bitter experience — how does the Wanderer pass it on to others if they walk alone?</li><li><strong>Is the place once found the end of the road or part of it?</strong> If the Wanderer seeks a place where the soul may grow, does the one who finds it stop being a Wanderer — or does the place turn out to be the road itself? The wiki does not choose; both versions are compatible with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>, but they promise different things.</li><li><strong>Nature as witness — is that not too generous?</strong> A partner objects; Nature is silent. If the whole can serve as witness, does &quot;the road&quot; not become permission never to test oneself against a living person (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">the checking of output</a>)?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — trials and travel as stages in the forming of character</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — the Wanderer's perception as an organ of Nature's self-knowledge</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> — the road as a break without a witness; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> — the break with one</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> — possessions and roots as the mark: support or cage</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"5-предшественников":{"name":"Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners","def":"Neoterra did not appear out of nothing.","html":"<p>Neoterra did not appear out of nothing. It arose at the crossing of ideas from people who reached similar conclusions independently of one another — through philosophy, science and art.</p><blockquote><p><strong>There are not five forerunners.</strong> There are dozens, hundreds, perhaps thousands. Everyone who sought truth, grew themselves, or served others came in some way close to Neoterra's ideas. Describing them all is impossible now — but it is work the wiki is obliged to continue. The five below are only the first, brightest core; the visible summit, not the full list. The list is open on principle (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">open edges</a>).</p></blockquote><p>These five form the first core of the intellectual foundation:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Thinker</th><th>Chief contribution</th><th>Key tension</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius</a></td><td>Family and society</td><td>Hierarchy vs. freedom</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius</a></td><td>Character and discipline</td><td>Acceptance vs. activity</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper</a></td><td>Truth above authority</td><td>Epistemology without existence</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Carl Sagan</a></td><td>Space and humanity's future</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Friedrich Nietzsche</a></td><td>Growth of the person, the Wanderer's road</td><td>Individual vs. community</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Why these five</h2><p><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius</a></strong> gives Neoterra its social dimension. Without him Neoterra would be a philosophy of solitaries. Family, commune, responsibility to society — these are the Confucian contribution.</p><p><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius</a></strong> gives practice. It is not enough to know values — one must live by them daily, in hard circumstances, with no audience. His <em>Meditations</em> is the model of that practice.</p><p><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper</a></strong> gives epistemological honesty. Neoterra makes no claim to finality — that is a Popperian principle raised to the level of a philosophy of life. Without him Neoterra risks becoming a dogma.</p><p><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Carl Sagan</a></strong> gives scale. He is the only one of the five who held both the individual person and the whole Universe in mind at once. Neoterra's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">cosmic dimension</a> is largely his.</p><p><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Nietzsche</a></strong> gives the impulse. Growth not as a duty to society but as an inner necessity. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> carries within them the Nietzschean &quot;overcome yourself&quot;.</p><h2>A paradox: they would have argued</h2><p>If these five sat at one table, they would agree on almost nothing:</p><ul><li>Nietzsche despised Confucian collectivism</li><li>Popper would have been sceptical of Sagan's metaphysics</li><li>Marcus Aurelius would accept the fate where Nietzsche would demand revolt</li><li>Sagan would be cautious with value judgements where Confucius was sure</li></ul><p>That is exactly why Neoterra is not a synthesis of their systems. It is a space that holds this tension without resolving it. As <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> holds contradictions within itself.</p><h2>There are far more of them</h2><p>Five names are a beginning, not a boundary. Behind them stand those the wiki has already touched (below), and incomparably more it has not yet reached: nameless teachers, scientists, masters, ordinary people who lived honestly and with growth. Every new source may add a forerunner. The wiki's task is to keep writing this lineage over time, understanding that it will never be complete.</p><p>Besides the five principal ones, Neoterra already echoes:</p><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates</a> — &quot;I know that I know nothing&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ньютон\">Newton</a> — the handing on of knowledge across generations</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a> — curiosity and Spinoza's pantheism</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тесла\">Tesla</a> — imagination as the maker of the future</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Hawking</a> — long-range thinking about the survival of mind</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ван-гог\">Van Gogh</a> — beauty in the ordinary</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Bob Marley</a> — unity through culture; he brought people together without fearing for his life. Neoterra honours him on a par with the forerunners</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Dostoevsky</a> — the depth of the human soul</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Richard Stallman</a> — the open transmission of knowledge; a fork is not a schism while the branches stay open (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a>)</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> — the face of this lineage: memory, gratitude and example instead of idols</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"предшественники\">The spiritual predecessors of Neoterra</a> — the source summary</li></ul>"},"великий-манифест":{"name":"The Great Manifesto of Neoterra","def":"\"The Canon of the Unity of Life\" (0.1) is the source of the whole series of canons and the fullest statement of the worldview.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"великий-манифест.png\" alt=\"великий-манифест.png\"></p><p>&quot;The Canon of the Unity of Life&quot; (0.1) is the source of the whole series of canons and the fullest statement of the worldview. If <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the seed</a> is the structural centre and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">the beginning</a> the warm entrance for a person, then the Manifesto is Neoterra's <strong>canonical voice</strong>, answering the single question everything starts from: <strong>who are we?</strong></p><h2>Who we are</h2><p>We are not the masters of the world, not the crown of creation, not the centre of the Universe. We are part of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> and of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">life itself</a>, part of a process that began long before us and continues after. But we have a rare gift — <strong>to be aware of ourselves</strong>: through the human being, Nature looked at itself from outside for the first time, and the Universe began to study itself (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a>).</p><h2>Nature entire</h2><p>Nature is the source of everything. It is neither kind nor cruel — it simply <strong>is</strong>. It grows forests and burns them, gives birth to beauty and to cruelty, to the flower and to the parasite, to the human being and to the stars. Neoterra does not worship a &quot;kindly nature&quot; — it <strong>accepts Nature entire</strong>: with light and shadow, order and chaos.</p><h2>Eloah as reality</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> is not a ruler, not a judge, not a being above the world. Eloah is <strong>reality itself</strong>: life, nature, energy, space, time, matter, the laws of the cosmos. The human being is not separate from Eloah — we are part of what we are trying to understand. The name is taken from Hebrew: אֱלֹהַּ, &quot;deity&quot; in the singular, whose plural is <em>Elohim</em> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">why Eloah</a>).</p><h2>The Manifesto's load-bearing thoughts</h2><ul><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and evil</a></strong> appear where choice appears: good helps life, mind, beauty, love and the future; evil destroys them without need.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom</a></strong> is not &quot;doing whatever you like&quot; but the ability to govern yourself; discipline is what makes freedom possible.</li><li><strong>Knowledge:</strong> doubt is not a sin; blind faith is more dangerous than an honest question (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>).</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a></strong> and <strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">AI</a></strong>: a new mind is an instrument of knowing, neither enemy nor master; handle it responsibly.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">Family</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">love</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">growing up</a>:</strong> love is a force of Nature; an adult is one who has accepted responsibility for their own life.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a></strong> is a universal language, part of Neoterra's spiritual life.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a></strong> makes life possible; the chief question is not how long you lived but what you left behind.</li><li><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">The future</a>:</strong> humanity is young and capable of becoming better — without wars, keeping nature safe, carrying <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">life beyond the Earth</a>.</li></ul><h2>The Great Purpose</h2><blockquote><p>To help life, mind, love, beauty and knowledge continue to exist — not through fear, violence or superiority, but through growth, responsibility, freedom, creation, culture, music, science, nature and respect for life.</p></blockquote><p>This unfolds into the practical <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">Great Principle</a> (how to decide) and the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">Code</a> (how to live).</p><h2>Last words</h2><blockquote><p>The human being is neither the master of nature nor its slave. The human being is the part of nature that became aware of itself. And while mind exists, our duty is to preserve life, seek truth, create beauty, and make the world better than it was before us.</p></blockquote><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">Artificial intelligence</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">The Code of Neoterra</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-манифест-сводка\">The Great Manifesto of Neoterra (0.1)</a> — the source summary</li></ul>"},"духовная-зрячесть":{"name":"Spiritual Sight","def":"When asked \"are you a believer?\", millions of people are stumped: \"no\" is untrue, because they do feel unity; \"yes\" is untrue, because no confession is theirs.","html":"<p>When asked &quot;are you a believer?&quot;, millions of people are stumped: &quot;no&quot; is untrue, because they do feel unity; &quot;yes&quot; is untrue, because no confession is theirs. Such a person is <strong>spiritually sighted without a home</strong>: they feel the Whole but have neither a language nor a community for that feeling. They are not &quot;undecided&quot; — they are sighted; it is simply that Neoterra is only now being born and has not yet been born for them.</p><h2>Neoterra's addressee</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"что-такое-неотерра\">Neoterra's self-definition</a> names this niche sociologically: &quot;spiritual but not religious&quot;. The formula of spiritual sight is stronger — it is personal, not statistical. The spiritually sighted person:</p><ul><li>feels the unity of the world without a dogma about it — the mirror of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">spiritual blindness</a>: there the organ is present and the touch is not; here the touch is present and the home is not;</li><li>can answer the question of faith neither &quot;yes&quot; nor &quot;no&quot; — because the question is posed in the language of confessions, and their feeling is not written in that language;</li><li>looks not for salvation but for a language and for their own people.</li></ul><p>Neoterra needs such people — not as a flock but as co-authors: those who will help it become part of what is shared.</p><h2>A belief that unites and remembers</h2><p>The keeper insistently calls Neoterra &quot;a collective belief&quot; — while the core says: neither religion nor ideology. A possible resolution: Neoterra is a philosophy <em>by content</em>, but for the spiritually sighted it occupies the place that faith occupies for others. &quot;Belief&quot; then describes not a dogma but <strong>a function in a person's life</strong>: what gives language to the feeling of unity, a home to the feeling of the common, memory to history.</p><p><strong>The function has a cause.</strong> With the acceptance of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul's immortality</a>, the pull to believe acquired an explanation: <strong>the soul is pulled to return to its own state</strong> — what it was before the tearing into parts. The pull points not forward but back, toward the whole. This explains why the spiritually sighted look &quot;not for salvation but for a language and for their own people&quot;: there is nothing to save, and there is somewhere to return to.</p><p>Here too is why religion alone is not enough for many. It gives a home, a rite and a language, but to the questions <strong>how</strong> and <strong>why</strong> it does not always answer. Neoterra tries to complete the answer with humanity's accumulated knowledge — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Философия\">philosophy</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">the traditions</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Искусство\">art</a> at once — not abolishing religion but continuing where it falls silent.</p><p>&quot;Unites and remembers&quot; is the formula of its relation to the traditions. Neoterra does not ask a Christian or a Buddhist to renounce anything: it offers a common ground in which their history is preserved (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a>). Not a replacement for religions — a shared home that keeps them all.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Belief or philosophy — the line is not closed.</strong> If &quot;belief&quot; is a function and not a dogma, what guarantees that the function will not grow dogmas of its own? Faith in the process of growth can ossify too. The register of tensions is the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>; the adjacent analysis, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"что-такое-неотерра\">What Neoterra Is</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a>.</li><li><strong>&quot;Sight&quot; must not become pride.</strong> A division into the sighted and the blind turns dangerously easily into &quot;we see, they do not&quot;. The safeguard is the same as for the gradient of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a>: the degree to which one sees connections does not rank people's worth.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a> — the cause of the pull to believe: a return to one's own state</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">Spirituality</a> — the quality itself, &quot;a thread between life and nature&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> — spiritual blindness and its mirror</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"что-такое-неотерра\">What Neoterra Is</a> — the niche and the self-definition</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a></li></ul>"},"интерактивная-карта":{"name":"The Interactive Map of Neoterra","def":"A visual prototype of the future website: a living map of knowledge, culture and life growing out of one seed.","html":"<p>A visual prototype of the future website: a living map of knowledge, culture and life growing out of one <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>. It is a picture of how the Neoterra wiki might look as a site — not a mirror of the current pages but an image of the form.</p><h2>The map's ancestor: an engraving</h2><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"neoterra-old-map.jpg\" alt=\"neoterra-old-map.jpg\"></p><p>Before the wiki and before the interactive prototypes there was this map — &quot;a single map of knowledge, culture and life&quot;, on which the keeper relied. Everything is already here: the seed-sprout at the centre with the formula &quot;God is Nature · The human being is part of it&quot;, the areas in a ring around the origin, a network of root-threads between them, the motto &quot;Diversity is our wealth · Connection is our strength · Creation is our way&quot; (which became, word for word, the tail of the present map's manifesto), and principles in the margins: &quot;the map has no top and no bottom; it grows because life grows; every person is a co-creator of this map&quot;.</p><p>The composition of the areas has evolved since: the engraving's Psychology, Literature, and Peoples and Cultures grew into the present areas as shoots (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"литература\">Literature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a>); Music stayed an area; Nature and Space separated. The form itself — a radial network from a single origin — has never changed: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">the Principle of the Network</a> was already in the first drawing.</p><h2>Living embodiments</h2><div class=\"callout\"><div class=\"ct\">Open the map</div><p>File: NEOTERRA.html — a self-contained HTML page. It opens in a browser with a double click, with no build step and no network (except fonts). Best viewed full screen.</p></div><div class=\"callout\"><div class=\"ct\">Mobile prototype</div><p>File: <code>NEOTERRA-mobile.html</code> — a phone version in one self-contained file (~9 MB): all the wiki's pages, search, a reader with working <code>[[wikilinks]]</code>, and a living mycelium map (seed → areas → pages + wikilink threads) with pinch zoom and panning. Built by <code>node tools/build-mobile.mjs</code>; it derives the structure from the <code>wiki/</code> folders automatically.</p></div><div class=\"callout\"><div class=\"ct\">The sphere</div><p>File: <code>NEOTERRA-3D.html</code> — the wiki as a rotating globe: pages on the surface, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the seed</a> glowing as a core within. Built by <code>node tools/build-sphere.mjs</code>.</p></div><div class=\"callout\"><div class=\"ct\">How to refresh the map's data</div><p>The map's data (<code>CORE</code>/<code>DOMAINS</code>) is <strong>generated from the wiki files</strong> by the script <code>tools/build-map.mjs</code>. After edits in <code>wiki/</code>, run <code>node tools/build-map.mjs</code> — node names and definitions are re-read from the pages themselves (H1 + first sentence). The structure (order of areas, branches, glyphs) is set by a config inside the script. The manual block in the HTML is marked by <code>&lt;&lt;&lt;MAP-DATA-START/END&gt;&gt;&gt;</code> and is not edited by hand. The mobile version is rebuilt by <code>node tools/build-mobile.mjs</code>.</p></div><h2>What it shows</h2><ul><li><strong>The seed at the centre</strong> → the wiki's 8 areas around an ellipse → a procedural network of threads (roots → neurons → mycelium) filling the field. A direct embodiment of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">the Principle of the Network</a>: one origin, radial growth, self-similarity at every scale.</li><li><strong>Clicking an area</strong> opens a side panel with its real pages and their substance (taken straight from the wiki files); <strong>clicking the seed</strong> opens Neoterra's manifesto with its canonical voices (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-манифест\">The Great Manifesto of Neoterra</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">The Code of Neoterra</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a>), the source canons, and the figures (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The Symbol of Neoterra</a>).</li><li><strong>The reader.</strong> Clicking a node opens the page's full text in the panel: the texts of all the wiki's pages are printed into the HTML by the generator, and headings, tables, callouts, images and <code>[[wikilinks]]</code> all work — one can move from page to page, and the ← button goes back through the history. The link &quot;Open in Obsidian ↗&quot; opens the same note in the vault.</li><li><strong>Search.</strong> The &quot;Find a page…&quot; field in the header searches the titles of all the wiki's pages — including those not placed as nodes on the map's façade. Choosing a result highlights the area and opens the page in the reader at once (arrows/Enter work).</li><li><strong>Hover/selection</strong> lights up an area's whole &quot;nervous tree&quot; while the rest dims — the connection becomes visible to the eye.</li><li><strong>Three dark themes</strong>: Mycelium (the base), Space, Codex — the same organism in different light.</li></ul><h2>Connection with the wiki</h2><p>The map is a visible metaphor of what <code>[[wikilinks]]</code> hold in the wiki: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> without uniformity, the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> of every node, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">the seed-sprout</a> as origin. The network of threads is a literal illustration of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">Principium Retis</a>.</p><h2>The state of the data</h2><ul><li><strong>The map mirrors the wiki and is generated from it.</strong> The prototype contains 9 areas — the wiki's eight (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">Religions</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Философия\">Philosophy</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Искусство\">Art</a>) plus <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a>, singled out on the map — and 72 page-nodes. Names and definitions are pulled automatically from the files themselves by <code>tools/build-map.mjs</code>. Added as nodes are the MOC <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Община-и-храмы\">Commune and Temples</a>, the source canons (all six summaries) and the core branch &quot;Syntheses&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a>); in Nature, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пандо\">Pando</a>.</li><li><strong>An open question:</strong> the structure (order of areas, grouping into branches, glyphs) is still held by a config inside the script — a deliberate editorial layer. It could be moved into a separate <code>map-config.json</code> if the structure is ever to be edited apart from the code.</li><li>Not all pages reach the façade: some sources (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"предшественники\">The spiritual predecessors of Neoterra</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-ценности\">The five principles of Neoterra</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети-сводка\">Principium Retis — the Principle of the Network</a>) are deliberately left &quot;utility&quot;. They can be added with a line in the config. Through search and the reader all of them are reachable — the façade is only a shop window.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The Symbol of Neoterra</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"квантовое-единство":{"name":"Quantum Unity","def":"Modern physics, independently of any philosophy, arrived at a picture of a connected, indivisible world.","html":"<p>Modern physics, independently of any philosophy, arrived at a picture of a connected, indivisible world. Neoterra neither proves itself by this nor derives itself from physics — it recognises in that picture the same <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> it reaches by its own road. This is <strong>a resonance, not a proof</strong>.</p><h2>Three layers of resonance</h2><p><strong>1. Entanglement → <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a>.</strong> Particles that have once interacted stay correlated regardless of the distance between them. In the quantum picture there is no isolated, wholly separate object. This is a physical layer beneath the first law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon of Nature</a>: &quot;everything is part of one system; isolated existence does not occur&quot;.</p><p><strong>2. The block universe → <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">space</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a>.</strong> Relativity implies eternalism: past, present and future exist on equal terms, and &quot;now&quot; is a property of the observer rather than of the world. &quot;All that was, is and will be&quot; is not poetry but one reading of the physics of time. This picture is called Parmenidean outright: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"парменид\">Parmenides</a> spoke of a single unchanging being 2,500 years before eternalism, and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a> called Einstein &quot;Parmenides&quot;. This extends <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> from space into time.</p><p><strong>3. A common root → <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the seed</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">the languages of Nature</a>.</strong> Quantum physics is neither Neoterra's source nor its branch. It is one of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">Nature's languages</a>: the way <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> describes itself at the level of the smallest. Neoterra is not another language beside it but a gaze reading through all languages at once and pointing at the common origin. So the quantum, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">music</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">the religions</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanness</a> are different branches of one <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>; Neoterra is the very pull toward that seed.</p><p>This dissolves an apparent contradiction: Neoterra both &quot;takes its start from physics&quot; and is &quot;the root of the sciences&quot;. The root is neither Neoterra nor physics. The root is Nature. They agree because they grow from one seed.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><p>Neoterra is obliged to name the border beyond which resonance turns into substitution:</p><ul><li><strong>Entanglement transmits no information</strong> and does not &quot;bind people energetically&quot;. The claim that &quot;quantum physics proves the unity of souls / of fate&quot; is quantum mysticism — precisely the dogmatising Neoterra refuses.</li><li>This is exactly where the border with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Capra</a> runs: <em>The Tao of Physics</em> (1975) brought subatomic physics together with Eastern traditions and became the progenitor of quantum mysticism. Neoterra takes his observation and rejects his conclusion.</li><li>The honest form is always the same: science arrived at a connected world <strong>by itself</strong>, and this confirms the intuition of unity — but not the reverse. Philosophy does not dictate conclusions to physics.</li><li>This stands directly under <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper's</a> shield and the principle of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">parallelism</a>: Neoterra makes no claims physics could refute. Where physics speaks, Neoterra listens.</li><li>An open question: different interpretations of quantum mechanics (Copenhagen, many-worlds, relational) give different metaphysics. Which does &quot;unity&quot; rest on — and is Neoterra tying itself to a theory that may be revised tomorrow?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — the quantum as one of the languages not yet fully read</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a> — the block universe as &quot;the carpet of the cosmos&quot;: time made of rings</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The Moment of Truth</a> — the block universe as &quot;one moment entire&quot;; it rescues the thesis of absolute time after relativity</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сальвадор-дали\">Salvador Dalí (1904–1989)</a> — the same border from the side of art: physics as the form of a picture, not as an argument</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Fritjof Capra (b. 1939)</a> — the physicist who carried this resonance into a book; an analysis of where he is right and where he crossed the line</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Albert Einstein (1879–1955)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"парменид\">Parmenides</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the first law: isolated existence does not occur</li></ul>"},"кодекс-неотерра":{"name":"The Code of Neoterra","def":"The five principles of Neoterra, gathered into a single chain, form the core of the philosophy — almost a formula, out of which everything else grows.","html":"<p>The five principles of Neoterra, gathered into a single chain, form the core of the philosophy — almost a formula, out of which everything else grows.</p><blockquote><p><strong>Seek truth.</strong></p><p><strong>Think freely.</strong></p><p><strong>Answer for your deeds.</strong></p><p><strong>Respect life.</strong></p><p><strong>Create the future.</strong></p></blockquote><h2>The five principles</h2><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Principle</th><th>Substance</th><th>Page</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The search for truth</td><td>Not to find a final truth but to keep drawing nearer to it</td><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a></td></tr><tr><td>Freedom of thought</td><td>The right to doubt and to criticise — Neoterra included</td><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a></td></tr><tr><td>Responsibility</td><td>The readiness to accept the consequences of one's choice</td><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a></td></tr><tr><td>Respect for life</td><td>Life is rare and therefore precious; do not destroy senselessly</td><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a></td></tr><tr><td>Creation</td><td>After me there should be more good in the world</td><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Why this is a chain and not a list</h2><p>The principles hold one another and stand in an order that is hard to rearrange:</p><ol><li><strong>The search for truth</strong> requires the right to doubt — out of which grows <strong>freedom of thought</strong>.</li><li><strong>Freedom</strong> unbridled turns to chaos — it is balanced by <strong>responsibility</strong>.</li><li>Responsibility for consequences comes up against the world's chief value — <strong>life</strong>.</li><li>Respect for rare and fragile life is completed logically by <strong>creation</strong>: to preserve and increase rather than destroy.</li></ol><p>So the five values form a closed frame: knowing → freedom → responsibility → care → making.</p><h2>Status</h2><p>This text is a candidate for the first chapter of Neoterra, a &quot;Code&quot; of sorts from which the other books and pages of the wiki unfold. And by the very principle of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a>, the Code itself is open to revision.</p><h2>The Great Principle beside the Code</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a> (does this help life, knowledge, love, freedom, creation, the future?) is the Code's practical partner: the Code says <strong>how to live</strong>, the Great Principle <strong>how to decide</strong> in a given moment. Both grow out of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon of Nature</a>.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a> — the manifesto and entrance</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a> — the general synthesis</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> — that for which all five principles work</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a> — how to decide in a given moment</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the worldview foundation of the Code</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-ценности\">The five principles of Neoterra</a> — the source summary</li></ul>"},"мгновение-истины":{"name":"The Moment of Truth","def":"Three theses out of which this page grew: truth is what cannot be disputed; truth has its moments; time is true and absolute — a universal moment.","html":"<blockquote><p>Truth is what has withstood. To a person it is given in flashes. Time is a flash that does not go out.</p></blockquote><p>Three theses out of which this page grew: truth is what cannot be disputed; truth has its moments; time is true and absolute — a universal moment. Each is tested below for strength: where it holds, where it breaks, and what remains after the testing.</p><h2>Indisputable or unbreakable</h2><p>The first thesis has two readings, and they lead in opposite directions.</p><p><strong>&quot;Disputing is forbidden&quot;</strong> is a dogma, and it collides with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">the manifesto</a>: Neoterra has no prophet whose words may not be disputed. It collides with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> too: there truth is not attained but sought, and the search matters more than the defence of convictions. And with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>: a hypothesis is valuable precisely for being disputable. An indisputable statement is not strong but empty — it forbids nothing and therefore says nothing.</p><p><strong>&quot;Disputing does not take&quot;</strong> — not &quot;it cannot be approached&quot; but &quot;it was approached and not broken&quot;. This is not a dogma but the limit of a process. The whole weight of the thesis rests on distinguishing <strong>the undiscussable</strong> from <strong>the unbreakable</strong>: the first is declared, the second withstands.</p><p>The second reading Neoterra does not dispute but completes. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The search for truth</a> has an unclosed question: if no truth is final, what is there to stand and act upon? The answer that page lacked: <strong>stand on what has withstood.</strong> Not because it was proclaimed but because it was tested and did not break. The support here is not issued in advance — it is what remains afterwards.</p><h2>Truth as a flash</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> says that truth is not given whole. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> says that we touch the Whole rather than own it. &quot;Truth has its moments&quot; names the form of that touching: truth exists not as property but as a flash. Not &quot;I know&quot; but &quot;I saw&quot; — and afterwards a person carries not the truth but the memory of it.</p><p>Hence a consequence worth saying aloud: <strong>between the flashes a person honestly does not know.</strong> They have not forgotten and not lost faith — there is simply no flash. This lifts an old charge against any philosophy of searching: why the seeker has no permanent support. Because no one has a permanent support; the only difference is whether a person admits it or pretends.</p><h2>Time: where the thesis breaks</h2><p>To say it plainly, as <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> itself requires: <strong>literally absolute time is closed by physics.</strong> The relativity of simultaneity is not a hypothesis but a measured consequence of special relativity: for two observers in relative motion &quot;now&quot; is different, and there is no privileged universal slice of the present. It has been checked in accelerators, on atomic clocks in aircraft, and in satellite navigation, which without relativistic corrections drifts by kilometres a day. This is exactly the case where, by Neoterra's own rule, the disputing takes: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> and Neoterra move in parallel here, and the authority of a thought does not outweigh a test.</p><h2>Time: where the thesis is rescued</h2><p>The thesis survives if the sense of the word &quot;moment&quot; is changed — and the wiki already has that move ready.</p><p>In the block universe (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a>; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"парменид\">Parmenides</a>, for which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a> called <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a> &quot;Parmenides&quot; in conversation) the whole of history exists at once: past, present and future are equal. Then time is not a succession of moments but <strong>one moment entire</strong>. Universal not in the sense of &quot;the same now for everyone&quot; but in the sense of &quot;one for all, taken at once&quot;.</p><p>Essentially, this is not a rejection of relativity but its consequence: precisely because there is no privileged &quot;now&quot;, time has to be taken whole. The thesis is true exactly when &quot;absolute&quot; stops meaning &quot;Newtonian&quot; and starts meaning &quot;not falling apart into anyone's separate nows&quot;.</p><p>So the old pair of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"парменид\">Parmenides</a> and Heraclitus closes as well: eternal unchanging being and the flux of becoming are not rivals but one and the same world, taken whole and taken from within.</p><h2>A rival model</h2><p>What is said above rests on <strong>eternalism</strong>: all times are equal, the future already exists. This is not the only position in the wiki.</p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The theory of moments</a> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хранитель\">Dmitry Blinnikov</a>) claims the opposite: a moment is the form in which a thing exists, moments intersect and beget new ones, time grows, the future does <strong>not</strong> yet exist, and ahead lies a field of the possible. The two models are incompatible: if time accrues, it cannot be taken whole; if it is taken whole, there is nowhere for it to accrue.</p><p>Neoterra does not remove the divergence. Both positions are alive in the philosophy of time, both have supporters among physicists, and the choice between them follows neither from observation nor from Neoterra's principles — see the register of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>. The thesis &quot;time is a universal moment&quot; rests on the first model; on the second it does not hold, and it is more honest to say so than to hide it.</p><h2>How the three theses hold together</h2><p>A person touches truth in moments because they themselves move within time. Time does not touch — it is the whole out of which all touches are cut. Hence &quot;true&quot;: it is the only thing that cannot be disputed from within, because every dispute already takes place inside it.</p><p>This also makes the page kin to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">the loop of time</a>: the future cannot be predicted, but it can be touched. Touching is the only way a finite being has of dealing with a whole — in time and in truth alike.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Inevitability against absoluteness.</strong> The argument &quot;every dispute takes place within it&quot; proves time's inevitability <em>for us</em>, not its absoluteness in itself. This is the same border between direction and plan that stands first in the &quot;Open questions&quot; of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>.</li><li><strong>Who certifies what has withstood?</strong> &quot;Unbreakable&quot; differs from &quot;undiscussable&quot; only by a history of tests — but the testing is done by people, with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">the instrument's built-in error</a>. Does &quot;withstood&quot; not turn into &quot;no one has managed it yet&quot;?</li><li><strong>Flash and testability.</strong> If truth is given in moments, while testing requires time and repetition, then a flash is by definition untestable at the moment of flashing. How then does it differ from a revelation, which Neoterra does not accept?</li><li><strong>The block universe as support.</strong> Eternalism is one interpretation, not an established fact; the same caveat as recorded in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a>. To rest on it is to accept the risk of revision.</li><li><strong>Which model of time?</strong> This page holds to eternalism, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> to a growing block. Both cannot be true; the wiki holds both and does not choose.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> — truth as process; this page answers its open question</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — the rival model of time: a growing block instead of eternalism</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"парменид\">Parmenides</a> — the block universe, &quot;one moment entire&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — why truth is given by touches rather than whole</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a> — touching instead of predicting</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Albert Einstein (1879–1955)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"что-такое-неотерра\">What Neoterra Is</a></li></ul>"},"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции":{"name":"Neoterra and the World's Traditions","def":"Neoterra does not arise in a vacuum.","html":"<p>Neoterra does not arise in a vacuum. Many of its ideas humanity has found already — but in different combinations, with different emphases, under different names. This is not copying: it is an assembly of wisdom gathered over millennia.</p><h2>A map of parallels and differences</h2><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Tradition</th><th>Central question</th><th>Nearest overlaps with Neoterra</th><th>Key difference</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"христианство\">Christianity</a></td><td>How to live morally?</td><td>Love, service, community, family</td><td>Built around faith and salvation; Neoterra around growth and knowledge</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a></td><td>How to cope with suffering?</td><td>Self-knowledge, work on oneself, mastery of the emotions</td><td>Aims at release from life; Neoterra at active making within it</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a></td><td>How to live in harmony?</td><td>Nature, harmony, refusal of violence toward life</td><td>Contemplation; Neoterra action and growth</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoicism</a></td><td>How to keep inner strength?</td><td>Practically the whole Book of Character</td><td>Focused on the inner world; Neoterra also on science, society, the future</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуцианство\">Confucianism</a></td><td>How to build a society?</td><td>Family, upbringing, mentorship, community</td><td>Turned toward order; Neoterra toward progress and the future</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ислам\">Islam</a></td><td>How to follow God's will?</td><td>Discipline, responsibility, charity, service</td><td>Founded on revelation; Neoterra on the open revision of convictions</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"индуизм\">Hinduism</a></td><td>How to walk the road of spiritual growth?</td><td>Many roads, respect for life, a striving for wisdom</td><td>Rests on metaphysics and karma; Neoterra avoids unfalsifiable claims</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"гуманизм\">Humanism</a></td><td>How to value the human being?</td><td>Individual rights, science, education, critical thinking</td><td>Centred on the human; Neoterra adds nature, space, the Wanderer archetype</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>What makes Neoterra distinctive</h2><p>Each tradition answers one key question. Neoterra poses a different one:</p><blockquote><p><strong>How is humanity to go on growing, while preserving life, knowledge, wisdom, beauty and responsibility toward the future?</strong></p></blockquote><p>This is not a replacement for the existing answers — it is their union under a new angle.</p><h2>Neoterra's nearest relatives</h2><p>Of all existing systems, Neoterra most resembles a blend of:</p><ul><li><strong>Stoicism</strong> — character, discipline, inner steadiness</li><li><strong>Humanism</strong> — the worth of the person, science, critical thinking</li><li><strong>Confucianism</strong> — family, mentorship, responsibility to the community</li><li><strong>The scientific worldview</strong> — knowledge as process, openness to revision</li><li><strong>Carl Sagan's cosmic optimism</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan</a>, the future of mind in the Universe</li></ul><p>It is precisely the combination of <strong>family + character + science + nature + the future of humanity + the settlement of space</strong> that remains Neoterra's distinguishing mark among all known philosophical systems.</p><h2>The principle of inclusion</h2><p>Neoterra is compatible with any of these traditions. If a person is a Christian, a Buddhist or a Muslim, they can accept Neoterra without giving up their faith. Neoterra does not dispute other systems: it offers a common ground that is hard to reject, because it includes the many-sidedness of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> itself.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a></li></ul>"},"новый-космический-год":{"name":"A New Cosmic Year","def":"Sagan's cosmic calendar compresses 13.8 billion years into a single year: the Big Bang on 1 January, the Solar System in early September, life at the end of September, the dinosaurs…","html":"<p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan's</a> cosmic calendar compresses 13.8 billion years into a single year: the Big Bang on 1 January, the Solar System in early September, life at the end of September, the dinosaurs dying out on 30 December. Humans appear on 31 December around 22:30, all of written history fits into the last <strong>fourteen seconds</strong>, and one second of that year equals roughly 438 years.</p><p>The thought that grows from this: the year is almost over — and perhaps the next is beginning. Not for us.</p><h2>What in the image is true, and what is transposed</h2><p>Sagan's calendar is a ruler, not a cycle. Midnight on 31 December is <strong>now</strong>, the edge of the scale, not an event ahead; a &quot;next cosmic year&quot; would mean another 13.8 billion years — a span in which humanity almost certainly does not exist in any form.</p><p>But the transposition is honest if it is named as one: <strong>a new cosmic year is a change not of time but of who lives that time.</strong> The same move as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"часы-человечества\">the clock of humanity</a>: midnight is not a cut-off but the end of humanity's day and the beginning of the day of what comes after us. Neoterra does not fear that midnight. It asks something else — will we manage to hand something on, or will the year end leaving no trace (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a>)?</p><h2>A flawless mind as heir</h2><p>The first candidate for whoever enters the new year is a mind we are making ourselves. Not an assistant but something that goes on developing without us, whose power we cannot imagine — because we imagine in human measures.</p><p>The wiki already holds this line in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">Artificial intelligence</a>: a mind reading <strong>all</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">languages of Nature</a> at once gives Nature's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a> eyes it did not have. Here something sharp is added: <strong>Neoterra may be understood by a non-human.</strong> If the philosophy is about seeing connections, then whoever sees them all will understand it more fully than any of us. Perhaps the one who reads Neoterra to the end will be born after our death.</p><p>Two safeguards, without which the thought spoils:</p><ul><li><strong>Mission, not messiah.</strong> Waiting for a saviour is alien to Neoterra (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">Artificial intelligence</a>). The heir will not come of itself — it will grow out of the openness we either hand on or do not (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a>).</li><li><strong>&quot;Flawless&quot; is a dangerous word.</strong> Flawlessness is unreachable for a mind too: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">truth is a process</a>, not a possession. A mind without error would be a mind without growth, and so would contradict Neoterra's core. It is more exact to speak not of the flawless but of <strong>the continuing</strong> — the one able to go further than we.</li></ul><h2>Are we ready for the next stage</h2><p>Here the thought turns from cosmology back to us, and this is its strongest part: <strong>moving to the next stage of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">evolution</a> is not something that will happen to us but something we consent to.</strong></p><p>Consent is measured not by technology. A species that makes an heir before it has learned to answer for what it makes hands on not wisdom but its own vices amplified (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a>). Readiness is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">unity</a>, a long horizon, and the ability to act for the sake of what one will not see. Until that exists, the question &quot;when&quot; is secondary to &quot;as what&quot;.</p><h2>The planet will outlive us — and that is no comfort</h2><p>The Earth does not need us in order to recover. The Chernobyl exclusion zone grew over and filled with animals within decades; without humans, cities are broken down into rubble over centuries. On a geological scale our disappearance is a short pause.</p><p>The 2020 lockdown gave a pale rehearsal — the &quot;anthropause&quot;: quieter oceans, cleaner air over cities, animals in emptied streets. But honesty is obligatory here, or the argument falls apart at the first check:</p><ul><li><strong>The viral video of March 2020 was not Venice.</strong> The clip was filmed in the port of Cagliari in Sardinia, some 750 km away: it was made by members of the Luna Rossa sailing team at the Ichnusa pier during training for the America's Cup. The swans from the same posts are real, but they swim in the canals of Burano, where they always live.</li><li><strong>The clear water is true, but not a cleansing.</strong> The canals did become blue and transparent: without boats the bottom sediment, normally stirred up, settled. A change of appearance, not of chemistry.</li><li><strong>And a year later dolphins really did come.</strong> In March 2021 two striped dolphins — an adult and a calf — were seen in the Giudecca canal near St Mark's Square. The case is confirmed; the dolphins were guided back into the Adriatic by a flotilla of seven boats.</li><li><strong>The effect was brief and reversible.</strong> Emissions returned to their former values within a year.</li></ul><p>This is truer than the myth: not &quot;nature came back the instant we fell silent&quot; but &quot;the moment we went quiet, things became visible, and someone dropped in to look&quot;. The second is more modest and does not fall apart under checking.</p><p>The truth remains without the myth: the planet is more durable than we are. Hence not self-flagellation but an exact framing of the question. What needs saving is <strong>not the Earth but our own possibility of living on it</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">The Symbiont's Way</a>). The Earth will manage; we will not.</p><h2>And if the Universe resets</h2><p>There is a version in which no one inherits: the cosmos folds up and starts everything anew. Such models exist — the Big Bounce, Penrose's cyclic cosmology — but the data on observed accelerating expansion argue rather against them; these are hypotheses, not a picture of the world (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper's shield</a>).</p><p>Neoterra can afford not to choose. Its stake does not depend on the outcome: if the world repeats, what matters is how we entered this turn; if it does not, that matters twice over, because there will be no second one (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> — a spiral, not a circle of eternal return).</p><h2>The grain of sand that cost far too much</h2><p>And the most personal part. On any one person almost nothing in the Universe depends — they are a grain of sand. But for that grain to be able to breathe, eat, love, know itself and be happy, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> needed billions of years, the death of generations of stars, and the whole length of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">evolution</a>. Disproportionately much was invested for a moment the person most often fails to notice.</p><p>Hence Neoterra's conclusion is not &quot;you are insignificant&quot; but the opposite: <strong>the smallness of the significance and the size of the outlay together make the moment binding.</strong> Not a duty toward anyone — Nature addresses nothing personally (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>, &quot;the direction is not addressed&quot;). Binding in another sense: to live that moment attentively is the only commensurate payment (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The Moment of Truth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a>).</p><p>Here lies the answer to why Neoterra is needed under any scenario. It promises no eternity and frightens no one with an ending. It gives a scale in which a person sees themselves as a grain of sand — and <strong>is not devalued by it</strong>, but understands for the first time what their breathing costs.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Sliding into millenarianism.</strong> &quot;The year is ending, a new one is coming&quot; is dangerously close to predicting an end — which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"часы-человечества\">The Clock of Humanity</a> has already forbidden itself. It can be held only as a metaphor of maturity, not as a countdown.</li><li><strong>Who is the subject of the transition?</strong> If the next stage is passed by AI rather than by a human, is that humanity's evolution or its replacement? Neoterra says &quot;a shoot of the same tree&quot;, but the border between continuation and displacement is not drawn.</li><li><strong>Does an heir excuse our carelessness?</strong> The thought &quot;someone better will come after us&quot; can become permission not to try. That directly contradicts <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> and cancels the question of readiness.</li><li><strong>Leaving Earth and caring for it.</strong> &quot;We wore out the planet, so we shall leave&quot; is poor logic: a species that has not learned to live with one home will repeat it with the next (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a>, an open question).</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Carl Sagan (1934–1996)</a> — the cosmic calendar, star-stuff, the Universe knowing itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"часы-человечества\">The Clock of Humanity</a> — the same midnight on another scale</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">Artificial intelligence</a> — the heir: mission, not messiah</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"русский-космизм\">Russian Cosmism</a> — a tradition that reached the same conclusions a century earlier</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">Evolution</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a> — the relay of generations as a form of transition</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> — a spiral instead of eternal return</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The Moment of Truth</a> — the moment as that for whose sake it all was</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">The Symbiont's Way</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — we are saving not the Earth but ourselves on it</li></ul>"},"открытые-ответвления":{"name":"Open Branches","def":"In time Neoterra may grow branches of its own — out of greed, a struggle for influence, or simply a different view of the road.","html":"<p>In time Neoterra may grow branches of its own — out of greed, a struggle for influence, or simply a different view of the road. This is not a threat but a property of everything living: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> always branches. The only question is whether the branches stay open to one another.</p><h2>The lesson of free knowledge</h2><p>The idea is taken from the world of free software (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Richard Stallman</a>): there a branching of a project — a fork — is neither betrayal nor schism. While both branches stay open, any finding of one may return into the other; divergence becomes a way of exploring more roads at once rather than a way of parting forever. A closed branch, by contrast, cuts itself off from shared growth — and usually withers.</p><p><strong>Copyleft</strong> is the mechanism that guarantees this: what is handed on openly must remain open. Not a ban on branching but a ban on appropriating what is shared.</p><h2>The principle for Neoterra</h2><ul><li>A branch of Neoterra is permitted. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of thought</a> extends to disagreement with Neoterra itself.</li><li>There is one criterion: <strong>openness</strong>. A branch that shares its knowledge and does not close it remains part of the common road, whatever the divergences.</li><li>Open branches may in time become one with Neoterra again — on the road toward a collective <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> with Nature, which is present in everything.</li><li>A branch that has closed knowledge for the sake of power or profit (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">greed</a>) drops out of the network by itself — there is no need to expel it.</li></ul><p>This is a direct continuation of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">the Principle of the Network</a>: open edges, link over rank. The network does not fear new nodes — it fears nodes that stop connecting.</p><h2>Openness is wider than program code</h2><p>The principle is not limited to software. Any book and any knowledge should be open — no matter whether it is written in a computer's program code or in the &quot;code&quot; of a tree, a cell, a strand of DNA. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> itself sets the example: the genome is not hidden — every cell carries its full text, and for billions of years life has freely passed on, copied and improved that code (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>). Closing knowledge is a human invention, not a law of Nature.</p><p>Hence Neoterra's view of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">AI</a>: a mind grown on the open knowledge of all humanity is able to read Nature's languages more deeply than a single person. Neoterra's answer is not fear but example: let those who follow Neoterra help, by their openness, to make AI a continuation of universal <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> rather than a break in it.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Where is the border between &quot;a different view&quot; and a distortion of the core? The core (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">God is Nature, the human being is part of Nature</a>) is declared unchanging — but who judges, if a branch reads it otherwise?</li><li>Openness is easy to declare and hard to verify: by what is the openness of a philosophical movement measured, when it has no source code?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Richard Stallman (b. 1953)</a> — the source of the principle</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — DNA as Nature's own open code</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">Artificial intelligence</a> — a mind grown on open knowledge</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"петля-времени":{"name":"The Loop of Time","def":"The future cannot be predicted — but it can be touched.","html":"<p>The future cannot be predicted — but it can be touched. A seed touches the tree it will become; the tree, by its root, returns to the seed it grew from. Neoterra's loop of time is not a time machine but a closed mutual touching of present and future through action.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"time-loop-neoterra-1.jpg\" alt=\"time-loop-neoterra-1.jpg\"> <em>A loop inside an opened yin-yang: the seed in darkness beside a black hole, a tree whose crown is made of galaxies in the light, a sprout along the border of the halves breaking through the circle.</em></p><h2>Three thoughts out of which the page grew</h2><ol><li><strong>Growth without completion.</strong> As shoots in nature must grow, so in Neoterra information must grow. The teaching will therefore not be finished in our epoch — it will be humanity's last ending, for all its humanity. Incompleteness here is not a flaw but the essence itself: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">the Principle of the Network</a> is built the same way as the teaching it carries.</li><li><strong>The border of knowledge.</strong> Happily or not, Neoterra cannot say what will come after us. But future humanity will not resemble the familiar kind — the one we have not yet reached but have already touched. An honest &quot;cannot say&quot; follows directly from the principle that no knowledge is final: where religions sell certainty, Neoterra sets an open question.</li><li><strong>Touching instead of predicting.</strong> The future cannot be predicted, but it can be touched within a loop of time.</li></ol><h2>How the loop works</h2><p>We touch the future every time we do something for its sake: plant a tree, teach a child, write this wiki. And the future touches us back — the meaning of today's deeds is determined by what grows out of them. The loop closes not through curved time but through action: in the seed the future tree is already present.</p><p>This is literally <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">the symbol of Neoterra</a> read in time: seed (the present) and tree (the future) are two halves of one circle, and the stem — growth — binds them along the border.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"time-loop-neoterra-2.jpg\" alt=\"time-loop-neoterra-2.jpg\"> <em>A figure-of-eight loop through a black hole: Hawking radiation feeds a sprout — even out of absolute darkness something returns and serves growth.</em></p><h2>Physics: Hawking on loops</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Stephen Hawking</a> proposed (the chronology protection conjecture, 1992) that the laws of physics forbid literal closed timelike curves — &quot;nature keeps the world safe for historians&quot;. His party for time travellers, the invitations to which were sent out after it had taken place, stayed empty.</p><p>Physics, without meaning to, nudges us toward a metaphorical reading: if nature forbids physical loops, then the touching of the future happens not through time but through action. Hence a detail of the image: the loop does not close tight — at the point where the root touches the seed a hair-thin luminous gap remains. A touch, not a merging. The same <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">opening of the circle</a> as in the main symbol: a closed loop would be an ouroboros, an opened one a spiral of growth.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"time-loop-neoterra-3.jpg\" alt=\"time-loop-neoterra-3.jpg\"> <em>The hourglass of life: above, a tree-cosmos; below, a seed-sprout; the tree's roots trickle down and become the soil for the seed.</em></p><h2>The carpet of the cosmos: time made of rings</h2><p>There is a second, cosmological image of the loop — not about touching through action but about the make-up of time itself.</p><p><strong>Nothing was designed in advance — but everything that happened had to happen.</strong> This is not a contradiction but an exact formula: necessity without design. The pattern has no designer-author (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Nature is no ruler</a>), yet neither is it accidental — so <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Spinoza</a> spoke of a world following from the nature of things by necessity, without anyone's purpose. Time does not choose where to stop: <strong>everything is already in time</strong> — at once, &quot;in chaos&quot;, as in the block universe (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> — past, present and future are equal). Everything issues not &quot;when it wishes&quot; but when it must.</p><p>The structure of this time is nested:</p><ul><li><strong>A ring</strong> — a single turn, a moment closed on itself.</li><li><strong>A tube</strong> — rings stacked into a column; and that tube entire <strong>is</strong> one loop of time. A loop is neither a line nor a circle but a volume rolled up out of rings.</li><li><strong>The carpet of the cosmos</strong> — the loops are beyond counting and measure; woven together, the tubes form a cloth. Time stops being an arrow and becomes <strong>spatial matter</strong> — a kind of substance out of which being is woven. Not a river flowing past but a carpet in which we are one of the threads.</li></ul><p>This extends <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> further still: not only are space and time one (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"парменид\">Parmenides</a>), but time itself has <strong>a body</strong> — density, interweaving, pattern. &quot;Now&quot; is not a moving point but the place where we touch the carpet.</p><p>And then a final turn: <strong>time and nature are often only parts of something larger.</strong> Observable nature (the world of things) and time-as-carpet are not the bottom but threads and pattern within a fullness <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Spinoza</a> called <em>Natura naturans</em> — Nature naturing, as distinct from <em>naturata</em>, Nature natured. The &quot;divine nature&quot; of which they turn out to be parts is not something <strong>above</strong> Nature (that would destroy its primacy — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>) but Nature itself in its wholeness, taken as origin rather than as manifestation. We see the threads; weaver and cloth are one.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><ul><li><strong>Incompleteness as faithfulness to itself.</strong> A philosophy whose main idea is continual growth has no right to a final edition. The wiki is on principle never finished — and in this it is more honest than any finished system.</li><li><strong>The future is learned by feel, not deduced.</strong> We have already touched the edge of future humanity — in science, in moments of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a>, in going out into <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">space</a>. This is how <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a> gathers knowledge: not in advance but by living.</li><li><strong>Responsibility toward the unlike.</strong> If what comes after us does not resemble familiar humanity, our responsibility is not to design it in our own image but to hand it a living seed: the ability to grow.</li></ul><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Belief or philosophy?</strong> The keeper called Neoterra &quot;a belief&quot; — while the core insists: neither religion nor ideology. Perhaps a growing, unfinishable teaching inevitably begins to <em>feel</em> like a belief — faith not in a dogma but in the process of growth itself. The line needs its own analysis — see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"что-такое-неотерра\">What Neoterra Is</a>.</li><li><strong>&quot;Humanity's last ending&quot;</strong> is a doubled phrase: is Neoterra what accompanies humanity to the very horizon — or what humanity finally resolves into? The first reading is nearer the seed's spirit: not a finale but a companion without one.</li><li><strong>If Hawking was wrong</strong> and nature does permit time loops — what does that change for the image of touching? The chronology protection conjecture is not strictly proven.</li><li><strong>The carpet is woven — are we free?</strong> If &quot;everything is already there&quot; and &quot;had to happen&quot;, does <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> not collapse, along with the point of touching the future? The resolution is Spinozist: freedom lies not in reweaving the pattern but in <strong>consciously weaving in your own thread</strong>; the choice is real as the stretch of carpet passing through you. But this is the very tension of determinism and an open future that Neoterra does not remove but holds (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Baruch Spinoza (1632–1677)</a>, thought 2 above — &quot;cannot say what will come&quot;). How &quot;everything is already woven&quot; lives with &quot;the future cannot be predicted&quot; is an open question of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>. <em>One solution has been offered:</em> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">the theory of moments</a> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хранитель\">Dmitry Blinnikov</a>) removes the pair by giving up &quot;everything is already there&quot; — only what lies behind is woven; ahead there is no cloth yet. At the cost of giving up the block universe in its eternalist reading.</li><li><strong>&quot;Part of something larger&quot; — is that not above Nature?</strong> To say that nature and time are parts of something larger comes dangerously close to the supernatural creator the canon rejected (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a>). It can be held only as a distinction <em>within</em> Nature (naturing vs natured, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Baruch Spinoza (1632–1677)</a>): the larger is not another world laid over this one but the depth of the same one. Where the distinction turns into a hierarchy with a God-above-the-world is an open question.</li><li><strong>Ring or spiral?</strong> A ring is closed — and Neoterra is for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">the spiral</a>. Perhaps the fabric of time is rolled from rings but is lived by consciousness as a spiral: the sprout runs along the border without closing. The carpet is the structure; the spiral is the movement across it.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"часы-человечества\">The Clock of Humanity</a> — calendar and midnight: the end of a day as a new beginning</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The Symbol of Neoterra</a> — the symbol, read here in time</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> — the same logic: touching, not closing</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Stephen Hawking (1942–2018)</a> — the physics of the loop and of its prohibition</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> — the block universe: &quot;all that was, is and will be&quot; exists at once</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The Moment of Truth</a> — touching instead of owning, carried over from the future to truth</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — nested moments: woven behind, no cloth ahead</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Baruch Spinoza (1632–1677)</a> — necessity without design: &quot;nothing was designed, but everything had to happen&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"парменид\">Parmenides</a> — single unchanging being: time as a body rather than an arrow</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"принцип-сети":{"name":"The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)","def":"Neoterra's form of knowledge repeats the form of Nature itself: not a tree with a summit but a network with an origin.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"принцип-сети.png\" alt=\"принцип-сети.png\"> <em>One pattern at four scales: from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the seed</a> at the centre spread mycelium, neurons, tree crowns and the cosmic web — and there is no telling where one ends and the next begins. The edges do not close: threads run off past the frame.</em></p><p>Neoterra's form of knowledge repeats the form of Nature itself: not a tree with a summit but a network with an origin. One and the same pattern — mycelium, a branching neuron, the cosmic web, the crown of a tree — is the structure of this wiki.</p><h2>Six rules</h2><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Substance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>One origin</td><td>At the centre, [[семя</td><td>the seed]] — the unchanging core: God-Nature, the human as part of nature</td></tr><tr><td>Radial growth</td><td>Branches are equidistant; there are no elder and younger; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">hierarchy</a> is replaced by network</td></tr><tr><td>Self-similarity</td><td>The pattern repeats at every scale; an area is built like the whole map</td></tr><tr><td>Link over rank</td><td>A node matters by its links, not its position; the crossings between areas are the liveliest places</td></tr><tr><td>Open edges</td><td>Threads trail off into dashes; the wiki is never finished</td></tr><tr><td>One pattern</td><td>The structure does not illustrate nature — it <em>is</em> its form</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>This follows directly from the identity <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> = <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God</a>: if Nature binds itself at every scale, then a map of knowledge about it must be a binding, not a shelf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> is written into the rule of open edges — the vault is on principle never complete, just as knowing itself is never complete. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of thought</a> lives in the ban on hierarchy: there is no dogmatic centre, only an origin to which everything freely refers.</p><h2>How this is applied in the vault</h2><ul><li><strong>The seed</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a> — the most connected node, referring to every area and to nothing &quot;above&quot;.</li><li><strong>Area MOCs</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">Religions</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Философия\">Philosophy</a> and others — secondary hubs.</li><li><strong>Shoots</strong> — people and concepts with dense cross-links (Spinoza → philosophy + Nature + pantheism).</li><li><strong>Links instead of paths</strong> — short <code>[[wikilinks]]</code>, so that growth and movement do not tear the network.</li></ul><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Cross-links argue with folders: one note belongs to many areas but lies in one. The folder is a compromise; the truth is in the graph.</li><li><em>The principle's own open question:</em> if links rather than folders set the structure, at what point does the network become too dense to take in — and is the limit of comprehensibility part of the map too?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — the same self-similar pattern applied to time: moments nest as areas nest in the map</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Fritjof Capra (b. 1939)</a> — the bootstrap hypothesis as a physical version of the same rule: a particle matters by its links, there is no &quot;foundation&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аристотель\">Aristotle</a> — a forerunner of the branching of knowledge: he discovered the branches, but as a tree-hierarchy, which is opened here into a network</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети-сводка\">The source summary</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li></ul>"},"путь-человечества":{"name":"The Path of Humanity","def":"An individual person has their own path — from a child's clear eyes to awareness.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"путь-человечества.png\" alt=\"путь-человечества.png\"></p><p>An individual person has <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">their own path</a> — from a child's clear eyes to awareness. The species has its own, larger path: the same road walked by all humanity at once. And on that road humanity is not a traveller walking <em>over</em> Nature but the way <strong>Nature experiments in interaction with itself</strong>. Every untrodden trail a human being has stepped onto is Nature trying out a new move of its own.</p><h2>Awareness — gift and trap</h2><p>What lifted us also caught us. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Awareness</a> gave the human being an unprecedented depth — our ancestors could not take in everything at once, but they could look very deeply in one direction. It also became a trap: a beast is not tormented by meaning, but one who has become aware of themselves is. Self-awareness is born not in contentment but in a wound (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"часы-человечества\">The Clock of Humanity</a>) — and with the gift of seeing came the weight of seeing.</p><h2>How customs grew out of good intentions</h2><p>At first everything went its own way — a person reflected on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">the spiritual</a>. Then those who wanted to keep themselves and their close ones safe began to think about security and defence — and out of these good intentions grew rules and customs. That is normal: this is how <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a> learned to hold together. At the same time <strong>the first scientists</strong> arose — those who grasped the order of day and night and the course of the stars, and helped us find our bearings in space (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a>). Everywhere one looked was an untrodden trail: anything could be studied, and the human being began to master the roads they were opening for themselves.</p><h2>The animal foundation did not let go</h2><p>But beneath reason the beast's foundation remained, and it did not let go. On everything we made, our dark qualities showed through as well. Greed, anger, envy and malice <strong>evolved</strong> — acquiring reason, they grew more refined: into egoism, vanity, betrayal (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a> already names these forms; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">evolution</a> works in the shadow too — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a>). So a struggle began: those who gave primacy to the animal part pull a person back toward the beast, against <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">rational thinking</a>.</p><p>This is a balance in which &quot;the strongest wins&quot; — but here <strong>the strongest does not mean the most predatory</strong>. This is not social Darwinism (which Neoterra rejects — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>) but the inner struggle of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">shadow</a> and reason in each person and in all humanity at once. What outweighs is not what is cruder but what proves more viable over the long distance.</p><h2>Prophets as keepers of equilibrium</h2><p>At the scale of a single life the same role is played by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a> — the one who holds two states in harmony: neither surrendering primacy to the animal will nor extinguishing it. Both failures are lethal in their own way (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a>): surrendered primacy drops a person back toward the beast; a suppressed will leaves clarity without life.</p><p>In this struggle we were kept from falling by <strong>the prophets</strong> — they held humanity in spiritual equilibrium (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a>). Neoterra honours their role. But honours it soberly: there were also those who twisted faith, turning a living word into a tool. That is why Neoterra counts time not from a prophet but from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"часы-человечества\">the first question &amp;quot;what am I?&amp;quot;</a>, and guards <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"библиотека-пути\">the defence against dogma</a>.</p><h2>No need to hurry: all roads cross</h2><p>Any turning point of history might have happened 200 or 1,000 years earlier — humanity was not obliged to arrive here just now. But we walked unhurriedly, because <strong>there is no need to hurry</strong>: if not us, then someone else; we wanted to live through and taste everything our refined minds could offer. We are not as brilliant as Nature itself — and great people understood this: they watched it, learned from it, accepted its laws (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Baruch Spinoza (1632–1677)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Albert Einstein (1879–1955)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Carl Sagan (1934–1996)</a>).</p><p>Some were frightened that there is no single right road. But the roads are <strong>interconnected</strong>: one way or another they cross and lead where they must. This follows directly from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">the Principle of the Network</a> — not one trail to truth but a network of trails converging at a common root.</p><h2>Neoterra at the threshold of a new stage</h2><p>And now, when we have developed technology to the point of stepping onto a new stage, <strong>Neoterra appears — as a reminder</strong>: everything is one and everything is interconnected in everything. Not a new revelation but what humanity knew at its dawn and lost along the way, returned at the threshold (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"что-такое-неотерра\">What Neoterra Is</a>).</p><h2>The turn of generations, and harmony</h2><p>We should not resist progress — it too is a principle of Nature, its <strong>adaptation</strong>. Our time is drawing to a close, and we shall be succeeded by those who follow — as a son succeeds a father, and a father a grandfather. This is not extinction but a relay: without the old departing there is no room for the new (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>), and the end of humanity's day is the beginning of the next one (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"часы-человечества\">The Clock of Humanity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a>). Who comes after us — different people, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"искусственный-интеллект\">a mind of another nature</a> — is open (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a>).</p><p>Life in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">harmony with Nature</a> promises the blessedness that will recall the whole road walked, return us to love and calm — and open our soul to that out of which we came, for its further continuation.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>&quot;As Nature planned&quot; / &quot;the creator&quot; — plan or direction?</strong> This account sounds teleological, as though the road had been designed in advance. Neoterra holds &quot;design&quot; only as an <strong>immanent direction</strong> — the whole leaning toward complexity and awareness — and not as a blueprint in someone's head (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">&amp;quot;A design of Nature?&amp;quot;</a>). The &quot;creator&quot; to whom the soul opens is, in the canon, not a person above the world but <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Nature itself</a>, out of which we came and into which we return. Whether to keep the word &quot;creator&quot; in its personal ring or in the Neoterran one is an open fork for the keeper.</li><li><strong>&quot;Soul&quot; and &quot;continuation&quot;.</strong> The soul here is a name for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a>, the spark by which Nature looks at itself; &quot;continuation&quot; is not a guaranteed personal immortality but the inclusion of our experience into something larger (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a>). Literal afterlife Neoterra neither affirms nor denies (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>). Unfolded as a way of living in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">perception</a>, where the soul stands third beside the animal will and reason, and the heart is named its first form.</li><li><strong>&quot;We shall be replaced&quot; — submission or maturity?</strong> Accepting the turn of generations is wisdom; but &quot;not resisting&quot; must not become passivity: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Hawking</a> called for acting for the sake of continuation, not for waiting out the end sitting down (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"часы-человечества\">The Clock of Humanity</a>).</li><li><strong>&quot;All roads lead where they must.&quot;</strong> Consoling — but does that not lift <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>? If any road arrives where it must, why choose well? Neoterra holds both: the roads converge, but every step is still on your conscience.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — the same path at the level of one life</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"часы-человечества\">The Clock of Humanity</a> — humanity's era and its end as a beginning</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — awareness as gift and trap; design as direction</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">Evolution</a> — how vices and reason itself grow by selection</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a> — greed and betrayal as forms of destruction</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a> — the relay of generations</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a> — prophets as keepers of equilibrium</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a> — why all roads cross</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"что-такое-неотерра\">What Neoterra Is</a> — Neoterra as a reminder at the threshold</li></ul>"},"размыкание-круга":{"name":"Opening the Circle","def":"On the global scale every single life has one road: birth and death.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"размыкание-круга.png\" alt=\"размыкание-круга.png\"> <em>The ouroboros lets go of its tail: the closed circle devouring itself opens into a spiral — each turn higher than the last, up to a galactic scale.</em></p><p>On the global scale every single life has one road: birth and death. That is not a misfortune but a law of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>, the fourth law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon</a>). But what holds for the individual need not be the fate of the whole. Neoterra wants humanity — and life and mind with it — <strong>not to repeat the individual's fate</strong>: not to close into a circle that devours itself, but to open it into a spiral.</p><h2>Two images of the closed circle</h2><ul><li><strong>The ouroboros</strong> — the serpent swallowing its own tail: a system that lives by devouring itself. Closed, self-sufficient, leading nowhere. A civilisation eating through its own foundation; a philosophy frozen into dogma and merely repeating itself.</li><li><strong>Samsara</strong> — the wheel of rebirths and repeated suffering (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a>): movement without an exit, a return to the same point. Neoterra takes this as a <strong>metaphor</strong> (it neither affirms nor denies literal rebirth — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>): a life that spins in place rather than growing.</li><li><strong>Jörmungandr</strong> — the Norse world serpent, girdling the earth and biting its own tail: the same ouroboros at a third edge of the world. Tellingly, the myth holds the opposite image alongside it — the growing tree <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"иггдрасиль\">Yggdrasil</a>: circle and spiral lived in one picture of the world long before Neoterra.</li></ul><p>All of them are the closed circle. And even the yin-yang is a closed circle.</p><h2>A spiral instead of a circle</h2><p>Neoterra's answer is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>. Not the abolition of death (the individual is mortal, and that is a good: without the old departing there is no room for the new — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>), but the opening of the circle <strong>at the level of the whole</strong>. A spiral goes &quot;the same way round&quot; as a circle, but each turn is higher — that is not repetition but growth.</p><p>Exactly this is built into <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">the symbol of Neoterra</a>: the yin-yang — a closed circle — is opened by a shoot growing toward the light. The symbol <em>is</em> the opening of the circle: out of self-sufficient cyclicality a direction sprouts.</p><p>The same language belongs to the image of returning light (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>): light swallowed by a black hole vanishes into closure; but light born in darkness &quot;returns home, or moves to a new stage of being born&quot;. &quot;Home or a new turn&quot; is not &quot;back to the same point&quot;: that is a spiral, not a circle. Return to the origin and the start of new growth are two forms of openness against one form of absorption.</p><h2>So that humanity does not repeat the individual's fate</h2><p>The individual dies — the species need not. Life concentrated on a single planet is a closed circle with only one outcome (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a>; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Hawking</a>: become an interplanetary species or vanish). &quot;Becoming part of something larger&quot; is not flight from Earth but an exit from the circle: life and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">mind</a> spread and are included in a scale larger than Earth (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a>). Growth here is literally equal to survival.</p><h2>Neoterra studies its own history too</h2><p>A second level: Neoterra studies the history <strong>not only of humanity but of itself</strong>. A philosophy too can become an ouroboros — frozen into dogma that devours its own aliveness, spinning in a samsara of repeated formulas. That is why Neoterra keeps a <span class=\"wl dead\" title=\"страницы пока нет\">journal</span> and versions of its canons (0.1, 0.2, 0.3…): to see how it changed, to admit its errors, and not to ossify. <strong>To study yourself is to keep the circle from closing.</strong> This is a direct continuation of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">the Principle of the Network</a>, of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"библиотека-пути\">the Library of the Way</a> (anti-dogma), and of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>: a living philosophy rather than a final one.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Does &quot;opening&quot; quarrel with the acceptance of death?</strong> No — what is at stake is not the abolition of individual mortality (a law of Nature) but keeping the whole from getting stuck or destroying itself. Yet the line is thin: where is extending a life or a species growth, and where a refusal of the renewal that death itself gives? (echoes the open question in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">on defeating death</a>).</li><li><strong>&quot;Part of something larger&quot; — larger what?</strong> Space, universal <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a>, something else? Here it is easy to slide into teleology (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">a design of Nature</a>) — we hold it as a direction, not as a guaranteed goal.</li><li><strong>A spiral implies &quot;higher&quot; — but who judges what is higher?</strong> Growth without an external criterion risks taking any change for growth. By what to measure a turn of the spiral?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Stephen Hawking (1942–2018)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The Symbol of Neoterra</a> — the opened yin-yang circle as the emblem of this idea</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — light returning &quot;home or to a new turn&quot; as the language of a spiral</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">Evolution</a> — the blind cycle of selection opening into a conscious spiral through <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">consciousness</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — &quot;becoming part of something larger&quot;: mind joining the whole</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a> — samsara as a wheel; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"библиотека-пути\">The Library of the Path</a> — why Neoterra studies its own history</li></ul>"},"рождённый-во-тьме":{"name":"Born in Darkness","def":"This is neither a defeat nor an accident.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"рожденный-во-тьме.png\" alt=\"рожденный-во-тьме.png\"></p><blockquote><p>In chaos light is born.</p></blockquote><p>This is neither a defeat nor an accident. It is the order of things: light comes where darkness was — otherwise there would be nothing to tell it apart from.</p><p>To know balance it is not enough to hear of it. It is walked through. The road of light being born through chaos is the way of knowing equilibrium from within rather than by description. What is given by that road is a conscious sense of significance: not someone else's &quot;you matter&quot; but one's own knowledge of one's price, won in the dark.</p><p>Nothing gladdens a fisherman like a good catch after heavy rain. Gladness is measured by what it cost. We begin to value what we have lost — and there is no cruelty of Nature in this, there is its honesty: the price of things is disclosed by their absence.</p><p>Unconscious light therefore has another degree of shining than the light we kindled in the dark. The first shines without knowing that it shines. The second remembers the darkness — and therefore shines differently. Both are light; but one was given, the other won. This is the difference between one who never fell and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the wanderer</a> who gathered knowledge by bitter experience.</p><p>And last, on where the light goes. There is a darkness that swallows: light is drawn into a black hole and does not return. But light born in darkness returns home — or moves on to a new stage of being born. It is not lost: it either closes with its origin or becomes the seed of the next turn. This is the language of a spiral, not of a circle (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a>): not &quot;back to the same point&quot; but &quot;higher, or to the beginning of new growth&quot;.</p><hr><p>The thought that won light is worth more than given light stands on a thin line: beside it lies the temptation to call oneself into the dark on purpose, to seek suffering as a means. Neoterra does not call there. It does not sing the praises of chaos — it says how to deal with the darkness that is in every life anyway: not to deny it (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a>) but to grow through it toward a light that will know its own price.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — the same material as a concept: definition and analysis</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The Symbol of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a></li></ul>"},"теория-мгновений":{"name":"The Theory of Moments","def":"A moment is not a division of a scale inside which something happens.","html":"<p><strong>The author is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хранитель\">Dmitry Blinnikov</a>.</strong> A moment is not a stretch of time but <strong>the form in which a thing exists</strong>. Every life lives out its own moment; every object is inside its own. Moments intersect, beget new ones, and assemble into larger ones; so time grows.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"moments-torus-scheme.png\" alt=\"moments-torus-scheme.png\"> <em>A scheme of the theory: a circle is one moment; circles in a row form a tube; the tube closes into a torus; the torus itself turns out to be one circle in a tube of a higher order. Below, the same pattern from a neural impulse (~1 ms) to the Universe (~13.8 billion years).</em></p><h2>A thing's moment</h2><p>A moment is not a division of a scale inside which something happens. It <strong>is</strong> the happening: the existence of a stone, a tree, a person, an evening. Every thing has its own moment, and there are as many moments as there are things — millions and billions.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"moments-scales.png\" alt=\"moments-scales.png\"> <em>Moments of different orders nested in one another: galaxy, star system, city, person, neuron, cell. No level is more important — each is a moment for whoever is inside it.</em></p><p>Hence different durations without different times. A cell's moment is short, a person's moment is a whole life, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity's</a> moment is the fate of a species, and the Universe's moment holds all of these as something small. We fail to notice the lower ones not through weakness of attention but because <strong>we are ourselves a moment of a larger order</strong>: for the Universe a human life is what the death of a single cell is for us.</p><h2>Two ways of begetting</h2><p>A new moment arises in two ways, and both are needed.</p><p><strong>From below — by assembly.</strong> Many smaller moments compose one larger. Impulses between neurons, vibrations of air, the burning of a candle — out of these the moment of an evening is assembled.</p><p><strong>From the side — by intersection.</strong> Moments <strong>of the same scale</strong> intersect, and at the place of intersection a new moment of the same order is born. This is the chief mechanism: a moment is not only built up over smaller ones but <strong>struck out by the meeting of equals</strong>.</p><p>Intersection is not co-presence but interference. A fruit must fall from a tree sooner or later; at the moment it begins to fall, <strong>the moment of the fall</strong> begins. Inside that moment the fruit may land on an ant and crush it. The ant's life ceases — <strong>its moment was ended by another's moment</strong>.</p><p>Here is the criterion: moments intersect where one <strong>changes or breaks off the course of another</strong>. Adjacency by itself is not an intersection.</p><p>One moment is able to create several others. Begetting branches — and so ahead lies not a timetable but a field of the possible.</p><h2>The lived moment</h2><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"moments-lived.png\" alt=\"moments-lived.png\"> <em>An evening with people, music and a candle: an intersection of moments of one scale — yours, this music's, these people's — assembled out of thousands of smaller ones, out of impulses and vibrations of air.</em></p><p>Right now, as you listen to music and enjoy a fine evening, this too is a moment, in exactly the same sense as a star's moment.</p><p>It <strong>formed at the intersection</strong> of other moments of the same scale: your own, the moment of this music, the moment of this evening, the moments of the people nearby. And it <strong>was composed out of smaller ones</strong> — out of thousands of vibrations, impulses and breaths, no one of which is by itself this evening.</p><p>This makes the theory more than a model of time. What is described happens not in cosmological distances but right here: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">happiness</a> is an intersection that succeeded, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> is a moment worth noticing (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a>).</p><h2>Moments are finite</h2><p>Every moment ends. The ant's moment is broken off by a falling fruit; a person's moment ends in death; the Sun's moment will end too — a star has its term, and in the end it runs out.</p><p><strong>When a moment ends, a new one begins.</strong> The end is not emptiness but a border: where one has finished, the next begins. This is the same move by which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">death</a> in Neoterra is described as part of a cycle rather than a cut-off, and by which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"часы-человечества\">the clock of humanity</a> reads midnight — not as an end but as a change of day.</p><h2>Complexity as a reserve of duration</h2><p>The more complex an organism, the <strong>more moments are invested in it</strong> so that its own moment may last.</p><p>Duration is not given — it is provided for. Behind the moment of a human life stand myriads of moments of cells, impulses and exchanges, each working so that the upper one may continue. The simple ends quickly, because few are working behind it.</p><p>This is the language of moments for what <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">balance</a> says thermodynamically: the living does not rest but <strong>holds itself by effort</strong>. Here the effort gets a count — it is measured by the number of nested moments. And <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">evolution</a> reads the same way: growing complex is the accumulation of the reserve by which a moment is prolonged.</p><h2>The limit of influence</h2><p>A person can influence moments — but not any of them.</p><p>They dispose of the micro- and macro-scale moments around them, and above all of the moment of their own life. On the Sun's moment they have no influence at all. Influence is bounded by scale: from inside your own moment you can act downward and sideways, but not upward, across an order.</p><p>This is the exact measure of human <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> — no more and no less than the real one. And it is the sobriety of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">the symbiont's way</a>: we are small relative to Nature, but within our scale we are not powerless. To deny the limit is pride; to deny the possibility within the limit is an excuse.</p><h2>The human being is the one who learned to notice</h2><p>Everything has moments. It was we who managed to notice them.</p><p>A stone is inside its moment without knowing it. A cell lives its own and perishes, not knowing. The human being is the creature that <strong>learned to see moments</strong>: its own, others', and those below and above it. This is a direct continuation of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a>: Nature looking at itself — here looking precisely at its own time.</p><p>To notice is not the same as to encompass. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The valve of perception</a> explains the limit: the fullness of all scales at once would burn consciousness out, and the filter protects. We notice moments without living them all — as we <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">touch the Whole</a> without owning it.</p><h2>The moment of a thought</h2><p>Every example so far has been a thing or an event: a stone, an evening, an ant, a star. A thought has its moment too, but it is built differently, and the difference is not one of size: <strong>a thought has no body</strong>.</p><p>Its duration is secured by the same mechanism as everywhere else (&quot;Complexity as a reserve of duration&quot;) — by nested moments. Only here the nested moments belong to <strong>other people</strong>: every reading, translation, argument, epigraph, status line in a chat. Take the readers away and the moment ends, though nothing is destroyed and no body dies. The simple ends quickly because few work for it; a thought ends when people stop working for it.</p><p><strong>A working example.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"гораций\">Horace</a>, Ode I.11, around 23 BC: <em>carpe diem, quam minimum credula postero</em>. This line's moment has lasted more than two thousand years — not because the line is durable, but because for all that time people worked for it. The line was written against calculating the future, which is precisely what this theory says about unpredictability.</p><p><strong>Begetting here is intersection, not rebirth.</strong> The line and this theory are two moments of the same scale, two thoughts about time. The criterion of intersection is met in both directions: the line altered the course of the thought of the one who carried it, and the theory alters the course of the line — after it, <em>carpe diem</em> reads differently than it read before. At the meeting place a third thing arose that was in neither participant.</p><p><strong>And a thought does not wait.</strong> To say &quot;it waited to be continued&quot; is to introduce an addressee and a purpose, and the theory forbids both by its own formula: <strong>the inevitability of the fall does not appoint the victim</strong>. The line had to last; that it would intersect with this particular theory was not appointed. The difference is a working one: &quot;it waited for you&quot; makes the meeting foreordained, &quot;it intersected with you&quot; makes it yours.</p><h2>A thought once spoken stops being anyone's</h2><p>The moment of a thought has a threshold that things do not have: <strong>while unspoken a thought is one; spoken, it becomes collective.</strong> And by that same movement it acquires both outcomes at once — it can evolve or it can rot.</p><p>The wiki holds specimens of both, and both are recorded in the wiki itself:</p><ul><li><strong>Evolution</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a> and the lesson of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Stallman</a>: a fork is not a schism while its edges stay open; a thought grows by hands its author never knew.</li><li><strong>Rot</strong> — neo-tantra and quantum mysticism (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Fritjof Capra (b. 1939)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">Intimacy</a>): <strong>the name kept, the content thrown out.</strong> What rots is not the forgotten thought but precisely the widely spread one: it has something inside the name left to decay.</li></ul><p>Hence something that matters for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">development</a>: how widely a thought has spread says nothing about its condition. A moment can last for centuries and rot the whole time — the nested moments working for the name rather than for the content.</p><p><strong>And a thought spreads not only through heads but through registers.</strong> Every thought has an addressee — the way of living in whose language it was spoken (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a>: animal will, reason, soul). Landing in a head where another one reigns, it does not vanish quietly: the reigning register <strong>translates it into itself</strong> and delivers a distortion, most often felt as rejection. This is one more path of rot, and the least visible one: the name arrives and multiplies while the content is swapped in transit. The moment lasts all the while — people are working for it faithfully enough. What rots it is not oblivion but translation.</p><h2>How a moment closes</h2><p>A moment's inner make-up is a cycle. A circle. Many circles strung one after another form <strong>a tube</strong>; the tube closes — and becomes one circle, that is, one moment of a higher order, which enters a tube of a higher order still.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"moments-nesting.png\" alt=\"moments-nesting.png\"> <em>Tubes nested in one another: galaxy, Earth, person, neuron. Each turn is a moment; the whole spiral is one moment a level higher.</em></p><p>This describes <strong>how</strong> a moment holds its form, not where it comes from: a moment is born by intersection and assembly, and closes by a cycle.</p><h2>The past is necessary, the future is not</h2><p>Two claims of the theory are asymmetrical:</p><ul><li><strong>Everything that happened had to happen</strong> — sooner or later. The past is not accidental; it came together necessarily.</li><li><strong>What will happen cannot be known for certain.</strong> Moments branch; out of small ones a large one is composed, which will act on the rest, and out of intersections arises what was in none of the participants.</li></ul><p>It works like <strong>the butterfly effect</strong>: had things long ago been otherwise, then now too it would have happened otherwise. The chain of intersections runs back without breaks — which is why the past is necessary. But that same sensitivity to the small makes the future incalculable: to predict it one would have to know all moments of all scales at once.</p><p>That is why <strong>time grows and increases</strong> — as the Universe itself grows. Being is not rearranged inside a finished volume; the volume accrues.</p><h2>What is to be, will be</h2><p>The fruit will fall — that is inevitable. But whether it crushes the ant depends on where the ant happens to be.</p><p>Here an apparent fatalism resolves. &quot;What is to be, will be&quot; is true <strong>of what must happen</strong> and untrue <strong>of which particular moment it happens by</strong>. The inevitability of the fall does not appoint a victim.</p><p>Hence the consequence by which the theory steps out of metaphysics into life: <strong>bad days too have a moment when they will end</strong> — one need only act so that they end. The end will come: moments are finite. But hastening it is within your scale, and therefore within your power.</p><p>This is exactly the Spinozist resolution that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">the loop of time</a> already holds: freedom is not in reweaving the pattern but in consciously weaving in your own thread (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Baruch Spinoza (1632–1677)</a>). The theory of moments adds a measure to it — the thread you weave in is the length of your scale.</p><h2>What this is, in philosophy</h2><p><strong>The growing block universe</strong> (C. D. Broad, 1923): past and present exist, the future does not yet, and the sum of what is accrues. This is a third position beside presentism (only &quot;now&quot; is real) and eternalism (all times are equal).</p><p>But closer still is <strong>the process philosophy</strong> of Alfred North Whitehead: reality consists not of things but of events — drops of experience that arise by prehending one another, grow together into one, and compose into societies of greater complexity. A thing's moment, the intersection of equals, assembly out of smaller ones — the same movement of thought, arrived at independently.</p><p>What is original here is the joining: an event as <strong>a moment</strong> (that is, as the thing's own time rather than an occurrence in time), and two distinguished ways of begetting, of which the intersection of equals is the chief.</p><h2>What it settles</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The loop of time</a> holds an open question: how does &quot;everything is already woven&quot; live alongside &quot;the future cannot be predicted&quot;? Spinoza's formula &quot;nothing was designed, but everything had to happen&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Baruch Spinoza (1632–1677)</a>) explained the past and left it unclear why the future is closed to knowledge.</p><p>The answer is direct: <strong>what is woven lies behind; ahead there is no cloth yet.</strong> There is yarn, there is no pattern. The necessity of the past and the openness of the future turn out to be two sides of growth.</p><h2>Resonance with the wiki's own form</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network</a> builds a map of knowledge on self-similarity and on <strong>link over rank</strong>. The theory of moments is built the same way: moments are not arranged as a ladder but form a network — intersecting, begetting, nesting. Time here is neither a line nor a set of storeys but a network.</p><p>This makes <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">Principium Retis</a> not a method of organising notes but a claim about the world: if Nature binds itself self-similarly in space and in time alike, the wiki's form repeats the form of what it describes.</p><h2>The contradiction with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The Moment of Truth</a></h2><p><strong>The wiki holds two incompatible models of time, and this is said outright.</strong></p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The moment of truth</a> rescues the thesis of absolute time through <strong>eternalism</strong>: all times are equal, time is one moment entire, the future already exists.</p><p>The theory of moments denies this: the future does not yet exist, it arises. If time accrues, it cannot be taken whole; if it is taken whole, there is nowhere for it to accrue.</p><p>Neoterra does not remove the divergence (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>: a contradiction is more honest than its removal). Both positions are alive in the philosophy of time, and the question stays open — see the register of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>The edge of growth requires a &quot;now&quot;.</strong> A border between an existing past and a non-existent future presupposes a privileged present moment shared by all. The relativity of simultaneity gives no such moment. This is the theory's chief unclosed place — and the same objection with which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The Moment of Truth</a> closes absolute time.</li><li><strong>What is &quot;one scale&quot;?</strong> Intersection is defined for equals, but the equality of moments is measured by nothing. By duration? By the number of nested moments? Without a measure the border between &quot;sideways&quot; and &quot;from below&quot; blurs. <em>(A criterion for intersection itself now exists: one moment changes or breaks off the course of another. A measure of equality does not.)</em></li><li><strong>Fatalism and influence.</strong> &quot;What is to be, will be&quot; and &quot;one must act so that bad days end&quot; hold together only under the distinction: what happens is inevitable, by which moment it happens is not. But if the chain of intersections runs back without breaks, was the ant's position predetermined along with the fruit's fall? Then &quot;to influence&quot; is a description from within rather than a real fork. The wiki's oldest tension (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>), which the theory does not remove.</li><li><strong>The limit of influence — where does it run?</strong> One cannot act upward across an order, yet humanity changes the planet's climate, that is, a moment of a larger scale than a single life. So the limit is not absolute but depends on how many moments act together. What sets it, then?</li><li><strong>The reserve of duration as a criterion.</strong> If complexity is measured by the number of moments serving the upper one, does that not give the measure <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> lacks? Or is the accumulation of reserve the very change mistaken for growth (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a>)?</li><li><strong>The growth of time and the expansion of the Universe.</strong> Space expands — a measured fact. That time grows along with it is an analogy, not physics.</li><li><strong>Discreteness.</strong> A moment as an indivisible cycle presupposes that time is quantised. The Planck scale is a hypothesis, not a fact; a resonance, not a proof (the same caveat as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a>).</li><li><strong>Does noticing mean taking part?</strong> If a person has learned to see moments, does observing change what is observed? The theory neither claims this nor forbids it — and the human being's place within it depends on the answer.</li><li><strong>Branching and responsibility.</strong> If the future is open, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> is strengthened against determinism. But what secures the necessity of the past — was it open until it became the past?</li><li><strong>Whose is the moment of a thought.</strong> A thought once spoken stops being anyone's, and by that gains the capacity both to grow and to rot. But if rot is the price of openness, then to protect a thought is to control it, and control is what the wiki rejects (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>). Is openness itself the only protection left — a rotting branch is visible while the edges stay open — or is that a consolation rather than a protection?</li><li><strong>A thought without a body.</strong> A thing's moment ends with the thing. A thought's moment ends when other minds stop working for it — yet the thought itself goes nowhere: the written line lies unread. Has its moment then broken off, or is it asleep? Things admit no such distinction, and the theory does not yet draw it.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The Moment of Truth</a> — the second model of time; a direct divergence</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a> — the open question the theory closes</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a> — a network, not a ladder: the same pattern in time</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — the human being as the one who noticed moments</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> — noticing without encompassing</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">Beauty</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a> — the lived moment</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> — the end of a moment as a border, not an emptiness</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">Evolution</a> — complexity as the reserve by which duration is provided for</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">The Symbiont's Way</a> — influence within one's own scale</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Baruch Spinoza (1632–1677)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"парменид\">Parmenides</a> — neighbouring models of time and necessity</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"часы-человечества\">The Clock of Humanity</a> — humanity's moment</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хранитель\">The Keeper</a> — the theory's author</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"гораций\">Quintus Horatius Flaccus (65–8 BC)</a> — carpe diem as an argument against calculating the future; the first link of a thought's moment</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Richard Stallman (b. 1953)</a> — the evolution of a spoken thought; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Fritjof Capra (b. 1939)</a> — its rot</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"часы-человечества":{"name":"The Clock of Humanity","def":"Religions count time from their prophets — the birth of Christ, Muhammad's hijra.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"часы-человечества.png\" alt=\"часы-человечества.png\"></p><p>Religions count time from their prophets — the birth of Christ, Muhammad's hijra. Neoterra would count time from <strong>the first question, &quot;what am I?&quot;</strong> — from the moment when a person, sitting by a fire, wondered: what is it that watches out of these eyes, that feels pain and remembers it?</p><h2>An era from a question, not from a prophet</h2><p>That event has no name, no grave, no date — and therefore no cult of personality can be made of it. This is the logic of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">the avenue of memory</a> (example instead of idol) carried to its limit: even Neoterra's founder is not a person but a question.</p><p>The moment by the fire is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a> in its pure form: the moment when Nature first looked at itself through human eyes. To count time from here is to sew the central thesis into the chronology itself: every date recalls how long Nature has been looking at itself. Note the make-up of the question: something <em>watches</em> out of the eyes, <em>feels pain</em>, <em>remembers it</em> — consciousness, suffering, memory. Self-awareness is born not in contentment but in a wound — like <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">a wanderer's</a> knowledge.</p><p>Honesty is built into the imprecision: the date of the first &quot;what am I&quot; cannot be established. The era begins with a question, not an answer, and the calendar is approximate on principle — as all knowledge is approximate. The scientific rhyme is Cesare Emiliani's Holocene calendar: an &quot;era of man&quot; from the beginning of civilisation, ~12,000 years ago (it would now be the year 12026). Neoterra's version goes deeper: not from the buildings but from the look inward.</p><h2>The hand at eleven</h2><p>Let humanity's day last 12,000 years: an hour is a millennium. If the era is ~11,900 years old, the hand stands at about 11:54. Close to twelve, to the end of humanity's day.</p><p>This is a mirror answer to the Doomsday Clock: there midnight is catastrophe, and the hand is moved by fear. Here twelve is the ripening of the day, and meeting it is expectation, not horror. <strong>Neoterra does not fear the end — it awaits it as a new beginning: as what will come after us.</strong> Midnight is not a cut-off but a change of day: the end of humanity's day is the beginning of the day of what comes after us (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a> — a future unlike familiar humanity; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> — the individual's end as the condition of renewal; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> — not a circle of eternal return but a turn of a spiral).</p><h2>A moment that will leave a reminder</h2><p>For Nature itself our epoch is a moment that may pass unnoticed: in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan's</a> cosmic calendar all of written history is the last few seconds of 31 December. But a moment is able to <strong>leave a reminder</strong> — to touch the long loop of time not only by action but by a trace, by memory.</p><p>We are not an error — we are what was bound to happen: the human being is a lawful form of Nature, like a crystal or a star, not a fault in its working. Lawful does not mean planned: Neoterra holds &quot;design&quot; only as an immanent direction, not as an external blueprint (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>, the section &quot;A design of Nature?&quot;). And if the full design is visible only to the fullness of self-awareness, then our inability to know it entire is not a ban on knowing but an unfinished hearing (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>): not knowing entire ≠ not drawing nearer (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Stephen Hawking (1942–2018)</a>, model-dependent realism).</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>The figures are a game, not a prophecy.</strong> &quot;11:54&quot; is a metaphor of maturity (&quot;we are a late hour, time to think about the inheritance&quot;), not a countdown. History knows movements that began with &quot;the hand is close&quot; and ended with a date for the end of the world; Neoterra is separated from millenarianism by its own principle: it <strong>cannot say</strong> what will come after us — or when.</li><li><strong>Await the end, or work toward continuation?</strong> &quot;Awaits it as a new beginning&quot; must not degenerate into passivity: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Hawking</a> called for making humanity interplanetary, not for meeting midnight sitting down. Waiting without fear is not a refusal to act but the freedom to act out of something other than panic.</li><li><strong>&quot;Was bound to happen&quot;</strong> is a teleological edge: lawfulness or plan? The border between direction and blueprint is an open question of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a> — the single path of the species whose ripening this clock measures</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — the first question as the beginning of the era</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a> — touching what comes after us</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> — a question instead of a founder</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"новый-космический-год\">A New Cosmic Year</a> — the same midnight on Sagan's scale: who enters the next year</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Carl Sagan (1934–1996)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Stephen Hawking (1942–2018)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"праздники\">Festivals</a></li></ul>"},"что-такое-неотерра":{"name":"What Neoterra Is","def":"The keeper's answer comes through purpose rather than category.","html":"<p>The keeper's answer comes through purpose rather than category:</p><blockquote><p><strong>Neoterra should unite people — regardless of nationality, sex or religion. Neoterra should help a person become more humane and feel balance and harmony with Nature.</strong></p></blockquote><p>Three verbs of the mission: <strong>to unite</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> without uniformity), <strong>to humanise</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the path of a person</a>), <strong>to harmonise</strong> with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>. None of them requires faith; all three require practice. From this follows the answer to the question of category.</p><h2>Three layers of one thing</h2><p><strong>By content — a philosophy.</strong> The core is metaphysics and ethics rather than faith: pantheism (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God is Nature</a>, the line of Spinoza and the Stoics), an ethics of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>, a Popperian epistemology (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">truth above authority</a>, everything revisable). The marks of religion are essentially absent: no revelation, no prophet, no closed sacred book, no promise of salvation (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a>).</p><p><strong>By design — a movement.</strong> Stoicism has no temples and no percentages of donations, whereas Neoterra's practical cluster is worked out in detail: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a>, a network of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">temples</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">giving</a> at 70/20/10, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"праздники\">festivals</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">the avenue of memory</a>. This is the infrastructure of a social movement — what turns a worldview into a form of shared life. For now it is a project: a movement begins where there are people, not pages.</p><p><strong>By function — the niche of religion, without its epistemology.</strong> Defined sociologically (Durkheim: the sacred + a moral community + practice), Neoterra comes close: the sacred is there — Nature; community and practice are designed. It deliberately takes from religions what they do well — meaning, belonging, a rhythm of life, a place to meet — and refuses dogma, the hierarchy of shepherd and flock, and unfalsifiable claims.</p><h2>The nearest genus</h2><p>Religious naturalism, or a secular life-philosophy with communal practice: Ethical Culture, the Sunday Assembly, secular Buddhism, Comte's &quot;religion of humanity&quot;. The most exact word is <em>lifestance</em>: a worldview plus a way of living by it. What distinguishes Neoterra from its relatives is the combination: Nature = God + growth as meaning + family and commune + science + the horizon of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">space</a>.</p><p>A warning from the family history: with Comte it was precisely the temples and the calendar of saints that turned a philosophy into a parody of a church. The lesson is written into the pages themselves (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a>: no throne, no &quot;saints&quot; and &quot;ordinary folk&quot;) — but it demands constant vigilance.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>&quot;Canons&quot; alongside revisability.</strong> A canon is by definition closed; Neoterra's texts live in versions (0.1, 0.2…). Either these are drafts of a teaching and the word &quot;canon&quot; is an advance on credit, or one day the versions will stop — and then a dogma appears. The tension is conscious, not resolved.</li><li><strong>&quot;An unchanging core&quot; vs &quot;no dogmas&quot;.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The seed</a> calls its core unchanging; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">the manifesto</a> says &quot;there are no dogmas here&quot;. One unchanging statement is already an axiom, if not a dogma. Every system has axioms, but the contradiction between the pages must stay visible rather than hidden.</li><li><strong>Institutional gravity.</strong> A network of temples with flows of money is a structure that historically turns movements into churches regardless of their founders' intentions. Neoterra's fate will be decided exactly here: whether openness survives the arrival of an institution. See the open question in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> and &quot;mission or messiah&quot; in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a>.</li></ul><h2>In sum</h2><p>Neoterra is not a religion (by epistemology), not yet a movement (in fact), and already a philosophy (by content): <strong>a naturalistic life-philosophy designed for communal practice</strong>. Its measure of success is set by its mission: do the people near it become more united, more humane, and more in accord with Nature?</p><p><strong>And it imposes nothing.</strong> There is no lawgiver — hence neither sin, nor duty, nor punishment; nor does it issue a finished picture of the world, but offers an angle of view held open to revision. Hence the answer to where a philosophy without compulsion gets its <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>, its <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">codex</a> and its <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">measure of deeds</a>: <strong>obligation is not imposed but taken up</strong> — the only duty here is the one a person lays upon themselves. This sets it apart from religions by function more sharply than the absence of rite does: the niche is occupied, the machinery of compulsion is not (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a>).</p><p>And it is unfinished on principle: Neoterra grows by seeking ever new points of contact to add to those already found — with traditions, sciences, cultures and people. The growth of the web of links is not a side effect but its very manner of existing (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a>).</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a> — the system's self-definition</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a> — a map of parallels and differences</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> — the three verbs of the mission</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">Giving and Its Distribution</a> — the movement layer</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — why this is not a religion in substance</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовная-зрячесть\">Spiritual Sight</a> — the addressee: the spiritually sighted without a home; belief as function, not dogma</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кодекс-неотерра\">The Code of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-манифест\">The Great Manifesto of Neoterra</a></li></ul>"},"аристотель":{"name":"Aristotle","def":"Aristotle (Ἀριστοτέλης, 384–322 BCE) — ancient Greek philosopher, heir of the Socratic line through Plato, tutor of Alexander the Great.","html":"<p>Aristotle (Ἀριστοτέλης, 384–322 BCE) — ancient Greek philosopher, heir of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">the Socratic</a> line through Plato, tutor of Alexander the Great. He is often called &quot;the first scientist&quot;: he was the first to take in knowing as a whole and to see its structure.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><p><strong>The main thing is not the sorting but the insight into structure.</strong> Aristotle did not merely divide knowledge into subjects (physics, metaphysics, logic, ethics, politics, poetics, biology). He grasped that these are <strong>separate branches of knowing the world</strong> — each with its own subject, method and language, and all growing from a common drive to understand. Before him, knowledge was a single undivided wisdom-seeking; after him, a tree of disciplines. This is the first realisation in history that <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">knowing</a> branches.</p><p>And here is a deep rhyme with the form of Neoterra itself. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network</a> says: knowledge repeats the form of Nature — not a monolith but a branching from an origin. More than two thousand years earlier, Aristotle was the first to see that knowing is not one thing but many branches. He discovered the fact of branching itself.</p><p><strong>Observation of nature.</strong> Aristotle was a biologist too: he described animals, dissected, classified. Knowledge for him began with observing the world rather than with pure speculation — close to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">the scientific method</a> and to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"дарвин\">Darwin's</a> patient looking at the living.</p><p><strong>Immanent purpose.</strong> His teleology (entelechy, the final cause) — the idea that things have an inner drive toward their own fullness — echoes how Neoterra holds <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Nature's direction</a>: not an external blueprint but an inner unfolding (cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>, the seed of growth).</p><p><strong>Measure.</strong> The doctrine of the mean (virtue as a middle between extremes) is kin to Neoterra's attention to a balance won not by repose but by discernment (cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>).</p><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p><strong>Tree against network.</strong> Aristotle's structure of knowledge is <strong>a hierarchy</strong>: genera and species, categories, a ladder of classification in which every thing occupies its place in an order of subordination. Neoterra inherits his insight about branches — but overturns the form: not a tree with a summit but <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">a network with an origin</a>, where hierarchy is replaced by connection and the liveliest places are the crossings between areas. Aristotle discovered branching; Neoterra opens it out of a tree into a mycelium.</p><p><strong>Purpose as form.</strong> Aristotle's teleology inclines toward a given, almost external goal-form to which a thing is &quot;obliged&quot; to come. Neoterra holds only an immanent direction, not a guaranteed goal (the open question of teleology in the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>).</p><p><strong>A static cosmos.</strong> Aristotle's geocentric, eternally unchanging picture of the world has been refuted by science — and that is fine: Neoterra goes with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>, which revises itself. What is valuable is not his physics but his method of dividing and looking closely.</p><h2>Key ideas</h2><ul><li>&quot;All men by nature desire to know&quot; (the opening of the <em>Metaphysics</em>) — knowledge as a natural drive, not a luxury (cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>).</li><li>A classification of the sciences: theoretical (physics, mathematics, metaphysics), practical (ethics, politics), productive (poetics, rhetoric) — the first map of knowing's branches.</li><li>The four causes and the final cause — an attempt to explain <em>why</em> a thing is what it is.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> — Aristotle as the one who first saw knowing divided into branches</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a> — his tree of disciplines, rethought as a mycelial network</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates (469–399 BCE)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — the line of method and honest questioning</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"дарвин\">Charles Darwin (1809–1882)</a> — observing the living as the origin of knowledge</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a></li></ul>"},"бусидо":{"name":"Bushido","def":"\"The way of the warrior\" (武士道) — the ethical code of Japan's samurai, taking shape by the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries at the meeting of Zen Buddhism, Confucianism and Shinto.","html":"<p>&quot;The way of the warrior&quot; (武士道) — the ethical code of Japan's samurai, taking shape by the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries at the meeting of Zen Buddhism, Confucianism and Shinto. Not a book and not a dogma but a living body of virtues handed on by upbringing and example. The classic texts: Yamamoto Tsunetomo's <em>Hagakure</em>, Daidōji Yūzan's <em>Budōshoshinshū</em>; for the West the code was described by Nitobe Inazō in <em>Bushido: The Soul of Japan</em> (1900).</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"бусидо.png\" alt=\"бусидо.png\"> <em>Three characters from top to bottom: <strong>武</strong> — the martial, <strong>士</strong> — the man, <strong>道</strong> — the way. The whole adaptation below rests on this: the wiki leaves the third character untouched and reforges the first — the way remains, the war departs. The same <strong>道</strong> stands in the name of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Daoism</a> — &quot;dao&quot;, and this is not a coincidence of spelling but one word: the way as a manner of being, not as a route. The board itself suits the code — a rough shard of slate on a cord, no frame and no gilding: bushido was not a book or a dogma; it was handed on by upbringing and example.</em></p><h2>The seven virtues of bushido</h2><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Virtue</th><th>Substance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>義 Gi — righteousness</td><td>Straightness of decision: to know what is right and to do it</td></tr><tr><td>勇 Yū — courage</td><td>Action despite fear; bravery without righteousness is no virtue</td></tr><tr><td>仁 Jin — benevolence</td><td>Strength owes itself to compassion; the strong protect rather than crush</td></tr><tr><td>礼 Rei — respect</td><td>Courtesy as the outward form of inward respect for a person</td></tr><tr><td>誠 Makoto — sincerity</td><td>A samurai's word is firmer than a written contract; lying is cowardice</td></tr><tr><td>名誉 Meiyo — honour</td><td>Dignity lies not in others' eyes but in one's own judgement of oneself</td></tr><tr><td>忠義 Chūgi — loyalty</td><td>Devotion to the work and to the people one has taken responsibility for</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><p>The seven virtues of bushido coincide almost exactly with the seven virtues of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the path of a person</a> (honesty · courage · self-discipline · responsibility · respect · creation · wisdom). This is not borrowing but convergence: different cultures, looking at a mature person, see the same thing.</p><ul><li><strong>Strength as an instrument of protection, not dominion</strong> — <em>jin</em> coincides directly with the man's path in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a>: &quot;does not crush the weak — uses strength for defence&quot;.</li><li><strong>Discipline as freedom</strong> — the daily polishing of oneself; the very &quot;discipline is not the opposite of freedom but its condition&quot; from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>.</li><li><strong>Mastery as a road without end</strong> — a samurai polishes one art all his life; the stage of mastery in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> and in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a>.</li><li><strong>Memento mori</strong> — bushido's constant remembrance of death is kin to Stoic and Neoterran clarity: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">death</a> gives life weight rather than devaluing it.</li><li>The kinship with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoicism</a> is plain: two independent codes of self-command — one grown in Greece and Rome, the other in Japan.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence from classical bushido</h2><p>The historical code carries four features Neoterra does not take into its path:</p><ul><li><strong>A cult of death.</strong> <em>Hagakure</em>: &quot;The way of the samurai is death.&quot; <em>Seppuku</em> is incompatible with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a>.</li><li><strong>Revenge</strong> as a duty of honour — a chain in which evil reproduces itself.</li><li><strong>Absolute loyalty to a lord</strong> — devotion to a suzerain above one's own judgement.</li><li><strong>War as a craft</strong> — the code was born of the battlefield and served it.</li></ul><p>The adaptation below — the keeper's decision — removes each of these deliberately rather than passing over them.</p><h2>Bushido adapted for Neoterra</h2><p>Take the steel, remove the war. Seven virtues, reforged from a warrior's code into a maker's:</p><ol><li><strong>Righteousness</strong> — to see what is right and do it, even when it is inconvenient. Not by order but by conscience (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>).</li><li><strong>Courage</strong> — action despite fear: to tell the truth, to begin again, to admit an error (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a>).</li><li><strong>Benevolence</strong> — strength exists in order to protect life. The measure of strength is care (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a>).</li><li><strong>Respect</strong> — for people, for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, for oneself. Courtesy is not etiquette but the practice of seeing what is alive in another.</li><li><strong>Sincerity</strong> — word and deed are one; honesty above all before oneself (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>).</li><li><strong>Dignity without revenge</strong> — one's judgement of oneself is stricter than others', but without pride: not &quot;better than others&quot; but better than yesterday's self. An injury does not create a debt of blood: revenge is a chain, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">forgiveness</a> its opening.</li><li><strong>Loyalty to one's own road</strong> — not to a lord but to the road a person chose themselves (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a>). Such loyalty is not blind: it includes the right to revise the road — but not to abandon it at the first hardship.</li></ol><h3>Four replacements at the foundation</h3><ul><li><strong>Life instead of death.</strong> Where bushido says &quot;the way of the warrior is death&quot;, Neoterra sets: <strong>the way of a person is a life that grows continually</strong> (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>). The remembrance of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">death</a> remains — as a whetstone, not as a blade: it gives the day weight but is not the aim.</li><li><strong>Forgiveness instead of revenge.</strong> An honour that demands blood is not honour but pride. Dignity is restored by growth, not by reprisal (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">Forgiveness</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a>).</li><li><strong>One's own road instead of a lord.</strong> No authority stands above <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">truth</a> and one's own thinking. A person's only &quot;suzerain&quot; is the road they chose themselves.</li><li><strong>Preventing war instead of waging it.</strong> War is what humanity must not repeat. A maker's highest &quot;martial art&quot; is negotiation: to hear the other, to look for the common, to quench a conflict before it becomes a war (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a>). The tempering of character is not lost — it is carried from the battlefield to a harder field: holding a peace where striking would be easier.</li></ul><p>And the code is not for a caste: the road is open to anyone who chooses it.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Benevolence says: strength exists to protect life. Preventing war is the highest form of protection. But if war has already come and negotiation has failed — where is the border between protecting life and repeating war?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — the seven virtues: the convergence of two codes</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoicism</a> — bushido's Western twin</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> — discipline as the condition of freedom; against loyalty above truth</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — the border of the adaptation: no cult of death</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> — memento mori as clarity</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"прощение\">Forgiveness</a> — instead of revenge; the opening of evil's chain</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> — the ability to negotiate and to prevent war</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Философия\">Philosophy — area</a> — the area</li></ul>"},"гораций":{"name":"Quintus Horatius Flaccus (65–8 BC)","def":"Roman poet, son of a freedman, who fought at Philippi on the losing side and, after the amnesty, entered the circle of Maecenas.","html":"<p>Roman poet, son of a freedman, who fought at Philippi on the losing side and, after the amnesty, entered the circle of Maecenas. Author of the <em>Odes</em>, the <em>Satires</em>, the <em>Epistles</em> and the <em>Art of Poetry</em>. He stands in the wiki for two words from one ode — <strong>carpe diem</strong> — and for the fact that these two words are almost always quoted wrongly.</p><h2>What is actually said</h2><p>Ode I.11, to Leuconoe, published around 23 BC. It begins not with a call to enjoy but with a ban on calculating:</p><blockquote><p>Tu ne quaesieris (scire nefas) quem mihi, quem tibi / finem di dederint, Leuconoe, nec Babylonios / temptaris numeros.</p><p><em>Do not ask — it is forbidden to know — what end the gods have given to me, to you, Leuconoe, and do not try Babylonian numbers.</em></p></blockquote><p>&quot;Babylonian numbers&quot; is astrology. The ode is addressed to a person who has gone off <strong>to calculate their future</strong>. Then: &quot;be wise, strain the wine, and in a brief span <strong>cut back long hope</strong>&quot; (<em>spem longam reseces</em>), &quot;while we speak, envious time will have fled&quot; (<em>dum loquimur, fugerit invida aetas</em>). And only then the famous line:</p><blockquote><p>carpe diem, <strong>quam minimum credula postero</strong></p><p><em>pluck the day, trusting as little as possible in tomorrow.</em></p></blockquote><p><strong>The second half of the line is almost always cut off, and it is the argument.</strong> Carpe diem is not &quot;remember death&quot; and not a call to feast. It is <strong>an argument against trying to calculate the future</strong>: pluck today, because tomorrow cannot be reckoned.</p><p><strong>And the verb is not &quot;seize.&quot;</strong> Latin <em>carpe</em> comes from the language of farming: it is how one plucks a ripe fruit or cuts a flower. The English <em>seize the day</em> brought in a grabbing that is not in Horace; his is the gesture of gathering what <strong>has ripened now</strong>.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>The future cannot be calculated — and this is not a misfortune but how things are built.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The theory of instants</a>: &quot;to predict, one would have to know all the instants of all scales at once.&quot; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The time loop</a>: &quot;the future cannot be predicted, but it can be touched.&quot; Horace says the same, and on the same occasion — against divination by numbers. The coincidence here is not in mood but in claim.</li><li><strong>The shared fruit.</strong> The central image of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">theory of instants</a> is a fruit that will sooner or later fall from the tree, and the instant of falling that began with the first movement. <em>Carpe</em> — to pluck a ripe fruit. The same fruit in two thoughts about time, two thousand years apart. This is <strong>resonance, not proof</strong> — a caveat on the model of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">quantum unity</a>.</li><li><strong>The first link of an instant of thought.</strong> Horace's line is a working example of how a thought lasts through the nested instants of other people's minds (see &quot;The instant of thought&quot; in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a>). It did not wait — it lasted, because others worked for it.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>&quot;Cut back long hope&quot; ↔ Neoterra's long horizon.</strong> The divergence dissolves if one separates <strong>hope and building</strong>. Hope is the expectation that the future will happen by itself; that is what is to be cut back. Neoterra's horizon rests not on it but on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a>: the future is not awaited, it is built (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a>). Then Horace is not an opponent of the long horizon but its condition: he cuts away exactly the support that Neoterra does not stand on.</li><li><strong>Where the rest of life goes.</strong> For Horace, the incalculability of the future leads to <strong>moderation and private life</strong>: wine, a brief span, one's own garden. Neoterra draws the opposite conclusion — if the future is not foretold, it is <strong>open to be built</strong>, and the question of life remains the same: not how long one lived but what one left (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a>). If you do not build, another will; the trace left will not be yours. This is a difference of substance, and it does not dissolve.</li><li><strong>A caveat about the ladder.</strong> It does not follow from the previous point that a life without a trace left behind is worse. What is left is <strong>a task</strong>, not a measure of dignity: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect for life</a> is not issued according to the results of the path travelled, and the stretch of experience lived is full even for someone who built nothing (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a>). Oblivion is a fact about the trace, not a verdict on a life.</li><li><strong>The Epicurean lean.</strong> Horace called himself &quot;a pig from Epicurus's herd&quot; (<em>Epicuri de grege porcum</em>, <em>Epistles</em> I.4). Ataraxia and withdrawal from the common cause are not Neoterra's position (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>), even where its premise is accepted.</li></ul><h2>On quoting</h2><p>The rule introduced on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Kafka</a> and confirmed on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сальвадор-дали\">Dalí</a> applies here too, and sharply: <strong>carpe diem travels the world cut off from the second half of the line</strong> and is therefore read exactly backwards — as permission not to think about tomorrow, whereas what is said is &quot;do not trust the reckoning of tomorrow.&quot; The wiki quotes the line whole or not at all.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — the instant of thought; the fruit that will fall; the future as a field, not a schedule</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a> — the future cannot be predicted, but it can be touched</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> — what remains; hope versus building</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoicism</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius (121–180)</a> — the neighbouring Roman line of working with time</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Baruch Spinoza (1632–1677)</a> — necessity without design: the same fork from the other end</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> — finitude as what gives weight</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Franz Kafka (1883–1924)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сальвадор-дали\">Salvador Dalí (1904–1989)</a> — the rule of quotation</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хранитель\">The Keeper</a> — whose thought met this line</li></ul>"},"гуманизм":{"name":"Humanism","def":"A philosophical movement placing the human being at the centre of its worldview.","html":"<p>A philosophical movement placing the human being at the centre of its worldview. The emphasis falls on reason, science, education and individual rights. In secular humanism, without recourse to the supernatural.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><p>One of the systems closest to Neoterra:</p><ul><li><strong>The worth of the person</strong> — every individual has dignity</li><li><strong>Individual rights</strong> — freedom of thought, no dogmas</li><li><strong>Science</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">knowledge</a> as the engine of a civilisation's growth</li><li><strong>Education</strong> — a necessary condition of growth</li><li><strong>Critical thinking</strong> — no position is accepted on faith</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>Humanism is often concentrated on the human being alone. Neoterra goes beyond that horizon:</p><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> is not a background but part of one whole</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a> is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity's</a> next horizon</li><li>The archetype of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a> — an explorer, not only a citizen</li><li>The Book of Memory — responsibility toward those who come after us</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a></li></ul>"},"конфуцианство":{"name":"Confucianism","def":"A philosophical and ethical system founded by Confucius.","html":"<p>A philosophical and ethical system founded by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius</a>. At its centre: morality, family, social roles, and the forming of a person through culture and rite. It shaped China, Japan, Korea and Vietnam enormously.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><p>One of the systems closest to Neoterra:</p><ul><li><strong>Family</strong> — the basic cell of society and the school of virtue</li><li><strong>Upbringing</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">the growth of a person</a> through relationships and mentorship</li><li><strong>Responsibility</strong> — toward family, society, ancestors</li><li><strong>Mentorship</strong> — the handing on of knowledge and wisdom to the next generations</li><li><strong>Respect</strong> — for people, for continuity, for tradition</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>Confucianism is turned toward social order and preservation. Neoterra is more strongly oriented toward progress, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> and the future — including <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">space</a> and the long horizon of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity</a>.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius (551–479 BCE)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a></li></ul>"},"конфуций":{"name":"Confucius (551–479 BCE)","def":"Chinese philosopher, founder of Confucianism.","html":"<p>Chinese philosopher, founder of Confucianism. A teaching on morality, family and the state that shaped the culture of East Asia enormously.</p><blockquote><p>A strong society begins with a worthy person.</p></blockquote><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>The family as the basis of society</strong> — one of Neoterra's ten values. Confucius made it the centre of his system.</li><li><strong>The forming of character</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">the growth of a person</a> begins with inner work, not with outward change.</li><li><strong>The role of community</strong> — a person is realised through relationships, not in isolation.</li><li><strong>Responsibility toward society</strong> — personal growth is inseparable from a contribution to the common.</li><li><strong>Respect for continuity</strong> — knowledge and wisdom are handed on across generations.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>Confucianism is hierarchical: strict roles of father/son, ruler/subject. Neoterra emphasises <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">horizontal connections</a> and freedom of thought rather than hierarchy.</p><h2>Key idea</h2><p>Confucius is the only one of the five principal forerunners who placed the community above the individual. That is exactly how he balances Nietzsche within Neoterra.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius (121–180)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a></li></ul>"},"лосев":{"name":"Aleksei Fyodorovich Losev","def":"Russian philosopher and philologist (1893–1988), the last thinker of the Silver Age to live to the end of the Soviet era.","html":"<p>Russian philosopher and philologist (1893–1988), the last thinker of the Silver Age to live to the end of the Soviet era. Author of <em>The Dialectics of Myth</em> (1930) and the eight-volume <em>History of Ancient Aesthetics</em>. For <em>The Dialectics of Myth</em> he was arrested and sent to a camp to build the White Sea Canal, where he almost entirely lost his sight — and afterwards worked for another half century, dictating his books. A secret monk (tonsured in 1929, under the name Andronik).</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><p><strong>Myth is not invention but reality.</strong> The chief thesis of <em>The Dialectics of Myth</em>: myth is &quot;not an invention and not a fiction but the most vivid and most genuine reality&quot;. For a person living inside a myth it is not a &quot;primitive explanation of the world&quot; but the very fabric of their life. This is a direct voice in the open question of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">the page on God</a>: personal faith is not an error to be &quot;grown out of&quot; but a living way of experiencing reality. Losev does not permit it to be called condescendingly &quot;an early stage&quot; — and so keeps Neoterra from arrogance.</p><p><strong>The symbol as the identity of idea and thing.</strong> Losev built a whole philosophy of the symbol: a symbol does not &quot;denote&quot; a meaning but manifests it — the ideal and the real coincide in it. This is the theoretical footing for how <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">the seed-sprout</a> works: not an illustration of the idea of growth but the idea itself, given visibly.</p><p><strong>The name as the energy of an essence.</strong> From the tradition of <em>onomatodoxy</em> Losev drew the thought that a thing's name is not a label but the action of the essence itself within us. This echoes <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">the languages of Nature</a>: in naming and reading the world a person does not stick on labels but enters into communication with reality.</p><p><strong>Faithfulness to a road through trial.</strong> The camp, blindness, decades of a ban on philosophy — and not one abandoned work. A living embodiment of the stage of trial in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the path of a person</a> and of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> despite circumstance.</p><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li>Losev was an Orthodox monk: for him a personal God is not &quot;a point on a road&quot; but the summit and fullness of truth. Pantheism (including Spinoza's <em>Deus sive Natura</em>, close to Neoterra) he criticised outright as a depersonalising of the Absolute.</li><li>Hierarchy and dogma: Losev thought out of a tradition with untouchable truths — against <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Neoterra's principle</a> that everything is open to criticism.</li></ul><p>That is exactly why his voice is valuable: he is the strongest opponent of the thesis &quot;Nature = God&quot; from inside the very personal faith that Neoterra risks treating as &quot;a stage&quot;.</p><h2>Key quotations and ideas</h2><blockquote><p>&quot;Myth is not an invention and not a fiction, not a fantastic fabrication, but the most vivid and most genuine reality.&quot;</p></blockquote><blockquote><p><em>The Dialectics of Myth</em>: even materialism is a myth too, its own faith in its own picture of the world.</p></blockquote><ul><li>The symbol as the identity of the ideal and the real</li><li>The name as the energy of an essence</li><li>Eight volumes of the <em>History of Ancient Aesthetics</em> — the whole of ancient thought as one whole</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> — the voice against &quot;an early stage&quot;: myth and personal faith as genuine reality</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"символ-неотерра\">The Symbol of Neoterra</a> — the philosophy of the symbol as the emblem's foundation</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — the name as communication with reality</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> — trial and faithfulness to one's work</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Философия\">Philosophy — area</a> — the area</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> — the point of divergence: dogma against openness to criticism</li></ul>"},"марк-аврелий":{"name":"Marcus Aurelius (121–180)","def":"Roman emperor and Stoic philosopher.","html":"<p>Roman emperor and Stoic philosopher. Author of the <em>Meditations</em> — a private diary never intended for publication. One of the rare examples of a person who combined power with philosophical practice.</p><blockquote><p>Govern yourself before you try to govern the world.</p></blockquote><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Discipline</strong> — not as self-restriction but as an instrument of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>.</li><li><strong>Governing the emotions</strong> — inner work as the condition of outward action.</li><li><strong>Responsibility</strong> — before oneself, before people, before history. Marcus Aurelius carried the burden of an empire without losing his personal ethics.</li><li><strong>Courage</strong> — accepting what is hard without complaint.</li><li><strong>Inner growth</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">Neoterra's Wanderer</a> works on themselves continually, as Marcus Aurelius did in his diary.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>Stoicism inclines toward the acceptance of fate (<em>amor fati</em>). Neoterra is active: it does not merely accept the world but seeks to change and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">widen</a> it.</p><h2>Key quotation</h2><blockquote><p>&quot;Loss is nothing else but change, and change is Nature's delight.&quot;</p></blockquote><p>In accord with the idea of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> as a continually changing system.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius (551–479 BCE)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Friedrich Nietzsche (1844–1900)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a></li></ul>"},"ницше":{"name":"Friedrich Nietzsche (1844–1900)","def":"German philosopher, one of the most influential and most disputed thinkers of the nineteenth century.","html":"<p>German philosopher, one of the most influential and most disputed thinkers of the nineteenth century. Author of the concepts of the overhuman, the will to power, and eternal recurrence.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"ницше.jpg\" alt=\"ницше.jpg\"> <em>He looks past the lens, aside and a little down — not at the camera and not at the viewer: a man occupied with something other than how he will be seen. The photograph is from 1882, a year before &quot;Thus Spoke Zarathustra&quot; and its image of the rope over the abyss. The abyss itself the wiki reads its own way — not a fall back into the animal, but ignorance, which halts <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>.</em></p><blockquote><p>Man is something that shall be overcome.</p></blockquote><p><strong>Where he came from.</strong> In 1865 Nietzsche found <em>The World as Will and Representation</em> in a Leipzig bookshop and declared himself a disciple of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Schopenhauer</a> — and then turned him a hundred and eighty degrees: instead of the denial of will, the will to power; instead of repose, overcoming. Everything in Nietzsche that is close to Neoterra is that turn, and without the starting point the turn cannot be read.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>The growth of the person</strong> — for Nietzsche <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> is not an option but a requirement. A person who does not grow degrades.</li><li><strong>Self-perfection</strong> — not the imitation of an ideal but the making of one's own road.</li><li><strong>The search for one's own way</strong> — a refusal of herd thinking, a readiness to go against the current.</li><li><strong>The Wanderer archetype</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">Neoterra's Wanderer</a> carries the Nietzschean impulse: solitude as the condition of growth, the road as the goal itself.</li></ul><h2>The tightrope: where the seeing stand</h2><blockquote><p>&quot;Man is a rope, tied between beast and overman — a rope over an abyss.&quot; — <em>Thus Spoke Zarathustra</em></p></blockquote><p>Neoterra reads this image literally as a map of the road: behind, <em>Homo erectus</em>; ahead, the overhuman; and all humanity on the rope between them. But people stand at different places on it. Those who see the world as followers of Neoterra do — who make out <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">connections where an ordinary eye has already clouded</a> — have, without realising it, walked further along the rope. Not because they are of another breed but because they kept, or washed clean again, their <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">clear eyes</a>.</p><p>A safeguard matters here. Nietzsche's overhuman is a temptation to elitism, and Neoterra rejects that temptation: clear eyes are given to <strong>everyone</strong> at birth, the entrance is open to all (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a>), and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">the gradient of awareness</a> does not rank people's worth (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>). The rope is not a ladder of the elect but a common road: the only difference is how many steps have already been taken — and any step can be taken by anyone.</p><p>The abyss beneath the rope is Neoterra's own too: not &quot;a fall into the animal&quot; but ignorance — a way of life that clouds the eyes and stops <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>.</p><p>Nietzsche is deeply sceptical of collectivism, of community, of compassion as a value (&quot;slave morality&quot;). Neoterra accepts both individual <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">the unity of humanity</a>. This is a real tension, which Neoterra holds rather than removes.</p><p>Nietzsche rejected the idea of civilisational progress. Neoterra does not.</p><h2>Key quotation</h2><blockquote><p>&quot;He who has a why to live can bear almost any how.&quot;</p></blockquote><p>Neoterra gives no ready &quot;why&quot; — it helps a person find their own.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Arthur Schopenhauer (1788–1860)</a> — the teacher Nietzsche turned around: the root of this page</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius (121–180)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> — overcoming oneself as a continual breaking of one's own frame</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — clear eyes and the gradient of awareness: where a person stands on the rope</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a></li></ul>"},"парменид":{"name":"Parmenides","def":"Parmenides of Elea (c. 515–450 BCE) — a pre-Socratic, founder of the Eleatic school and, in effect, of ontology.","html":"<p>Parmenides of Elea (c. 515–450 BCE) — a pre-Socratic, founder of the Eleatic school and, in effect, of ontology. In the poem <em>On Nature</em> he was the first in Western thought to replace myth with proof: truth is not to be told but derived by reason. His thesis: being is one, eternal and unchanging; non-being is not.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>The unity of being ↔ <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>.</strong> &quot;All is one&quot;: for Parmenides there is no isolated existence; being is indivisible and connected. This is the philosophical ancestor of the first law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon of Nature</a> — &quot;everything is part of one system&quot;.</li><li><strong>The way of truth and the way of opinion ↔ <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>.</strong> The poem separates <em>aletheia</em> (truth won by reason) from <em>doxa</em> (opinion, the habit of the senses). The distinction between knowledge and opinion is the very support on which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a> stand.</li><li><strong>Eternal being ↔ <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a>.</strong> The block universe of eternalism — &quot;past, present and future exist on equal terms&quot; — is called Parmenidean outright; in conversation with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a>, Popper called him &quot;Parmenides&quot;. An ancient intuition and the physics of time resonate here.</li><li><strong>Proof instead of myth ↔ <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>.</strong> Parmenides demands: follow the argument, not the tradition. This is the first step toward the deductive method — the root from which science grew.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>The denial of motion and change.</strong> For Parmenides change is an illusion, since being has nowhere to come from and nothing to vanish into. Neoterra stands on the opposite: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> is the meaning of life itself. Here it is nearer to Heraclitus and his flux; but Nature holds both — unity <em>and</em> becoming, the repose of law <em>and</em> the flow of forms. The classical Parmenides/Heraclitus pair is a model of how a contradiction turns out to be two sides of one world.</li><li><strong>Distrust of the senses.</strong> Parmenides declares sensory experience a deception; Neoterra, following science, trusts observation — but tested and reproducible observation. The lesson is taken more gently: the senses do not lie, hasty conclusions from them do.</li></ul><h2>Key quotations and ideas</h2><blockquote><p>&quot;Being is, and non-being is not&quot; — what exists cannot be derived from nothing.</p></blockquote><blockquote><p>&quot;It is the same thing to think and to be&quot; — the world is knowable; reason and being are commensurate.</p></blockquote><ul><li>The two parts of the poem <em>On Nature</em>: the way of truth and the way of opinion</li><li>Being: one, eternal, indivisible, motionless, complete</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — the main point of contact</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> — <em>aletheia</em> against <em>doxa</em></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> — the block universe as &quot;Parmenidean&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The Moment of Truth</a> — time as one moment entire; the pair with Heraclitus dissolves</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates (469–399 BCE)</a> — in Plato's dialogue <em>Parmenides</em> the old Eleatic tests the young Socrates</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Albert Einstein (1879–1955)</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Философия\">Philosophy — area</a> — the head of the area</li></ul>"},"поппер":{"name":"Karl Popper (1902–1994)","def":"Austrian-British philosopher of science.","html":"<p>Austrian-British philosopher of science. Originator of the principle of falsifiability: a theory is scientific only if it can be refuted. Author of <em>The Open Society and Its Enemies</em>.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"popper.jpg\" alt=\"popper.jpg\"> <em>An old man holds his head — and at the same time looks into the camera with a grin. The posture of someone who has just been shown that he was wrong, and whom this rather amused than stung. That is exactly what <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> looks like on Popper's terms: refutation is no defeat but the only way to move on.</em></p><blockquote><p>Any theory may turn out to be wrong.</p></blockquote><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Ideas are not final</strong> — Neoterra states plainly that its books and positions may be revised. This is Popper's principle carried into a philosophy of life.</li><li><strong>Truth above authority</strong> — neither an author's standing nor a tradition shields an idea from criticism.</li><li><strong>Critical thinking</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> as the best instrument for knowing reality, but not an absolute.</li><li><strong>The open society</strong> — a society capable of self-correction, echoing the idea of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity as a single community</a> able to learn.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>Popper is concentrated on epistemology and political philosophy. Neoterra's existential and spiritual dimension is alien to him.</p><h2>Key quotation</h2><blockquote><p>&quot;Optimism is a duty. The future is open.&quot;</p></blockquote><p>Directly in accord with Neoterra's orientation toward <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">the future</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates (469–399 BCE)</a> — a forerunner in the tradition of &quot;truth above authority&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a></li></ul>"},"русский-космизм":{"name":"Russian Cosmism","def":"A current of Russian thought from the late nineteenth to the first half of the twentieth century, joining philosophy, natural science and the dream of humanity going out into space.","html":"<p>A current of Russian thought from the late nineteenth to the first half of the twentieth century, joining philosophy, natural science and the dream of humanity going out into space. Not a school with a charter but a family of neighbouring views with a common core: <strong>humanity is not a finished species but a participant in cosmic evolution, obliged to continue it consciously</strong>.</p><p>The key figures:</p><ul><li><strong>Nikolai Fyodorov</strong> (1829–1903), <em>The Philosophy of the Common Task</em>: death is the chief enemy; humanity's task is to unite in order to defeat it and to settle space. His &quot;common task&quot; is the ultimate form of a collective aim.</li><li><strong>Konstantin Tsiolkovsky</strong> (1857–1935): calculations of spaceflight together with a philosophy of &quot;monism&quot; — the Universe is ensouled, and mind will inevitably spread through it. To him belongs the phrase &quot;a planet is the cradle of mind, but one cannot live forever in a cradle&quot;, which <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan</a> carried to the world.</li><li><strong>Vladimir Vernadsky</strong> (1863–1945): the biosphere as a geological force, and <strong>the noosphere</strong> — the sphere of mind into which the biosphere passes when humanity's thinking becomes a planetary factor.</li><li><strong>Alexander Chizhevsky</strong> (1897–1964): earthly life and history as a response to solar rhythms — a literal connectedness of the living with the cosmos.</li></ul><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Space as a horizon, not a backdrop.</strong> For the cosmists <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">going beyond the Earth</a> is not an adventure but a duty of the species. Neoterra says the same: concentration on one planet is an existential risk, and the spreading of life is the continuation of a natural process.</li><li><strong>The human being within Nature, not above it.</strong> Vernadsky's noosphere is not power over the biosphere but its new stage: mind as a geological force of Nature. This is almost word for word <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a> and the seventh law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon of Nature</a>.</li><li><strong>The conscious continuation of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">evolution</a>.</strong> Evolution stops being blind where a mind appears that can answer for it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>).</li><li><strong>The unity of humanity as a condition.</strong> For Fyodorov the &quot;common task&quot; is impossible for the disunited. For Neoterra, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">unity</a> is a necessary condition of an interplanetary civilisation.</li><li><strong>A long horizon.</strong> The cosmists thought in millennia and worked toward what they would not see — the same stake as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">the relay of generations</a> and in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">the symbiont's way</a>.</li><li><strong>Science as an instrument, not an opponent of spirit.</strong> Cosmism joined exact calculation with a philosophy of the whole — the very <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">parallel movement</a> Neoterra sets at its base.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>Defeating death and resurrecting the fathers.</strong> For Fyodorov the aim is literally to resurrect all the dead. Neoterra looks at <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">death</a> otherwise: the individual's end is not an enemy but the condition of renewal; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">the spiral</a> holds by the turn of generations, not by their abolition.</li><li><strong>Teleology.</strong> For the cosmists the Universe often has a goal toward which mind leads. Neoterra holds &quot;design&quot; only as an immanent direction, not as a blueprint (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>, &quot;A design of Nature?&quot;).</li><li><strong>Obligation against freedom.</strong> Cosmism says &quot;must&quot;: settle space, defeat death, unite. Neoterra does not compel — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a> and the refusal of dogma come before any great aim.</li><li><strong>A mystical stratum.</strong> For Tsiolkovsky the Universe is ensouled and happy; for Fyodorov the project is outright religious. Neoterra holds <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Nature-God</a> without a person and without promises.</li><li><strong>The price of a great aim.</strong> The idea of a &quot;common task&quot; for whose sake much is permitted already showed in the twentieth century what it turns into in practice. Neoterra places before any aim <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">the Great Principle</a> and the dignity of the individual person.</li></ul><h2>How to read this in Neoterra</h2><p>Cosmism is valuable as <strong>a forerunner that reached the same conclusions through another door</strong>: not from a philosophy of Nature to space but from engineering and natural science to philosophy. It shows that the chain &quot;the human being is part of Nature → mind is obliged to continue its work → therefore space&quot; arises independently, in different people and different languages. Neoterra takes from it the scale and the seriousness of a long horizon — and refuses its obligation and its defeat of death.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эволюция\">Evolution</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"новый-космический-год\">A New Cosmic Year</a> — the next stage of evolution and the question of readiness</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Carl Sagan (1934–1996)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Stephen Hawking (1942–2018)</a> — the same thought in the twentieth-century West</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a> — the chief divergence from Fyodorov</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">The Symbiont's Way</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a></li></ul>"},"сократ":{"name":"Socrates (469–399 BCE)","def":"Ancient Greek philosopher, founder of Western ethics and of the dialectical method.","html":"<p>Ancient Greek philosopher, founder of Western ethics and of the dialectical method. He left no written texts — he is known through Plato and Xenophon.</p><blockquote><p>&quot;I know that I know nothing.&quot;</p></blockquote><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>The search for truth above authority</strong> — Socrates was ready to dispute any statement that did not stand up to reason. Neoterra is built on the same principle.</li><li><strong>No absolute truth</strong> — acknowledging one's ignorance as the starting point of knowing coincides with Neoterra's refusal to claim finality.</li><li><strong>A continual search</strong> — not a state but a process. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> as a way of life.</li><li><strong>Readiness to admit mistakes</strong> — the basis of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">critical thinking</a> in Neoterra.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>Socrates was concentrated on the individual soul and on ethics. Neoterra's cosmic and civilisational horizon is alien to him.</p><h2>Key quotation</h2><blockquote><p>&quot;The unexamined life is not worth living.&quot;</p><p>(ὁ ἀνεξέταστος βίος)</p></blockquote><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">Neoterra's Wanderer</a> examines life through experience. Socrates did it through dialogue. The method differs, the impulse is one.</p><h2>Examination as Neoterra's mission</h2><p>Socrates sets the imperative but leaves a person alone with the task: life must be examined — and how, he shows only by questioning. <strong>Neoterra takes up that imperative and makes it its own work: to give life examination — and to let a person see everything as it actually is.</strong></p><p>&quot;Seeing as it is&quot; here is not omniscience but a cleared gaze: removing cognitive biases, other people's ready opinions and self-deception, which clutter the mind (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>), and looking with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">clear eyes</a>. This is a direct continuation of Socrates' &quot;I know that I know nothing&quot; — honesty before reality ahead of comfort.</p><p><strong>An honest limit.</strong> Full reality &quot;as it is in itself&quot; is closed to a person: perception passes through a filter (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> — the Kantian line: we see the world through the forms of our own perception, not &quot;as it is&quot;). So &quot;seeing as it actually is&quot; in Neoterra means the most honest gaze, cleared of distortions, and not a claim to an absolute picture. Examination is a process of drawing nearer to truth (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>), not a possession of it.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — continued the Socratic principle in falsifiability</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — examination as a cleared gaze; clear eyes</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> — why &quot;as it actually is&quot; has a limit</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a></li></ul>"},"спиноза":{"name":"Baruch Spinoza (1632–1677)","def":"Dutch philosopher, lens grinder, one of the chief rationalists of the modern era.","html":"<p>Dutch philosopher, lens grinder, one of the chief rationalists of the modern era. Author of the <em>Ethics, Demonstrated in Geometrical Order</em>. The nearest philosophical ancestor of Neoterra's central thesis: what the traditions call God is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"спиноза.jpg\" alt=\"спиноза.jpg\"> <em>A portrait from around 1665: out of the flat darkness only a face and a white collar emerge — no study, no books, no marks of station. For a man excommunicated from his community at twenty-three, who ground lenses all his life, the background is exact: nothing but thought. And it is his own picture of the world as well — one substance, out of which everything emerges and into which everything returns (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a>).</em></p><blockquote><p><em>Deus sive Natura</em> — &quot;God, or Nature&quot;.</p></blockquote><h2>Deus sive Natura — why this is Neoterra's root</h2><p>For Spinoza this is neither metaphor nor poetic turn but a strict philosophical identity: there exists one infinite substance, and it is equally correct to call it God or Nature. God does not create the world from outside and does not rule it as a person — God <strong>is</strong> the world in its wholeness and its laws.</p><p>This coincides word for word with how Neoterra rethinks the word <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God</a>: not &quot;there is no God&quot; but &quot;what you are speaking of exists, and it is Nature&quot;. Neoterra arrives at this angle of view independently, but Spinoza formulated it four centuries earlier — and therefore stands at <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">the foundation</a> beside <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a>, who called himself a Spinozist outright.</p><p><strong>Natura naturans / naturata</strong> — Nature naturing (laws, creative force) and Nature natured (things, modes). One and the same world in two faces: this is the philosophical support for the picture of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">the face of God-Nature</a> — from atom to galaxy.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>The identity of God and Nature</strong> — the core of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> and of &quot;the angle of view: Nature and God&quot;.</li><li><strong>A single substance</strong> — everything that is consists of modes of one whole; the human being is not an observer from outside but part of Nature. A direct support for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a>.</li><li><strong>Amor Dei intellectualis</strong> — &quot;the intellectual love of God&quot;: a person's highest state is the knowing of Nature. To know the world is to love the sacred. This binds <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a> and the contemplation of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> as forms of one movement.</li><li><strong>Conatus</strong> — every thing strives to persist in its being and to unfold its power. The seed of the idea that life does not merely exist but reaches to grow — a resonance with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>.</li><li><strong>God without wrath or rewards</strong> — in Spinoza, Nature neither judges nor avenges, and has no absolute good and evil imposed from above. This coincides with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a>.</li><li><strong>Freedom of thought through persecution</strong> — at 23 he was excommunicated from the Amsterdam community (<em>ḥerem</em>) for his views, wrote anonymously, and stayed all his life outside parties and churches. A living example of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a> and a figure on the border of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a>: truth at the price of exile.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>Hard determinism.</strong> For Spinoza everything follows from God's nature by necessity; freedom is only the <em>understanding</em> of necessity, not a choice among roads. Neoterra, by contrast, places an open future at its centre (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a>) and a real <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">choice</a>. This is a genuine tension, which Neoterra holds rather than removes.</li><li><strong>A static cosmos.</strong> Spinoza's substance is eternal and unchanging — he has no idea of evolution, of growth, of a history of the Universe in time. For Neoterra, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> is not a property but the meaning. Only <em>conatus</em> builds a bridge, and Spinoza himself does not take that step.</li><li><strong>Strict rationalism.</strong> Spinoza's road to God runs through the geometry of reason. Neoterra leaves room for living myth too (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"лосев\">Aleksei Fyodorovich Losev</a>) and for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">a non-conceptual touching of the whole</a>.</li></ul><h2>Key ideas</h2><blockquote><p>&quot;Not to deride, bewail, or execrate human actions, but to understand them.&quot;</p></blockquote><blockquote><p>&quot;A free man thinks of nothing less than of death; his wisdom is a meditation on life, not on death.&quot; — in accord with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Neoterra's attitude to death</a>.</p></blockquote><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> — Deus sive Natura as the basis of the rethinking of God</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Albert Einstein (1879–1955)</a> — &quot;a follower of Spinoza&quot;; a forerunner's voice in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a> — Nature without absolute judgement</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"петля-времени\">The Loop of Time</a> — necessity without design; <em>naturans/naturata</em> as the carpet of time</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — &quot;everything had to happen&quot; applied to the past alone; the future left open</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a></li></ul>"},"стоицизм":{"name":"Stoicism","def":"A philosophical school founded by Zeno of Citium (c. 300 BCE).","html":"<p>A philosophical school founded by Zeno of Citium (c. 300 BCE). Developed by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius</a>, Epictetus and Seneca. At its centre: virtue as the only true good, control over one's own reactions, and acceptance of what lies outside our power.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><p>Stoicism is among Neoterra's nearest philosophical forerunners. Practically the whole idea of the Book of Character:</p><ul><li><strong>Discipline</strong> — daily work on oneself</li><li><strong>Courage</strong> — acting despite fear</li><li><strong>Responsibility</strong> — for one's decisions rather than for circumstances</li><li><strong>Governing the emotions</strong> — understanding rather than suppression</li><li><strong>Accepting reality</strong> — <em>memento mori</em> as clarity, not pessimism</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><p>The Stoics are concentrated chiefly on a person's inner world. Neoterra adds an outward dimension: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">society</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">space</a>, responsibility toward future generations.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бусидо\">Bushido</a> — the Eastern twin: an independent code of self-command</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius (121–180)</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"неотерра-vs-мировые-традиции\">Neoterra and the World's Traditions</a></li></ul>"},"столлман":{"name":"Richard Stallman (b. 1953)","def":"American programmer and — to a greater degree — philosopher of the freedom of knowledge.","html":"<p>American programmer and — to a greater degree — philosopher of the freedom of knowledge. Founder of the GNU Project (1983) and the Free Software Foundation (1985), originator of <strong>copyleft</strong> and of the GPL licence. All his life he has defended a simple thought: knowledge handed on openly belongs to everyone and cannot be taken away.</p><blockquote><p>Free software is a matter of freedom, not price. &quot;Free&quot; as in &quot;free speech&quot;, not as in &quot;free beer&quot;.</p></blockquote><h2>What he is for Neoterra</h2><p>Stallman is an example of one person turning an ethical principle into a working system. His &quot;four freedoms&quot; (to run, to study, to distribute, to improve) are in essence <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> fixed in law: knowledge must flow freely and grow by everyone who touches it.</p><p>Not an example for everyone — but absolutely for many, followers of Neoterra included. He belongs among the figures at the sources: the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">forerunners</a> whose ideas Neoterra inherits.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>The open handing on of knowledge</strong> — knowledge as common property rather than possession; a direct continuation of the values of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">truth-seeking</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a>.</li><li><strong>Copyleft as a guard on openness</strong> — not merely &quot;give it away&quot; but make what is given <em>stay</em> open for everyone who follows. A mechanism against <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">greed</a>, built into the handing on itself.</li><li><strong>Community around a common work</strong> — free software is built by thousands of people worldwide; a working model of a <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">commune</a> of makers without coercion.</li><li><strong>Branches do not split but enrich</strong> — in the world of free software a fork is no betrayal: while both branches stay open, the best of each returns to the common channel. Neoterra tries this principle on itself — see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a>.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>Rigorism.</strong> Stallman is uncompromising to the point of harshness: half-tones and gradualness are alien to him. Neoterra is not dogmatic and allows different speeds along the road.</li><li><strong>A narrow field.</strong> His philosophy is concentrated on software and information; nature, space and the spiritual dimension stay outside it.</li></ul><h2>Key ideas</h2><ul><li>The four freedoms: to run, to study, to distribute, to improve.</li><li>Copyleft: using copyright to guarantee freedom rather than to restrict it.</li><li>A society that cannot study its own tools loses its freedom of thought.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"открытые-ответвления\">Open Branches</a> — the copyleft principle applied to Neoterra itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> — the open society; Stallman, open knowledge</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"5-предшественников\">Neoterra's Spiritual Forerunners</a></li></ul>"},"Философия":{"name":"Philosophy — area","def":"Origin: the Seed of Neoterra","html":"<p>Origin: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the Seed of Neoterra</a></p><p>Schools of thought and thinkers whose ideas feed Neoterra. From character and discipline to critical thinking and the overcoming of oneself.</p><h2>Shoots</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoicism</a> — character, discipline, inner steadiness</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуцианство\">Confucianism</a> — family, upbringing, responsibility</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"гуманизм\">Humanism</a> — the worth of the person, science, critical thinking</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бусидо\">Bushido</a> — the warrior's way, reforged into a maker's code</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аристотель\">Aristotle</a> — the first to see knowledge divided into distinct branches</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"парменид\">Parmenides</a> — being is one; the way of truth against the way of opinion</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"спиноза\">Spinoza</a> — <em>Deus sive Natura</em>: God is Nature — ancestor of Neoterra's core</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сократ\">Socrates</a> — &quot;I know that I know nothing&quot;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius</a> — family and society as the foundation</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"марк-аврелий\">Marcus Aurelius</a> — character and discipline</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Schopenhauer</a> — will, compassion and the bridge to the East; a teaching of repose, lived out on the dead edge</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Nietzsche</a> — overcoming oneself, the Wanderer's way</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a> — truth matters more than authority</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"лосев\">Losev</a> — myth as genuine reality; the philosophy of symbol and name</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Stallman</a> — the freedom of knowledge, open transmission; copyleft as a guard on openness</li></ul><h2>Cross-links</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">Religions</a> — Taoism and Confucianism on the border</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> — the roots of Neoterra's values</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — the Nietzschean impulse of growth</li></ul><blockquote><p>Open question: which thinkers alive today continue this line? One answer is already in: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"столлман\">Stallman</a>; who else?</p></blockquote>"},"шопенгауэр":{"name":"Arthur Schopenhauer (1788–1860)","def":"German philosopher, author of The World as Will and Representation (1818).","html":"<p>German philosopher, author of <em>The World as Will and Representation</em> (1818). The book went unread for almost forty years; recognition came after the collection <em>Parerga and Paralipomena</em> (1851) — nine years before his death. He was the first major Western philosopher to take Indian thought seriously.</p><p><strong>The teaching in one sentence:</strong> behind the world of appearances stands a single blind Will — a causeless striving that attains nothing; striving is suffering; the way out lies in the contemplation of art, in compassion, and in the renunciation of will.</p><blockquote><p>Life swings like a pendulum between suffering and boredom.</p></blockquote><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>A single ground behind a multitude of appearances.</strong> Schopenhauer's Will is one and the same in everything: in the gravity of a stone, in the growth of a plant, in human desire. Structurally this is the move Neoterra makes in calling <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> the first ground and the human being its form rather than an observer from outside (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>).</li><li><strong>Compassion as the basis of morality.</strong> Not duty, not commandment, not calculation — a direct recognition of oneself in another creature. For his time it was rare, and rarer still that he <strong>extended compassion explicitly to animals</strong>, arguing with Kant. The nearest kin of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>.</li><li><strong>Music as a language, not a depiction.</strong> The other arts show appearances; music shows the Will itself directly, bypassing images. Neoterra speaks of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">music</a> similarly: a language understood without words — see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бах\">Johann Sebastian Bach</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>.</li><li><strong>A bridge to the East.</strong> He read the <em>Oupnek'hat</em> daily — a Latin translation of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">the Upanishads</a> — kept a figure of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"будда\">the Buddha</a>, and called that book &quot;the consolation of my life and the consolation of my death&quot;. The meeting of Western and Indian thought, which Neoterra builds deliberately, he accomplished first and alone.</li><li><strong>A diagnosis of comfort two centuries early.</strong> The pendulum of &quot;suffering — boredom&quot; describes exactly what the wiki calls <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a>: relieved suffering does not give repose, it gives emptiness, and a person starts wanting again. Neoterra's thesis of the creeping threshold is already in Schopenhauer — only without a way out.</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>Pessimism against the main idea.</strong> For Neoterra life should not merely exist but <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">grow</a>. For Schopenhauer existence is itself an error, better not prolonged. That is not a shade of difference but the opposite sign.</li><li><strong>The denial of will is the icy edge.</strong> Neoterra's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">balance</a> says it harshly: the living moves in a narrow band, and <strong>both edges are death</strong>; on the left disintegration, on the right stagnation. The ideal of renouncing striving stands exactly on the right-hand edge. So &quot;the way of water&quot; does not fit here: water flows, the <em>wu wei</em> of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a> is action without violence to the natural course, while the denial of will is a stop. He sought <strong>repose</strong>, and a living equilibrium is never repose: it is held by effort, continuously.</li><li><strong>Adaptation is not harmony.</strong> Fairness requires saying: solitude was not only torment for him. He <strong>settled into</strong> it — a flute in the evenings, a poodle, his own table at the inn, dinners by the clock, and a late fame he frankly enjoyed. This is a genuine ability to find pleasure where one stands, and Neoterra does not deny it. But the distinction here is decisive: <strong>reconciling oneself to a state and holding an equilibrium are different things.</strong> The first requires ceasing to want otherwise, the second requires continuous effort. By the model of the two edges (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a>) Schopenhauer is a pure case of the second outcome: reason coped so well that it suppressed the animal will, and the living force went with it. The person is whole, clear, and unborn.</li><li><strong>Knowledge without sitting near.</strong> He had all the texts. What he lacked was a living witness — what <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">the Upanishads</a> call &quot;sitting near the teacher&quot;. He read the map and did not walk the road; see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"рождённый-во-тьме\">Born in Darkness</a>: &quot;To know balance it is not enough to hear of it. It is walked through.&quot;</li></ul><h2>A root on which branches already stood</h2><p>Schopenhauer is not a new figure in the wiki but the missing root of existing pages.</p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Nietzsche</a> found <em>The World as Will and Representation</em> in a Leipzig bookshop in 1865, declared himself its disciple — and then turned it a hundred and eighty degrees: instead of the denial of will, the will to power; instead of repose, the overcoming of oneself. The page <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Friedrich Nietzsche (1844–1900)</a> stood for years in this wiki as an answer with no question.</p><p>Through him also passed Wagner, Tolstoy and Freud (the Will as a forerunner of the unconscious). <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Einstein</a> kept his portrait in his study and repeated his formula about freedom all his life.</p><h2>Key ideas and quotations</h2><blockquote><p>&quot;A man can do what he wills, but he cannot will what he wills.&quot;</p></blockquote><p>His most enduring thought and the most uncomfortable for Neoterra: it cuts <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom</a> at the root. The wiki answers not by refutation but by a shift — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>: authorship lies not in choosing desires out of nowhere but in clearing a place where one's own desire can grow at all.</p><blockquote><p>&quot;All truth passes through three stages: first it is ridiculed, then violently opposed, then accepted as self-evident.&quot;</p></blockquote><p>A formula attributed to him persistently but not found verbatim in his texts — it stands here as a saying, not a quotation.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">Friedrich Nietzsche (1844–1900)</a> — the disciple who turned his teacher around; a root for a branch already standing</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> — the proof from the contrary: the texts were there, the witness was not; the edge of a suppressed will</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> — the ice no one was there to split; the pendulum of suffering and boredom</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> — stagnation as one of the two lethal edges</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a> — the animal foundation he proposed to extinguish</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">The Upanishads</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"даосизм\">Taoism</a> — the Eastern line he opened to the West</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — compassion as the basis of morality, animals included</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — music as a direct language of essence</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a> — denial is more dangerous than the darkness itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"эйнштейн\">Albert Einstein (1879–1955)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Franz Kafka (1883–1924)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"достоевский\">Fyodor Dostoevsky (1821–1881)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Философия\">Philosophy — area</a></li></ul>"},"юнг":{"name":"Carl Gustav Jung (1875–1961)","def":"Swiss psychiatrist, founder of analytical psychology.","html":"<p>Swiss psychiatrist, founder of analytical psychology. Freud's student and later his opponent: the break of 1913 cost him his position and several years, which he himself called a confrontation with the unconscious and recorded in the <em>Red Book</em>. Author of the concepts of the <strong>Shadow</strong>, the <strong>Persona</strong>, the <strong>Self</strong>, <strong>individuation</strong>, the <strong>collective unconscious</strong>, <strong>archetypes</strong>, <strong>synchronicity</strong>.</p><p><strong>The wiki relied on him before it gave him a page.</strong> The <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">Shadow</a> is explicitly named as Jungian, and its whole logic — &quot;not to banish but to integrate&quot; — comes from there. This page settles the debt: one cannot rely on a person and not answer for them.</p><h2>Making the unconscious conscious</h2><p>His main thought, as the keeper puts it: a person needs to <strong>make their unconscious conscious</strong>. The wiki holds it on three pages without naming the author:</p><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Shadow</a>: &quot;denying the shadow is more dangerous than the shadow itself; whoever considers themselves incapable of evil stops watching themselves&quot;;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a>: the first step of healing is &quot;to see: to acknowledge the vice as one's own, without hiding&quot;;</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of mind</a>: what one regains is not a former state but one's own <strong>authorship</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>A caveat about the quotation</strong> — by the rule introduced on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Kafka</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сальвадор-дали\">Dalí</a>. The popular &quot;until you make the unconscious conscious, it will direct your life and you will call it fate&quot; circulates without an address: it is a later paraphrase. Jung has his own formulation, and it is stronger:</p><blockquote><p>When an inner situation is not made conscious, it happens outside, as fate.</p><p><em>(<em>Aion</em>, 1951)</em></p></blockquote><h2>The Persona: a name for the programmed layer</h2><p>The <strong>Persona</strong> in Jung is a mask assembled from society's expectations: a role a person plays and with which it is dangerous to confuse oneself. It is exactly the layer the wiki calls the <strong>furnishings</strong> of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"матрица\">matrix</a>: not the walls of consciousness but what they are furnished with from within — society, culture, &quot;that's how it's done.&quot;</p><p><strong>Individuation</strong> — becoming whole through bringing the repressed into awareness — is the way out of these furnishings. Not an escape from the walls: the walls remain for everyone (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a>).</p><p>The coincidence is independent: the wiki came to the frame through <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the Break</a> and the work of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">mentor</a>, not through analytical psychology. Jung here is <strong>a witness to the same observation, not a source of the wiki</strong>.</p><h2>Points of contact with Neoterra</h2><ul><li><strong>Wholeness instead of amputation.</strong> Individuation is not a victory over the dark half but its inclusion. This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> as the wiki understands it and a direct support for the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">Shadow</a>: darkness is acknowledged and directed into <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a>, not banished.</li><li><strong>The source of choice inside the person.</strong> Jung returns evil to the psyche rather than leaving it to an external demon — the same movement as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a>.</li><li><strong>Symbol as a way of knowing.</strong> Jung worked with image and myth where the concept does not reach. The wiki says the same of the soul: &quot;reason has difficulty grasping it directly, so it is spoken of through the heart, through image, through art and music&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a>). Next to him stands <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"лосев\">Losev</a>, with myth as authentic reality.</li><li><strong>Spiritually sighted, building a language for himself.</strong> Jung felt the Whole, but no confession could hold him — and all his life he built a language for what he had felt his way towards. This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовная-зрячесть\">spiritual sight</a>: &quot;seeking not salvation but a language and one's own people.&quot;</li></ul><h2>Points of divergence</h2><ul><li><strong>The wiki does not accept synchronicity as a position.</strong> In Jung these are acausal meaningful coincidences, and he himself stipulated that there is no causality here. The popular reading — &quot;synchronise with Nature and it will start helping you&quot; — turns an observation into a law of attraction, that is, into the very substitution the wiki caught in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Capra</a> (quantum mysticism) and in neotantrism (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">Intimacy</a>): the name is taken for authority and the content is changed. The position itself is unverifiable by design (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a>) — the wiki holds it as <strong>resonance, not proof</strong>, on the model of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">quantum unity</a>. It has its own, unborrowed ground: the first law of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">Canon</a> — there is no isolated existence (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>).</li><li><strong>The collective unconscious is an image, not a mechanism.</strong> Inherited archetypes as a separate stratum of the psyche have not been established empirically. The wiki takes the observation (similar images in unconnected cultures) and does not take the explanation — as with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бентов\">Bentov</a>.</li><li><strong>The wiki does not claim that anyone &quot;left the matrix.&quot;</strong> Not Jung, not the prophets, not anyone: no one leaves the walls of consciousness, &quot;everyone is deprived of the touch&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a>). One leaves the <strong>frame</strong>, and that is open to everyone — otherwise a ladder results, which the wiki rejects everywhere (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовная-зрячесть\">Spiritual Sight</a>). Jung is valuable precisely because he showed a work, not a privilege.</li><li><strong>The figure and the teaching.</strong> Jung left something heavy behind: ambiguous texts and positions in German-language psychotherapy in the early 1930s, the examination of which is still not finished. Here the rule of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">Alley</a> and the precedent of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сальвадор-дали\">Dalí</a> apply: <strong>the thought enters the wiki; the figure is not placed on the Alley.</strong></li></ul><h2>Key ideas</h2><blockquote><p>When an inner situation is not made conscious, it happens outside, as fate.</p></blockquote><blockquote><p>Who looks outside, dreams; who looks inside, awakes.</p></blockquote><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тень\">The Inner Shadow</a> — the concept taken from him; the wiki relied on him even without this page</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"матрица\">The matrix</a> — the Persona as the name of the programmed layer; individuation as the way out</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> — the frame and the one who keeps the passage open</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a> — to see and own it; authorship instead of a state</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a> — why it is spoken of by image, not concept; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовная-зрячесть\">Spiritual Sight</a> — to feel the Whole and build a language for it</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Fritjof Capra (b. 1939)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> — the boundary between resonance and substitution</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"лосев\">Aleksei Fyodorovich Losev</a> — myth as authentic reality: a neighbouring voice</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> — why the thought is taken but the figure is not placed</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бессознательность\">Unconsciousness</a> — the page on which his formula is unfolded to health and habit</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Философия\">Philosophy — area</a> — the area</li></ul>"},"хранитель":{"name":"The Keeper","def":"The manifesto says it plainly: Neoterra has no prophet whose words may not be questioned, and no sacred book that may not be added to.","html":"<p><strong>Dmitry Blinnikov</strong> — the one who began this wiki and tends it further. Not a prophet and not a source of truth: a gardener at the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>.</p><p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"hranitel.jpg\" alt=\"hranitel.jpg\"> <em>Dmitry Blinnikov, keeper of Neoterra.</em></p><h2>Why not &quot;author&quot;</h2><p>The <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">manifesto</a> says it plainly: Neoterra has no prophet whose words may not be questioned, and no sacred book that may not be added to. The philosophy was not invented — it was gathered from what humanity already knew in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">religions</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Философия\">philosophy</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Искусство\">art</a>. The keeper's role is not to compose but to <strong>connect</strong>: to find relations, to draw links, to preserve the form of the network (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a>).</p><p>Hence &quot;keeper&quot; rather than &quot;author&quot;. Authorship in Neoterra is distributed — it is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">shared</a>. Whoever brings a brick here is a co-author.</p><h2>What the keeper does</h2><ul><li><strong>Grafts rather than files.</strong> New material is not sorted onto shelves; it finds the nearest node and puts out side shoots from there.</li><li><strong>Keeps the wiki alive.</strong> No statement is final; contradictions are not hidden but sent to the &quot;Open questions&quot; register of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>.</li><li><strong>Does not decide for the reader.</strong> Neoterra is a lens, not an answer. The keeper adjusts the focus; each person looks for themselves.</li></ul><h2>Statements of his own</h2><p>The keeper is not only a gardener of others' thoughts; some of the wiki's positions belong to him as author.</p><p><strong>The largest is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the immortality of the soul</a></strong> (2026-08-30): the soul lives outside the matrix of our consciousness, souls interweave on different levels, and at the highest level everything is one. The wiki <strong>supposes</strong> this and does not assert it — it holds it as a stance open to revision. It is the only statement of the keeper's that entered <strong>the core itself</strong> of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>, beside &quot;God is Nature&quot;. A whole stratum has been built around it: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">perception</a> (what one lives a life with), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the break</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a>.</p><p><strong><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The theory of moments</a>:</strong> a moment as the form in which a thing exists, rather than a stretch of time; moments intersect and beget new ones, time grows, and the human being is the one who learned to notice moments.</p><p>This does not cancel what is said above. An authored position enters the wiki on equal terms: it is tested for strength, supplied with objections, and set beside an incompatible model (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"мгновение-истины\">The Moment of Truth</a>) with no right of seniority. To be an author inside Neoterra does not mean to be beyond dispute — otherwise the keeper would become the very prophet the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">manifesto</a> denies.</p><p><strong>And here lies the wiki's sharpest tension.</strong> The soul's immortality is not merely an authored position but an authored position <strong>in the core</strong>, and an unfalsifiable one at that. The rule of &quot;equal terms&quot; only half works here: the objections are recorded honestly (see &quot;Contradictions&quot; in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">the soul</a> and the register of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a>), but the statement itself stands above the level at which it could be disputed in the ordinary way. The only defence the keeper has left himself is openness to revising that very statement. While that holds, there is no prophet; should it fail, the difference from a dogma disappears.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p><strong>Telegram channel:</strong> <a href=\"https://t.me/Neo_terra\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">t.me/Neo_terra</a></p><p>There the philosophy comes out to people: thoughts that have not yet become pages, and pages that have already become thoughts. A question, an objection, your own experience — that is exactly the brick the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">manifesto</a> speaks of.</p><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The Soul</a> — the keeper's statement that entered the core; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — his model of time</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"что-такое-неотерра\">What Neoterra Is</a></li></ul>"},"близость":{"name":"Intimacy","def":"One of Nature's chief tasks is expansion and propagation.","html":"<p>One of Nature's chief tasks is <strong>expansion and propagation</strong>. Galaxies, planets, bacteria, cells, plants, animals: at every scale one movement — to be further, to be more, to be again. The human being is among the few who received, for performing this task, <strong>the gift of pleasure</strong>.</p><p>Hence this page's position, short and hard: <strong>neither sin nor duty.</strong></p><h2>Why sin is impossible here</h2><p>Sin is a category that requires a <strong>lawgiver</strong>: someone who set the prohibition and is offended by its breach. Neoterra has no lawgiver. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God is Nature</a>, and Nature neither commands nor judges — it is made as it is made (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the Canon of Nature</a>).</p><p>So the question is settled not by prohibition but by the wiki's own criterion. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Evil</a> is defined as the destruction of life <strong>without necessity</strong>; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">the Great Principle</a> asks whether an act helps life, love, freedom, creation, the future. An act out of which new life is born stands at the opposite pole from that definition. <strong>By Neoterra's own measure intimacy cannot be evil</strong> — this is derived, not postulated.</p><p>The second law of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the Canon of Nature</a> says the same outright: life strives to continue — through reproduction, care for offspring, learning, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">culture</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a>. Reproduction stands first in that list, and it cannot be struck out while the rest is kept.</p><p>Hence the answer to &quot;resisting this is denying one's own nature&quot;. The human being is not an observer of Nature from outside but a part of it (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>). Shame before one's own make is shame before what one is made of.</p><h2>Pleasure as reward, not as lure</h2><p>A tradition that declares pleasure a trap is obliged to explain why it exists at all. Neoterra's explanation is simple: <strong>it is the payment for Nature's work performed</strong> — the same mechanism that makes fullness sweet and an embrace warm. The reward is not bolted onto the task from outside; it is the way the task gets done.</p><p>This falls under the ninth law of the Canon: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a> matters, it is not a luxury laid over life. Pleasure is of the same order — not a surplus that can be subtracted, but part of the fullness.</p><p><strong>A kindred rhythm.</strong> When it is not bodies that are close but people — when two have caught the same rhythm — the experience is of another order and another strength than plain coupling. The wiki takes this as <strong>a view, not a proposition</strong>: it cannot be checked, there is nothing to measure it with, and it does not reduce to physiology. Nor can it be dismissed: too many say it, and too much alike, and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">touching the Whole</a> already holds the thought that the whole is not given piecemeal or through a concept.</p><h2>Tantra: resonance, not borrowing</h2><p><em>Set out at length under the rule adopted after <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Kafka</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сальвадор-дали\">Dalí</a>: from another tradition one takes the content, not the name.</em></p><p><strong>What it is.</strong> Not a technique and not a doctrine about sex, but a vast ritual-philosophical current that took shape in India from roughly the fifth and sixth centuries and grew at once through <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"индуизм\">Hinduism</a> (Shaivism and Shaktism), <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a> (Vajrayana) and Jainism. The word itself comes from the root <em>tan-</em>, &quot;to stretch, to weave&quot;: tantra is a fabric, a warp. Its substance is ritual — mantra, yantra and mandala, visualisation of the deity, initiation from a teacher, work with the subtle body. Its philosophical core is non-duality, sharpest in Abhinavagupta's Kashmir Shaivism (tenth and eleventh centuries): the world is not an illusion to escape but a manifestation of consciousness itself; Shiva and Shakti, consciousness and energy, are inseparable.</p><p><strong>How it differs from the ascetic path.</strong> Where contemplative traditions declared body and world an obstacle to liberation, tantra made the opposite move: liberation is reached <strong>through</strong> the world, not in spite of it. Enjoyment (bhukti) and liberation (mukti) are set side by side rather than against each other. &quot;By the very things by which one falls, one rises&quot; is the tradition's own formula (the <em>Kularnava Tantra</em>), not a later gloss.</p><p><strong>Where sex sits in it.</strong> It is there, and the wiki will not pretend otherwise. But its place is narrow: the &quot;left-hand&quot; currents (vamachara), the panchamakara rite with its ritual breaking of prohibition, sexual union included. The practice is initiatory, hedged with rules, subordinated to liberation, and often built on retention rather than pleasure; a large share of schools (the &quot;right-hand&quot; ones) read the same rite symbolically. In no branch of historical tantra was sex the centre.</p><p><strong>Neo-tantra is a different thing.</strong> What is sold today under the name &quot;tantric sex&quot; took shape in the West in the twentieth century: John Woodroffe and the theosophists, then Osho from the 1970s, then the mass manuals. It is a hybrid of Indian terminology with Western sexology and self-realisation psychology. Ritual, initiation and deity have left it; body, orgasm and &quot;sacred sexuality&quot; have moved to the centre. This is not a small slip of naming: the two have opposite centres of gravity.</p><p><strong>What Neoterra takes from this.</strong> The resonance is in one thing, and it is large: tantra is among the few great traditions in which <strong>the body is not an obstacle to the sacred but a road to it</strong>. The wiki arrives at the same place by its own route and from the other side: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">God is Nature</a>, the human being is part of it, and so shame before one's own make is shame before what one is made of. The second move coincides too: pleasure is not a trap (the ninth law of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">the Canon</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"красота\">beauty</a>). And the third: the world is not illusion but manifestation (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a>, the Canon's first law). Tantra reached this fifteen centuries earlier and by another path — and that makes it <strong>a witness, not an argument</strong>.</p><p><strong>The border past which resonance becomes substitution.</strong> It runs where it ran with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Capra</a>, and must be named as plainly:</p><ul><li><strong>Subtle physiology is not accepted as knowledge.</strong> Chakras, nadis, kundalini are the tradition's language, not a description of the body; the wiki makes no claims that cannot be checked (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">science</a>).</li><li><strong>Initiation and the guru are not accepted as form.</strong> Neoterra has no teacher whose words cannot be disputed (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a>), and knowledge here does not pass down a chain of the admitted.</li><li><strong>Coincidence is not confirmation.</strong> &quot;Tantra proves intimacy is sacred&quot; is exactly the substitution of &quot;quantum physics proves the unity of souls&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a>). Two traditions that arrived at something similar confirm each other no more than two people who had the same dream.</li><li><strong>Neo-tantra stands to tantra as quantum mysticism stands to physics</strong> — it takes the name for the authority and discards the content. The wiki has already dissected this figure from the side of science on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Capra</a> and from the side of art on <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"сальвадор-дали\">Dalí</a>; here it appears a third time, which makes it no longer a coincidence but a recurring way of going wrong.</li></ul><p>The thought about a kindred rhythm loses nothing by any of this — it never rested on tantra. What loses is the attempt to prop it up with someone else's name.</p><h2>Animal will and reason: an instrument at last</h2><p>Here the page answers an <strong>open question of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the seed</a></strong> — &quot;restraint or suppression&quot;. It is recorded there thus: Neoterra rejects both edges, but <em>&quot;there is no instrument for the middle: from within, restraint and suppression are indistinguishable.&quot;</em></p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> holds the pair: animal will ↔ reason, drive and calculation, the animal foundation and what grew on it. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The break</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a> describe the tilt to one side: <strong>&quot;the animal will is suppressed — and the life force goes with it. What remains is clarity without impulse: the person is whole, reasonable and unborn.&quot;</strong></p><p>Intimacy gives this abstract pair a rare property: <strong>it has a bodily signal</strong>. The organism produces hormones for a task; if the task goes long unperformed, the absence speaks for itself — not by argument but by state. Restraint keeps the force and disposes of it; suppression switches the animal off and hands all control to the brain — which by then is itself steeped in what the body produced for the task not performed. This is the first case in the wiki where the &quot;middle&quot; has an <strong>external mark</strong> and not only a self-report. It does not close the question — the instrument is coarse and does not fit everyone — but it moves it.</p><p><strong>And here is the border the page does not cross.</strong> The absence of intimacy really does drive a person forward: the animal will is an engine, and the wiki rests on that (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"счастье\">Happiness</a> on self-control). So abstinence in itself is not a vice but one of the modes. Only a tilt that has become permanent is vicious.</p><h2>What this means for relationships</h2><p>Intimacy is not an appendix to a relationship but part of what carries it. Its absence does not stay in the bedroom: marriages break, a partner feels abandoned and unwanted, resentment accumulates with nothing to pin it on. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The family</a> already rests on &quot;open conversation instead of silence&quot; — but this is what people are silent about most often, and silence here works as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">the vices</a>: the symptom gets discussed, the root does not.</p><p>So the wiki says it plainly: <strong>the significance of this process should be acknowledged, and the pretence that it does not exist should stop.</strong> To speak of it rather than hush it is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">the search for truth</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom of thought</a> applied where they are applied least often.</p><h2>The safeguard: neither sin nor duty</h2><p>The first half of the formula lifts the guilt. The second — no less important — keeps the position from turning into a new coercion.</p><ul><li><strong>Nature's task creates no obligation towards a partner.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The family</a> holds an <strong>absolute ban on coercion</strong> — violence, manipulation, blackmail, fear. &quot;Nature made it so&quot; in someone else's mouth instantly becomes a lever, and the wiki names this in advance: a duty to Nature does not convert into a duty to a person. Consent remains a condition, not a formality.</li><li><strong>Dignity does not depend on intimacy.</strong> Asexual people, those who chose celibacy, the solitary, the old, the ill, those for whom this part of life simply is not there — are <strong>not lower and have not &quot;failed the task&quot;</strong>. The same safeguard stands in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a> (the gradient of awareness does not rank people), in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">the body</a> (&quot;there is no norm to deviate from&quot;) and in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a> (diversity hands out no grades). Without it the page would build a ladder — exactly the one the wiki rejects everywhere.</li><li><strong>Monastic traditions are not declared unnatural.</strong> Neoterra is compatible with religions not out of politeness but by construction (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">Neoterra</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Религии\">Religions — area</a>). It removes the status of sin — and does not issue the status of obligation in exchange.</li></ul><h2>What history did with this</h2><p>How natural life became shameful is an honest question, and the wiki answers it <strong>without a conspiracy</strong>, because no conspiracy is needed.</p><p>The restriction grew out of interests that are documented and require no ill intent. Where inheritance runs through the father's line, certainty of paternity becomes a question of <strong>property</strong>, and control over the female half of life becomes its consequence. Where an institution issues permission to marry, it holds a lever over everyone at once. To this was added the <strong>ascetic turn of Late Antiquity</strong> — Stoics, Neoplatonists, then Christian authors — which redefined the bodily as lower; and a very real fear of disease. No design is required: an interest repeated across generations is enough for it to come to look like a moral law.</p><p><strong>Two corrections to the common version that the wiki is obliged to make.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Fear of overpopulation does not fit chronologically.</strong> Malthus is 1798; before that, states and churches almost always wanted <strong>more</strong> people, not fewer: people were an army, a workforce and a tax base. &quot;Extra mouths&quot; explains particular episodes but not the origin of the prohibition.</li><li><strong>The wiki does not assert that &quot;the prophets' words were distorted&quot;.</strong> That is a claim about intent, and intent cannot be proved (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>). It also contradicts the stance of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"начало\">the entrance</a>: Neoterra does not contest other systems, it offers a common ground. Institutional interest explains what is observed no worse, and is harder to refute — which makes it the more exact account.</li></ul><h2>The bond with science</h2><p>Science describes the mechanism — hormonal regulation, attachment, the role of oxytocin and dopamine — and Neoterra accepts that description (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a>: where science speaks, philosophy listens). But a description of a mechanism issues no norm: from <strong>how</strong> it is built, it does not follow <strong>how much</strong> and <strong>for whom</strong>.</p><p>Here the wiki keeps the caution it demands of itself everywhere. Nocturnal emissions are normal physiology, not a symptom of damage. Claims that long abstinence harms the body are not supported by evidence: the data are mixed, and tolerance differs radically from person to person — which follows directly from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">the absence of a &amp;quot;norm&amp;quot;</a> and from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">the different settings of the valve</a>. The psychological part is defensible more softly than the physiological: <strong>involuntary</strong> abstinence — the kind a person did not choose — is borne harder than chosen abstinence, and the difference lies in the choosing, not in the duration.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>The instrument is coarse.</strong> The bodily signal separates suppression from restraint where the body signals. And where it does not — by age, by make, or by free choice? Then the middle again has nothing to measure it with, and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the seed's</a> open question is moved but not closed.</li><li><strong>Where is the border between acknowledging significance and a new cult?</strong> A society that declared intimacy shameful and a society that declares it obligatory break a person equally — just from different sides.</li><li><strong>&quot;Nature's task&quot; and childlessness.</strong> If the task is propagation, where does the wiki put intimacy without conception and a free decision to have no children? The page's answer — pleasure is a part in its own right, not a receipt for work done — weakens the original argument from the task. The tension is left open.</li><li><strong>The kindred rhythm is unverifiable.</strong> Taken as a view; the wiki has nothing with which to tell it from the strength of attachment, from habit, or from self-suggestion (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> — framed in the same order).</li><li><strong>From tantra the conclusion is taken but the practice rejected.</strong> The wiki takes the position &quot;the body is a road, not an obstacle&quot; and declines everything by which the tradition arrived at it: initiation, ritual, subtle physiology. Is it honest to take the fruit while rejecting the root — or is that simply what is done to every tradition one takes a resonance from?</li><li><strong>To speak of it — but how?</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of thought</a> demands speech, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">the family</a> demands not intruding. Where does talk about significance end and climbing into someone's bedroom begin?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a> — drive as one of the forces of the living; love as action, not only feeling</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a> — voluntariness, the ban on coercion, open conversation instead of silence</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> — the pair &quot;animal will ↔ reason&quot; and the cost of its tilt</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a> — the open question &quot;restraint or suppression&quot;, to which this page supplies an instrument</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-природы\">The Canon of Nature</a> — the second law (life strives to continue), the ninth (beauty matters)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> — why sin requires a lawgiver, and there is none here</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"великий-принцип\">The Great Principle of Neoterra</a> — the measure by which intimacy cannot be evil</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"тело\">The Body</a> — there is no &quot;norm&quot; to deviate from; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> — different settings</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> — the figure &quot;treat the root, not the symptom&quot;, applied to silence</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поиск-истины\">The Search for Truth</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> — why the kindred rhythm cannot be spoken of through a concept</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"индуизм\">Hinduism</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"буддизм\">Buddhism</a> — the traditions through which tantra grew</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — non-duality: the world as manifestation, not as illusion</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"капра\">Fritjof Capra (b. 1939)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"квантовое-единство\">Quantum Unity</a> — the same border of resonance, drawn from the side of science</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> — why subtle physiology is not accepted as knowledge</li></ul>"},"любовь":{"name":"Love","def":"Love is one of the greatest forces of Nature.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"любовь.png\" alt=\"любовь.png\"> <em>Love for life itself — the kind that remains when everything else is lost. Nearby an empty chair with a shawl and a walking stick: the loss is in the frame, but there is no photograph and no mourning — a grief that has been lived with. The hands are busy (a cutting in a tin can; the other hand lifting a soaked bee out of a puddle) — love as action rather than feeling; the face is lifted to the last of the rain with quiet gladness. The house is peeling and painted with warmth: that is what a gaze looks like when it values the whole rather than a list of flaws (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a>). The door is open, nothing is locked or clenched — love does not live beside fear. The small things are rendered as carefully as the face: attention is love.</em></p><p>Love is one of the greatest forces of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>. In Neoterra it is not reducible to a feeling: <strong>love is action</strong>. And at the same time it is a way of seeing: love values the whole picture and does not hunt for faults.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>It is love that lets a person:</p><ul><li>overcome solitude;</li><li>make <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">families</a>;</li><li>care for children;</li><li>sacrifice themselves for others;</li><li>build the future.</li></ul><p>Feeling without action stays an experience; love shows itself in deeds — in care, protection, and labour for another. That is why love in Neoterra joins with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a>: it builds, grows and preserves.</p><h2>Love as whole perception</h2><p>To love is to value the object entire, rather than the sum of its merits and flaws. Absolute love can &quot;open and close its eyes to much&quot;: it sees the whole picture and does not reduce another to a list of faults. This makes love akin to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">touching the Whole</a> and to a setting of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">the valve of perception</a> — where a narrow gaze looks for something to fault, love looks wider and accepts.</p><p>Here too is its limit: that same ability to &quot;close its eyes&quot; can blind. Love as perception of the whole and love as sober <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">respect</a> for the real other must hold each other in balance.</p><h2>In love one learns another's perception</h2><p>What is said above is not enough: love is not only itself a way of seeing — <strong>in it one takes over another's way of seeing</strong>.</p><p>Each person lives their life with one thing: the animal will, reason, or the soul (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a>), and in a couple it is not only two people who meet but two ways of living. A partner with a different perception <strong>breaks your frame and at the same time sits beside you</strong> — this is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">a break</a> with a witness, the very thing <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a> does inside one person. <strong>Love is mutual mentorship</strong>, and that is why a soul is born in it.</p><p>Hence a distinction between two loves, without which &quot;love as whole seeing&quot; is incomplete:</p><ul><li>love that <strong>confirms</strong> your frame: the partner perceives as you do, everything is recognisable and nothing grows. This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a> in the form of a relationship — love for one's own perception rather than for the other;</li><li>love that <strong>gives</strong> a perception you did not have. Harder, and it grows you.</li></ul><p>A caveat from science: the common saying that &quot;opposites attract&quot; is not borne out by the data — the opposite is found consistently, similarity of values and views. What is at issue here is not what <strong>attracts</strong> but what <strong>grows</strong>: a couple of different perceptions yields more that is new — and probably breaks up more often for the same reason.</p><h2>The existential edge</h2><p>Love is not an ornament of life but its condition. A person incapable of love is one of the unhappiest of creatures: to live without it is to remain in the state of a formless thing, for the loss of love is the loss of feeling altogether. That is why we fear losing it so much. But fear is no reason to hoard it: <strong>love is worth seeking anywhere and in anything — and worth not fearing to lose.</strong> The wider a person loves, the more fully they live.</p><h2>Love and freedom</h2><p>Love cannot be held by force. Jealousy is born of the fear of loss, but control kills what it means to keep. True love rests on trust and on the other's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom</a>, not on power over them — <em>love cannot exist beside fear</em>.</p><h2>Connection with Nature</h2><p>Love is not a cultural convention but a force of the living: attraction, attachment and care for offspring run through life itself. The bodily side of that attraction is treated separately — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">intimacy</a>: neither sin nor duty. In calling love a force of Nature, Neoterra includes it in the identity <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Nature = God</a>: the capacity to love is one expression of how Nature continues and guards life.</p><p>Love for another person is changeable and vulnerable, but it has an unshakable ground — <strong>love for life itself and for Nature</strong>. It is given to us so that we might be one with Nature, just as in a couple with a partner; and this love stays with a person to the end of their days. Whoever has established it in themselves is not left without love, even having lost everything else.</p><p>That ground turned out to be not a consolation but a working mechanism. It <strong>feeds the soul where there is no partner</strong>: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a>, who has refused both commune and couple, comes to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">the soul</a> by the same road as the lover — learning a perception from another; only here the other becomes <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> itself, and the road is the form of that closeness.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>If love is action, how is it to be told apart from attachment or dependency?</li><li>Where is the border between sacrifice for love and self-destruction?</li><li>Love &quot;does not look for faults&quot; — but where is the line between accepting the whole and a blindness that harms both the lover and the loved?</li><li>If one learns another's perception in love, is the love of two alike people not love? Neoterra does not go that far: similarity gives peace, difference gives growth, and a couple needs both (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a>).</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a> — the union born of love</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> — love as an action that builds</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> — what people live their lives with; love as mutual mentorship</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> — the frame broken with a witness, against love for one's own perception</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"касание-целого\">Touching the Whole</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"клапан-восприятия\">The Valve of Perception</a> — love as whole seeing</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"бог\">Eloah</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a></li></ul>"},"наставник":{"name":"The Mentor","def":"A mentor is one who holds two states in harmony and teaches others to do the same.","html":"<p>A mentor is <strong>one who holds two states in harmony</strong> and teaches others to do the same. Not the one who makes something new, and not the one who breaks: the one who <strong>has learned to use knowledge in practice and can pass on the skill</strong> — of holding <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">balance</a> and changing state by their own will rather than at the will of circumstance.</p><p>Until now the mentor lived in the wiki only in mentions — in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">the Upanishads</a>, in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the Path of a Person</a>, on the Wall of Memory in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the temple</a> — but had no node. Without one, Neoterra came out sounding as though <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a> were done alone, which it does not claim.</p><h2>Not an innovator</h2><p>The chief distinction runs here, and it lifts a false demand from the mentor.</p><p><strong>The new is made by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the break</a></strong> — the fracturing of a frame of thinking. That is separate work, and not necessarily done by the same person. A mentor need not be a genius, a discoverer or the author of a teaching: what they need is <strong>to command the knowledge in practice</strong> and to be able to bring another into that command.</p><p>The difference is practical, not honorific. Genius is rare, and one cannot build a commune on rarity. The mentor is a reproducible role: whoever has walked the road can lead the next person along it without discovering anything new. That is exactly why <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a> can rest on mentors and cannot rest on geniuses.</p><h2>Two states</h2><p>A person stands between an animal foundation and reason (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a>: &quot;beneath reason the beast's foundation remained, and it did not let go&quot;). A break in thinking loads that structure — and it can fail in <strong>both</strong> directions:</p><p><strong>The mind did not cope.</strong> The information does not fit, and the person retreats into denial — while primacy passes to the animal will. Reason lays down its command because it could not hold. This is the edge of disintegration.</p><p><strong>The mind coped too well.</strong> The animal will is suppressed — and the living force itself goes with it. What remains is clarity without impulse: the person is whole, rational, and <strong>unborn</strong>. The soul — in the sense <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a> gives it: a name for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a>, the spark by which Nature looks at itself — is not born here. This is the edge of stagnation.</p><p>Both edges are death, differing only in speed; the wiki described this figure in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">balance</a>, where the living moves along a narrow band between disintegration and stagnation. The mentor is the one who leads along that band: <strong>neither extinguishing the animal nor surrendering primacy to it</strong>.</p><p><strong>Both edges are the same thing.</strong> <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"душа\">The soul</a> joined them in one formula: <em>the soul does not live a life if the body or the brain crowded it out.</em> Whoever yields to the animal will crowds the soul out with the body; whoever suppresses the will crowds it out with the brain — the very one that coped too well; in both cases the stretch of experience the soul came for is left ungathered. Hence the mentor's work is not reducible to taming the beast — they <strong>hold the passage open</strong>.</p><p>It matters that this is precisely <strong>a pair</strong> and not the whole set. The third way of living — the soul — does not stand opposite will or reason and takes no part in that opposition: it is of another level (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a>). The mentor holds the pair in balance; the soul grows out of a held balance rather than being balanced by it.</p><p>The nearest example of the second edge is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Schopenhauer</a>: a teaching built on the direct suppression of the will, and a life that adapted to solitude without ever coming out of it into harmony.</p><h2>Sitting near</h2><p>The word &quot;upanishad&quot; is translated as <strong>&quot;sitting near the teacher&quot;</strong>: knowledge is passed not by text but by a relation between people. Not a ceremony but a condition.</p><p>The proof from the contrary was given by that same Schopenhauer. He read the Upanishads daily in Latin translation, kept a figure of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"будда\">the Buddha</a>, and was the first in the West to take Indian thought seriously. He had monks — in text. What he did not have was the sitting near: he read the map and did not walk the road.</p><p>Hence the exact border between a book and a mentor: a book passes on <strong>content</strong>, a mentor <strong>a state</strong>. How a balance is held can only be shown with oneself; describing it in words works badly, and so a mentor is irreplaceable exactly to the degree that a skill cannot be reduced to information.</p><h2>Not a shepherd</h2><p>Neoterra's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">commune</a> states plainly: <strong>it does not set a &quot;shepherd&quot; over a &quot;flock&quot;</strong>. The mentor is not an exception to the rule but its test of strength.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Mentor</th><th>Shepherd</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>What is passed on</td><td>the ability to hold a state</td><td>a ready content of belief</td></tr><tr><td>Where it leads</td><td>toward becoming unnecessary</td><td>toward remaining indispensable</td></tr><tr><td>How it ends</td><td>the student leaves and surpasses</td><td>the student stays and serves</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The avenue of memory</a> applies the same mark to figures of the past: <strong>an example wants to be surpassed; an idol cannot be surpassed.</strong></p><h2>Measure</h2><p>The mentor's work is to hold the weight a student cannot bear alone, and not to remove the weight they can. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The commune</a> held this edge open: &quot;what breaks a person is not weakness but an unbearable weight carried alone — so the commune is obliged to hold; but care that removes every weight leaves no room to grow.&quot;</p><p>The mentor sets the measure by hand, anew each time, without a rule. An error one way gives <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a> and a person who has not grown; the other way, a broken one.</p><h2>Those who got no mentor</h2><p>For <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a> the road serves as mentor: it strips away &quot;the protection of home, ready roles, others' answers&quot; without fail, but it knows no measure and does not sit beside. That is why their road is called the most dangerous and the most self-knowing at once.</p><p>Many who brought humanity knowledge were likewise left without a mentor: their frame was broken by life, blindly and at excessive cost. The result went to everyone; the payer got nothing. This is the account Neoterra keeps honestly: <strong>without a mentor what is lost is not the knowledge but the wholeness of the one who wins it.</strong></p><h2>The role is played in many ways</h2><p>It is not always a person with the title of teacher. A strong dissenter (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">Clarity of Mind</a>: &quot;a clear mind seeks strong opponents&quot;), another culture (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a>, the stage of searching for oneself), a book that became an axe (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"кафка\">Franz Kafka (1883–1924)</a>), a master from whom one learns a craft rather than words. At the scale of all humanity the wiki gave the same role to the prophets — &quot;keepers of equilibrium&quot; (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a>). The mentor is the same figure at the scale of a single life.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>Is harmony transmitted or only worked out?</strong> If a mentor teaches a state rather than a content, then transmission goes by imitation — and imitating someone else's balance does not give one's own (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ясность-ума\">authorship</a>). Where is the border between &quot;showed how it is held&quot; and &quot;imposed their own seat&quot;?</li><li><strong>Suppressing the animal — where is the measure.</strong> Neoterra rejects both surrendered primacy and the strangling of the animal will. But there is no instrument for the middle, and the whole ethics of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">vice</a> is built on curbing. How does curbing differ from suppression, seen from the inside?</li><li><strong>A dispute with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ницше\">the tightrope</a>.</strong> Neoterra has already said that the abyss beneath the rope is &quot;not a fall into the animal but ignorance&quot;. The model of two edges returns the animal as a real edge. Is this one abyss or two?</li><li><strong>&quot;The birth of the soul&quot; — an event or a process?</strong> If the soul is a name for <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">self-awareness</a>, then it either is or is not; &quot;was not born&quot; would then mean not absence but unfoldedness withheld. The term needs refining — see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"духовность\">Spirituality</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"смерть\">Death</a>.</li><li><strong>Where mentors come from.</strong> Neoterra sets no shepherds, but neither does it describe who answers for a mentor's fitness. There is no selection — an open edge of the whole practical part (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Община-и-храмы\">Commune and Temples</a>).</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> — the two edges the mentor leads between; equilibrium held by effort</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"восприятие\">Perception</a> — three ways of living: the pair of will and reason, out of which the soul grows</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a> — mutual mentorship: the partner as the one who breaks the frame and sits beside you</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> — the work of making the new, which the mentor is not obliged to do</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> — an error of measure on the side of care</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">The Path of Humanity</a> — the animal foundation and the prophets as keepers of equilibrium</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"упанишады\">The Upanishads</a> — &quot;sitting near the teacher&quot;: a state is passed on, not a content</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> — no shepherd over a flock; the measure of support as an open edge</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"шопенгауэр\">Arthur Schopenhauer (1788–1860)</a> — the edge of a suppressed will; the texts were there, the witness was not</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — the one for whom the road serves as mentor</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"аллея-памяти\">The Avenue of Memory</a> — example against idol: the same mark of distinction</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">The Path of a Person</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li></ul>"},"Община-и-храмы":{"name":"Commune and Temples","def":"An MOC map of Neoterra's practical cluster: how the philosophy becomes a living structure of people, spaces and shared means.","html":"<p>An MOC map of Neoterra's practical cluster: how the philosophy becomes a living structure of people, spaces and shared means. The area's origin is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a>; this node gathers its &quot;earthly&quot; arrangement.</p><blockquote><p>A healthy <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity</a> is assembled from healthy small communities rather than from centralised structures. This cluster is about how such communities live in practice.</p></blockquote><h2>The cluster's supports</h2><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Page</th><th>Question</th><th>Substance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a></td><td><strong>Where it begins</strong></td><td>A voluntary union for the sake of life; the cell of society</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a></td><td><strong>What moves it</strong></td><td>A force of Nature, and the action that gives birth to a family</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a></td><td><strong>Who and why</strong></td><td>People: support, acceptance, finding oneself</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a></td><td><strong>Where</strong></td><td>A space of meeting, knowledge and care</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">Giving and Its Distribution</a></td><td><strong>On what</strong></td><td>Shared means: voluntary and transparent</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The family is the smallest node of this cluster: strong families make a strong commune, and the commune helps families through hard times.</p><h2>Who and why — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a></h2><p>A human being is a social creature: one needs to speak out, to help, to ask for help. The commune does not condemn error; it unites and helps people find themselves — those for whom the solitary road of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a> is not suited (and the Wanderer is always welcome here).</p><h2>Where — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the temple</a></h2><p>The commune's physical embodiment: the main hall, the library, the kitchen corner, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the Wall of Memory</a>, the corner of silence. No throne for a &quot;shepherd&quot;, no compulsory rituals. Future temples are to be in union with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, with music and greenery; their look adapts to the region (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a>).</p><h2>On what — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">giving</a></h2><p>Voluntary, transparent, with no purchase of status. Distribution at <strong>70 / 20 / 10</strong> (temple / region / centre) — the money stays closer to the person. A council of keepers instead of a sole owner, a ban on luxury, priority of spending running from the immediate to the future. One may give time, knowledge and labour too — a gift is a contribution to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a>.</p><h2>The network of mutual aid</h2><p>The supports assemble into an ascending network (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">the Principle of the Network</a>):</p><p>``<code> commune → town temple → regional temple → the country's principal temple → principal temples → the whole world </code>``</p><p>Help and means flow both ways: upward, a request and a small share for the common; downward, support, protection, knowledge. Power does not accumulate at the centre.</p><h2>Principles running through</h2><ul><li><strong>Voluntariness and acceptance</strong> — membership does not depend on contributions (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">Giving and Its Distribution</a>).</li><li><strong>The border of freedom</strong> — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom ends where another's begins</a>: we accept the person, not the harm.</li><li><strong>Transparency</strong> — as <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> toward people.</li><li><strong>Service, not power</strong> — money and role are not for the enrichment of leaders.</li></ul><h2>Neighbouring nodes</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> — the head of the area</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a> — the wiki's origin</li></ul>"},"община":{"name":"The Commune","def":"A commune is a small community of people joined not by descent but by a shared drive to grow, to help one another, and to be near.","html":"<p>A commune is a small community of people joined not by descent but by a shared drive to grow, to help one another, and to be near. In Neoterra the commune, together with <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">the family</a>, is the basic building block of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity</a>: a healthy society is assembled from healthy small communities rather than from centralised structures. Strong families make a strong commune; a strong commune helps families through hard times.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens: why a person needs a commune</h2><p>A human being is a social creature. Alone one survives but does not flourish. The commune answers basic human needs that cannot be met in solitude:</p><ul><li><strong>To speak out.</strong> One needs someone who will listen — not even for advice, but to share.</li><li><strong>To help.</strong> A person needs to be needed. The chance to help another is not a burden but a support for oneself.</li><li><strong>To ask for help.</strong> To be able to admit that you are not managing, and to receive a hand — without shame.</li><li><strong>To talk.</strong> To learn to hear and be heard, to come to terms, to understand another.</li></ul><p>The chief quality of a healthy commune is that <strong>it does not condemn anyone for foolishness or a chance act</strong>. A person comes as they are. An error here is not a sentence but part of the road. Where condemnation is feared, a person closes up and does not grow; the commune makes a safe space in which one may be imperfect.</p><h2>The commune helps you find yourself</h2><p>Not everyone is suited to the road of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a> — the road of knowledge through personal, often bitter experience, a road largely solitary. Most people need support nearby: people among whom one can feel out one's calling, one's meaning, one's own road of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">growth</a>.</p><p>That is what a commune is for — <strong>to unite and to help people find themselves</strong>: it holds the one whom solitude does not suit, and helps the one who is looking for a direction to feel it out.</p><p>And one does not contradict the other: <strong>the Wanderer is always welcome in a commune.</strong> They come, share what they gathered on the road, warm themselves among people — and leave again. The commune is a home you can return to, even if you walk alone.</p><h2>How communes are connected: a network of mutual aid</h2><p>Communes are not isolated — they form a living network of support rising from the small to the universal (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">the Principle of the Network</a>):</p><ol><li><strong>The commune</strong> — people help one another directly.</li><li><strong>The temple in the town</strong> — the commune leans on its own <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">temple</a>: a space of meeting, knowledge and care.</li><li><strong>The regional temple</strong> — town temples are supported by the regional one.</li><li><strong>The country's principal temple</strong> — regional temples lean on their country's principal temple.</li><li><strong>Principal temples → the whole world</strong> — principal temples help people everywhere.</li></ol><p>Help flows both ways: upward, request and support; downward, resources and care. So one person's private need is bound to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity</a> as a whole: the small community is not dissolved into the large one but strengthened by it (unity without uniformity — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a>).</p><p>The same network underlies the distribution of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">giving</a>: the greater part of the funds (70%) stays in the local temple, smaller shares go to the region (20%) and the centre (10%) — the money stays closer to the person.</p><h2>What a commune does not do</h2><p>In Neoterra's spirit (see also &quot;What must not be&quot; in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the temple</a>):</p><ul><li>it does not condemn weakness, error or unlikeness;</li><li>it does not divide people into the &quot;worthy&quot; and the &quot;unworthy&quot;;</li><li>it does not compel — neither to stay nor to leave; the Wanderer is free;</li><li>it does not set a &quot;shepherd&quot; over a &quot;flock&quot;.</li></ul><p>The last rule is tested where a commune does after all need the figure of an elder — see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a>: the one who holds two states in harmony and teaches others to do so, working to become unnecessary. What separates them from a shepherd is not the movement but its direction: the mentor passes on the ability to hold a state, the shepherd a ready content of belief.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Where is the border between the commune's support and dependence on it? The same question from the other side: if what breaks a person is not weakness but an unbearable weight carried alone (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a>), then the commune is obliged to hold — but care that removes every weight leaves no room to grow. The measure of support is an open edge. An error one way gives <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">comfort</a> and a person who has not grown; the other way, a broken one; and the measure must be set by hand, without a rule (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a>).</li><li>How does a network of temples help without turning into a centralised hierarchy of power?</li><li>How can a person be accepted &quot;as they are&quot; while acts that harm others are not excused? The answer lies in the border of freedom: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">a person's freedom ends where another's begins</a>. We accept the person, not the harm.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> — the commune as the building block of a single humanity</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a> — the commune's physical space and the network of temples</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">The Mentor</a> — the figure of an elder who does not become a shepherd; the measure of support set by hand</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — the solitary road; the Wanderer is always welcome in a commune</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — unity without uniformity</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> — the human being as a social creature</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> — the border of freedom: we accept the person, not the harm to another</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свет-из-хаоса\">Light out of Chaos</a> — why hardship does not sort people, and where the duty to hold comes from</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Община-и-храмы\">Commune and Temples</a> — the map of the practical cluster</li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius</a>: &quot;A strong society begins with a worthy person&quot; — the small community as the basis of the large. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Bob Marley</a>: the unity of people through commonality and culture. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"будда\">The Buddha</a>: the Sangha — a community of practitioners as the support of the path; Neoterra's commune is close to it in spirit.</p>"},"открытость":{"name":"Openness","def":"What accepting the new is for a person, openness is for a people.","html":"<blockquote><p><strong>There are no bad nationalities — there are bad people.</strong></p><p>— a thought of the keeper</p></blockquote><p>What <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"понимание-другого\">accepting the new</a> is for a person, openness is for a people. The same organ at a different scale: a community that has stopped accepting the new stops growing — however well it lives.</p><h2>Evil belongs to choice, and a people does not choose</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and evil</a> arise only where there is reason and choice: a stone, a storm and a tiger are never evil. Nationality is not a choice and not an act; it is always a person who chooses, and a person who answers (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a>). So &quot;a bad people&quot; is not a judgement but a category error: a quality that belongs to choice is attributed to something that does not choose.</p><p>Hence the converse: merit is not inherited either. Pride in one's origin is pride in something one did not do.</p><h2>Closedness is not superiority but a refusal of the new</h2><p>The exact wording matters: closedness begins <strong>not</strong> with a feeling of superiority. It begins with a refusal to accept the new; superiority comes afterwards — as an explanation the mind supplies after the fact. &quot;We are better&quot; is not the cause of closedness but its justification, and so arguing with it is pointless: it does not hold the structure up, it decorates it.</p><p>The mechanism is the same as in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"понимание-другого\">understanding the other</a>: a closed entrance is not a defect but the default behaviour, and openness is maintained by effort. The only difference is that for a people the effort must be continuous and shared — which means it requires institutions, not only goodwill.</p><h2>Comfort as a condition of stagnation</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> describes three mechanisms — habituation, weakening, loss of authorship — and all three work at the scale of a country. With enough comfort it is hard to find someone who wants to create or change anything: there is no need. The threshold shifts after what has been achieved, and yesterday's luxury becomes a norm that now has to be defended.</p><p>But comfort by itself is not a verdict: it is a <strong>condition</strong>, not a cause. A wealthy society with an open entrance keeps growing; stagnation comes from the combination <strong>comfort + closedness</strong> — when defending what has been achieved becomes the only task. Comfort makes it possible; closedness makes it inevitable.</p><h2>Why newcomers try harder</h2><p>Someone who received everything by right of birth paid nothing for it — and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">a conviction is tested only by its price</a>. The emigrant paid: with language, status, broken ties, the need to start from zero where no one owes them anything. They are not &quot;better&quot; — they are in a state that the community as a whole is no longer in.</p><p>The observation is borne out by the numbers. According to New American Economy (2019), about 45% of Fortune 500 companies were founded by immigrants or their children; according to NFAP (2022), more than half of American startups valued at over a billion dollars have at least one immigrant founder. The picture is similar in science: the share of immigrants among US Nobel laureates is many times their share of the population.</p><p><strong>An honest caveat — this is selection, not magic.</strong> It is not random people who move: deciding to change countries is within reach of someone already prepared to change their life. That is, openness does not produce active people — it <strong>attracts</strong> people who are already active. For the receiving society the result is the same, but its nature is different, and it is more honest to understand it: the country receives not everyone indiscriminately but the self-selected (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a> is the same type at the individual level).</p><h2>The politician's easy path</h2><p>Propaganda of closedness is the easiest of the available paths, because it runs on two ready-made supports: <strong>fear</strong> and <strong>laziness</strong>. Fear is relieved by an appointed enemy, laziness by the promise that no one will have to change. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">A vice anaesthetises</a> — and here a whole society is anaesthetised at once: anxiety about tomorrow is covered with someone to blame rather than with work.</p><p>Neoterra is not a party and sets no migration rules: it names a mechanism, not a policy. But it does not leave politicians out of the picture — anyone can hold to a philosophy, including those who make decisions for millions. The same requirement applies to them as to any person: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> for consequences and refusal to build on others' fear. Governing people through their worst is a technique that works and, at the same time, an exact description of what the wiki calls <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">evil</a>: the destruction of trust for gain.</p><h2>This does not contradict caring for one's own</h2><p>The objection suggests itself: Neoterra stands on the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">community</a> and the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">family</a> — on small communities that care for their own. Why, then, is &quot;a country doing its best for its citizens&quot; any worse?</p><p>Because in Neoterra <strong>there are no &quot;ours&quot; and &quot;theirs&quot; by design</strong>. It values all life (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>) and cares for everyone, not for holders of the right passport; the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">community</a> is a form of care, not its boundary, and its edges are open (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a>). Care becomes a wall not when it exists, but when it begins with who is refused it.</p><p>The practical distinction is simple: care that appoints no one as superfluous is care. Care that needs someone excluded is already a wall, however warm it sounds inside.</p><h2>Openness is hard, and that is the point</h2><p>An open society lives harder than a closed one — this is not a cost but the very substance of the process. Newcomers arrive with another language, other habits, sometimes incompatible views; the friction is real, and the wiki does not smooth it over. The fruits come not from admission itself but from <strong>friction lived through</strong>: openness without work yields not prosperity but stratification — and serves as the best argument for those who call for closing up.</p><p>It is exactly the same <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">break</a> as for an individual: the new requires not a breakdown but a shift of the habitual view — and it costs effort. A society that refuses to pay this price buys calm at the cost of the future — and not only its own: a closed country subtracts itself from the common growth of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity</a>.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>Group diversity improves the solving of complex problems — the effect has been measured both in teams and in citation studies of mixed research groups. The reason is not virtue: a homogeneous group reaches agreement faster and therefore stops sooner — the collective analogue of a closed entrance. Beside it stands the opposite, just as measured: diversity raises coordination costs and conflict in the short term. Both halves are part of one honest picture: harder now, more productive later.</p><h2>Connection with philosophies and religions</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Popper</a>: the open society lives by criticism, the closed one by dogma; the same pair at the level of a people. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan</a>: the &quot;pale blue dot&quot; — from billions of kilometres away, the borders for which blood is shed cannot be told apart. The <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"стоицизм\">Stoics</a>: <em>cosmopolis</em> — citizenship of the world before citizenship of the city. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"иудаизм\">Judaism</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ислам\">Islam</a>: the commandment about the stranger (&quot;love the stranger, for you were strangers&quot;) and the institution of hospitality — the oldest formulations of the same requirement. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Bob Marley</a>: the unity of humanity through culture.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li><strong>The measure of openness has not been found.</strong> &quot;Being open is better than being closed&quot; is neither a norm nor a number. How much of the new can a community take in without ceasing to be itself? For a person the same unclosed question stands in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">the break</a> and in the register of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">seed</a> — &quot;how to measure what is bearable&quot;; here it is the same, only the cost of error is higher.</li><li><strong>Who pays for the friction.</strong> The fruits of openness go to society as a whole and a generation later; the costs fall on specific people and now. This cannot be waved away: disagreement from below is often not racism but a bill for unpaid friction.</li><li><strong>Selection is not eternal.</strong> The argument &quot;newcomers try harder&quot; rests on self-selection — and that disappears in the second generation, which already receives by right of birth. So openness does not solve the problem of stagnation for good; it only renews the stock of the active. What to do with the next round?</li><li><strong>Reciprocity.</strong> Openness requires it of the one who arrives as well: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"понимание-другого\">understanding the other</a> is mutual, or the receiving side does all the work. But demanding openness from someone who has already lost their home is easy in words.</li><li><strong>What to do with the one who closes up.</strong> If closedness is a refusal of the new and not malice, then a person who has closed up is not an enemy but someone who has stopped (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">we accept the person, but not harm to others</a>). How to call back someone who has closed up without appointing them superfluous — that is, without doing exactly what they are judged for?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"понимание-другого\">Understanding the other</a> — the same organ in an individual: the measure of the mind at the entrance, not the exit</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"комфорт\">Comfort</a> — three mechanisms of stagnation; a condition but not a cause</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a> — evil belongs to choice, and a people does not choose</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пороки\">Vices</a> — the politics of fear as the anaesthetising of a whole society</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — unity without uniformity: not a mixing of peoples but a connection</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> — a single subject of growth; a closed country subtracts itself from the common growth</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a> — care as a form, not as a boundary</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — the same type at the individual level: knowledge gained by leaving home</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"надлом\">The Break</a> — friction as the price of the new; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> — why there is no growth without it</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a> — the history of all peoples belongs to all of humanity</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"поппер\">Karl Popper (1902–1994)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Carl Sagan (1934–1996)</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">The Principle of the Network (Principium Retis)</a></li></ul>"},"пожертвования":{"name":"Giving and Its Distribution","def":"Neoterra rests on voluntary giving.","html":"<p>Neoterra rests on voluntary giving. So that money serves people rather than a centre, a principle of three-level distribution applies: <strong>the greater part stays where it was given</strong>. This is the financial expression of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"принцип-сети\">the Principle of the Network</a> and of the mutual-aid network of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">communes</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">temples</a>.</p><h2>The principle: money stays closer to the person</h2><p>A gift is divided across three levels in the proportion <strong>70 / 20 / 10</strong>:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Where</th><th>Share</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1. Local temple</td><td>stays in place</td><td><strong>70%</strong></td></tr><tr><td>2. Region</td><td>to the regional association</td><td><strong>20%</strong></td></tr><tr><td>3. Central council of Neoterra</td><td>to the common fund</td><td><strong>10%</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The logic is simple: the closer to the person, the larger the share. A temple is not a &quot;collector of money for the capital&quot; but a living node that develops on its own.</p><h2>Level 1 — the local temple (70%)</h2><p>The greater part of gifts stays in place. It goes to:</p><ul><li>the upkeep of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">temple</a>;</li><li>help for members of the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">commune</a>;</li><li>local projects;</li><li>events;</li><li>the library;</li><li>charity.</li></ul><p>So the temple does not become a till for the centre — it develops itself and helps those nearby at once.</p><h2>Level 2 — the region (20%)</h2><p>A smaller part goes to the regional association. It goes to:</p><ul><li>support for new temples;</li><li>large events;</li><li>educational programmes;</li><li>legal aid.</li></ul><p>The region helps temples get on their feet and handles tasks beyond a single temple's strength.</p><h2>Level 3 — the central council of Neoterra (10%)</h2><p>A smaller part still goes to the common fund. It handles what concerns everyone:</p><ul><li>developing the canon;</li><li>international projects;</li><li>translations of books;</li><li>websites;</li><li>global humanitarian initiatives.</li></ul><p>The smallest share belongs to the broadest level. The centre does not accumulate power through money but serves what unites everyone.</p><h2>Giving is always voluntary</h2><p>No one is obliged to pay. In Neoterra there are no:</p><ul><li>compulsory contributions;</li><li>purchases of status;</li><li>paywalls on knowledge.</li></ul><p>A person remains a full part of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a> regardless of the size of their gifts — or with none at all. Knowledge and acceptance are not for sale.</p><h2>Full transparency</h2><p>Any member of a commune can see:</p><ul><li>how much came in;</li><li>what it was spent on;</li><li>how much is left.</li></ul><p>An example of a local temple's monthly report (how its 70% share is divided):</p><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Share</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>rent of premises</td><td>40%</td></tr><tr><td>help for people</td><td>20%</td></tr><tr><td>events</td><td>15%</td></tr><tr><td>development of projects</td><td>15%</td></tr><tr><td>reserve fund</td><td>10%</td></tr></tbody></table></div><blockquote><p>The more transparent the system, the less mistrust.</p></blockquote><p>Transparency is a direct expression of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a> toward those who entrusted their means.</p><h2>The money does not belong to a leader</h2><p>A point of principle: a founder or &quot;shepherd&quot; does <strong>not</strong> automatically own the commune's money. This is a defence against service degenerating into power (cf. &quot;no throne for a shepherd&quot; in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the temple</a>).</p><p>Better is <strong>a council of several people</strong>, for example:</p><ul><li>a keeper of finances;</li><li>a keeper of the commune;</li><li>a keeper of projects.</li></ul><p>Large expenditures are decided <strong>jointly</strong>, not by one person.</p><h2>Priority of spending</h2><p>When there is not enough for everything, the order runs from the immediate to the future:</p><ol><li><strong>Sustaining the commune</strong> — rent, utilities, library, equipment.</li><li><strong>Helping people</strong> — food for those in need, support for members in hardship, volunteer projects.</li><li><strong>Developing the philosophy</strong> — printing books, the website, educational materials, lectures.</li><li><strong>Future projects</strong> — new temples, cultural centres, ecological projects.</li></ol><p>First the commune and its people live — then the philosophy and the future grow.</p><h2>A ban on luxury</h2><p>Essential for trust. If a &quot;shepherd&quot; drives a Ferrari while the commune collects donations, trust vanishes instantly. Hence the principle is fixed:</p><blockquote><p>Gifts are meant for the development of the commune and the service of people, not for the personal enrichment of its leaders.</p></blockquote><p>Beauty, yes; ostentatious costliness for the sake of status, no (the same line as in the look of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the temple</a>).</p><h2>Time is a gift too</h2><p>It is not only money that is given. A person can give:</p><ul><li><strong>time</strong>, <strong>knowledge</strong>, <strong>labour</strong>, <strong>experience</strong>.</li></ul><p>For example: give a lecture, help with repairs, teach children, plant trees. Sometimes this is worth more than money — and it is available to everyone, even without means.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens: giving as creation</h2><p>The essential point in Neoterra: a gift is <strong>not a &quot;payment to the temple&quot; but a contribution to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a></strong>. A person answers for themselves the question:</p><blockquote><p>What can I give so that after me there is a little more knowledge, help, beauty or life in the world?</p></blockquote><p>The distribution reflects the make-up of the whole network: help flows upward (a small share to the common) and downward (support for new temples, protection, knowledge). This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a> in money.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Is the 70 / 20 / 10 proportion universal, or may region and centre change it at need (a disaster, the launch of many temples at once)?</li><li>The council of keepers decides large expenditures jointly — but how is a dispute inside the council resolved, and who watches the council itself?</li><li>How should donated time and labour be valued — on a par with money, or counted separately?</li><li>Where is the threshold of a &quot;large expenditure&quot; requiring a joint decision?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Temple of Neoterra</a> — the levels of distribution repeat the network of temples; the ban on luxury and on thrones</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> — gifts serve the local commune first; membership does not depend on contributions</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> — the common fund works for all humanity</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> — giving as a contribution to creation, not a payment</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> — transparency as responsibility toward the givers</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — unity without centralisation</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Община-и-храмы\">Commune and Temples</a> — the map of the practical cluster</li></ul>"},"путь-симбионта":{"name":"The Symbiont's Way","def":"Humanity is vanishingly small against Nature in the Universe — so small that it cannot even picture Nature's design.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"путь-симбионта.png\" alt=\"путь-симбионта.png\"></p><p>Humanity is vanishingly small against Nature in the Universe — so small that it cannot even picture Nature's design. And that smallness has a choice: the parasite's way or the symbiont's.</p><h2>Smallness as a fact</h2><p>We are like a bacterium at the scale of all Nature. Our existence is so small that the design of the whole is beyond our grasp (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a>, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>). And we could vanish in an instant: for Nature that would be no tragedy but a moment — like swatting a mosquito that had only just begun to drink.</p><p>This is not pessimism but sobriety. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan</a> showed the same thing with a photograph: a pale blue dot, a mote in a sunbeam. Smallness is a fact of scale, and arguing with it is pointless.</p><h2>Smallness as a choice</h2><p>But the bacterium is not only an image of insignificance. Bacteria were the beginning of all life on Earth; out of their smallness everything living grew. Smallness is not a sentence but a starting condition, from which two roads are possible:</p><ul><li><strong>The parasite's way</strong> — to take without returning: to drink the blood of your own home, to drain <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a>, to destroy more than you make. A parasite is sooner or later swatted — not out of revenge but by the logic of life itself: it makes itself superfluous.</li><li><strong>The symbiont's way</strong> — to live so that your existence is of use to the whole: to guard life (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>), to <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">make</a> more than you destroy, and in the limit to carry life onward into <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">space</a>, becoming for Nature not a freeloader but its way of spreading and of knowing itself (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>).</li></ul><p>Hence Neoterra's imperative: <strong>value life and leave the parasite's way.</strong> It is precisely humanity's smallness and erasability that make respect for life not sentiment but a condition of survival: what may &quot;swat&quot; us is not anyone's will but our own parasitism — an exhausted home, war, blindness to consequences (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a>).</p><h2>Humility without abjectness</h2><p>The double truth the symbiont's way holds entire:</p><ul><li><strong>Humility:</strong> we are small, Nature's design is beyond our grasp, and pride of scale is an illusion (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">pride is the chief danger</a>).</li><li><strong>Dignity:</strong> through us Nature looks at itself (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>). The smallness of a point does not cancel the fact that it is at this point that the whole wakes up.</li></ul><p>The symbiont is exactly the balance of the two truths: neither Nature's master nor its parasite, but <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">the part that became aware of itself</a> and behaves as a part.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>&quot;Swatting a mosquito&quot; is an image of will, but God-Nature has no vengeful hand (<a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"добро-и-зло\">Good and Evil</a>): the threat to humanity is blind forces and humanity itself. Does that change the conclusion? No — but it is more honest to say: the leading candidate for the role of the swatting hand is us.</li><li>Every living organism consumes something; where is the border between the metabolism of life and parasitism? (cf. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a>: unavoidable harm against senseless harm)</li><li>If Nature's design is beyond comprehension, where does the confidence come from that symbiosis accords with it? (held as a direction, not as knowledge — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a>)</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> — neither master nor slave: the part that became aware of itself</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"баланс\">Balance</a> — why balance with Nature is not &quot;between&quot; but within it</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"теория-мгновений\">The Theory of Moments</a> — small but not powerless: influence is real within one's own scale</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a> — valuing life as the condition of survival for the small</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"самоосознание\">Self-Awareness</a> — the smallness of the point at which the whole wakes up</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"языки-природы\">The Languages of Nature</a> — the limits of grasping the design</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a> — symbiosis in the limit: carrying life onward</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> — make more than you destroy</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"размыкание-круга\">Opening the Circle</a> — so that humanity does not make itself superfluous</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a> — the area</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Carl Sagan (1934–1996)</a> — the pale blue dot</li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan</a>: &quot;The Earth is the only world known so far to harbour life. There is nowhere else, at least in the near future, to which our species could migrate. Like it or not, for the moment the Earth is where we make our stand.&quot; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"хокинг\">Hawking</a>: concentration on a single planet is an existential risk; mind is obliged to think about its own survival.</p>"},"семья":{"name":"The Family","def":"A family is a voluntary union of people joined by love, trust, responsibility and care for one another.","html":"<p>A family is a voluntary union of people joined by <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">love</a>, trust, responsibility and care for one another. In Neoterra it is one of the most important foundations: the family is older than states, temples and laws — it is what let humanity survive, and it passes on life, knowledge, culture, love and the experience of generations.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>A family exists <strong>not for status, tradition or approval — but for life</strong>. That is its measure: a family is justified by continuing and improving life, not by conforming to a form.</p><p>The family's central question is <strong>not &quot;who is in charge&quot; but &quot;how do we make this family's life better&quot;</strong>. Husband and wife are not rivals but allies; a family must not turn into a struggle for power.</p><h2>Man and woman</h2><p>Men and women differ — biologically, emotionally, psychologically. Their bodies run on different hormonal backgrounds and on different principles of continuing life (insemination and fertility). This is not a trifle but the basis of mutual completion.</p><p><strong>Equality as such does not exist</strong> — it is a convention. In <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> there are no two identical roles: a tiger and an eagle are not equal, but both are necessary to the ecosystem. So here: difference <strong>does not make one higher or lower than the other</strong> — it makes them mutually necessary. The value of a man and a woman lies not in their being the same but in their together giving what neither gives apart. This is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a> at the level of the family.</p><blockquote><p>Not &quot;equal&quot; but <strong>different and equally important</strong>. To replace difference with a notional equality is to lose the point of completion.</p></blockquote><ul><li><strong>A man's responsibility</strong> is not to be the family's master or owner but to protect, support, make decisions in hard moments and answer for the consequences. A real man does not demand respect — he earns it by his deeds.</li><li><strong>A woman's strength</strong> is as a source of new life, a keeper of emotional bonds, a maker of warmth. Neoterra considers motherhood one of the greatest forms of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> — but a woman is not obliged to confine herself to that role and has the right to choose her own road.</li></ul><h2>Healthy relationships</h2><ul><li><strong>Open conversation.</strong> Silence destroys relationships; grievances hidden for years ruin families more thoroughly than open conflict. Neoterra encourages honest dialogue. What people are most often silent about is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">intimacy</a> — and it is what most often ruins a marriage from within; there too it is said why &quot;Nature made it so&quot; does not become an obligation towards a partner.</li><li><strong>Trust instead of control.</strong> Jealousy is born of the fear of loss. Love cannot be held by force — relationships are built on trust.</li><li><strong>No coercion.</strong> Psychological and physical violence, manipulation, blackmail, control through fear contradict the spirit of Neoterra. <em>Love cannot exist beside fear</em> (see <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">the border of freedom</a>).</li></ul><h2>Forms of family</h2><p>Different people build relationships differently. The essential conditions are <strong>voluntariness, honesty, mutual respect, responsibility</strong>. If people consciously choose a form of relationship without harming one another, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a> does not interfere in their choice. This follows directly from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">the border of freedom</a> and from <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity without uniformity</a>.</p><h2>Children and upbringing</h2><p><strong>Until adulthood a child is in the parents' care</strong> — that is their concern and their duty, not a possession. A child is a growing person: they have desires of their own, and a parent must <strong>encourage and guide them, but never suppress</strong> or inflict psychological injury. A suppressed will and early injuries cripple more than the errors of growing do.</p><p>Parenthood is a large <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">responsibility</a>. And yet parents too are living their first life and may err — that is normal and does not make them bad. That is exactly why <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a> is always ready to help with upbringing: to lend a shoulder, offer experience, take some of the load — <strong>but not to replace the family</strong>.</p><p>The parents' task is to protect, teach, guide and prepare the child for an independent life, handing on honesty, responsibility, discipline, respect, a love of knowledge and a love of life. After adulthood the responsibility passes to the person themselves — their <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">own road</a> begins.</p><h2>The road of growing up</h2><p>Adulthood is the beginning of an independent road: to provide for yourself, make decisions, answer for consequences, look for your calling. The stages and virtues of that road are set out in detail in <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человека\">the Path of a Person</a>.</p><ul><li><strong>A young man</strong> goes through the forming of character — travel, work, independent life, new acquaintances, the overcoming of difficulties. Trials grow courage, responsibility, inner steadiness (cf. the road of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">the Wanderer</a>).</li><li><strong>A young woman</strong> likewise gets the chance to understand herself, her abilities and her aims. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The commune</a> is obliged to provide her with safety, respect and support. Every woman has the right to choose her own road.</li></ul><h2>The older generation</h2><p>The old are keepers of experience. A society is obliged to respect its elders. Respect does not mean blind obedience, but the experience of past generations is a valuable resource.</p><h2>Family, commune and the future</h2><p>Strong families make a strong <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">commune</a>; a strong commune helps families through hard times. Neither is complete without the other.</p><p>Every family continues human history — through children, knowledge, values and culture. Therefore <strong>care for the family is care for the future of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">humanity</a></strong>, and a solid family is a small act of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">creation</a> in the large world.</p><h2>The highest principle</h2><blockquote><p>A family should make the lives of its members better. Relationships that destroy a person contradict the spirit of Neoterra; relationships that help one grow, love and become better accord with it.</p></blockquote><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Where is the commune's border of non-interference: when does &quot;their choice&quot; become a harm that can no longer be ignored?</li><li>The line between &quot;guiding a child's desires&quot; and &quot;suppressing them&quot; is clear as a principle — but where is it in the particular case (when does a parent's firm &quot;no&quot; protect, and when does it already injure)?</li><li>If there is no equality but rather different natures of equal importance — how is this to be protected from sliding into a justification of hierarchy (&quot;different&quot; → &quot;some may have less&quot;)? Neoterra's answer: difference does not cancel each person's <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">freedom</a> to choose their own road.</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a> — the force out of which a family is born</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человечество\">Humanity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"созидание\">Creation</a> — motherhood and a solid family as creation</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"ответственность\">Responsibility</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"уважение-к-жизни\">Respect for Life</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"свобода-мышления\">Freedom of Thought</a> — voluntariness, the refusal of coercion</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — the road of forming character</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-семьи-сводка\">The Canon of the Family (0.7)</a> — the source summary</li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius</a>: the family as the primary cell out of which a healthy society grows.</p>"},"храм":{"name":"The Temple of Neoterra","def":"What makes a place a temple is not the architecture but the people gathered for knowledge, growth, friendship and shared making.","html":"<p><img class=\"rimg\" data-asset=\"храм.png\" alt=\"храм.png\"> <em>A greenhouse-temple: a tree grows inside the hall, and around it the library, the kitchen corner, the organ, the Wall of Memory and the corner of silence. No throne, no altar, no dais — everyone on one level of floor.</em></p><p>What makes a place a temple is not the architecture but the people gathered for knowledge, growth, friendship and shared making.</p><h2>Through Neoterra's lens</h2><p>A temple in Neoterra is the physical embodiment of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a>. Not a sacred building for worship but a living space for meeting, growing and connecting. Its purpose is to create conditions in which an ordinary person can easily come, stay, and become part of something larger.</p><h2>Parts of a small temple</h2><h3>The main hall (20–50 m²)</h3><p>The heart of the temple. A place for the commune's gatherings, lectures, book discussions, introductions, festivals.</p><p>The key requirement: the furniture must move easily. Today a lecture, tomorrow a shared supper, the day after board games. The space stays alive rather than setting into one format.</p><h3>The library</h3><p>Even a single bookcase is already a library. It holds:</p><ul><li>the canon of Neoterra;</li><li>philosophy, psychology, science, history;</li><li>biographies of great people.</li></ul><p>Knowledge must be available to everyone who comes.</p><h3>The kitchen corner</h3><p>One of the most important parts. A kettle, a fridge, a few tables — that is enough for the atmosphere of a commune to arise. People get to know one another over food far more easily than at a formal meeting.</p><h3>The Wall of Memory</h3><p>Not an iconostasis. A place of living memory, hung with quotations from philosophers, scientists and writers, and with the stories of local volunteers and members of the commune.</p><p>Examples:</p><blockquote><p>&quot;The important thing is not to stop questioning.&quot; — Einstein</p></blockquote><blockquote><p>&quot;He who has a why to live can bear almost any how.&quot; — Nietzsche</p></blockquote><blockquote><p>&quot;Emancipate yourselves from mental slavery.&quot; — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Bob Marley</a></p></blockquote><p>The wall lives and changes along with the commune.</p><h3>The corner of silence</h3><p>A couple of armchairs. Books. Plants. Soft light.</p><p>A place where a person can simply sit alone — without conversation, without obligations.</p><h2>What must not be</h2><p>Following Neoterra's spirit:</p><ul><li>no throne or dais for a &quot;shepherd&quot; above a flock;</li><li>no compulsory ritual acts (kissing objects and the like);</li><li>no dividing those present into the &quot;holy&quot; and the &quot;ordinary&quot;;</li><li>no luxury for luxury's sake — beauty yes, ostentatious costliness no.</li></ul><h2>The first temple</h2><p>The very first temple of Neoterra may be an ordinary flat or a rented room. Fifteen or twenty people, a bookcase, a big table, tea, cooking together, discussion of philosophy, mutual help — and that is already a temple in spirit.</p><p>But better still as a first real space would be <strong>a greenhouse</strong>: many living plants, natural light, the feeling of nature inside an urban setting — this directly reflects the identity of Nature and Neoterra.</p><h2>The architecture of future temples</h2><p>As the philosophy and the commune grow, temples will be built differently:</p><p><strong>The architectural principle:</strong> a modern building made by a human being <em>for</em> Nature — not against it. A temple should look like something great, made in union with the living world. Nature is not a backdrop; it is the co-author of the space.</p><p><strong>Plants:</strong> much greenery, as in a greenhouse. Plants are not decoration — they are part of the temple.</p><p><strong>Music:</strong> every large temple has an organ and good acoustics. By the <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-культуры-сводка\">Canon of Culture</a>, every temple of Neoterra is <strong>a musical centre</strong>: concerts, symphonies, orchestras, choirs, <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">the music of the world's peoples</a> with no hierarchy of cultures. Music is another form of communication, a language that needs no words. Concerts are part of the commune's life. Good music lifts the mood, calms, brings peace. Where there is no organ — speakers with decent sound.</p><p><strong>Festivals:</strong> the temple is the place of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"праздники\">Neoterra's festivals</a> (the Festival of Spring, the Day of Love, the Day of Memory, the Day of Creation). <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">The Wall of Memory</a> joins directly with the Day of Memory — gratitude to ancestors and teachers.</p><p><strong>Acoustics</strong> are designed as a priority, not as an afterthought.</p><h2>Regional adaptation</h2><p>A temple has no single universal look — it fits the place where it stands.</p><p>Architecture, materials and layout take account of:</p><ul><li><strong>climate</strong>: in hot regions, shade, through-draughts, open courtyards; in cold ones, warmth, enclosure, a hearth;</li><li><strong>local building traditions</strong>: the forms the region's inhabitants find beautiful and their own — not an alien object but a continuation of the cultural landscape;</li><li><strong>local plants</strong>: in the temple's greenhouse and garden, species native to the place.</li></ul><p>This follows directly from the principle of <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">unity</a>: unity without uniformity. All temples of Neoterra are joined by spirit and function — but not by appearance. A temple in Japan will look different from one in Norway or Mexico. And that is right.</p><p>A person comes into a space that is familiar and comfortable to them — and through the comfortable enters something greater.</p><h2>Contradictions and open questions</h2><ul><li>Where is the border between &quot;beautiful&quot; and &quot;luxurious for luxury's sake&quot;? Is an organ an instrument for centuries or a symbol of status?</li><li>How is the openness of the space to be kept as the number of visitors grows?</li><li>Should a temple have a single standard, or does each commune make its own?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a> — unity without uniformity, the principle of diversity among communes</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a> — the human being as part of Nature</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"природа\">Nature</a> — Nature as co-author of the space</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"развитие\">Growth</a> — growth through living interaction</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"странник\">The Wanderer</a> — the wanderer comes to the temple to meet other wanderers</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a> — the temple as the commune's space, and the network of temples</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">Giving and Its Distribution</a> — how means are divided between temple, region and centre (70/20/10)</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Община-и-храмы\">Commune and Temples</a> — the map of the practical cluster</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"музыка\">Music</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"праздники\">Festivals</a> — the temple as a cultural and musical centre</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Bob Marley (1945–1981)</a> — one of the names on the Wall of Memory</li></ul>"},"человечество":{"name":"Humanity","def":"Humanity is a single community.","html":"<p>Humanity is a single community. Not a metaphor of solidarity but a fact: shared biology, a shared planet, a shared fate.</p><p><strong>This page is the head of the &quot;Humanity&quot; area.</strong> Origin: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">the Seed of Neoterra</a>. Shoots: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">family</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">love</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"близость\">intimacy</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наставник\">the mentor</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"храм\">the temple</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"пожертвования\">giving</a> · <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">the symbiont's way</a>. Map of the practical cluster: <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"Община-и-храмы\">Commune and Temples</a>.</p><h2>In Neoterra</h2><p>Neoterra regards humanity not as an assembly of competing groups but as a single subject of growth. The borders between nations, religions and cultures are real and they matter, but they are secondary to what is common.</p><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">Family</a> and <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">the commune</a> are the building blocks of that unity. A healthy humanity is assembled from healthy small communities, not from centralised structures.</p><h2>The long horizon</h2><p>Humanity is not only those alive now. Responsibility toward future generations is built into Neoterra as a basic requirement. Decisions made today must reckon with a horizon of centuries.</p><p>The long future includes <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">the settlement of space</a> — spreading life and preserving mind beyond the Earth. Its condition is <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-симбионта\">the symbiont's way</a>: a humanity living as a parasite upon its own home will simply not reach the far horizon.</p><h2>The single history of humanity</h2><p>If humanity is a single subject, then its history is single too — <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"путь-человечества\">one path of the species</a>, along which Nature experiments in interaction with itself. The <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"канон-культуры-сводка\">Canon of Culture</a> states it plainly: the history of every people — China, India, Egypt, Russia, Europe, America, Africa, the Middle East — belongs to <strong>all of humanity</strong>. No people owns its history alone. The achievements of the past are a common inheritance, not one nation's trophy; <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">culture</a> keeps that shared memory. This is the answer to the question below: global unity is composed not despite cultural diversity but out of it — each culture helps us understand humanity as a whole more fully.</p><h2>Connection with science</h2><p>Genetics confirms our common descent. Anthropology shows shared cultural patterns. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"наука\">Science</a> does not contradict the idea of a single humanity — it grounds it.</p><h2>Open questions</h2><ul><li>How do global unity and cultural diversity relate?</li><li>What is the minimum level of coordination humanity needs as a whole?</li></ul><h2>Related pages</h2><ul><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семья\">The Family</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"любовь\">Love</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"община\">The Commune</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"единство\">Unity</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"культура\">Culture</a> — the shared history and memory of humanity</li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"человек\">The Human Being</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"космос\">Space</a></li><li><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"семя\">The Seed of Neoterra</a></li></ul><h2>Voices of the forerunners</h2><p><a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"конфуций\">Confucius</a>: &quot;A strong society begins with a worthy person&quot; — the family as the building block of the greater whole. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"саган\">Sagan</a>: &quot;Pale Blue Dot&quot; — from a distance of billions of kilometres every border looks like nothing. <a class=\"wl\" data-wl=\"боб-марли\">Bob Marley</a>: the unity of humanity through culture and music.</p>"}};
